1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 d5 6. Bd3 Nc6 7. O-O Be7 8. c4 Nb4 9. cxd5 {*} Nxd3 $5 10. Qxd3 Qxd5 11. Re1 Bf5 12. g4 Bg6 $146 13. Nc3 Nxc3 $1 14. Qxc3 f6 (14... Kf8) 15. Qxc7 (15. Bf4) 15... O-O {Breaking up White's centre and thereby preventing Anand from gaining a grip on the position White now struggles to find a good role for his bishops.} 16. Rxe7 (16. Nh4 $5 {(positionally ambitious, but White is after a bind and also wants to exploit the black knight's position on the rim)} Bd6 17. Nxg6 hxg6 18. Qc3 f5) 16... Qxf3 17. Rxg7+ Kh8 18. Bh6 (18. Bf4 Be4) 18... Qxg4+ ({Now Black gets to change the structure and is never really in any trouble. Thus White should investigate} 18... Be4 $1 {which looks like a much better try for an edge for example,} 19. Rxh7+ Bxh7 20. Qg7#) 19. Qg3 Qxd4 20. Rxg6 (20. Rxb7 Rg8 21. Re1 Rac8 {should also be a draw, although perhaps Black might have tried this.} (21... Qd5 22. Ree7 Qd1+ 23. Kg2 Be4+ 24. Rxe4 Rxg3+ {also would have been fine for Black.} {White is too late to be able to capture on h5, but} 25. hxg3 Qd5 26. Rbe7 f5) (21... Bf7 22. Rxf7 Rxg3+ 23. hxg3 {would also have given Black plenty of counterplay.}) 22. Ree7 {was the alternative, but just as in the game} Qd1+ $1 {ensures Black of counterplay and White isn't at all better after} 23. Kg2 Be4+ 24. Rxe4 Rxg3+ {.} {Enabling the knight to be redeployed, although} 25. hxg3 Qd5) 20... hxg6 $1 21. Qh3 Kg8 {Anand's play has been a little pedestrian over the last few moves, not that the white position was especially easy to handle in a more active vein. Black has clearly fully equalised and indeed if anyone now needs to be careful, it's White due to his split structure.} 22. Bxf8 Rxf8 (22... Qxb2 23. Qe6+ Kxf8 24. Qd6+) 23. Qb3+ Rf7 24. Rd1 Qg4+ 25. Kf1 Kg7 {Trying to bring a piece to c4 or f5, but White's bishops are well centralised and he is able to hold the balance without any real difficulty.} 26. h3 Qe4 27. Qd5 Qc2 28. Rd2 Qc1+ 29. Kg2 Re7 30. Qd8 Qc6+ 31. Qd5 $1 {The opposite-coloured bishops ensure the draw. This was quite a success for the rare 9...0-0, but should the line become more popular we'll probably start seeing some tests of the critical 13 Bxd4.} Qxd5+ $5 1/2-1/2

