1. d4 {Atalik,S Atalik} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. Nc3 {Enough with Petrosian System!} Bb7 5. a3 d5 6. cxd5 Nxd5 7. e3 (7. Qc2 Nxc3 8. bxc3) 7... Be7 {Judit likes this system,it does not offer black much however it is a tough nut to crack.} (7... g6 8. Nxd5 exd5 9. b4) 8. Bb5+ c6 9. Bd3 {I prefer this} O-O (9... c5 10. e4 (10. Bb5+ Bc6 11. Qa4 Qd7 12. Bxc6 (12. Ne5 Nxc3) 12... Nxc6 13. Nxd5 exd5) (10. O-O cxd4 11. exd4 Nd7 12. Re1 O-O) 10... Nxc3 (10... cxd4 11. Nxd5 exd5 12. e5) 11. bxc3) 10. e4 (10. Qc2 h6 11. e4 Nxc3 12. bxc3 c5 13. O-O Qc8) (10. O-O c5 11. e4 (11. Nxd5 Qxd5 12. e4 Qh5 13. dxc5 Rd8 (13... Bxc5 14. b4 Be7 15. Bb2 Rd8 16. Qe2 Nd7 17. Rac1) 14. Qe2 bxc5 (14... Nd7 15. cxb6 Nc5 16. Nd2 Qg6 17. Bc2 axb6 18. f3 Ba6 19. Nc4) 15. Bf4 Nc6)) 10... Nxc3 11. bxc3 c5 12. O-O Nc6 13. Be3 (13. Bb2 Bf6 14. e5 Be7 15. Qc2 (15. Qe2 Na5 16. Nd2 cxd4 17. cxd4 Qd5 18. f4 f5) 15... h6 16. Qe2 Na5) 13... Qc7 (13... Bf6 14. e5 Be7 15. dxc5 (15. Qb1 h6 16. dxc5)) (13... cxd4 14. cxd4 Rc8 (14... Bf6 15. Bb1 (15. e5 Be7 16. Be4 Na5 17. Bxb7 Nxb7) 15... g6 (15... Na5 16. Qd3) (15... Ba6 16. e5 Bxf1 17. exf6 Ba6 18. fxg7) 16. Qd3 Bg7 17. Ba2) (14... Na5 15. Qe2 Kh8) 15. Qe2 Na5 16. Rfe1 Rc3) 14. Qe2 Rfd8 (14... Rad8) 15. h4 Bf6 {Atalik: 'transposes to the text.'} (15... Na5 16. h5) 16. e5 $5 {I wanted to place my queen on f3 that was why I went for this exchange.} Be7 17. Rad1 (17. Ng5 Bxg5 18. Bxg5 cxd4 {transposes to the text.} (18... Rd7 19. Qe4 g6 20. Bf6 cxd4 21. Qf4 Qc8 22. Rac1) 19. Bxd8 Rxd8 20. cxd4 {looks more accurate if you want to exchange on e4 everything.} (20. Qe4 g6) {to} 20... Nxd4 21. Qe3 Nb3) 17... Na5 (17... cxd4 18. cxd4 Bxa3 19. Bxh7+ $11 Kxh7 20. Ng5+ (20. Qd3+ $11 Kg8 {was played by GM Lautier against me in Ohrid 2001.} 21. Qxa3 a5) 20... Kg8 21. Qd3 $132 Ba6 22. Qh7+ (22. Qxa6 Be7) 22... Kf8 {has even Karpov's trademark on. has even Karpov's trademark on. Atalik: 'has even Karpov's trademark on.'} 23. Qh8+ Ke7 24. Qxg7 Rf8 25. Nxe6 Kxe6 26. d5+ $11 Kd7 {Ü 84/430 Ü 84/430} {I was calculating the following line during the game. I was calculating the following line during the game. Atalik: 'I was calculating the following line during the game.'} 27. dxc6+ Kc8 28. Qg4+ Kb8 29. Qa4) 18. Ng5 $1 $146 {Showing good fighting ability but nothing more.} Bxg5 {Draw offer.} (18... g6 $11 19. h5 $1 {(Grischuk,A) Grischuk Grischuk Atalik: 'Grischuk'} (19. Nxh7 Kxh7 20. h5 Kg7 $1 $14 {and white is slightly better. and white is slightly better. Atalik: 'and white is slightly better.'} 21. Qg4 Rh8 22. hxg6 Rh4) 19... cxd4 20. cxd4 Bxg5 21. Bxg5 Rxd4 22. Bf6 $14 {and once GM Adorjan was aiming for such an ending against GM Sax.. and once GM Adorjan was aiming for such an ending against GM Sax.. Atalik: 'and once GM Adorjan was aiming for such an ending against GM Sax..'}) 19. Bxg5 $14 Rd7 20. Qg4 $6 {I have forgotten my prepared move against 19...f6.} (20. Qh5 h6 21. Bxh6 gxh6 22. Qxh6 $11 f6 23. exf6) 20... Kh8 $11 21. Qh5 h6 22. Bxh6 {Here I have decided to force a draw because after white has lost the d line black objectively could not be better.} (22. Bf6 Kg8 23. Qg4 g6 24. h5) 22... gxh6 (22... f5 23. exf6 (23. Be3+ Kg8 24. Qg6) 23... gxh6 24. Qxh6+ Kg8 25. Rfe1 cxd4 26. cxd4 Rxd4 27. Rxe6 $11) 23. Qxh6+ Kg8 24. Bh7+ Kh8 25. Bf5+ {½-½ (25) Atalik,S (2575)-Polgar,J (2685) Bled 2002 CBM 92 [Atalik]} Kg8 $1 26. Rd3 $1 1/2-1/2

