1. d4 {Krasenkow,M Krasenkow,Michal Krasenkow,Michal Krasenkow Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 c5 5. dxc5 Qc7 6. Nf3 Bxc5 7. g3 Qb6 8. e3 Be7 9. g4 (9. Bg2) (9. b3) 9... d6 (9... Nxg4 10. Rg1) (9... Nc6 10. Rg1 Nb4 (10... d6) 11. Qd1) 10. Rg1 (10. b3 Nc6 11. Bb2 d5 (11... Bd7) (11... Nxg4 12. Rg1 Nge5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. O-O-O (14. Rxg7) 14... Ng6 15. h4 Bxh4 16. Ne4 O-O) 12. g5 Nd7 13. cxd5 Nb4 (13... exd5 14. Nxd5 Qa5+ 15. Qd2) 14. Qd1 (14. Qd2 O-O 15. dxe6 fxe6 16. Be2 Qc6 17. e4 Rd8) 14... Nxd5 15. Nxd5 exd5 16. Qxd5 (16. Bxg7 Qa5+ 17. Nd2 Rg8)) (10. a3 Nc6 (10... Qc6 11. Be2) 11. Be2 (11. g5 Nd7 12. b4 Nde5 (12... a5 13. b5 Nce5 14. Nxe5 dxe5 15. Na4 Qc7 16. Bg2 Nc5 17. Nxc5 Bxc5 18. Bb2) 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. f4 Nf3+ (14... Qc6 15. Bg2 (15. Qe4 Qxe4 16. Nxe4 Nf3+ 17. Kf2 Nh4 18. Bb2)) 15. Kf2 Nh4) (11. b4 Nxg4 12. Rg1 Nge5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. Be2 O-O (14... Qc6)) 11... Nxg4 (11... Nd7 12. b4 Nce5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. f4 Qc6 15. Qe4 (15. Qa4 Qxa4 16. Nxa4 Ng6 17. Bb2 Bd7) 15... d5 16. Nxd5 exd5 17. Qxe5 dxc4 18. O-O f6 19. Qc3 Be6) 12. Rg1 Nge5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. Rxg7 Qc6 15. Qe4 Qxe4 16. Nxe4 Ng6) (10. g5 Nfd7 11. Bd2 Nc6 12. O-O-O Nc5) 10... Nc6 11. a3 Nd7 12. b4 Nde5 {Krasenkow: 'Quite logical. White must react energetically, otherwise Black's control of the e4 square will be an important factor.'} (12... a5 13. b5 Nce5 14. Nxe5 Nxe5 15. Be2) 13. Nd2 {Krasenkow: '!' Krasenkow,Michal: '!' '!' Krasenkow,M: '!'} (13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. Be2 Qc6 15. Qe4 d5 16. Nxd5 exd5 17. Qxe5 dxc4 18. g5 (18. Bb2 f6)) 13... Bh4 (13... Bd7 14. Bb2 (14. g5 h6) 14... O-O 15. Be2 Bh4 16. c5 dxc5 17. Na4 Qc7 18. b5 (18. Nxc5 Rfd8) 18... Ne7 19. Qxc5 Qxc5 20. Nxc5 Rac8 21. Nxb7) (13... O-O 14. Bb2) 14. Qe4 (14. Ke2 O-O 15. f4 Ng6 16. Nf3 Bf6 (16... Bd7 17. f5) 17. g5 Bxc3 18. Qxc3 e5) (14. c5 dxc5 15. b5 Ne7 16. Bb2) 14... Qd8 (14... O-O 15. g5 Ng6 16. Bb2 (16. Nf3 f5 17. Qc2 Nce5) 16... f5 17. gxf6 Rxf6 18. Nd1 (18. Rg2 Bd7)) (14... Nxg4 15. Nd5 (15. Rxg4 f5 16. Qxc6+ bxc6 17. Rxh4) (15. Qxg4 Qxe3+ 16. Ne2 Bxf2+ 17. Kd1 Bxg1 18. Qxg7 (18. Nxg1 O-O) 18... Qd4 19. Nxd4 Bxd4 20. Qh6 Bxa1 21. Ne4) 15... Bxf2+ (15... Qd8 16. Qxg4 (16. Rxg4 f5) 16... exd5 17. Qxg7 Bf6 (17... Qf6 18. Qxf6 Bxf6 19. Rb1) 18. Qxh8+ Bxh8 19. Rg8+ Ke7 20. Rxd8 Nxd8 21. Ra2) 16. Ke2 Qd8 17. Qxg4 Bxg1 18. Qxg7 exd5 (18... Rf8 19. Nf6+ Ke7 20. Nf3) (18... Kd7 19. Qxf7+ Ne7 20. Bh3) 19. Qxh8+ Ke7 20. Qxh7 Bg4+ 21. Ke1 Qh8 22. Qxh8 Rxh8 23. h3) 15. Bb2 O-O 16. g5 (16. Qg2 Qf6 (16... a5 17. b5 Ne7 18. O-O-O Qc7 19. f4 N5g6 20. Nf3) 17. g5 (17. b5 Na5 18. g5 Qf5) 17... Qf5) (16. Be2) 16... Bxg5 (16... Ng6 17. Nf3 f5 18. gxf6 Qxf6 (18... Bxf6 19. O-O-O) 19. Rxg6 hxg6 (19... Qxf3 20. Rxg7+ Kxg7 21. Qxh4) 20. Qxh4 Qxf3 21. Ne4 d5 22. Ng5 Qh5 23. Qg3) 17. Qg2 Bh6 $146 {Krasenkow: '?!' Krasenkow,Michal: '?!' '?!' Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: 'N'' Krasenkow,M: '?!' Krasenkow: 'An unsuccessful attempt to improve on the following game. Black just weakens the c4-square.'} (17... Bf6 18. Nde4) 18. O-O-O (18. f4 Qh4+ 19. Qg3 Qxg3+ 20. hxg3 Ng4 21. Ke2 f5 22. Bg2 e5 23. Nd5 Bd7) 18... d5 (18... f5 19. Be2 (19. Qh3 Kh8 20. Kb1 f4 21. Nde4) (19. f4 Ng4 20. Qh3 Ne7 21. Be2 e5) 19... f4 20. Kb1 Qe7) 19. f4 (19. cxd5 exd5 20. Nxd5 (20. Qxd5 Be6) 20... Bg4 21. b5 Rc8 (21... Bxd1 22. bxc6 bxc6 23. Bxe5 Qxd5 24. Qxd5 cxd5 25. Kxd1) 22. bxc6 Rxc6+ 23. Kb1 Bxd1 (23... Rg6 24. Bxe5 Bxd1 (24... Bf5+ 25. Ka1 Rxg2 26. Bxg2) 25. Bg3) 24. Bxe5 Bc2+ 25. Ka1 Bg6) 19... Ng6 (19... d4 20. fxe5 (20. Nb3 dxc3 21. Rxd8 (21. Bxc3 Qe7) 21... cxb2+ 22. Kxb2 Rxd8 23. fxe5 g6) (20. exd4 Ng6 21. Ne2 Nce7) 20... dxe3 (20... dxc3 21. Bxc3) 21. Kb1 exd2 22. Ne4 Ne7 (22... Qc7 23. Nf6+ Kh8 24. Qe4 gxf6 25. Bd3 f5 26. Qh4) 23. Rxd2 Qc7) 20. cxd5 {Krasenkow: 'A typical move exchanging the defender of the light squares in Black's camp. After the bishop exchange the white knight will be comfortably placed on c4.'} exd5 (20... Nce7 21. Nc4) 21. Nxd5 Nce7 (21... Be6 22. Ne4 Kh8 (22... Bxd5 23. Rxd5 Qe7 (23... Qxd5 24. Nf6+ gxf6 25. Qxd5) 24. Kb1) 23. Nc5 b6 24. Nxe6 fxe6 25. Nf6 Qc8 (25... Qc7 26. Nxh7) 26. Ng4 (26. Nxh7 Nce7+ 27. Kb1 Kxh7 28. Bd3 Qe8)) 22. Nc4 Nxd5 23. Rxd5 Qe8 (23... Qh4 24. f5 (24. Rd4 Rd8 25. Bd3 $13 {1-0 Kuerten,D-Westerlund,B/ICCF 1997/ICCF tele 1/2002 (64)} {However,} Rxd4 $142 {Krasenkow transposing to the 11...f6 system.} 26. Bxd4 {Krasenkow is the main theoretical move, quite sufficient for equality. GM Judit Polgar tries another plan, condemned by theory... and fails to rehabilitate it.} Be6) (24. Bd3 Be6 25. Rd4 Rad8) 24... Bxf5 (24... Qe1+ $6 25. Kc2) (24... b5 25. fxg6 hxg6 (25... Qe1+ 26. Kc2) (25... bxc4 $1 26. gxh7+ (26. Qg3 Qxg3 27. gxf7+ Kxf7 28. Rxg3 Be6 29. Ra5 Ke7) 26... Kxh7 27. Bxg7 (27. Be2 Bb7) 27... Rg8 28. Qc2+ f5 29. Rxf5 Qe1+ 30. Kb2 Bxg7+ 31. Rxg7+ Rxg7 32. Rh5+ Kg8 33. Bxc4+ Kf8 $44 {0-1 Kraidman,Y-Smyslov,V/Hastings 1976/Inf 23 (35)} 34. Rh8+ {Krasenkow} Ke7 35. Qe4+) 26. Rxb5 (26. Rd4 Qe1+ 27. Rd1 Bxe3+ 28. Nxe3 Qxe3+ 29. Kb1 Bf5+ 30. Ka1 a5 31. Bd3 Bxd3 32. Rge1 Qf4 33. Rxd3 axb4) 26... Be6 27. Rc5 Rac8 28. Qg3 $14 {/= 1-0 Lombard,A-Scholz Solis,G/Buenos Aires 1978/EXT 2000 (75)} Qe7 $1 $132 29. Bd4 {Krasenkow} Rfd8 30. Kb2) 25. Rxf5 Rac8 26. Kb1 Rxc4 27. Bxc4 Qxc4 28. Re1 (28. Rc1 $16 {1-0 Anikaev,Y-Yuferov,S/USSR 1977/Inf 24 (41)} Qd3+ {Krasenkow} 29. Qc2 Qxe3) (28. Rd1 {Krasenkow} Nh4 29. Qd5 Qxd5 30. Rfxd5 Bxe3 31. Rd8)) (23... Qc7 24. f5 (24. Kb1 Be6 25. Rc5 Qd7 26. Be2 b6 27. Ne5 Qd2 28. Nxg6 hxg6 29. Rc3 Bf5+ 30. Ka1 Rac8 31. Bg4 (31. Ba6 Qxc3) 31... Qxc3 32. Bxc3 Rxc3 33. Bxf5 gxf5 34. Qd2 Rfc8) 24... Bxf5 25. Rxf5 Bxe3+ 26. Kb1 Bxg1 27. Qxg1 Rad8) 24. f5 {Krasenkow: 'Black is now totally passive and can't prevent White preparing a decisive break.'} Bxf5 (24... b5 25. fxg6 hxg6 26. Re5 Be6 27. Na5) (24... Bxe3+ 25. Nxe3 Qxe3+ $14 {½-½ Petrosian,T-Karpov,A/Moscow 1976/URS-ch (63)} 26. Kb1) 25. Rxf5 b5 26. Kb1 (26. Ne5 Qc8+ 27. Nc6 Bxe3+ (27... Qxf5 28. Ne7+ Nxe7 $6 29. Qxg7+ Bxg7 30. Rxg7+ $16 {1-0 Schinzel,W-Boehlig,H/Warsaw 1978/EXT 2002 (29)} Kh8 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'is perhaps a lesser evil:'} 31. Rxf7+ $14 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Kg8 32. Rg7+ Kh8 33. Rg6+ (33. Rf7+) 33... Qf6 34. Bxf6+ Rxf6 35. Rxf6) 28. Kd1 Qd7+ 29. Qd5 Qxd5+ 30. Rxd5 Bxg1) (26. Nd2 Qxe3 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} (26... Bxe3) 27. Rf3 Qe1+ (27... Rac8+ 28. Kb1 (28. Kd1 Qe6) 28... Qxd2 29. Qxd2 Bxd2 30. Bxb5) 28. Kc2 $11 Rac8+ {Krasenkow} 29. Rc3 Rfd8 30. Bd3 Qe3) (26. Nd6 Qe6) 26... bxc4 27. Bxc4 Rc8 (27... Qxe3 $5 28. Rxf7 {Krasenkow}) (27... a5) 28. Qg4 Qxe3 (28... Bxe3 29. Rgf1 Rc7 30. h4 $14 {1-0 Salai,J-Shields,G/IECC 2000/81 telechess (55)} Qd8 $5 {Krasenkow is tempting. After} 31. h5 Qh4 32. Be2 (32. Qxh4 Nxh4 33. Re5 Rxc4 34. Rxe3 f6 (34... g6 35. Re7 {0-1 Thorbergsson,F-Hecht,H/Siegen 1970/EXT 2002 (45) White eventually managed to build up an attacking position but lost the game after all.}) 35. Re7 Rf7 36. Re8+) 32... Qxg4 33. Bxg4 Ne7 34. R5f3) 29. Rgf1 (29. Bxf7+ Rxf7 30. Rxf7 Kxf7 31. Rf1+ Ke7) (29. Rxf7 Rxc4 30. Rxf8+ Kxf8 31. Rf1+ Nf4) 29... Rc7 30. h4 Re7 (30... Nh8) 31. h5 {Krasenkow: '!' Krasenkow,Michal: '!' '!' Krasenkow,M: '!' Krasenkow: 'Still!'} Nh8 ({a prophylactic approach is interesting:} 31... Ne5 32. Bxe5 Rxe5 33. Rxf7 Rxf7 34. Qc8+ Re8 35. Bxf7+ Kf8 36. Bxe8+) (31... Re4 32. Rxf7) 32. Bc1 Qe4+ (32... Re4 33. Qg2 (33. Bxe3 Rxg4 34. Be2 Re4 (34... Rxb4+ 35. axb4 Bxe3 {½-½ Lakic,N-Andersson,U/Banja Luka 1976/MCL}) 35. Bxh6 Rxe2) 33... Qd4 34. Bxh6 Rg4 35. Qe2 (35. Qc2 Qxc4 36. Be3 Qa6 $1 (36... g6 37. Qxc4 Rxc4 38. Ra5) (36... a6 37. Qxc4 Rxc4 38. Ra5 Rc6)) 35... Qxc4 (35... gxh6 36. Bxf7+ Nxf7 37. Rxf7) 36. Qxc4 Rxc4 37. Rg1 Ng6 38. Be3 (38. hxg6 hxg6 (38... gxh6 39. gxf7+ Kh8) 39. Rf4 $36 Rc7 $5 {Krasenkow Here is how the great Ulf Andersson defended this position:} 40. Bg5 f6 41. Bh4 g5 42. Bxg5 fxg5 43. Rxf8+ Kxf8 44. Rxg5) 38... Ne7 (38... Rc3 39. Bxa7 Rxa3 40. Bc5) 39. Rfg5 g6 40. Bxa7 Ra8 41. Bc5 f6 42. R5g2 $18 {1-0 Tukmakov,V-Kuzmin,G/Leningrad 1977/URS-ch (41)} Kf7 {Krasenkow}) 33. Qxe4 Rxe4 34. Bd5 Rg4 (34... Bxc1 35. Bxe4 Bxa3 36. Rb5) 35. Bxh6 gxh6 36. Kb2 Kg7 (36... Rg5 37. Kb3 Rd8 38. Bxf7+ Nxf7 39. Rxf7 a5 40. R7f5 axb4 41. axb4) 37. Kb3 Rg5 38. Ka4 Rd8 (38... Re8 39. Bb3 $16 {[%cal Yd2c4]} Rxf5 $2 {Krasenkow} 40. Rxf5 f6 $143 {Krasenkow} 41. Rb5 Re7 $14 42. Ka5 $5 {Krasenkow} Nf7 {Ü 24/577 Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: 'Ü 24/577''} 43. a4 {Krasenkow}) 39. Bc4 {Krasenkow: 'The complications have ended in a gloomy endgame for Black. His pawns are falling like ripe apples and his g7 knight is still out of play.'} (39. Bb3) 39... Rd4 40. Bb3 Rh4 (40... Rd6 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 41. Ra5 a6 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 42. Bc4 {Krasenkow: '!?' Krasenkow,Michal: '!?' '!?' Krasenkow,M: '!?' Krasenkow: 'was probably more accurate but didn't solve Black's problems:'}) (40... Rd3 {Krasenkow} 41. Rc5) 41. Ra5 {Krasenkow: 'It is essential to capture the a7 pawn and not c5. White's passed a5 pawn becomes extremely formidable.'} Rxa5+ (41... Rg3 $16 42. Rxa7 $1 $16 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Rhh3 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 43. Rb1 Rxh5 (43... Rh4 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 44. Bxf7) 44. b5 Rh4+ 45. Ka5 $18 Rhh3 46. Kb4 Rh4+ 47. Bc4 Rgg4 48. Rc1) (41... Rhxh5 42. Rxa7 Rf5 $16 43. Rxf5 $5 {Krasenkow} Rxf5 44. b5 {but White needn't hurry.}) 42. Kxa5 Rxh5+ 43. Ka6 Rh3 44. Rb1 Ng6 45. Kxa7 {Krasenkow: 'The principle of two weaknesses: a threat to move the a5-pawn forward is combined with an attack on the black king.'} Ne5 (45... f5 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 46. b5 Ne7 47. a4 f4 48. b6 Nc6+ 49. Ka6) 46. b5 Rd3 (46... h5 47. b6 Nc6+ 48. Ka6 $18 h4 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 49. b7 Rc3 50. Kb5 h3 (50... Nb8 51. a4 $18) 51. Bd5 $18 Nb8 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 52. a4 h2 53. a5 Ra3 54. Rb2) 47. b6 Nc6+ 48. Ka6 h5 49. b7 h4 50. Kb6 Nb8 51. a4 Rd4 (51... h3 52. Bc4 Rg3 53. Bb5 h2 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 54. Rh1) 52. Kc5 Rg4 (52... Rd7 53. Bd5 h3 $18 54. Rh1 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'}) 53. Bc4 Nd7+ (53... f5 54. Bb5 $18 Kf6 $1 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: '!''} 55. Kb6 f4 56. a5 h3 $18 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: '+-''} 57. a6 {Krasenkow} Nxa6 {was simpler} 58. Kxa6 {Krasenkow} Rg8 59. Rh1 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'}) 54. Kd6 Nb8 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 55. Bb5 1-0

