1. e4 {Ftacnik,L Hansen, Carsten} c5 2. a3 Nc6 (2... g6 $16) 3. b4 cxb4 (3... e5) 4. axb4 Nxb4 5. d4 d5 6. c3 Nc6 7. exd5 Qxd5 8. Na3 {Hansen, Carsten: '!?'} Bf5 (8... Bd7 9. Nc4 (9. Nf3 e5 (9... Nf6 {Hansen, Carsten: '='} 10. Bc4 Qe4+ 11. Be3) 10. Bc4 Qe4+ 11. Be3 {, and just when it looks like White is winning, Black has} exd4 $1 {Hansen, Carsten: '=!' Hansen, Carsten: 'is of course a draw by repetition'} 12. Bxf7+ Kd8 13. Nxd4 $5 Qxg2 14. Nxc6+ Qxc6 (14... bxc6 $1 15. Rf1) 15. O-O Bxa3 16. Rxa3) 9... e6 10. Nf3 (10. Nh3 e5) 10... Be7 $1 11. Bd3 Rd8 12. Bf4 Bc8 13. Ne3 Qd7 14. Bb5 Bd6 15. Bxd6 $40 Qxd6 {Hansen, Carsten} 16. Rxa7) (8... e5 9. Nb5 Kd8 10. Bg5+ Be7 $11 11. dxe5 Qxd1+ $11 12. Rxd1+ Bd7 $1 $11 {is of course a draw by repetition} 13. Bf4) (8... Qe4+ 9. Be2 Bd7 $13 10. Nf3 e6 11. Ng5 $1 Qf5 12. Nb5 Rc8 13. Bd3 Qd5 14. O-O $1) 9. Nb5 Rc8 10. Nxa7 Nxa7 {Hansen, Carsten: '?!' Judit plays a dangerous line, but in the critical position even avoids the main defence 10...e5 that has yet to be refuted. White has a dangerous initiative for the pawn, but can he aspire to more than the equality?} 11. Rxa7 $146 e5 {Hansen, Carsten: '?!'} (11... Nf6 12. Nf3 g6 13. c4 Qe4+ 14. Be2 $18 Bg7 15. O-O $18 O-O $2 16. Ne5) 12. Nf3 $5 {Carlsen is uncorking a dangerous idea, that would be challenging enough without the limitations of the blindfold game..} exd4 $6 13. Nxd4 (13. Qxd4 Nf6 14. Qxd5 Nxd5 15. Bb5+ $18 Kd8 16. Rxb7 Nxc3 17. O-O) 13... Bd7 14. Nb5 Qxd1+ $2 {[%mdl 256] Hansen, Carsten: '??' Polgar feels, that developing the bishop from c8 is imperative, but unfortunately it is too slow. Suddenly the black queen is cut off from the kingside and White will just win.} (14... Nf6) 15. Kxd1 Bc6 (15... Bc5 $18 16. Rxb7 Nf6) 16. Bd3 (16. Nd4) 16... Bc5 17. Re1+ Ne7 18. Ba3 Bxa3 19. Rxa3 $1 {Black has grabbed three pawns, but her position is completely hopeless.} Rd8 20. Nd4 Kd7 21. Ra7 Rhe8 (21... Nc8) 22. Kc2 Kc7 23. Rb1 Rb8 24. f3 Nd5 25. Nxc6 $1 {Hansen, Carsten: '!?' Carlsen is enjoying himself and tries to win with an impressive attack.} Kxc6 26. Bb5+ Kb6 27. Rxb7+ $1 ({Hansen, Carsten: 'Strictly speaking, the strongest move is'} 27. Rxb7+ $18 {Hansen, Carsten: '!'} Rxb7 {Hansen, Carsten} 28. Bxe8+ {, though the text move is more than adequate as well.} {Hansen, Carsten: 'After'} Kc7 {Hansen, Carsten: '!' Hansen, Carsten: 'it is immediate curtains'} 29. Rxb7+ Kxb7 $18 {Hansen, Carsten: ', and Black doesn't have anything better than'} 30. Bxf7 {Hansen, Carsten} Ne3+ 31. Kd3 Nxg2 32. c4) 1-0

