{Postny,Evgeny: 'Boris Gelfand has an excellent score against Judith Polgar, but in the current game Judith bounced back.'} 1. d4 {Postny,Evgeny} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 c5 4. Nf3 (4. d5 {Postny,Evgeny would lead to Benoni defense.}) 4... cxd4 5. Nxd4 d5 6. Bg2 e5 7. Nf3 d4 {Postny,Evgeny: 'This is a known line where Black seizes space in the center, but is slightly lagging in development.'} 8. O-O (8. Nxe5 $4 {Postny,Evgeny} Qa5+ $19) 8... Nc6 9. e3 d3 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Risky move, as this pawn might become a target.'} ({Nowadays the main line} 9... Be7 {Postny,Evgeny is played nearly automatically.} {After} 10. exd4 exd4 {the main question is whether the d4 is strong or weak.}) 10. Nc3 Bb4 11. Bd2 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Boris refrains from winning a pawn by a standart combination 11.Nxe5, giving preference to a more solid continuation.'} (11. Nxe5 {Postny,Evgeny} Nxe5 12. Qa4+ Nc6 13. Bxc6+ bxc6 14. Qxb4 {White won a pawn, but gave an important light-squared bishop. An engine shows clear edge for White, but from human point of view the matters are far from clear.} Bh3 (14... d2 $2 15. Bxd2 Qxd2 16. Rad1 Qc2 17. Qd6 Bd7 18. e4 $18 {[%cal Ge4e5] ½-½ (49) Sosonko,G (2530)-Miles,A (2555) Bad Lauterberg 1977}) 15. Re1 (15. Rd1 Bg4 16. Rd2 Qd7 17. Qc5 O-O-O 18. e4 $14 {½-½ (27) Hunger,H (2362)-Kudela,S (2322) ICCF email 2007}) 15... Bg4 (15... h5 16. Qc5 Qb6 17. Qxb6 axb6 18. e4 O-O-O 19. Bg5 Rd4 20. Bxf6 gxf6 21. Rad1 Rhd8 22. f3 Rxc4 23. Kf2 $14 {½-½ (52) Hofland,L (2310)-Pezzica,G (2288) ICCF email 2003}) 16. Qc5 d2 17. Bxd2 Qxd2 18. Qxc6+ Ke7 19. Rad1 Bxd1 20. Rxd1 Qxb2 21. Nd5+ Nxd5 22. Rxd5 Rhd8 23. Qc5+ Ke6 24. Qc6+ {½-½ (24) Baumgartner,U (2301)-Myakutin,V (2361) ICCF email 2005}) 11... O-O (11... Bg4 {Postny,Evgeny} 12. h3 Bh5 13. g4 Bg6 14. Nh4 O-O 15. Nxg6 hxg6 16. Nd5 Bd6 17. Bc3 $16 {½-½ (90) Alavi,S (2445)-Edouard,R (2640) Europe Echecs INT 2020}) 12. a3 (12. Nd5 {Ü 49/567} Nxd5 {Postny,Evgeny} 13. cxd5 Qxd5 14. Nd4 Qd6 15. Nxc6 Bxd2 16. Nxe5 Qxe5 17. Qxd2 Bf5 $11) 12... Bxc3 (12... Be7 {Postny,Evgeny} 13. b4 (13. e4 Be6 14. b3 Bg4 $1 15. Be3 Nd4 16. Bxd4 Bxf3 17. Qxf3 Qxd4 18. Nb5 Qb6 19. Qxd3 a6 20. Nc3 Qxb3 21. Rfb1 Rad8 22. Qxd8 Qxb1+ 23. Rxb1 Rxd8 24. Rxb7 Bxa3 $11) 13... Bg4 14. Qb3 a5 15. h3 Bxf3 16. Bxf3 axb4 17. axb4 Rxa1 18. Rxa1 Bxb4 $11 {½-½ (31) Trana,A (2348)-Kudela,S (2286) ICCF email 2004}) 13. Bxc3 Ne4 $146 {Postny,Evgeny: '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Judith finds the way to sacrifice a pawn for the initiative.'} (13... Bg4 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!'} 14. h3 {Postny,Evgeny} Bxf3 15. Qxf3 $14) (13... Re8 14. Nd2 {Postny,Evgeny} Bg4 15. f3 (15. Qb1 $6 Be2 16. Re1 Rc8 $13) 15... Be6 16. b4 $14) ({After} 13... e4 $2 {Postny,Evgeny} 14. Nd2 {Black will lose her central pawn.}) 14. Bxe5 (14. Bb4 $6 {Postny,Evgeny} Re8 (14... Nxb4 15. axb4 Bg4 $13) 15. Ne1 Bf5 16. Nxd3 Nxg3 17. fxg3 Qxd3 18. Qxd3 Bxd3 19. Rfd1 e4 $11 {½-½ (39) Huebner,R (2603)-Muzychuk,A (2532) Marianske Lazne 2009}) (14. Nxe5 $4 {Postny,Evgeny} Nxc3 15. Nxc6 Ne2+ 16. Kh1 bxc6 $19) 14... Bg4 15. Bd4 (15. h3 $6 {Postny,Evgeny} Bxf3 (15... Nxe5 16. hxg4 Nxc4 17. Nd4 Nxg3 $1 18. fxg3 Nxe3 19. Qxd3 Nxf1 20. Bxf1 Qb6 $15) 16. Bxf3 Nxf2 $1 17. Rxf2 Nxe5 18. Bxb7 Rb8 19. Bd5 Qg5 20. Kg2 Qxe3 $13 {½-½ (70) Velten,P (2310)-Graca,R (2246) Nimes 2012}) 15... Ng5 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Black has to play very dynamically in order to keep her d3 passer alive.'} (15... Nxd4 16. exd4 Ng5 17. Qxd3 Bxf3 18. Bxf3 Qxd4 19. Rfd1 Nxf3+ 20. Qxf3 Qxb2 21. Rab1 $16) 16. Bc3 (16. h4 $6 {Postny,Evgeny} Nxf3+ 17. Bxf3 Bxf3 18. Qxf3 Nxd4 19. exd4 Qxd4 $11 {0-1 (68) Wismeijer,J (2069)-Gomez,J (2524) Bangkok 2014}) 16... Rc8 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!'} (16... d2 17. h4) (16... Qd7 17. b4 (17. h4 {Postny,Evgeny} Ne4 18. Qc1 Bh3 19. Qb1 Bxg2 20. Kxg2 Nxc3 21. bxc3 $14 {[%cal Gf1d1]})) (16... Re8 $5) 17. b4 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!'} (17. h4 $1 Ne4 18. Bd4 {Postny,Evgeny: '!'} Nxd4 (18... Bf5 {Postny,Evgeny} 19. b4 $16) 19. exd4 Rxc4 (19... d2 20. Qc2 Bxf3 21. Bxf3 Nd6 22. Qxd2 Nxc4 23. Qf4 $16) (19... Bxf3 {Postny,Evgeny} 20. Qxf3 Nd2 21. Qxd3 Nxf1 22. Rxf1 $16 {Good bishop plus two central pawns worth more than a rook.}) 20. Qxd3 {Postny,Evgeny: ''} Bxf3 21. Qxc4 Bxg2 (21... Nd2 22. Qd3 Bxg2 23. Rfd1 $18) 22. Kxg2 Nd2 23. Qb5 Nxf1 24. Rxf1 $16) 17... Re8 (17... d2 $5 18. b5 (18. Ra2 Qd3) 18... Ne7 19. Ra2 Rxc4 20. Rxd2 Qb6 $44) 18. h4 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Now this is not as effective, as on the previous move. The black rook is already on e8 and therefore the knight on e4 will be protected.'} (18. Ra2 {Postny,Evgeny} Qd7 19. Rd2 Red8 20. b5 Ne7 21. Ne5 Bxd1 22. Nxd7 Be2 23. Ne5 f6 24. Bb4 Nf5 25. Nxd3 Bxf1 26. Kxf1 Rxc4 27. Bxb7 Ne4 28. Bxe4 Rxe4 $11) 18... Ne4 19. Bb2 Qd7 20. Qc1 d2 $2 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Judith goes "all-in".'} ({Postny,Evgeny: 'Swapping the light-squared bishops by'} 20... Bh3 $5 $44 {Postny,Evgeny: 'was a worthful alternative.'} 21. Nd2 Bxg2 22. Kxg2 Qe6 (22... Nxd2 {Postny,Evgeny} 23. Qxd2 Re4 24. Rac1 Rxh4 25. gxh4 Qg4+ 26. Kh2 Qxh4+ $11)) 21. Qc2 Bf5 (21... Rcd8 {Postny,Evgeny} 22. b5 Qf5 {[%csl Rf3]} 23. Ng5 d1=Q 24. Raxd1 Bxd1 25. Qb1 $1 Be2 $1 (25... Nxg3 $6 26. Rxd1 $14) 26. Bxe4 Rxe4 27. bxc6 Bxf1 28. c7 Rc8 29. Nxe4 Qf3 30. Qxf1 Qxe4 31. Qd1 f6 32. Qd7 Qe8 33. Qd5+ Qf7 34. Qd8+ Qe8 $11) 22. Qb3 {Postny,Evgeny: 'It is very natural to move the queen away, but the cold-blooded 22.Rfd1 was actually better.'} (22. Rfd1 $5 {Postny,Evgeny: '!'} f6 (22... Nxf2 $2 23. Qc3 $18) (22... Nxg3 $2 {Postny,Evgeny} 23. Qxd2 $18) 23. Nh2 $13 (23. Rxd2 {Postny,Evgeny} Nxd2 24. Qxd2 Qxd2 25. Nxd2 $14) (23. Nxd2 $2 {Postny,Evgeny} Nxf2 $17)) 22... Be6 (22... Bg4 $5) (22... Bh3 {Postny,Evgeny}) 23. Qc2 (23. Rad1 $5 Bg4 {Postny,Evgeny} 24. Ng5 $5 {Interesting exchange sacrifice in order to eliminate Black's most active light pieces.} Bxd1 25. Rxd1 Nxg5 26. hxg5 Ne5 27. c5 Rcd8 28. Qc2 {White's bishops are excellent, but the d2 is still alive, so from practical point of view this position is rather double-edged.}) (23. Nxd2 $1 Nxd2 (23... Qxd2 24. Bxe4 Bxc4 25. Qxc4 Qxb2 26. Bd5 $16) 24. Qc3 f6 (24... Nd4 25. exd4 Nxc4 26. d5 Nxb2 27. dxe6 $18) 25. Rad1 Red8 26. Bc1 Nb1 (26... Nxf1 {Postny,Evgeny} 27. Rxd7 Rxd7 28. Bxf1 Ne5 $11) 27. Qb3 Qf7 28. Qxb1 Bxc4 29. Rfe1 $14) 23... Bf5 24. Qa4 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Gelfand does not wish to make a draw by repetition of moves.'} Qd3 ({After} 24... Bh3 {Postny,Evgeny} {White has nothing better than to repeat moves by} 25. Qc2 (25. Rad1 $6 Bxg2 26. Kxg2 Qd3 $15)) 25. b5 Nd8 (25... Nc5 26. Qd1 Na5 27. Nxd2 Red8 28. Bd4 $16) 26. Qxa7 (26. b6 $5 Nc6 27. bxa7 Bg4 $13) 26... Ne6 {Postny,Evgeny: '?!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Basically, this is a piece blunder, but the position still remains complicated.'} (26... Qxc4 $5 27. Qd4 {Postny,Evgeny} Ne6 28. Qxc4 Rxc4 29. a4 Rc2 30. Bd4 Bg4 31. a5 Bxf3 32. Bxf3 Nxd4 33. exd4 Nxf2 $1 34. a6 (34. Rxf2 $4 Re1+ 35. Rf1 Rcc1 $19 {Picturesque position with all four rooks on the first rank!}) 34... bxa6 35. bxa6 Nh3+ 36. Kh1 Nf2+ 37. Kg1 $11) 27. g4 {Postny,Evgeny: '!'} (27. Qxb7 Nd6 28. Qd5 Nxc4) 27... Bxg4 28. Ne5 {Postny,Evgeny: 'A lot of black pieces are hanging now.'} Qc2 29. Nxg4 Qxb2 (29... h5 $5 30. Nh2 Rxc4 (30... Qxb2 31. Bxe4 Rxc4 32. Rab1) 31. Be5 N6c5 {Postny,Evgeny} 32. Nf3 Nxf2 $1 33. Rxf2 (33. Nxd2 $6 Qxd2 34. Rxf2 Qxe3 $13) 33... d1=Q+ 34. Rxd1 Qxd1+ 35. Rf1 Qb3 36. Bf4 Qxb5 37. Nd4 $14) 30. Bxe4 Rxc4 31. Bf3 $2 {Postny,Evgeny: 'The turning point.'} (31. Rab1 Qc3 (31... Rc1 32. Qa4 Qc3 (32... Rxf1+ 33. Rxf1 Nc5 34. Qc2) 33. Qb4 Qxb4 (33... Rc8 {Postny,Evgeny} 34. f4 h5 35. Qxc3 R8xc3 36. Nf2 Nc5 37. b6 {White's extra piece should eventually prevail, although Black keeps practical chances.}) 34. axb4 Rec8 (34... f5 {Postny,Evgeny} 35. Rfxc1 (35. Bxf5 $6 Nd4 $1 {[%cal Ge8e1]}) 35... dxc1=Q+ 36. Rxc1 fxe4 37. Rc4 $16) 35. f4 Rxb1 36. Bxb1 Rc1 37. Nf2 $18) (31... d1=Q 32. Rfxd1 Qe2 33. Qxb7 (33. Bg2 Rxg4 34. Qxb7 $16) 33... Nc5 34. Qe7 Qxg4+ 35. Bg2) 32. Bf3 h5 33. Nh2 Rxh4 34. Rfd1 $16) 31... Rc1 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Now White is forced to give a whole rook for the passed pawn.'} 32. Raxc1 dxc1=Q 33. Rxc1 Qxc1+ 34. Kg2 h5 35. Nh2 Nc5 {Postny,Evgeny: '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'White still got a pawn for the exchange, but his king is in trouble. When you got a vulnerable king against Judith, usually you have no chance to survive. This game is no exception.'} 36. Bxb7 (36. Bxh5 {Postny,Evgeny was slightly more stubborn, but still after} Qc2 {White's position is in bad shape.}) 36... Qc2 {Postny,Evgeny: '-+'} 37. Bd5 Qg6+ 38. Kh1 Nd3 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Queen + knight is a well-known nasty duo.'} 39. Nf3 Nxf2+ 40. Kh2 Ng4+ 0-1

