1. d4 {[%emt 0:00:09] Anand Anand Anand Anand E97: King's Indian: Classical Main Line (6...e5 7 0-0 Nc6): 8 Be3 and 8 d5 Ne7, not Ne1} Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. c4 Bg7 4. Nc3 O-O 5. e4 d6 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. Be3 Ng4 9. Bg5 f6 10. Bc1 f5 11. dxe5 (11. Bg5 Bf6 12. Bxf6 Nxf6 13. exf5 $1 (13. dxe5 dxe5 14. Qxd8 Rxd8 15. Nd5 Nxe4 {Portisch,L-Kasparov,G/Linares/1990/}) 13... Bxf5 14. d5 $14) 11... Ngxe5 12. exf5 Bxf5 13. Be3 (13. Nd5 Nxf3+ 14. Bxf3 Nd4) 13... Qf6 14. Rc1 (14. Nd5 Nxf3+ 15. Bxf3 Qf7 $1 (15... Qxb2 16. Nxc7 Rac8 17. Nb5 $13) 16. Qd2 Ne5 17. Be2 c6 $15) 14... Rae8 15. b3 h6 {Covers g5} (15... a5 16. c5 $11) 16. Qd2 (16. Nb5 $1 Re7 17. Nfd4 $132) 16... g5 (16... Ng4 17. Bf4 $11) 17. Nd4 (17. Nxe5 $5 {should be investigated more closely} Qxe5 18. Bh5 $14) 17... Nxd4 {''} 18. Bxd4 g4 (18... Nf3+ 19. Bxf3 Qxd4 20. Qxd4 Bxd4 21. Nb5 $15) 19. Kh1 (19. Be3 c6 $14) 19... Qg6 20. Rg1 Qh5 21. Nd5 (21. Rce1 c5 $6 22. Be3) 21... Be4 22. Nxc7 ({Weaker is} 22. Bxa7 c5 23. Nc3 Nc6 24. Nxe4 Rxe4 $17) 22... Nf3 $1 {'??'} (22... Nd3 $1 {would hold out} 23. Bxd3 Bxd4 24. Bxe4 Rxe4 $14) 23. gxf3 $2 {'+-'} (23. Bxf3 $1 Rxf3 (23... gxf3 24. g4 $1 $16) 24. Rc3 (24. Nxe8 Rh3 25. Qf4 g3 26. Qxg3 Rxg3 27. Bxg7 Qxe8 28. fxg3 Kxg7 $17) (24. Bxg7 Rh3 25. Qxd6 g3 26. Qxg3 Rxg3 27. Nxe8 Qxe8 28. fxg3 Kxg7 $15) 24... Rh3 25. Rxh3 gxh3) 23... Rxf3 {Do you see the mate threat?} 24. Rg2 (24. Bxf3 {is no comparison} Bxf3+ 25. Rg2 Qh3 $19) 24... Qh3 $1 {The mate threat is Rg3} (24... Rh3 25. f3 $1) 25. Rcg1 (25. Nxe8 {'??' going for material but overlooking...} Rxf2 $19 (25... Rg3 {Discovered attack} 26. Nf6+ Bxf6 27. Bf3 Rxg2 28. Qxh6 Qxh6 29. Be5 Rxh2+ 30. Bxh2 Bxf3+ 31. Kg1 Qxc1#)) (25. Bf1 $145 $1 {! Polgar,J} Rd3 26. Qxd3 Bxd3 (26... Bxg2+ 27. Kg1) 27. Bxd3 Qxd3 28. Nxe8 Bxd4 $13) 25... Re5 $3 {Threatening mate: g3} 26. Bxf3 {'??' gives the opponent counterplay} (26. Nd5 Rh5 27. Bxg7 Qxh2+ 28. Rxh2 Rxh2+ 29. Kxh2 Rh3#) (26. Bxe5 $145 $1 {! = Polgar,J ! = Polgar,J Deflection from f2} Bxe5 (26... Rxf2 {Discovered attack}) 27. Rxg4+ Kf7 28. Rg7+ Kf8 (28... Bxg7 29. Rxg7+ Kxg7 30. Qd4+) 29. Rg8+ Kf7 30. R1g7+ Kf6 31. Ne8+ Ke6 32. Nc7+ Kf6 33. Ne8+ $10) 26... Bxf3 {'-+'} 27. Bxe5 (27. Qf4 Qxg2+ 28. Rxg2 Re1#) 27... Bxe5 28. Qd5+ Kh8 $1 {Do you see the mate threat?} 29. Qxe5+ dxe5 $19 {0-1 (29) Granda Zuniga,J (2615)-Polgar,J (2550) Aruba 1992 CBM 030 [Anand,Viswanathan]} 0-1

