1. c4 {Tsesarsky Tsesarsky} Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. e4 d6 4. d4 Bg7 5. Be2 O-O 6. Bg5 $6 {this move idea is to provoke h7-h6 move, and after  retreat to e3 and d1-d2 White will attack h6.} ({Regular continuation is} 6. Nf3 e5 7. O-O Na6 8. Be3 Qe8 9. dxe5 dxe5 10. Nd2 c6 11. c5 (11. Rb1 Qe7 12. a3 (12. Qa4 Rd8 13. b4 Ng4 14. Bxg4 Bxg4 15. b5 $132 {1-0 Korsus,B-Gaede,D/Germany 1999/EXT 2001 (39)}) 12... Nc5 13. b4 Ne6 14. Qc1 Nd4 15. Bd1 Ng4 16. Bxg4 Bxg4 17. f3 Be6 $15 {[%csl Gd4] ½-½ Kurr,G-Kassebaum,R/Germany 1998/EXT 99 (49)}) (11. a3 {-see comments to the game 1-0 Barlov,D-Tosic,M/Belgrade 1998/CBM 64 (33)[Huzman,A]}) 11... Be6 (11... Qe7 12. Bxa6 bxa6 13. Qa4 (13. Nc4 Ng4 $132 {0-1 Keller,T-Hausrath,D/GER 1995/EXT 2001 (29)}) (13. f3 {½-½ Kristiansen,J-Volke,K/Kecskemet 1989/TD (46)  and ½-½ Shabtai,R-Gofshtein,L/Tel Aviv 1990/EXT 97 (71)}) 13... Rd8 14. h3 $14 {1-0 Shipov,S-Yuneev,A/Cheliabinsk 1991/EXT 97 (23)}) (11... Nc7 12. Nc4 Qe7 13. Qc2 (13. Qd6 Qxd6 14. cxd6 Ne6 15. Nxe5 Nxe4 16. Nxc6 Nxd6 17. Ne7+ Kh8 18. Rfd1 $14 {½-½ Marcetic,N-Sahovic,D/Vrsac 2000/EXT 2001 (28)}) 13... Rd8 14. Rad1 Rxd1 15. Rxd1 $14 {1-0 Peralta,F-Netolitzky,G/Internet ICC 2000/EXT 2001 (20)}) 12. Nc4 (12. Qa4 Nc7 13. b4 Qe7 14. Qc2 Nfe8 15. Rab1 f5 $132 {0-1 Baumann,C-Segal,A/Graz 1991/EXT 97 (29)}) 12... Bxc4 13. Bxc4 Qe7 14. Bxa6 bxa6 15. f3 $14 {½-½ Hammerstad,A-Bekker Jensen,A/Gausdal 2000/CBM 74 ext (22)}) 6... Na6 7. Nf3 Qe8 {[%cal Gg5d8] Elegant refutation! Black ignores g5 and doesn't play h7-h6. The last move idea is to play e7-e5 and to avoid unpleasant pin.} 8. O-O e5 9. dxe5 dxe5 10. Nd2 c6 11. Be3 {Wrong opening plan recognition. White lost tempo. In this wellknown theoretical position White's move.} Qe7 $132 12. Nb3 (12. Qa4 $5 h5 13. f3 Nd7 14. Rab1 Bf6 15. Rfd1 Bg5 $132 {½-½ Dao Thien Hai-Lingnau,C/Budapest 1994/CBM 40 (47)}) 12... Rd8 13. Qc2 Ng4 $1 {Now White had to exchange one of .} 14. Bxg4 $6 $15 ({After} 14. Bd2 Nb4 15. Qb1 Qh4 16. h3 Nf6 $132 {[%cal Gc8h3] Black pieces allocated on active positions.}) 14... Bxg4 15. a3 Be6 16. Ne2 f5 {Black wants to open position for his pair of .} 17. f3 Qf7 {[%csl Rc4][%cal Gf7c4]} 18. Rac1 f4 {Advantage transformation. Now Black wishes to arrange Attack by g6-g5-g4 promotion.} 19. Bf2 g5 20. Kh1 g4 21. fxg4 Bxg4 22. Ng1 (22. Bh4 Rd6 $15 {[%cal Gd6h6]}) 22... Qh5 {[%csl Rf3][%cal Gh5f3]} 23. Nd2 {[%cal Gd2f3]} Kh8 24. Ndf3 {White neutralizes pressure, but Polgar's fantasy hasn't ended yet.} Bf6 25. Rcd1 Rg8 {[%cal Gg8g2]} 26. Rd6 {Tsesarsky: 'Of course, Black evaluated his position properly and doesn't want draw after'} Be7 27. Rd2 Bf6 28. Rd6 Rg6 $1 ({Of course, Black evaluated his position properly and doesn't want draw after} 28... Be7 29. Rd2 Bf6) 29. Be1 Bg7 $6 {Badly.} ({Much better was} 29... Rag8 $15 {[%csl Rg2][%cal Gg8g2]}) 30. Rxg6 {White was very glad to change pair of .} hxg6 31. Bc3 Re8 (31... Nc5 $132) 32. Qf2 b6 33. Rd1 Nc5 34. Qe2 g5 35. b4 Ne6 36. Rd6 c5 {[%csl Gd4] preparing d4 point for e6.} 37. bxc5 bxc5 38. Qb2 Nd4 39. Bxd4 cxd4 $2 $16 {after this mistake an advantage pass to White...} ({Right was} 39... exd4 40. Rd5 Bf6 41. Rxc5 Rxe4 $132) 40. Qb5 {[%cal Gf3g5,Gb5e8] threatening xg5!} a6 41. Qd5 (41. Rxa6 $1 Bc8 42. Ra7 g4 (42... Bf6 43. Qc6 $16) 43. Nxd4 $1 $16) 41... Kh7 (41... Bc8 $5 42. c5 $1 $16 (42. Rd8 $2 Bf6 43. Rxe8+ Qxe8 $15)) 42. Rd8 Bf6 43. Qb7+ Kg8 44. Rxe8+ Qxe8 45. Qxa6 Be6 46. c5 $1 ({Badly is} 46. Nh3 $2 g4 47. Nfg5 {[%csl Re6,Rf6][%cal Gg5e6,Ga6f6]} gxh3 $1 48. Nxe6 (48. Qxe6+ Qxe6 49. Nxe6 d3 $19) 48... Qg6 49. Qc8+ Kf7 50. Qd7+ Be7 51. Nd8+ Kf8 52. Qxh3 (52. Ne6+ Kg8 $19) 52... Bxd8 53. Qh8+ Qg8 54. Qxe5 Qxc4 55. Qxf4+ Ke8 $19) 46... g4 47. Nd2 Bg5 48. Nc4 f3 (48... Bf6 49. c6 $16) 49. gxf3 Bf4 50. fxg4 (50. Ne2 gxf3 51. Nxf4 exf4 52. Nd2 Qg6 53. Qf1 $18) 50... Bxg4 51. h3 Qh5 52. Kg2 $4 $11 (52. Qa8+ $1 Kg7 53. Qb7+ Kh8 (53... Kg6 54. Qb3 Be6 55. Qb6 $18) 54. Qb3 Be6 55. c6 $18) 52... Bxh3+ 53. Nxh3 $8 Qg4+ 54. Kf2 Qg3+ 55. Kf1 (55. Ke2 $4 d3+ 56. Kf1 (56. Kd1 Qf3+ 57. Ke1 Qe2#) 56... Qxh3+ 57. Ke1 Qg4 $1 $19 {Tsesarsky: '-+' '-+'}) 55... Qxh3+ 56. Ke1 Qc3+ 57. Ke2 $4 {Why? After d4-d3 promotion with check position of White becomes hopeless.} ({Right was} 57. Kf1 $1 Qf3+ 58. Ke1 (58. Kg1 Qd1+ (58... Bg3 59. Qc8+ Kg7 60. Qd7+ Kh6 61. Qf5 $16) 59. Kf2 Qc2+ 60. Kf3 Qd1+ 61. Kf2 Qc2+ $11) 58... Bg3+ 59. Kd2 Qc3+ 60. Kd1 Qd3+ 61. Kc1 Bf4+ 62. Kb2 Qc3+ 63. Ka2 Qc2+ $11) 57... d3+ 58. Kf2 Qc2+ 59. Kg1 Qh2+ 60. Kf1 Qh3+ 61. Kf2 (61. Ke1 Qg4 $19) 61... Bg3+ 0-1

