{Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,J: '67/99 ''} 1. c4 {Shipov Polgar,J Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,J Polgar,Judit'} Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. e4 d6 4. d4 Bg7 5. f3 O-O 6. Be3 c5 7. Nge2 (7. d5 {leads to another version of the same kind of lines. White's idea is to play Nh3-f2, something Black should never allow. But as White will have to develop his knight from g1 before Black will have to play ...Nbd7, this should not be a big problem.}) 7... Nc6 8. d5 (8. Qd2 {is a true Sämisch King's Indian and beyond the scope of this book.}) 8... Ne5 9. Ng3 e6 10. Be2 exd5 11. cxd5 a6 12. a4 h5 ({Another option is the pawn sacrifice} 12... Bd7 13. O-O b5 $5 {which is very sharp, but probably OK:} 14. Z0 (14. axb5 axb5 15. Bxb5 ({or} 15. Rxa8 Qxa8 16. Bxb5 Bxb5 17. Nxb5 Qa6 {followed by ...Rb8 with full compensation}) 15... Bxb5 16. Nxb5 Qb6 {and Black regains the pawn:} 17. Qe2 Rab8 18. Na7 Qxb2 19. Qxb2 Rxb2 20. Rfb1 Rc2 21. Ra6 (21. Nb5 Nc4 22. Bf4 Nh5 $1 23. Nxh5 Bxa1 24. Rxa1 gxh5 {would favour Black}) 21... Nc4 22. Bf4 Ra8 23. h4 Nd7 24. Kh2 h5 25. Kh3 Nde5 26. Rb7 $4 Nd3 $1 {won a piece in Seirawan-Ivanchuk, Roquebrune (blitz) 1992.}) (14. h3 Rb8 $1 15. b3 ({or} 15. axb5 Bxb5 $1 16. Nxb5 axb5 17. b3 Ned7 18. Ra6 {with unclear play in B.Lalic-Timoshchenko, Piestany 1996; there was no reason for the players to agree a draw just yet}) 15... Ne8 $1 {(this is good in most lines here)} 16. Rc1 bxa4 $1 {(the standard reaction)} 17. bxa4 (17. f4 axb3 18. fxe5 Bxe5 {gives Black far more than enough for the piece}) 17... Rb4 $5 18. Bxa6 Qa5 19. Bb5 Bxb5 20. axb5 Nc7 21. Kh1 Nxb5 22. Nxb5 Qxb5 {and Black was better in Reilly-Nunn, Islington 1990.})) 13. O-O Nh7 14. Qd2 h4 15. Nh1 f5 (15... g5 {Shipov,Sergei} 16. Nf2 Qf6 17. h3 Bd7 18. Rab1 Rac8 19. Nfd1 Ng6 $1 $13 20. b4 $2 cxb4 21. Rxb4 Qxc3 $1 22. Nxc3 Bxc3 23. Qa2 Bxb4 $17 {Haba,P-Rasik,V/CZE/1994/0:1/34/}) 16. Nf2 Re8 (16... Bd7 $5 {is another possibility.} 17. Kh1 {Shipov,Sergei} Re8 18. exf5 gxf5 19. Nh3 Ng6 20. Rfe1 Qf6 21. f4 Re7 22. Bh5 Bh6 $132 {Vyzmanavin,A-Georgiev,Ki/Burgas/1993/0:1/55/}) 17. Kh1 Rb8 18. Rg1 Rf8 $146 {Shipov,Sergei: '!' '!' '!' Shipov,Sergei: ' 19.g3?! fe!/' Shipov,Sergei: ' 19.g3?! fe!/ Polgar,J: 'N'' Shipov: '!'} (18... Kh8 {Ü 59/99 Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 59/99'' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 59/99' Polgar,J: '- 59/99 Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 59/99'''} 19. g3 {Shipov,Sergei} b5 20. axb5 axb5 21. gxh4 $1 Qxh4 22. Rg3 b4 23. Ncd1 Bd7 24. f4 $1 $16 {Vyzmanavin,A-Georgiev,Ki/Groningen/1993/1:0/41/}) 19. exf5 Bxf5 20. g4 (20. Nfe4 {Shipov,Sergei} h3 21. g3 Bxe4 22. fxe4 Nf3 23. Bxf3 Rxf3 $15) 20... hxg3 21. hxg3 (21. Rxg3 $5 {Endre Vegh: 'was worth considering.' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'}) 21... Qe7 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} (21... b5 22. axb5 axb5 23. Kg2 $6 {0-1 (55) Gulko,B-Polgar,J Yerevan Olympiad 1996 [Endre Vegh]} (23. f4 $5 Nf7 24. g4 Bd7 25. Rg3 {looks better.}) (23. Nxb5 $6 {Shipov,Sergei} Rxb5 24. Bxb5 Nxf3 $17)) 22. Kg2 $6 (22. f4 $5 Nf7 23. g4 Bd7 24. Rg3) 22... b5 23. axb5 {Shipov,Sergei: '0-1 (55) Gulko,B (2615)-Polgar,J (2665) Yerevan (ol) 67/99 1996 CI1-130 [Polgar,Judit]'} axb5 {Shipov,Sergei: '' '' '' Shipov: ''} 24. Bh6 {Shipov,Sergei: '?!' '?!' '?!' Shipov: '?!'} (24. g4 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} Bd3 $1 25. Bxd3 Nxf3 26. Qe2 Bxc3 27. bxc3 Rbe8 $44 {Endre Vegh: 'is dangerous for White,'}) (24. f4 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} Nc4 25. Bxc4 bxc4) ({Endre Vegh: 'but'} 24. Rh1 $5 {Endre Vegh: 'was a possibility.' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'}) (24. Nxb5 {Shipov,Sergei} Nxf3 $1 $36) (24. Nce4 $5 {Shipov,Sergei}) 24... b4 25. Bxg7 Kxg7 (25... bxc3 $2 {Shipov,Sergei} 26. Bxf8) 26. Ncd1 (26. Nce4 {Endre Vegh: 'was a decent alternative; maybe White feared' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} Bxe4 27. Nxe4 Nxf3 {Endre Vegh: '!?'} 28. Bxf3 Rxf3 29. Kxf3 Rf8+ 30. Ke3 Re8 $1 {Endre Vegh: 'where Black regains her piece. But sometimes you have to enter these kind of positions.'} 31. Qd3 Nf6 $44) 26... Ng5 {Shipov,Sergei: '!' '!' '!' Shipov,Sergei: ' fg3!/' Shipov: '!'} 27. f4 ({Endre Vegh: 'but'} 27. Rh1 {Endre Vegh: 'was a better choice, as after' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} Nexf3 $2 28. Bxf3 Nxf3 {White has} 29. Qh6+ $1 {.}) ({Instead} 27. Ne3 $2 {runs into} Nexf3 $1 28. Bxf3 Be4 $3 29. Bxe4 Rxf2+ 30. Qxf2 Qxe4+ 31. Kf1 Rf8 {with a winning position for Black,}) 27... Ne4 ({Endre Vegh: 'Worse is'} 27... Nc4 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} 28. Bxc4 Be4+ {Endre Vegh: '?'} (28... Bh3+ 29. Nxh3 Qe4+ 30. Kf1 Qxc4+ 31. Qe2 Qxe2+ 32. Kxe2 Nxh3 33. Rh1 {and the black knight is out of play, even if it doesn't drop off.}) 29. Kf1 Nf3 30. Qe3 {Endre Vegh: 'does not work'}) 28. Qe3 Nxf2 29. Nxf2 (29. Kxf2 {Endre Vegh: '?' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} Rbe8 30. fxe5 {Endre Vegh: '?'} (30. Re1 Qd7 $1 {would also be a lot better for Black}) 30... Qxe5 31. Qxe5+ Rxe5 {Endre Vegh: 'leaves the white king is in trouble.'}) 29... Nc6 {Shipov,Sergei: '' '' '' Shipov: ''} 30. Qxe7+ Nxe7 {Shipov,Sergei: '' '' '' Shipov,Sergei: '× d5/' Shipov: ''} 31. Ra7 Rf7 32. Kf3 $2 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,J: '?''} ({Endre Vegh: 'Better was'} 32. g4 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} Bc2 33. Nh3 Be4+ 34. Bf3 Bxf3+ 35. Kxf3 Nxd5 36. Rxf7+ Kxf7 37. Rd1 Nb6 38. Rxd6 c4) ({or} 32. Bf3 {.}) 32... Bc2 {Shipov,Sergei: '!' '!' '!' Shipov,Sergei: ' b3/' Shipov: '!'} (32... Nxd5 $2 {Shipov,Sergei} 33. Rxf7+ Kxf7 34. Bc4 Be6 35. Re1 Nc7 (35... Re8 $2 36. Ne4 $18) 36. Ne4 Bxc4 37. Nxd6+ $14) 33. Ne4 Nf5 ({Endre Vegh: 'After'} 33... Bxe4+ {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit'} 34. Kxe4 Re8 35. Kf3 Nf5 36. Rxf7+ Kxf7 37. Kf2 {Endre Vegh: 'it is not clear that White is worse.'}) 34. Rxf7+ Kxf7 35. Ng5+ Kf6 36. Bc4 (36. Ra1 $5 Re8 37. Ra7 {does not save White either, because of} Nd4+ 38. Kg4 Bf5+ 39. Kh4 Rh8+ 40. Nh7+ Rxh7+ 41. Rxh7 Nxe2 {and Black wins.}) 36... Re8 37. Ra1 Re3+ 38. Kf2 Rxg3 {Shipov,Sergei: '!' '!' '!' Shipov: '!'} 39. Ra7 Rxg5 {Shipov,Sergei: '' '' '' Shipov: ''} 40. fxg5+ {