1. d4 {Psakhis,L Psakhis} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. g3 c5 5. Bg2 Qa5+ 6. Nc3 Ne4 7. Bd2 {Another interesting move} (7. Qd3 $5 {was played one day early in Leon, but we hope, that there not too chances, that Karpov will see text of this game.} cxd4 8. Nxd4 Nc5 9. Qd1 Nc6 10. e3 Ne6 11. O-O Qc5 12. Ndb5 a6 13. Na4 Qxc4 14. Nbc3 Rb8 15. Nb6 Qc5 16. Ncd5 O-O 17. b4 $44 {1-0 Kasparov,G-Topalov,V/Leon m 1998 (40)}) 7... Nxd2 8. Qxd2 d6 (8... O-O 9. e3 d6 10. O-O Nc6 (10... Bg4 $5) 11. h3 cxd4 12. Nxd4 Bd7 13. Rfd1 Nxd4 14. exd4 Bc6 15. Nd5 Qd8 16. Rac1 $14 {1-0 Karpov,A-Khalifman,A/Linares 1995 (40)}) 9. O-O $6 {After this natural move Black has no shadow of troubles. Stronger was 9.h3!} (9. e3 Bg4 $5 10. Ng1 Nc6 11. h3 Bf5 12. Nge2 O-O 13. Rd1 cxd4 14. exd4 e5 $13 {½-½ Epishin,V-Khalifman,A/Sankt_Peterburg 1995 (38)}) (9. h3 Nc6 10. e3 O-O 11. O-O a6 12. a3 (12. Rfd1 Rb8 13. Nd5 Qxd2 14. Rxd2 b6 15. Rc1 Bd7 $11 {0-1 Izeta,F-Azmaiparashvili,Z/San Roque 1996 (57)}) 12... Rb8 13. Rfd1 b5 14. b4 Qb6 $132 {0-1 Abramovic,B-Malaniuk,V/Nis 1996 (55)}) 9... Nc6 10. e3 Bg4 11. d5 {N Only chance to continue fight, after} (11. dxc5 dxc5 12. h3 Rd8 13. Qe2 Bf5 14. Rad1 Bxc3 15. Rxd8+ Nxd8 16. bxc3 Qxc3 $17 {Black got clear advantage 1-0 Rapoport,I-Gritsak,O/Polanica Zdroj op 1996 (36)}) 11... Bxf3 {Not bad move, but easy were to play} (11... Ne5 $5 12. Nxe5 Bxe5 $11) 12. Bxf3 Ne5 (12... Bxc3 13. bxc3 Ne5 14. Be2 Qa4 15. Qb2 $14) 13. Be2 Qb4 14. Ne4 Qxd2 15. Nxd2 {[%cal Ga7a6,Gb7b5,Gh2h4,Gf2f4] I think chances are more or less equal, but Karpov after the game insist, that White,s position is slightly better.} Kd8 {Maybe beggining of not the best plan.I would prefer 15...0-0} 16. Ne4 Kc7 17. Rab1 Nd7 (17... a6 18. b4 $140 cxb4 19. Rxb4 b6 20. Rfb1 Nd7 $11) 18. Rfc1 (18. Ng5 h6 $1 19. Nxf7 $2 Rhf8) 18... h6 (18... a6 $5 $11) 19. Rc2 Nf6 (19... a6) 20. Nc3 Nd7 21. Ne4 (21. Nb5+ Kb6 (21... Kb8 $5) 22. b4 cxb4 23. Rxb4 Kc5) 21... Nf6 22. Nd2 Nd7 23. Kg2 a6 24. b3 Rhb8 25. h4 $1 {[%csl Rh6][%cal Gh4h5]} b5 (25... h5 $5 26. Ne4 $14 {[%csl Rg5]}) 26. h5 g5 27. f4 $1 gxf4 (27... b4 $5 28. Rf1 (28. fxg5 hxg5 29. Ne4 Bh6 30. Rf1 Ne5 $13) 28... gxf4 29. gxf4 a5) 28. gxf4 bxc4 (28... b4 $5) 29. Bxc4 a5 30. Kf3 a4 31. Ne4 {[%cal Ge4g3,Gg3f5]} axb3 (31... Nb6 32. b4 $1) 32. axb3 Nb6 33. Rg1 Bh8 34. Ng3 $1 Bf6 $6 (34... e6 $142 35. dxe6 $140 Nxc4 36. bxc4 fxe6 37. Ne4 Ra3 $132 {[%csl Re3,Rh6]}) 35. Nf5 $16 {[%csl Yf5,Rh6]} Nxc4 36. bxc4 Rh8 37. Rgg2 {[%cal Gc2a2]} Ra1 (37... Ra4 38. Ra2 Rxc4 39. Ra7+ Kb6 40. Rga2 $36) 38. Ra2 $1 e6 39. Ng3 Rxa2 (39... Ra8 40. Rxa8 Rxa8 41. Ne4 Bh8 42. dxe6 fxe6 43. Rg6 $18) 40. Rxa2 Kb6 41. Ne4 Be7 42. Rb2+ (42. Rg2 $5) 42... Kc7 43. Rg2 Kd7 44. Rg7 Ke8 45. dxe6 fxe6 46. Rg6 Kf7 (46... Kd7 $5 $16) 47. Ng3 (47. f5 exf5 48. Nxd6+ Bxd6 49. Rxd6 Rg8 $1) 47... Bf6 (47... Bh4 48. f5 $1 Bxg3 49. fxe6+ Ke7 50. Kxg3 $18) 48. f5 $1 exf5 (48... Ke7 49. fxe6 Rf8 (49... Kxe6 50. Ne4 $18) 50. Ke4 Kxe6 51. Rxh6 $18) 49. Nxf5 $18 {[%csl Rd6,Rf7,Rh6] Karpov brilliantly played ending and compleatly overplayed his young opponent, got winning position,but, not the first time in the match, missed his chances in big time troubles.Alas!} Bg5 50. Nxd6+ Ke7 51. Ke4 Rf8 52. Kd5 Rf1 53. e4 Rd1+ 54. Kc6 Rh1 55. Nf5+ Kf8 56. Nxh6 Rxh5 57. Nf5 Kf7 58. Rd6 Bf4 59. Rd7+ Kf6 60. Kxc5 Rh8 61. Kd5 Rh1 62. c5 Rd1+ 63. Kc6 Re1 64. Nd6 Ke6 65. Rd8 Rc1 66. Re8+ Kf6 67. Rf8+ Kg5 68. Rf5+ Kg4 69. e5 $6 (69. Kd5 Rd1+ 70. Ke6 Rc1 71. Ne8 $18) 69... Bg3 $1 70. e6 $4 $138 (70. Kd5 $18) 70... Bxd6 71. Rd5 (71. Kxd6 Kxf5 72. e7 Rd1+ 73. Kc7 Re1 74. Kd7 Rd1+ $11) 71... Be7 1/2-1/2

