1. d4 {Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Ftacnik Polgar,Judit Ftacnik' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit Polgar,Judit Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. c4 b6 4. a3 Bb7 5. Nc3 d5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'This is still Black's most solid way of meeting the 4 a3 variation.'''} 6. cxd5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Other moves we have looked at include 6 Qc2 and 6 Bg5.'''} Nxd5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Keeping the diagonal open for the bishop, this recapture is much more popular than 6... exd5.'''} 7. Qc2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Preparing in some lines to play e2-e4, while if Black captures on c3, White can recapture with the queen.'''} Nxc3 (7... Be7 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) (Polgar,Judit) can be seen in Gretarsson-Sargissian, Bled 2002  (ECO code E12).}) 8. Qxc3 h6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Both 8...Bd6 and 8...Nd7 are met by the slightly awkward 9 Bg5, so Black expends a tempo to prevent this move.'''} 9. e3 Nd7 10. b4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Preparing to play Bb2 and dissuading Black from striking out with ...c7-c5.'''} (10. Bb5 $5 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) (Polgar,Judit) Ü 46/(692) Ftacnik,Lubomir: '(Polgar,Judit) Ü 46/(692) Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 46/(692)''} Bd6 11. Bc6 (11. O-O $2 Bxf3 12. Bxd7+ (12. gxf3 $4 Qg5+ {picks up the bishop}) 12... Kxd7 $1 13. gxf3 Qg5+ {and Black has the initiative - Aseev}) 11... Bxc6 12. Qxc6 O-O 13. b4 e5 14. Bb2 Qe7 {(Dreev-Aseev, Barnaul 1988)} 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 Bxe5 17. Bxe5 Qxe5 18. O-O a5 $1 19. b5 a4 {, which is assessed as equal by Aseev.}) 10... Be7 11. Bb2 O-O 12. Rd1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Continuing with the policy of preventing the ...c7-c5 break.'''} (12. d5 $2 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} Bf6 $17) (12. Bd3 $5 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit}) (12. Bb5 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} c6 $1 13. Bxc6 Rc8 14. d5 Bf6 15. Qb3 Bxc6 16. dxc6 Rxc6 17. Nd4 Bxd4 18. Bxd4 Qg5 19. O-O Rfc8 {was completely equal in the game Hergott-Howell, Groningen 1988.}) 12... a5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'N!?' Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'Striking out at the b4-pawn. White's reply is very natural.''' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'N!?' 'N!?'' Polgar is looking for the compensation, that would balance the dangerous battery along the a1-h8 diagonal. Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar is looking for the compensation, that would balance the dangerous battery along the a1-h8 diagonal. Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: 'Polgar is looking for the compensation, that would balance the dangerous battery along the a1-h8 diagonal.'''} (12... Rc8 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit}) 13. b5 (13. bxa5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Rxa5 14. Rc1 c5 $15) (13. Be2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '!?'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '!?' '!?''} axb4 14. axb4 Nf6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: ''' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '' '''} (14... Ra4 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} 15. O-O $36) 15. b5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Nd5 16. Qc4 Bb4+ 17. Kf1 Bd6 $15) 13... Rc8 14. Qb3 (14. Be2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} c6 15. bxc6 Bxc6 16. Qd3 $11) (14. Qd2 $5 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} c6 15. bxc6 Bxc6 16. Ba6 Rc7 17. O-O) (14. Ne5 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} Nxe5 15. dxe5 Qe8 {isn't a problem for Black, who will break out with ...c7-c6.}) (14. Bc4 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} c6 15. Qd3 (15. bxc6 Bxc6 16. Qd3 (16. d5 Bf6) 16... Be4 17. Qxe4 Rxc4) 15... cxb5 16. Bxb5 Nf6 17. O-O) 14... c6 15. bxc6 (15. Be2 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} cxb5 16. Bxb5 Be4 $15) 15... Bxc6 16. Bb5 $2 ({Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'White should be content with''} 16. Be2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'although Black has equalised after'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Bd5 (16... a4 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} 17. Qd3 Nf6 18. O-O b5 {Note that} 19. Ne5 $4 {is a blunder:} Be4 $1 20. Qxb5 Rb8 {and the b2-bishop is lost.}) 17. Qb5 $11) (16. Rc1 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} a4 17. Qd3 b5 $17) (16. Ba6 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} Rc7 17. O-O b5 (17... a4 18. Qd3 Qa8 19. Qe2 Rb8 20. Bb5 Bxb5 21. Qxb5 Qa5 $15) 18. Bxb5 Rb7 19. a4 Qb8 20. Bc3 Bxb5 21. axb5 Rxb5 22. Qa4 Bb4 $15) 16... Bb4+ {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: '!' John Emms: 'I suspect that Karpov simply overlooked this very strong reply.'''} (16... Bd5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 17. Qd3 Nf6 18. O-O Be4 19. Qe2 Rc2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} (19... Qd5 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit}) 20. Rd2 Bxf3 21. gxf3 Rxd2 22. Qxd2 Qd5 23. Qe2 Qh5 24. a4 $11) 17. axb4 Bxb5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '' Polgar,Judit: 'John Emms: 'White is already in big trouble as the bishop on b5 prevents him from getting his king into safety.''' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '' '''} 18. bxa5 $6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '?!''' Karpov was surely not very happy about the last few moves, but this simple capture will only make matters worse. Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Karpov was surely not very happy about the last few moves, but this simple capture will only make matters worse. Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: 'Karpov was surely not very happy about the last few moves, but this simple capture will only make matters worse.'''} (18. d5 $5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!?'''} a4 (18... Bc4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 19. Qc3 f6 20. dxe6 Bxe6 21. Qa3 $11) 19. Qa3 e5 $1 $17 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '!'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '!' '!' Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!'''} (19... exd5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 20. Rxd5 Bc6 21. Rd2 Qe8 $11)) 18... Bc4 19. Qa3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '?'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '?' '?''} (19. Qc3 $2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Be2 $1 $17) (19. Qa4 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit} bxa5 20. Bc3 Qf6 $1 (20... Nb6 21. Qxa5 Ra8 22. Q