1. e4 {Marin,M Marin,M} e5 {Marin,M: 'No Sicilian today.' No Sicilian today.} 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Bb7 10. d4 Re8 11. Nbd2 Bf8 12. a4 Na5 $5 {Marin,M: 'This (previously rare) move has been brought into fashion by Morozevich.' This (previously rare) move has been brought into fashion by Morozevich.} 13. Bc2 (13. Ba2 {Volokitin,A (2662)-Morozevich,A (2731)/Biel 2006/[Marin] (0-1, 59) Marin,M: 'Volokitin,A (2662)-Morozevich,A (2731)/Biel 2006/[Marin] (0-1, 59)'}) 13... b4 14. Bd3 {Marin,M: '*'} (14. d5 {Grischuk,A (2717)-Morozevich,A (2721)/Monte Carlo 2006/CBM 111 ext (0-1, 76) Marin,M: 'Grischuk,A (2717)-Morozevich,A (2721)/Monte Carlo 2006/CBM 111 ext (0-1, 76)'}) 14... d5 $1 $146 ({Inserting the moves} 14... bxc3 {Marin,M: 'Ü 101/270'} 15. bxc3 {Marin,M: 'before breaking the centre with' before breaking the centre with} d5 $6 {Marin,M: 'offers White the possibility to maintain the initiative with' offers White the possibility to maintain the initiative with} 16. Qc2 $1 (16. exd5 {Ivanchuk,V (2729)-Miton,K (2653)/Sochi 2007/CBM 118/[Ftacnik] (1-0, 35) Marin,M: 'Ivanchuk,V  (2729)-Miton,K (2653)/Sochi 2007/CBM 118/[Ftacnik] (1-0, 35)'}) 16... dxe4 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Rxe4 g6 19. Bg5 Qd6 20. dxe5 Qe6 21. Nd4 $36 {Sutovsky,E (2656)-Miton,K (2648)/Montreal 2007/CBM 119 (1-0, 32) Marin,M: 'Sutovsky,E (2656) -Miton,K (2648)/Montreal 2007/CBM 119 (1-0, 32)'}) 15. exd5 ({Marin,M: 'Now,' Now,} 15. Qc2 {Marin,M: 'is less recommendable because of' is less recommendable because of} b3 $1 16. Qb1 (16. Nxb3 dxe4 17. Nxa5 exd3 18. Nxb7 Qd5 $1 {[%csl Rb7,Rc2]}) 16... exd4 17. e5 dxc3 18. exf6 c2 $1 {Golubev}) ({Marin,M: 'After' After} 15. Nxe5 {Marin,M: 'Black can finally insert' Black can finally insert} bxc3 16. bxc3 {Marin,M: 'and then transpose to an analysis given by Ftacnik in the notes to the game Ivanchuk/ Miton' and then transpose to an analysis given by Ftacnik in the notes to the game Ivanchuk/Miton} dxe4 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Rxe4 (18. Bxe4 Bxe4 19. Rxe4 f6 $17) 18... Bxe4 19. Bxe4 Rxe5 20. Bxa8 c6 $15 {Ftacnik}) 15... exd4 {Marin,M: 'Safest.' Safest.} (15... Qxd5 {Marin,M: 'looks risky, but might be playable, too.' looks risky, but might be playable, too.} 16. c4 Qd8 17. Nxe5 Qxd4 $1 18. Ndf3 Qd6 {Marin,M: 'Black has moved quite a lot with his queen, but only needs one tempo (... Rad8) to complete his development.' Black has moved quite a lot with his queen, but only needs one tempo (...ad8) to complete his development.} (18... Bxf3 $2 19. Bxh7+ $1) 19. Bf4 Rad8 20. Ng5 {[%csl Gf7] Marin,M: 'Apparently, very dangerous.' Apparently, very dangerous.} Rxe5 $5 21. Rxe5 h6 (21... Nc6 $2 22. Rd5 $1) 22. Nf3 {[%csl Ga5]} Nc6 {[%csl Gd3]} 23. Rd5 Qxf4 24. g3 {[%csl Gf4] Marin,M: 'Is this the end?' Is this the end?} Nxd5 $1 {Marin,M: 'Not really, just the beginning.' Not really, just the beginning.} 25. gxf4 Nxf4 26. Ne1 Nd4 $1 $44 {Marin,M: 'Despite his material advantage, White might be in trouble already.' Despite his material advantage, White might be in trouble already.}) 16. c4 c6 17. dxc6 Rxe1+ 18. Qxe1 Bxc6 $11 {Marin,M: 'Black has a normal development and a central passed pawn. White's structure is more compact, but he is slightly underdeveloped and the weakness of the b3-square suggests permanent prudence.' Black has a normal development and a central passed pawn. White's structure is more compact, but he is slightly underdeveloped and the weakness of the b3-square suggests permanent prudence.} 19. Qd1 g6 20. Ne5 Bb7 21. Ndf3 Nd7 22. Bg5 Qc7 23. Nxd7 Qxd7 {Marin,M: '='} 24. Ne5 Qd6 25. Ng4 Bg7 26. Nh6+ Kf8 27. Bd2 Re8 28. Rc1 Qc5 29. Qg4 Nc6 30. Qf4 $6 Ne5 $15 {[%csl Yd3][%cal Gd4d3]} 31. Be4 $2 {Marin,M: 'It is not recommended to play with hanging pieces against Judit.' It is not recommended to play with hanging pieces against Judit.} g5 $1 $19 32. Qf5 Bxe4 33. Qxe4 Bxh6 34. h4 Ng6 35. Qb7 a5 36. Qb5 Re5 {Marin,M: '0-1 (36) Kasimdzhanov,R (2690)-Polgar,J (2708) Vitoria Gastei