[%cal Re4e5] e5} Nfd7 16. Rc1 {Khalifman,Alexander: '!' Not the only promising move for White.} (16. Qd2 f6 17. a5 Na8 18. Rec1 Ne5 19. b4 cxb4 20. Nd1 Qe7 21. Nxe5 fxe5 22. Be3 b5 23. axb6 Nxb6 24. Qxb4 Nd7 25. Qe1 $16 {Brumen,D-Kljako,D/Pula op/2000/}) (16. a5 $5 Na8 17. Nd2 (17. Ra3 $5 b5 18. axb6 Rxb6 19. Qa1 $16) 17... b5 18. axb6 Naxb6 19. Bxa6 Bxa6 20. Rxa6 Ne5 21. Qe2 c4 22. Bxe5 Bxe5 23. Qe3 Rb7 (23... Bxc3 $1 24. bxc3 Nxd5 25. Qd4 Qc5 26. Nxc4 Nxc3 $1 27. Qxc3 d5 $14) 24. Na4 Nxa4 25. Rxa4 c3 26. bxc3 Qxc3 27. Nf3 $16 {Karpov,A-Timman,J/FIDE WCh Kuala Lumpur/1990/}) 16... Ne5 17. Nxe5 Bxe5 18. Bxe5 dxe5 $146 (18... Rxe5 $143 19. f4 Re8 20. e5 $1 Bf5 (20... dxe5 21. d6 $16) 21. a5 Nc8 22. e6 c4 23. g4 Qc5+ 24. Kh1 Bd3 25. Bxd3 cxd3 26. Qxd3 Qf2 27. Ne4 $18 {Adler,J-Kljako,D/Bled op/1992/}) 19. Qd2 {Despite the improvement on move 18 Black hasn't solved the opening problems. Khalifman decides to play for the attack, a positional course was also enticing:} (19. a5 {Khalifman,Alexander: '!'} Nd7 20. Qa4 {Khalifman,Alexander: ''} (20. Ra1 $14) 20... b5 21. axb6 Rxb6 22. Qa5 $1 $36 {[%csl Ra6,Rc5]}) 19... Nd7 $6 {Ignoring development backfires.} (19... Bd7 $5 20. a5 (20. d6 Qd8 21. a5 Nc8 $132) (20. b3 Nc8 21. d6 Nxd6 22. Nd5 Qd8 23. Rxc5 Rc8 $11) (20. b4 cxb4 21. Nb5 Qd8 22. Nd6 a5 $5 $44) 20... Nc8 21. Nb1 Nd6 22. Na3 $14) 20. d6 $1 (20. b4 $5 {Khalifman,Alexander} Qd6 (20... cxb4 21. Na2 Qd8 22. Qxb4 $16) 21. b5 a5 22. Nd1 b6 23. Ne3 $16) 20... Qa5 (20... Qd8 $6 {Khalifman,Alexander} 21. Nd5 $16) 21. Red1 $32 {[%csl Gd6,Rf6,Rg7,Rh6] d6,עg8} Kg7 (21... b5 22. axb5 axb5 23. Ra1 (23. Nd5 Qxd2 24. Rxd2 c4 25. Ra1 $36) 23... Qb4 24. Ra7 $16 (24. Nd5 Qxe4 25. Ra7 Bb7 $14)) (21... b6 {Khalifman,Alexander} 22. Qh6 $5 $40) 22. Qe3 (22. b3 $5 {Khalifman,Alexander} Nf6 23. f4 Bd7 24. Qb2 $36) 22... b6 {[%csl Ra5] ףa5} (22... b5 23. axb5 axb5 24. Nd5 $16) (22... Qb4 $6 {Khalifman,Alexander} 23. Nd5 $1 Qxa4 (23... Qxb2 24. Bc4 $18) 24. Bb5 $3 axb5 (24... Qa2 25. Bxd7 B