1. e4 {Blatny,P Blatny,P Blatny,P Blatny,P C42: Petroff Defence: 3 Nxe5 and unusual White 3rd moves} e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 d5 6. Bd3 Be7 7. O-O Nc6 8. c4 Nb4 9. Be2 O-O 10. Nc3 Bf5 11. Qb3 Nf6 12. c5 a5 13. Ne1 Qd7 14. a3 Nc6 15. Nf3 Ne4 (15... Be4 $5 {should not be overlooked} 16. Qd1 Bf5 $11) 16. Nxd5 {''} a4 17. Nxe7+ Qxe7 18. Qxb7 Na5 19. Qd5 Bg6 (19... Bg4 20. Bf4 Nxc5 21. Rae1 $16) 20. Be3 (20. Bd1 Rfd8 21. Qa2 Qd7 $18) 20... Rab8 21. c6 Nb3 22. Rad1 Nd6 23. Qe5 Qd8 24. Qf4 f6 25. d5 Re8 26. Nd4 (26. Qxa4 Re4 27. Nd4 Nxd4 28. Rxd4 Rxb2 $18) 26... Re4 (26... Nxd4 $5 27. Rxd4 Rxb2 $16) 27. Ne6 {'+-'} Qe7 28. Qf3 Bf5 {'?'} (28... Na5 29. Bd3 Nac4 30. Bxe4 Bxe4 $18) 29. Bf4 Bg6 30. Bd3 Nd4 31. Nxd4 Rxd4 32. Bxg6 Rxd1 33. Bxh7+ {'!' Demolition of pawn structure} (33. Rxd1 $6 hxg6 34. Qe3 Qxe3 35. fxe3 Nb5 $18) ({Less advisable is} 33. Qxd1 hxg6 34. Re1 Qd8 $18) 33... Kxh7 34. Qxd1 {Annihilates a defender: d1} (34. Rxd1 $6 Rxb2 35. Qe3 Qd8 $18) 34... Rxb2 (34... Kg8 35. Re1 Qd8 36. Qg4 $18) 35. Qxa4 $18 (35. Re1 {and the result of the game is clear: White will win} Ne4 36. Bxc7 $18) 35... Re2 36. h3 (36. Qd1 {seems even better} Re4 37. Qf3 Kg8 38. Bxd6 cxd6 $18) 36... Nf5 (36... g5 37. Bh2 $18) 37. Qb4 Qf7 (37... Re4 38. Qxe7 Nxe7 39. Bxc7 Nxd5 40. Ba5 $18) 38. Qc4 Re8 39. Qd3 g6 40. Rb1 Rd8 41. Rb7 $18 (41. Rb5) 41... Rxd5 (41... Nd6 {cannot change destiny} 42. Qg3 Nxb7 43. Bxc7 $18 (43. cxb7 $6 Rb8 $16)) 42. Qb3 (42. Qb1 $142 Nd6 43. Qb3 $1 $18) 42... Nd4 43. Qc4 $4 {[%mdl 8192]} (43. Qe3 $18) (43. Qb6 $18 {'!' secures the point} Ne2+ 44. Kh2 cxb6 45. Rxf7+ Kg8 46. Be3 Kxf7 47. c7 $18) 43... Nf3+ $19 {'-+!' Demolishes the pawn shield} 44. gxf3 Rd1+ {Discovered attack} 45. Qf1 Rxf1+ 46. Kxf1 Qc4+ 47. Kg2 Qxf4 48. a4 Kh6 49. Ra7 Qg5+ 50. Kf1 Qc1+ 51. Kg2 Qxc6 $19 {0-1 (51) Morozevich,A (2723)-Polgar,J (2677) Frankfurt 1999 CBM 072 [Blatny,Pavel]} 0-1

