,T/Sailauf 1992 (48)}) (13... Qa5 14. Rh3 b4 15. Nb3 Qb6 16. axb4 Qxb4 17. Rd4 Qb6 18. Na4 Qa7 19. Qd1 Nb6 20. Na5 Rb8 21. Nxb6 Qxb6 22. Nc4 Qa7 23. Nxd6+ Bxd6 24. Rxd6 Bxe4 25. Qd4 Qxd4 26. Rxd4 {1-0 Lasinskas,P (2197)-Kabir,R (2038)/Frankfurt 2002 (62)}) (13... Rc8 14. Rh2 Nb6 15. g5 Nc4 16. Bxc4 Qxc4 17. Rd3 f5 18. Qe3 fxe4 19. Nxe4 e5 20. fxe5 dxe5 21. Re2 O-O 22. Nf5 Qe6 23. Nxe7+ Qxe7 24. Rd7 {1-0 Montell Lorenzo,J (2334)-Regue Farran,E (2053)/Hospitalet 2002}) 14. Rh2 (14. f5 Ne5 15. Qh3 Qd7 16. Be2 O-O-O $13) 14... Nc5 15. Rhd2 {The centralization of both rooks is unusual in this system, but limits Black's counterplay.} (15. Kb1 Na4 16. Nxa4 bxa4 17. Qe2 Rb8 18. Bg2 $13) 15... h5 $5 16. g5 (16. gxh5 f5 17. Bd3 Bxh4 $11) 16... f5 17. Bd3 O-O-O 18. Qe3 fxe4 19. Bxe4 {Motylev is prepared to exchange the bishop as the knights would be controlling the whole center. Motylev is prepared to exchange the bishop as the knights would be controlling the whole center. Motylev is prepared to exchange the bishop as the knights would be controlling the whole centre.} (19. Nxe4 Kb8 20. Kb1 Na4 21. c3 Nb6 22. Qf3 $14) 19... d5 (19... Nxe4 20. Nxe4 Kb8 (20... d5 21. Nf2 $1 Bd6 22. Nd3 $16) 21. Kb1 $14) 20. Bg2 Bd6 $1 21. Rf2 Kb8 22. Kb1 Rhe8 (22... Rhg8 23. Rdf1 Nd7 $14) 23. Rff1 $6 {White is losing time and the rook move is not very constructive.} (23. Nce2 Na4 (23... e5 24. fxe5 Bxe5 25. Nf4 $14) (23... Ne4 24. Rff1 Qc4 $14) 24. Bf3 Nb6 25. Bxh5 Nc4 (25... Rh8 26. Qf3 Nc4 27. Ng3 $14) 26. Qg3 $14) 23... Nd7 24. Nce2 (24. Qf3 Rh8 25. Na2 Nb6 $14) 24... Nb6 25. Ng3 Nc4 26. Qf3 Rc8 (26... e5 27. fxe5 Nxe5 28. Qb3 Nc4 29. Ngf5 $16) 27. Nxh5 Rh8 $1 28. c3 (28. Rf2 $2 Rxh5 29. Qxh5 Nxb2 $19) 28... Qa5 (28... Bxa3 $5 29. bxa3 Nxa3+ 30. Kb2 (30. Kc1 Rxh5 $19) (30. Ka2 Qa5 31. Rd3 Rxc3 $3 32. Rxc3 Nc4+ 33. Kb1 Qb4+ 34. Rb3 Nd2+ 35. Kc2 Qxd4 36. Qd3 Nxb3 $19) 30... Nc4+ 31. Kb1 Na3+ $11) 29. Rd3 $2 {[%mdl 256] The first player had to pay the price for the untimely grabbing of the h5 pawn. Polgar has managed to create very unpleasant threats on the queenside. A defensive move with the rook will cost material and ultimately also the game. The first player had to pay the price for the untimely grabbing of the h5 pawn. Polgar has managed to create very unpleasant threats on the queenside. A defensive move with the rook will cost material and ultimately also the game. The first player had to pay the price for the untimely grabbing of the h5 pawn. Polgar has managed to create very unpleasant threats on the queenside. A defensive move with a rook will cost material and ultimately also the game.} (29. Nf6 $1 Rxh4 (29... Bxa3 30. Nb3 Qa4 31. Nd7+ Ka8 (31... Kc7 32. Nbc5 $16) 32. Nd2 Bc5 $14) (29... Nxa3+ 30. bxa3 Rxc3 31. Nb3 Rxf3 32. Nxa5 Rxa3 33. Nxb7 Kxb7 34. Nxd5 exd5 35. Rxd5 $16) 30. Qg3 Rhh8 31. Rd3 Qc7 $15) 29... e5 $1 30. fxe5 Nxe5 31. Qf6 Qd8 $1 {Black shows her class with a fine retreat of the queen. White's pieces are hanging in the air and the consequences are dire.} (31... Nxd3 32. Qxd6+ Qc7 33. Qxc7+ Rxc7 34. Nf4 $11) 32. Nf4 (32. Qxd8 Rcxd8 33. Nf4 Nxd3 34. Nxd3 Rxh4 35. Rxf7 Rg4 $17) 32... Qxf6 33. gxf6 Nxd3 34. Nxd3 Rcg8 35. Bf3 Rh6 {Some caution is still required, but the black position is already winning. Some caution is still required, but the black position is already winning. Some caution is still required, but Black's position is already winning.} (35... Rxh4 $2 36. Nf5 $11) 36. Be2 Kc7 37. h5 Bc8 38. Kc1 (38. Nb4 Rg5 39. b3 Bh3 $17) 38... Bg4 39. Bxg4 Rxg4 40. Nb4 (40. Rf5 Rh4 41. Rxd5 R4xh5 42. Rxh5 Rxh5 $19) 40... Bxb4 41. axb4 Rxh5 {The rest requires just a little bit of technique. The rest requires just a little bit of technique. The rest requires just a little bit of technique.} 42. Rf2 Kd6 43. Kb1 Rhg5 44. Nf5+ Ke6 45. Nd4+ Kd7 46. Nb3 Rg2 47. Rf3 (47. Nc5+ Kd6 48. Rxg2 Rxg2 49. Nxa6 Rf2 $19) 47... R5g3 48. Rf4 Rh3 49. Nc5+ Kd6 50. Rf1 Rhh2 51. Nd3 Rd2 52. Rf3 d4 (52... d4 $1 53. cxd4 Kd5 54. Kc1 Ke4 55. Ne1 Rxb2 $19) 0-1

