1. e4 {Movsesian Movsesian Movsesian: 'Ribli'} c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nc3 Qc7 6. Be3 a6 7. Qd2 Nf6 8. O-O-O Bb4 9. f3 {Movsesian: 'Ribli: 'Übrigens spielt Judit Polgar - wie Movsesian auch - diese Variante mit beiden Farben.''} Ne5 10. Nb3 d5 {Movsesian: 'Ribli: 'Dieser Zug wird selten gespielt. Die Hauptvariante ist 10...b5.''} 11. Bd4 O-O 12. Kb1 $5 $146 {Movsesian: '!?' '!?' Movsesian: 'Ribli: 'Früher spielte Weiß 12.a3. Der Partiezug scheint mir noch stärker.''} ({Movsesian: 'All the moves before were already played several times. White here always opted for'} 12. a3 {Ü 86/169 Movsesian: 'e.g'} Bd6 {Movsesian} 13. exd5 exd5 14. Qf2 b5 15. Bxb5 axb5 16. Nxb5 Qb8 17. Nxd6 Qxd6 18. Bc5 Qd8 19. Bxf8 Qxf8 $13 {Vallejo Pons-Kasimdzanov, Pamplona 2002}) 12... dxe4 13. Qf4 Bd6 14. Nxe4 Nxe4 15. Qxe4 Nc6 {Movsesian: 'Black has first to retreat the knight to develop the c8 bishop. '} (15... Bd7 $2 16. Bxe5 Bxe5 17. Rxd7 Qxd7 18. Bd3 $1 $18) 16. Bc3 Bd7 17. g4 $1 {Movsesian: 'A good move. White is fighting against the f7-f5 idea, trying to get strong attack. '} Rfe8 18. Bd3 g6 19. Rhe1 $5 {Movsesian: 'Not an easy move to make. White rook on h1 looks more promising, due to opening of the "h" file in future, but it was more important to avoid Bd6-e5 at this moment. ' Movsesian: 'Ribli: 'Mit diesem Zug verhindert Weiß die Möglichkeit 19...e5.''} e5 {Movsesian: 'Black is lacking space, so this is a try to get black's pieces to work.'} 20. h4 Ne7 21. Bc4 (21. Bxe5 {Movsesian: 'will just help black'} Nc6 22. Bxd6 Qxd6 23. Qc4 Rxe1 24. Rxe1 Qg3 $1 $44 {Movsesian: '!' '!' Movsesian: 'with sufficient compensation '}) 21... Bc6 ({Movsesian: 'Of cource not'} 21... b5 $2 22. Bxf7+ Kxf7 23. Qd3) 22. Qd3 $5 {Movsesian: 'Provoking the rook to come to d8, where can be later attacked by a bishop from a5'} Rad8 23. Qe3 Nc8 {Movsesian: ''!' Ribli. ' Movsesian: 'Ribli: 'Ein guter Verteidigungszug - Schwarz verteidigt sich gegen 24.a5 und bereitet das Springermanöver b6-a4 vor.''} 24. h5 Nb6 25. Na5 (25. Bxf7+ Qxf7 26. Qxb6 Bc7 $1 {Movsesian: 'and black is OK again here.'}) 25... Na4 26. Bd2 Bc5 27. Qe2 Bd5 28. hxg6 hxg6 29. Bxd5 $6 {Movsesian: 'First step to the wrong direction.'} (29. Qh2 {Movsesian: '!' '!' Movsesian: 'was a winning continuation'} Bxf3 30. Rh1 Bxh1 31. Rxh1 Kf8 32. Bg5 $18) 29... Rxd5 30. Rh1 $2 {Movsesian: 'Gives up the whole advantage. I just underestimated black's only reply, thinking that the position is winning anyway.'} (30. Qh2 Qb6 31. Nb3 Qf6 32. Nxc5 $16 {Movsesian: 'was still keeping a big advantage for white.'}) {Movsesian: 'Ribli: '} 30... e4 $1 {Movsesian: ''!' Ribli. ' Movsesian: 'Ribli: 'Mit diesem starken Zug kann Schwarz nach h2 die Damen tauschen.''} ({Movsesian: 'Not'} 30... Qb6 {Movsesian: '?' '?'} 31. Nb3 Qf6 32. Qe4 $1 $18 {Movsesian: '!' '!' Movsesian: 'and white is winning'}) 31. fxe4 (31. f4 {Movsesian Ribli} e3 32. Qh2 Kf8 $13) (31. Nb3 {Movsesian Ribli} Qe5 32. Bc1 exf3 33. Qxf3 Rxd1 34. Qxd1 Ba3 35. c3 $14) 31... Ba3 $3 {Movsesian: ''!?' Ribli. '} (31... Bd4 $1 {Movsesian Ribli} 32. Qd3 Nxb2 33. Qh3 Nxd1 34. exd5 Nc3+ 35. Bxc3 Bxc3 $36) 32. Qh2 (32. bxa3 Qe5 33. Nc4 Rb5+ 34. Bb4 Nc3+ 35. Ka1 Qg7 $1 $40 {Movsesian: '!' '!' Movsesian: 'and black has very unpleasant threats'}) 32... Qxh2 33. Rxh2 Rb5 34. b3 Rd8 35. c4 Rxa5 36. bxa4 Bb4 $11 37. Kc2 Bxd2 38. Rdxd2 Rxd2+ 39. Rxd2 Rxa4 40. Kd3 Kf8 41. Rb2 b5 42. cxb5 axb5 43. Rxb5 1/2-1/2

