1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Qb6 5. Nb3 Nf6 6. Nc3 e6 7. Be3 Qc7 8. Bd3 a6 9. f4 h5 10. h3 b5 11. O-O Bb7 {#By an oddity of move order, they have reached the same position as Sax-Banikas (2000), won by Sax, except that in that game it was black to move, so White has gained a tempo.} 12. Nc5 $2 (12. Qe2 {was more logical.}) 12... Qb6 13. Nxb7 Qxe3+ 14. Kh1 $2 (14. Rf2 Ra7 15. e5) 14... Ng4 15. Qe1 Rb8 16. Nd5 Qxe1 17. Raxe1 Rxb7 18. hxg4 hxg4+ 19. Kg1 exd5 20. exd5+ Kd8 {#} 21. dxc6 Bc5+ 22. Rf2 {#} g3 $1 ({After} 22... g3 23. cxb7 {Black finishes with} gxf2+ 24. Kf1 Rh1+ 25. Ke2 fxe1=Q+) 0-1

