{ChessCalisthenics: 'D02: 1 d4 d5 2 Nf3 sidelines, including 2...Nf6 3 g3 and 2...Nf6 3 Bf4'} 1. d4 {ChessCalisthenics} Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 d5 5. O-O O-O 6. Nbd2 Nbd7 7. c4 (7. c3 a5 8. a4 Re8 9. Re1 e5 10. dxe5 Nxe5 11. Nxe5 Rxe5 12. Nf3 Re8 $10 {Negulescu,A-Lputian,S/Erevan/1988} 13. Bg5 {ChessCalisthenics} c6 14. e4 dxe4 15. Qxd8 Rxd8 16. Rxe4 h6 17. Bxf6 Bxf6 18. Ne5 Bf5 19. Ree1 Bxe5 20. Rxe5 Rd2 21. b4 axb4 {Negulescu,A (2430)-Lputian,S (2555)/Yerevan 1988/EXT 2000/0-1 (41)}) 7... c5 $5 {Quite risky move perfectly suiting Judit's agressive style.} (7... dxc4 8. Nxc4 Nb6 (8... c6 9. b3 Nb6 10. Nfe5 Nxc4 11. Nxc4 Bf5 12. Bb2 Qc8 13. Re1 $14 {Ernst,L-Steblecki,S/Germany 1995}) 9. Nce5 Bf5 10. b3 Be4 11. Bb2 a5 12. Qc1 a4 13. b4 Nfd5 14. a3 c6 15. Rd1 Qc8 16. Nd3 $14 {Barcza,G-Polgar,I/HUN-ch 1966}) 8. b3 {ChessCalisthenics: 'N'} (8. cxd5 Nxd5 (8... cxd4 9. Nxd4 Nb6 $1 10. e4 Nfxd5 11. exd5 Bxd4 12. Ne4 Bg7 (12... Be5 13. Bh6 Re8 14. Qb3 Nxd5 15. Rad1 e6 16. Nc3 Bxc3 17. bxc3 $44 {Callergard,R-Ernst,T/Naestved 1988} Qe7 {ChessCalisthenics} 18. Bxd5 exd5 19. Rfe1 Be6 20. Qa4 f6 21. Re3 Qf7 22. h4 a6 {Callergard,R (2330)-Ernst, T (2450)/Naestved 1988/EXT 2000/1/2-1/2 (31)}) 13. Nc3 Nc4 14. Qb3 Nd6 $10 {Sosonko,G-Ye Jiangchuan/Luzern 1989}) 9. e4 Nb4 10. Qb3 a5 11. d5 a4 {½-½ Izeta Txabarri,F-Urban,K/Pula 1997/CBM 57 ext (11)}) 8... b6 9. Bb2 Bb7 10. Rc1 Ne4 $6 {After this move white gets better chances without any effort, but I can understand Judit who didn't want to play.} (10... dxc4 11. Nxc4 cxd4 12. Qxd4 (12. Nxd4 Bxg2 13. Kxg2 Rc8 14. f3 a6 15. e4 b5 $11) 12... Nh5 13. Qh4 Bxb2 14. Nxb2 e5 15. Qxd8 Rfxd8 16. Rfd1 $14 {[%cal Gc1c7]}) 11. Nxe4 dxe4 12. Ng5 cxd4 (12... Bh6 13. h4 cxd4 14. Qxd4 e5 15. Qd6 $14) (12... Nb8 $5 {[%csl Rd4]} 13. e3 cxd4 14. exd4 Qd7 15. Nxe4 Nc6 16. Nc3 Nxd4 (16... Bxd4 17. Nd5 $18) 17. Bxb7 Qxb7 18. Nd5 Nc6 19. Bxg7 Kxg7 20. Qf3 $14) 13. Bxd4 Bh6 14. Be3 (14. h4 $5 Qc7 15. Qc2 $14) 14... Ne5 $5 {Sacrificing an exchange for a pawn, but black hardly had another alternative.} 15. Ne6 $5 {ChessCalisthenics: '!'} (15. Bxe4 Bxe4 16. Nxe4 Bxe3 17. fxe3 Qc7 18. Qc2 $14) (15. Nxe4 $143 {ChessCalisthenics} Bxe3 16. fxe3 Qc7 $14) 15... Qxd1 (15... fxe6 {ChessCalisthenics} 16. Bxh6 {Discovered attack}) 16. Rcxd1 Bxe3 17. Nxf8 Bxf2+ 18. Rxf2 Rxf8 19. e3 Rc8 20. Rfd2 Rc7 $1 {It's very important for black to keep the rooks on the board.} 21. Rd8+ Kg7 22. Bf1 $5 f5 23. Be2 Bc8 24. Kf2 Bd7 25. h3 h5 26. Ke1 Kf6 27. Rd2 {[%cal Ge1d1,Gd1c2,Gc2c3]} (27. Kd2 Nc6 28. Ra8 Bc8 $1 29. Kc3 Bb7 30. Rf8+ Kg7 31. Re8 Kf7 $11) 27... Be6 $1 {[%cal Ge5c6]} 28. Rf8+ (28. Kd1 Nc6 29. Ra8 Bc8 30. Kc2 Bb7 $11) 28... Kg7 29. Ra8 Nc6 30. g4 $5 fxg4 31. hxg4 h4 $1 32. Bd1 $2 {After this careless move it's white who is fighting for equality.} (32. g5 $1 Ne5 (32... Bc8 $6 33. Kf2 Bb7 34. Re8 Kf7 $2 35. Rh8 $18 {[%csl Rh4]}) 33. Kf2 Nf7 34. a4 Nxg5 35. a5 bxa5 36. Ra2 Rb7 37. Bd1 Rd7 $13) (32. Kf1 {ChessCalisthenics} Ne5 $14) 32... g5 $1 {[%csl Rg4]} 33. Bc2 Ne5 34. Bxe4 Nxg4 35. Rg2 h3 36. Rg3 Rd7 $1 {[%csl Ra8]} 37. Rxh3 Nf6 38. Bg2 Bxh3 39. Bxh3 g4 $15 40. Bg2 Kg6 41. Rc8 Kf5 42. Bc6 $6 {Bishop has nothing to do on c6.} (42. c5 $1 bxc5 43. Rxc5+ e5 44. Rc4 $11) 42... Rd6 43. Ke2 e5 44. b4 $2 {It wasn't too late to come back to g2.} (44. Bg2 $8) 44... e4 $1 45. Rc7 (45. c5 bxc5 $1 (45... Rd3 $2 46. cxb6 axb6 47. Bxe4+ Kxe4 48. Rc4+ $18) 46. bxc5 Rd3 47. Bb5 Rc3 48. c6 (48. Kd2 g3 $1 $19) 48... g3 49. Kf1 Rxe3 50. c7 Rc3 $17) 45... g3 46. Bb7 Kg6 $1 $19 47. Bc8 (47. Kf1 {ChessCalisthenics} Rd2 48. a4 Rb2 $15) 47... Rd2+ 48. Kf1 Rxa2 49. b5 {ChessCalisthenics: '??'} (49. Kg1 $142 $17 {ChessCalisthenics}) 49... Nh7 {[%cal Gh7g5,Gg5f3]} 50. Bg4 {ChessCalisthenics} Ng5 $19 {0-1 (50) Nikolic,P (2653)-Polgar,J (2681) Kallithea 2002 CBM 092 [Finkel,Alexander]} 0-1

