uzern 1997/CBM 62}) 11... Bd6 12. Bxf6 gxf6 13. Qh5 f5 $13 {Morozevich,A-Zakharevich,I/Novgorod 1997/CBM 60}) (10... h6 11. Bxf6 Qxf6 12. Qd3 a6 13. Rad1 Be7 14. Nc6 $1 $14 {Ciganikova,A-Rakay,K/SVK 1999/EXT 2000}) 11. Bf3 $5 {[%cal Gf3a8] Keeping the bishop on diagonal a8-h1 looks more logical than} (11. Bd3 O-O 12. c3 Qd5 $1 13. Nf3 Rd8 14. Bc2 Qxd1 15. Raxd1 Bd7 $11 {Pandavos,P-Ellison,D/Balatonbereny op 1992}) 11... O-O 12. Re1 (12. c3 e5 13. Nc2 h6 14. Bxf6 Bxf6 15. Ne3 Rb8 $11) 12... Qb6 (12... a6 {Ü 82/260}) 13. Nb3 (13. Nf5 exf5 (13... Bc5 $5) 14. Rxe7 Ne4 15. Bxe4 fxe4 $11) 13... Rd8 14. Qe2 Bd7 15. Bd2 $5 {[%cal Gd2a5]} Bb4 {Black must play this move first:} (15... a5 $6 {Van Wely,Loek: '?' Van Wely,Loek: 'Finkel,Alexander: '?!''} 16. Qe5 $1 {[%csl Ra5] Van Wely,Loek: 'Finkel,Alexander: '!''} Bb4 (16... Bd6 $2 17. Bxa5 Bxe5 18. Bxb6 Bxb2 19. Rab1 Bc3 20. Bxd8 $18) (16... a4 17. Ba5 Rxa5 18. Qxa5 Qxa5 19. Nxa5 $18) 17. Be3 Qa6 18. Nc5 Bxc5 19. Bxc5 $14) 16. c3 Bd6 {[%csl Ge5]} 17. c4 $5 a5 18. Rac1 $5 {Starting extremly interesting complications.} (18. c5 $2 Bxc5 19. Nxc5 Qxc5 20. Bxb7 Rab8 {[%csl Rb2]} 21. Be3 Qb4 22. Bf3 Qxb2 $17) (18. Bc3 Qc7 19. h3 Bc6 $13) 18... a4 19. c5 Bxh2+ 20. Kh1 $5 ({Not perfectly clear is Van Wely,Loek: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Not perfectly clear is''} 20. Kxh2 Qc7+ 21. Kg1 (21. Qe5 Qxe5+ 22. Rxe5 axb3 23. axb3 Bc6 $15 {[%cal Gd8d2]}) 21... axb3 22. axb3 Bc6 23. Bg5 $13) 20... Qc7 21. Na5 (21. Ba5 $2 {Van Wely,Loek: 'Finkel,Alexander: '?''} Qf4 22. Bxd8 Rxd8 $1 {Van Wely,Loek: 'Finkel,Alexander: '!''} (22... Qh6 $2 {[%cal Gh6h1]} 23. Bxf6 Bf4+ 24. Bh5 axb3 25. Rcd1 Qxf6 26. g3 Bc6+ 27. Kg1 $16) 23. g3 Qh6 24. Qe3 (24. Kg2 e5 $19) 24... g5 25. Kg2 e5 $19 {[%cal Gh6h3]}) 21... Bb5 $1 {Great defensive resourse! After this move black siezes the initiative.} 22. Qxb5 Rxd2 23. Nc4 $8 (23. Qxb7 $2 Rxa5 $19) (23. Nxb7 Rxf2 24. Nd6 Rb8 $17) 23... Rxf2 24. Qxb7 Rb8 $1 {Another great move from black's side.} 25. Qxc7 (25. Qc6 $6 Qf4 $1 {[%cal