1. e4 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre Polgar,Judit Polgar,Judit Ftacnik Polgar,Judit: 'Polgar,J Ftacnik' Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre Polgar,Judit Polgar,Judit Ftacnik Polgar,Judit: 'Polgar,J Ftacnik' C83: Open Ruy Lopez: 9 c3 Be7} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. c3 Be7 10. Nbd2 (10. Bc2 {Polgar,Judit-Hubner,Munchen 1991.}) 10... Qd7 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre: '?!' Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre: 'This is a quite rare sideline. 10...0-0 and 10...Nc5 are much more common.'} (10... Nc5 {-50/369,370.}) (10... O-O {Ftacnik}) 11. Bc2 Nxd2 (11... Bf5 12. Nd4 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre} Bg6 13. f4 $146 Nxd4 14. cxd4 c6 15. Nxe4 dxe4 16. Be3 $16) 12. Qxd2 Bg4 $6 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre: 'Black tries to switch into an aggressive mood. His intention is to win e5 or to create double pawns. However, it costs him extra time and the absence of the e6-bishop results an insecure king's position.'} (12... O-O 13. Qd3 g6 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre} 14. Bh6 Rfd8 15. Rad1 $36 {would have been also unpleasant, as it was seen in Kolev - Villuela Arrollo, St Cugat 1996.}) 13. Qf4 Bxf3 (13... O-O 14. Ng5 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre: '?!' Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre: 'is premature due to'} (14. Re1 $1 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre The precise continuation, overprotecting e5 first.} Rad8 15. h3 Bh5 16. Bf5 Qe8 17. g4 Bg6 18. Nd4 $16) 14... h6 $2 (14... Bxg5 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre} 15. Qxg5 f6 16. exf6 Rxf6 17. Qh4 Bf5 $13) 15. Nh7 Rfe8 16. h3 $1 Bh5 (16... Be6 17. Nf6+ gxf6 18. exf6 Bf8 19. Qg3+ Kh8 20. Qd3 $18) (16... Be2 17. Nf6+ $1 (17. Re1 Bh5 18. Nf6+ $2 Bxf6 $19) 17... gxf6 (17... Bxf6 18. exf6 Bxf1 19. Qg3 g6 20. Bxh6 $1 {Plan Bg7,Qh4.}) 18. Bf5 Qd8 19. Qxh6 $18) 17. Nf6+ gxf6 18. Bf5 Qd8 19. Qxh6 Bg6 20. Bxg6 fxg6 21. Qxg6+ Kh8 22. Qh5+ Kg8 23. Bh6 Nxe5 (23... Bf8 24. Qg6+ Kh8 25. exf6 Ne5 26. Bg7+ Kg8 27. f7+ $1 Nxf7 28. Bf6+ $18) 24. f4 $16) 14. Bf5 Qd8 15. Qxf3 {Polgar,Judit Hera,Imre: 'White is ready to give his central pawn, since it would instantly open up the position.'} 