1. e4 {Marin} g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 c6 4. f4 d5 5. e5 Nh6 6. Nf3 f6 7. h3 Nf5 8. Bd3 Ng3 9. Rg1 f5 10. Be3 Qb6 {Istrãtescu deviates from the game of his then friend Nevednichy, possibly as a result of a joint analysis.} 11. Qc1 Na6 12. Na4 Qd8 13. Bxa6 Qa5+ 14. Qd2 Qxa6 (14... Qxa4 15. Bd3 Ne4 16. Bxe4 (16. Qe2 Ng3 17. Qf2 Ne4) 16... fxe4 17. Nh4 Rf8 18. g4 e6 19. a3 Bd7 20. O-O-O O-O-O 21. Rdf1 {Black's position may seem solid, but he has hidden problems of coordination. For instance, the generally desirable} Rf7 $6 {allows} 22. f5 $1 exf5 23. gxf5 gxf5 24. Nxf5 Bxf5 25. e6 Bxe6 26. Rxf7 Bxf7 27. Rxg7 Bg6 28. Qf2 $40) 15. Nc5 Qb6 (15... Qb5 16. a4 (16. O-O-O Ne2+) 16... Qb6 (16... Qxb2 $2 17. Kf2 Ne4+ 18. Nxe4 dxe4 19. Rgb1 $16) 17. O-O-O Ne4 18. Qe1 Qc7 19. Ng5 $14 {There is no obvious way of taking advantage of the weakness induced by a2-a4.}) 16. O-O-O Qb5 17. Kb1 (17. a4 Qe2) 17... b6 18. Nd3 Ne4 19. Qe1 Be6 $6 (19... c5 $2 20. dxc5 bxc5 21. Nxc5 Nxc5 22. Rxd5 $18) ({The only way of getting chances for counterplay in this game I could find is the somewhat mysterious} 19... Rb8 $5 20. g4 (20. b3 a5 21. a4 $6 Qa6 22. g4 b5 $36) 20... c5 21. Nh4 {This will cause losses of time, but it is not easy to force Black to obstruct the c8-f5 diagonal.} (21. gxf5 Bxf5 22. Nh4 O-O {allows Black to maintain his stability on the light squares.}) 21... e6 22. Nf2 Rb7 23. Nf3 Bf8 24. gxf5 exf5 25. h4 c4 26. c3 Qa4 27. h5 b5 28. hxg6 b4 $1 $132) 20. Ng5 $1 $36 Kd7 (20... Nxg5 21. fxg5 Bd7 22. Nf4 e6 23. g4 fxg4 24. h4 O-O-O 25. Qg3 c5 26. Qxg4 $36) 21. g4 Raf8 22. Nxe4 (22. Nxe6 Kxe6 23. Nf2 Nxf2 24. Qxf2 Kd7 25. Qh4 e6 26. Rd3 $14) 22... fxe4 (22... dxe4 23. Nc1 Kc7 24. Ne2 $14) 23. Nc1 (23. f5 Bxf5 24. a4 Qc4 25. b3 exd3 $3 $44) (23. a4 $5 Qxa4 (23... Qc4 24. b3 Qa6 25. Nb4 Qb7 26. f5 $18) 24. f5 exd3 (24... Bxf5 25. gxf5 exd3 26. Rxd3 $1 Rxf5 27. Ra3 Qb5 28. Rxa7+ Ke6 29. Qh4 $40) 25. fxe6+ Kxe6 26. Rxd3 $40) 23... Rf7 24. Ne2 h5 $6 25. f5 $1 gxf5 26. gxh5 $16 f4 27. Nxf4 Bf5 28. b3 e6 29. a4 Qa6 30. Qd2 Qc8 31. Rg3 Bh6 32. Nxd5 cxd5 33. Bxh6 e3 34. Bxe3 Rxh5 35. Qe2 Qc3 36. Bf4 Bxc2+ 37. Qxc2 Qxc2+ 38. Kxc2 Rxf4 39. Rg7+ Ke8 40. Rd3 Rf7 41. Rg8+ Rf8 42. Rxf8+ Kxf8 43. Rc3 Rh4 44. Rc8+ Kf7 45. Rc7+ Kg6 46. Rxa7 Rxd4 47. Rb7 Rb4 48. Kc3 Rh4 49. Rxb6 Kf5 50. a5 Rxh3+ 51. Kd4 Rh1 52. Rb8 Rd1+ 53. Kc5 Kxe5 54. a6 Ra1 55. Kb6 Kd4 56. a7 Kc3 57. a8=Q Rxa8 58. Rxa8 d4 59. Kc5 d3 60. b4 d2 61. Ra1 1-0

