1. e4 {Lukacs Lukacs} e5 2. d4 exd4 3. Qxd4 {The Centre Counter is a rare guest in the modern tounament practice.} Nc6 4. Qe3 Nf6 5. Bd2 {White wants to avoid the main lines after} (5. Nc3 Bb4) 5... Be7 6. Nc3 d5 (6... O-O 7. Bc4 $1 {White doesn't want to allow the breakthrough in the  after d7-d5.} (7. O-O-O {is strongly met by} d5 $1 (7... Re8 $6 {(Mason-Chigorin,Paris 1900)} 8. Bc4 $1 $36 {Keres}) 8. exd5 Nxd5 9. Qg3 {Lukacs: '- 6...0-0'} Bh4 $1 10. Qf3 Be6 (10... Nxc3 $5 11. Bxc3 Qg5+ 12. Bd2 Qc5 13. Be3 Qa5 $15 {is an untested idea of Aljechin.}) 11. Be3 Nxc3 $1 12. Rxd8 Nxa2+ 13. Kb1 Raxd8 14. Be2 Nab4 15. Nh3 Rfe8 16. Nf4 (16. Rd1 Bd5 17. Qh5 Bf6) 16... Bf5 17. Rc1 g6 $44 {Mieses-Aljechin, Schveningen 1913}) 7... d6 8. O-O-O Ne5 (8... Be6 9. Bxe6 fxe6 10. f4 $14 (10. Qh3 {is less clear} Qc8 11. Nge2 b5 $1 12. Ng3 Ne5 13. Be1 Kh8 14. Nce2 c5 15. Nf4 Nfg4 $13 {Borge-L.B.Hansen, 1996})) 9. Bb3 Be6 10. f4 Nc4 11. Bxc4 Bxc4 12. Nf3 c6 13. Nd4 Re8 14. Qg3 Bf8 15. Rhe1 $14 {Shabalov-Shliperman, New York 1995}) 7. exd5 Nxd5 8. Qg3 (8. Nxd5 $6 {centralizes the enemy .} Qxd5 9. Ne2 Bg4 $5 (9... O-O 10. Nc3 Qc5 11. O-O-O Bf5 $11 {Tanasdy-Mohd, Singapure 1997}) 10. Nf4 Qd7 11. f3 O-O-O $1 12. O-O-O $11 {Sultan Khan-Marshall, Liege 1930} (12. fxg4 $2 {leaves the black  in the limbo.} Bh4+ 13. Kd1 Rhe8 14. Qd3 Qxg4+ 15. Be2 Rxe2 $1 16. Qxe2 Qxf4 17. Kc1 Nd4 $17)) 8... Nxc3 $6 ({There was nothing wrong with} 8... O-O 9. Bh6 (9. O-O-O {- 6...0-0}) 9... Bf6 10. O-O-O Be6 $1 (10... Bxc3 11. bxc3 Qf6 12. Bxg7 Qxg7 13. Qxg7+ Kxg7 14. Rxd5 $14) (10... Nd4 11. Bxg7 Bxg7 12. Rxd4 $16) 11. Ne4 Kh8 $11 {Anand}) (8... Ncb4 $5 9. Nxd5 (9. O-O-O Nxc3 10. bxc3 Nxa2+ 11. Kb1 Be6 12. c4 Nb4 13. Be2 (13. Qxg7 $2 Bf6) 13... c5 $1 14. Bxb4 Qb6 15. Qxg7 Qxb4+ 16. Kc1 Rf8 $13) (9. Bb5+ c6 10. Ba4 Bf5) 9... Qxd5 10. Bxb4 (10. Qxc7 $6 Bf5 $44) (10. Qxg7 $2 Nxc2+ 11. Kd1 Nxa1 $17) 10... Qe4+ 11. Ne2 Qxb4+ 12. Qc3 Qxc3+ 13. Nxc3 O-O $11 {Blanco Fernandez-Otero Villa Clara 1995}) 9. Bxc3 Bf6 10. Bb5 $5 $146 (10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. O-O-O O-O 12. Nf3 Be6 (12... Bf5 $6 {is met by} 13. Qf4 $1 Rae8 (13... Qe6 14. Bc4 Qe4 15. Qxe4 Bxe4 16. Rd7 Rac8 17. Re1 Bxf3 18. gxf3 Nb8 $14) 14. Bd3 Bxd3 15. Qxf6 gxf6 16. Rxd3 Re2 17. Rd2 $14 {Mi.Adams-Anand, Linares (m/6) 1994 CBM43}) 13. a3 Rac8 $11) 10... Qd5 $5 (10... O-O 11. Ne2 (11. Bxc6 bxc6 12. Bxf6 (12. Ne2 Ba6) 12... Qxf6 13. O-O-O Rb8 {gives attacking chances for Black on the b .}) 11... Bxc3+ 12. Qxc3 Re8 13. O-O Qd5 14. Bxc6 Qxc6 15. Qxc6 bxc6 16. Nd4 c5 17. Rfe1 $14 {with a slightly better  for White because of Black's corrupted  structure.}) 11. Bxf6 gxf6 12. Bxc6+ (12. Qg7 $5 Rf8 13. Bxc6+ Qxc6 14. O-O-O $14 {see later!}) 12... Qxc6 13. O-O-O (13. Qg7 $5 Rf8 14. O-O-O $14 Bf5 15. Rd2 Qa6 16. Ne2 $1 Qxa2 17. Nc3 Qa1+ 18. Nb1 $44 {and Black's  is in the middle.}) 13... Bd7 (13... Bf5 14. Rd2 $14) 14. Qa3 $5 (14. Ne2 O-O-O 15. Nd4 Qa4 $132) (14. Qe3+ Qe6 15. Qd4 $14) 14... Qb6 (14... Qxg2 {looks overoptimistic:} 15. Qe3+ Be6 (15... Kf8 $4 16. Rxd7 $1) 16. Nf3 $44) 15. Re1+ (15. Nf3 O-O-O 16. Rd2) 15... Be6 16. Qa4+ $6 ({She had to go for the slightly better  after} 16. Qe3 O-O-O 17. Qxb6 axb6 18. Ne2 Rhg8 19. Rhg1 $14) 16... c6 17. Rd1 Rg8 $1 ({Hunting for pawns by} 17... Qxf2 {is again unhealthy} 18. Nf3 Qxg2 19. Qf4 $44) 18. Nf3 Rxg2 19. Qf4 Qc5 $1 20. Qe4 (20. Qxf6 Rxf2) 20... Qf5 (20... Rxf2 $2 {gives away the important g .} 21. Rhg1 $1 Ke7 22. Nd4 Rd8 (22... Rxh2 23. Qf4) 23. Nxe6 Rxd1+ 24. Rxd1 fxe6 25. Qxh7+ $18) 21. Qe2 (21. Qe3 Rg4 $1) 21... Qf4+ 22. Kb1 Qc4 $15 23. Qxc4 Bxc4 24. Rhg1 Rxg1 25. Rxg1 Kf8 {Now already White has to play carefully the slightly worse .} 26. Rg4 Bd5 (26... Be6 27. Rf4 (27. Rh4 $5 Ke7 $1 28. Rxh7 Rg8) 27... Rd8 $17) 27. Rf4 Re8 28. Kc1 Re2 29. c4 (29. Nd4 Re5) 29... Re4 (29... Bxf3 30. Rxf3 Ke7 $17) 30. Rxe4 Bxe4 31. Nd2 (31. Nd4 c5) 31... Bf5 32. b4 Ke7 33. Kb2 Ke6 34. Kc3 Ke5 35. a4 h5 36. c5 Be6 37. Kd3 a5 $5 (37... f5 38. Nf3+ Kd5) 38. bxa5 Kd5 39. Kc3 Bf5 40. Kb4 Bd3 41. Kc3 Be2 42. Nb3 Bd1 43. Nd4 Kxc5 (43... Bg4 $1 44. f3 (44. Nb3 Bd1) 44... Be6 45. Nb3 h4) 44. Nf5 Bg4 45. Ne3 Bf3 (45... Be6) 46. h4 Be4 47. Nf1 $1 Bf3 48. Ng3 f5 (48... Kd5 49. Kd3 c5 50. Ke3 $1 Bd1 51. Ne4) 49. Nxf5 Bg4 50. Nh6 $11 Be6 51. Ng8 f5 52. Nf6 Bf7 53. Nd7+ Kd6 54. Nb6 f4 55. Kd4 Bd5 56. Nc8+ Kd7 57. Nb6+ Kd6 58. Nc8+ Kd7 59. Nb6+ Kd6 1/2-1/2

