1. e4 {Psakhis,L Psakhis} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Ng5 Ngf6 6. Bd3 e6 7. N1f3 Bd6 8. Qe2 h6 9. Ne4 Nxe4 10. Qxe4 Qc7 11. Qg4 Kf8 12. Be3 b6 (12... c5 13. dxc5 Bxc5 (13... Nxc5 14. O-O-O e5 15. Bf5 Ne6 16. Nh4 Qe7 17. Bxe6 Bxe6 18. Nf5 Bxf5 19. Qxf5 b6 20. Rd5 $16 {1-0 Marciano,D-Arlandi,E/Makarska 1996 (33)}) 14. O-O-O Nf6 15. Qh4 Bxe3+ 16. fxe3 Bd7 17. Rhf1 Rc8 18. Kb1 Bc6 19. e4 Kg8 20. c3 Nd7 21. Bc2 $36 {1-0 Polgar,J-Karpov,A/Budapest m (2) 1998 (49)}) (12... Nf6 $1 13. Qh4 b6 14. O-O-O Bb7 15. Rhe1 c5 16. dxc5 bxc5 17. Nd2 Nd5 18. Nc4 Nxe3 19. Nxe3 Rb8 $13 {½-½ Polgar,J-Karpov,A/Budapest m 1998 (48)}) 13. Nd2 $5 {[%cal Gd2c4,Gc4d6,Ge1c1] N} (13. O-O-O Bb7 14. Rhe1 Rc8 15. Kb1 Nf6 16. Qh3 c5 17. dxc5 bxc5 18. c4 Bxf3 19. Qxf3 Ke7 $15 {½-½ Fressinet,L-Speelman,J/Bardeaux 1998 (61)}) 13... Nf6 $5 (13... c5 14. Nc4 Nf6 15. Qe2 $36 {[%csl Rf8]}) 14. Qe2 (14. Qh4 $5 {was maybe more agressive, than move in the game, but , please, don,t forget, that score was already 2,5-0,5 to Polgar.}) 14... Nd5 (14... e5 15. dxe5 Bxe5 16. Nc4 $14) 15. Nc4 Ba6 (15... Nxe3 16. fxe3 $14 {[%cal Gh1f1,Gf1f7]}) (15... Nf4 $5 16. Bxf4 Bxf4 17. g3 Bg5) 16. Nxd6 (16. O-O-O $5 Nf4 17. Bxf4 Bxf4+ 18. Kb1 Rd8 19. g3 Bg5 20. Ne5 $13) 16... Bxd3 17. Qxd3 Qxd6 18. O-O Rd8 (18... b5 19. a4 b4 (19... a6 $2 20. axb5 cxb5 21. Qxb5 $1) 20. c4 $1 $36) 19. Rad1 (19. c4 $5 Nxe3 20. fxe3 $14) 19... b5 $5 20. a4 a6 (20... b4 21. c4) 21. c4 (21. b3 $5 {[%cal Gc2c4]}) 21... bxc4 22. Qxc4 Ra8 {[%cal Gf8e7,Gh8b8]} (22... a5 23. Bd2 Ra8 24. Rc1 $36 {[%csl Ra5,Rc6]}) 23. b4 $5 {Very interesting effort to get initiative.White has less than nothing after} (23. Rc1 Ke7 $1 24. Qxc6 Qxc6 25. Rxc6 Rhb8 {with more than enough compensation for a pawn.}) 23... Qxb4 $1 (23... Nxb4 $2 24. d5 $1 cxd5 25. Bc5 $1 $18) 24. Qxc6 Ke7 $1 {Looks dangerous, but Karpov correctly calculated variations.} 25. Bd2 (25. Rb1 Rhc8 $1 26. Qxd5 $140 $2 Qxb1 27. Bg5+ $2 f6 $19) 25... Qd6 26. Qb7+ Kf6 (26... Qd7 $5 27. Bb4+ Nxb4 28. Qxb4+ Qd6 $11) 27. Qb3 Rhc8 (27... Rhb8 28. Qh3 Rb2 29. f4 $5 $40 {[%cal Rf4f5]}) 28. Rc1 (28. Qh3 Rc4) 28... Kg6 (28... g5 $5) 29. Qd3+ f5 (29... Kf6) 30. Rfe1 {[%csl Re6]} Rxc1 31. Rxc1 (31. Bxc1 Kh7 32. Ba3 Qc6 {[%cal Gd5f4]}) 31... Rb8 32. h3 (32. g3 $5) 32... Kf7 33. Rc5 Rb7 34. g3 Rb2 35. a5 $14 {[%csl Ra6]} Rb7 36. Qf3 {[%cal Gg3g4]} (36. Qc2 Qd7 37. Rc6 Rb2 $1) 36... Rc7 37. Qd3 Rxc5 (37... Rb7 38. Qc4) 38. dxc5 Qc6 39. Qc4 Ke7 40. Bc3 $5 {Karpov had usual for him in this match time troubles, but defended well and made draw without big problem.} Kf7 41. Be5 g5 42. Bd6 Nf6 43. Qe2 h5 (43... g4 44. hxg4 fxg4 (44... Nxg4 45. f3 Nf6 46. Kf2) 45. Qe3 $14) 44. Be5 g4 45. Bxf6 (45. hxg4 Nxg4 $5) 45... gxh3 $1 (45... Kxf6 46. hxg4 hxg4 47. Qb2+ Ke7 48. Qg7+ Kd8 49. Qa7 $36) 46. Qxh5+ Kxf6 47. Qh6+ Ke5 48. Qxh3 Qxc5 $11 49. Qh8+ Kd5 50. Qa8+ Qc6 51. Qxc6+ Kxc6 52. f3 Kd5 53. Kf2 e5 54. Ke3 Ke6 55. Kd3 Kd5 56. Ke3 e4 57. fxe4+ fxe4 1/2-1/2

