1. e4 {Finkel,Alexander: 'Finkel,A  '} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Be7 6. Bxf6 Bxf6 7. Nf3 O-O 8. Bc4 Nc6 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: 'A move so unusual that Judit is prompted to move her bishop again.'} 9. Bb5 $146 {Finkel,Alexander: 'Harmless continuation.'} (9. c3 {Ü 49/(338)} e5 10. d5 Na5 (10... Nb8 $5 11. O-O Bg4 12. h3 Bxf3 13. Qxf3 Be7 14. Bb5 a6 15. Ba4 Nd7 $11 {Ivanchuk,V-Ehlvest,J/Reggio Emilia8990}) 11. Bd3 b6 12. Qc2 g6 (12... Kh8 13. O-O Nb7 14. Rfe1 Qxd5 $6 15. Nxf6 gxf6 16. Be4 $36 {Garcia Martinez,S-Braga,F/Havana-B 1983}) 13. Nxf6+ Qxf6 14. O-O Bg4 15. Nd2 Nb7 16. Rae1 Nd6 17. Qa4 Bf5 $11 {Levenfish,G-Bondarevsky,I/Leningrad/Moscow 1939}) (9. Nxf6+ Qxf6 10. O-O e5 11. Nxe5 Nxe5 12. dxe5 Qxe5 13. c3 {½-½ Balashov,Y-Dreev,A/RUS-ch 1995}) 9... Bd7 (9... Nxd4 $2 10. Nxf6+) ({and} 9... Bxd4 $2 10. Bxc6 {both cost a piece.}) 10. Qd2 (10. Nc5 $2 Be8 $1) 10... Be7 11. O-O (11. O-O-O Nb4 $1 $15) (11. Be2 $5 Nb4 12. Ne5 Bc6 (12... Be8 13. O-O Nd5 14. Rfe1 Nf6 15. Bf3 $14) 13. Nxc6 Nxc6 14. c3 e5 15. d5 Nb8 $13) 11... Ne5 $1 {Byron Jacobs: '!?'} 12. Nxe5 ({Finkel,Alexander: 'May be better was'} 12. Be2 Nxf3+ 13. Bxf3 Bc6 $11 14. Qe3 Bxe4 15. Bxe4 c6 $11 {with balance.}) 12... Bxb5 13. c4 Ba6 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: 'Far more ambitious than the retreat to e8.'} (13... Be8 $5 14. Rad1 f6 (14... Bd6 $5) 15. Nf3 b5 16. b3 Rb8 17. Qe2 bxc4 18. bxc4 Bh5 19. Ng3 Bf7 $13) 14. Rac1 (14. Qc3 $142 b6 $11) 14... c5 $1 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: 'To win, it may be necessary to take risks. Shirov stretches things to the limit in trying to make the most of the pair of bishops.' Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' Finkel,Alexander: 'Shirov plays this game at his best:now he sacrifices a pawn and in the endgame doesn't take it back till the right moment.' Finkel,A: '!'} 15. dxc5 Qxd2 16. Nxd2 Rfd8 $1 {Byron Jacobs: 'Taking back immediately permits the fork at d7, so he comes up with this scheme.'} (16... Bxc5 $2 {Finkel,Alexander: '?!' '?!' Finkel,A: '?!'} 17. Nd7 Rfd8 18. Nxc5 Rxd2 19. b4 $16 Rc8 20. a3 $14) 17. Nb3 {Byron Jacobs: 'From b3 the knight is temporarily holding on to c5, but that pawn cannot now get additional support, e.g. with b2-b4, and also the one behind it may become opened up as another object of attack. (Perhaps this is how a mind wired like Shirov's works!?)'} (17. Ne4 {Byron Jacobs: 'might have been met with'} Rd4 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: '.'} 18. Rfe1 f6 19. Nf3 Rxc4 $15) 17... Rac8 $1 $15 18. f4 b6 $6 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: 'A move of great ambition.' Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' Finkel,A: '!'} ({Finkel,Alexander: 'Of course not'} 18... f6 {Byron Jacobs: 'and 19...Bxc5 restored material equality without risk.'} 19. Ng4 $5 (19. Nf3 b6 $15 (19... Bxc5+ 20. Nxc5 Rxc5 21. b3 b6 22. Rfd1 $11 {with equality.})) 19... Rxc5 $3 (19... Bxc5+ 20. Nxc5 Rxc5 21. Ne3 $11) (19... b6 20. cxb6 axb6 21. Ne3 $13) 20. Nxc5 Bxc5+ $15) 19. Rfd1 $1 ({If} 19. cxb6 axb6 {then ...f7-f6 will cause the c4-pawn to fall.} 20. Rfd1 f6 $1 (20... Rxd1+ $6 21. Rxd1 f6 22. Rd7 Bf8 23. Ra7 $1 Bxc4 24. Nxc4 Rxc4 25. Ra6 Rc2 26. Rxb6 Rxb2 27. Rxe6 $11) 21. Nd7 Bxc4 22. Rd4 (22. Nxb6 $2 Rxd1+ 23. Rxd1 Bxb3 24. axb3 Bc5+ $19) 22... Bxb3 23. Rxc8 Rxc8 24. axb3 Rc2 $17) 19... Rxd1+ (19... bxc5 20. Na5 $1 Rxd1+ 21. Rxd1 Rd8 22. Rxd8+ Bxd8 23. Nac6 Bb6 24. Nb8 Bc8 25. Nbd7 f6 26. Nxb6 axb6 27. Nd3 Bb7 $11) 20. Rxd1 Rc7 $2 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: 'Keeping the rook out of the seventh rank.' Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' Finkel,Alexander: 'Covering square d7.' Finkel,A: '!'} (20... f6 21. Rd7 fxe5 22. Rxa7 Bxc4 23. Rxe7 Bxb3 24. axb3 Rxc5 25. Rxe6 exf4 26. Rxb6 Rc2 $11) 21. Rd6 $1 {Byron Jacobs: '!?' Byron Jacobs: 'Judit tries to throw a spanner in the works, but Shirov refuses to be flustered and sticks to his plan of regaining the pawn in a situation where the activity of his minor pieces will be superior to that of White's.'} ({Finkel,Alexander: 'Deserved attention'} 21. cxb6 {Finkel,Alexander: '!?' '!?' Finkel,A: '!?'} axb6 22. Nd4 (22. Rd7 Rxd7 23. Nxd7 Bxc4 24. Kf2 Bxb3 25. axb3 h5 26. Ke3 b5 $15 {[%cal Gg8h7,Gh7f5]}) 22... Bxc4 $11) 21... Kf8 $1 (21... Bxd6 {Finkel,Alexander: '?!' '?!' Finkel,A: '?!'} 22. cxd6 Rc8 23. d7 (23. c5 $2 {Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' Finkel,A: '!'} f6 (23... bxc5 24. d7 Rd8 25. Nxc5 Bb5 26. a4 Bxa4 27. Nxa4 f6 28. Nd3 Rxd7 29. Nac5 $14) 24. Nc6 {Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' Finkel,A: '!'} Rxc6 25. d7 Rc8 26. dxc8=Q+ Bxc8 $11) 23... Rd8 24. Nd4 Bb7 25. b4 Kf8 26. b5 $18) 22. cxb6 (22. Nd4 Bxc4 $1) 22... Bxd6 23. bxc7 Bxc7 $6 {[NB 9/d] Byron Jacobs: 'White is still that pawn up, but the bishops are starting to weave their combined magical effect.' Finkel,Alexander: '' '' Finkel,A: ''} (23... f6 24. Nd7+ Ke8 (24... Ke7 $2 25. Nb8 $16) 25. Ndc5 Bc8 26. Nd3 Bxc7 $14) 24. c5 $6 {Finkel,Alexander: '!?' '!?' Finkel,A: '!?'} (24. Nc5 $1 Bxe5 25. Nd7+ Ke8 $1 (25... Ke7 26. Nxe5 f6 27. Nc6+ Kd6 28. Na5 Kc5 29. b3 $16) 26. Nxe5 f6 27. Nc6 Bxc4 28. b3 Bd3 $1 (28... Bb5 $2 29. Nxa7 Bd7 30. a4 Kd8 31. Kf2 Kc7 32. Ke3 Kb6 33. Nb5 Bxb5 34. axb5 Kxb5 35. Kd3 $1 Kb4 36. Kc2 $18 h6 (36... h5 37. h4 $1 e5 (37... Kc5 38. Kc3 Kb5 39. b4 e5 40. fxe5 fxe5 41. g3 e4 42. Kd4 Kxb4 43. Kxe4 Kc3 44. Kf5 Kd4 45. Kg6) (37... Kb5 38. Kc3 Kc5 39. b4+ Kb5 40. Kb3 e5 41. fxe5 fxe5 42. Kc3 e4 43. Kd4 Kxb4 44. Kxe4 Kc4 45. Kf5 Kd4 46. Kg6) 38. fxe5 fxe5 39. Kb2 e4 40. Kc2 e3 41. Kd3 Kxb3 42. Kxe3 Kc2 43. Kf4 Kd3 44. Kg5 Ke4 45. Kxh5 Kf5 (45... Kf4 46. g4) 46. g3) 37. h3 $1 (37. h4 h5 38. Kb2 e5 39. fxe5 fxe5 40. Kc2 e4 41. g3 e3 42. Kd3 Kxb3 43. Kxe3 Kc3 44. Kf4 Kd3 45. Kg5 Ke4 46. Kxh5 Kf5 47. g4+ Kf6 48. g5+ Kf5 $11) 37... g5 (37... h5 38. h4) (37... Kc5 38. Kc3 Kd5 39. b4 e5 40. fxe5 Kxe5 41. Kc4) 38. fxg5 hxg5 39. g3 f5 40. Kd3 e5 41. h4 f4 42. h5 $1 fxg3 43. Ke2 e4 44. h6 g2 45. Kf2 e3+ 46. Kxg2 Kc3 47. h7 e2 48. h8=Q+) 29. Nxa7 Kd7 30. Kf2 Kc7 31. a4 Kb6 $1 (31... Kb7 $2 32. Nb5) 32. Ke3 $1 (32. Nb5 Bxb5 33. axb5 Kxb5 34. Ke3 Kb4 35. Kd4 h6 36. h3 h5 37. h4 Kxb3 38. Kc5 Kc3 39. Kd6 Kd4 40. Kxe6 Ke4 $11) (32. Nc8+ Kc7) 32... Bf1 33. Nb5 Bxg2 $1 (33... Bxb5 $2 34. axb5 Kxb5 35. Kd3 Kb4 36. Kc2 $18) 34. b4 h6 $1 (34... Bc6 $2 35. Nc3 $16) 35. Nd4 Bh3 36. Kf3 g5 37. Kg3 Bf5 38. Nxf5 exf5 $11) ({Much better was} 24. Nd4 $1 g5 25. g3 Bxe5 26. fxe5 Bxc4 27. b3 Bd5 $15 {and white has good chanses to hold the endgame.}) 24... g5 $1 $44 {Byron Jacobs: '!'} 25. Nc6 $2 (25. g3 gxf4 26. gxf4 f6 27. Nd4 $1 (27. Nc6 Bxf4 28. Nxa7 Bc4) 27... Ke7 28. Ndc6+ Ke8 (28... Kf8 29. Nd7+ Kf7 30. Nxa7) 29. Ng4 Kf7 $5 (29... Kd7 30. Nb4 Bb5 31. Nxf6+ Ke7 $14) 30. Nxa7 Bxf4 $44) 25... gxf4 26. a4 $6 (26. Nxa7 {Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' Finkel,A: '!'} Be5 $15 27. Kf2 Bxb2 28. c6 Ke7 29. Kf3 Kd6 $15) 26... Bc4 $1 27. Nd2 $6 Bd5 {Byron Jacobs: 'Reaching its optimum square.'} 28. Nxa7 Ba5 $19 {Byron Jacobs: '!' Finkel,Alexander: '' '' Finkel,Alexander: 'This ending is a classic example of "what the pair of bishops is capable to do".' Finkel,A: ''} 29. Nb1 Bb4 30. Nb5 Bxc5+ 31. Kf1 f3 $2 (31... Ke7 32. N1c3 Bc4+ 33. Ke1 Kd7 $19) 32. gxf3 Bxf3 $17 33. Nd2 Bd5 {Byron Jacobs: 'Now the bishops totally outgun the knights.'} 34. Ke2 Ke7 {Finkel,Alexander: '' '' Finkel,A: ''} 35. Kd3 f5 36. Nc3 Bb7 37. Kc4 Be3 $1 38. Kd3 Bg1 $1 39. b4 $2 (39. h3 $17) 39... Bxh2 40. b5 h5 $1 $19 41. a5 h4 42. Ke2 (42. a6 Bg2 43. b6 (43. Nc4 h3 44. b6 Bb8 $19) 43... h3) 42... h3 43. a6 Bg2 44. Kf2 Bd6 (44... Be5 $2 45. Nf3 $1) 45. Nf3 (45. Na4 Ba8 46. Nf3 h2 47. Nxh2 Bxh2 48. b6 Bc6 $19) 45... Bc5+ 46. Kg3 (46. Ke2 Bg1) 46... f4+ $1 47. Kg4 (47. Kxf4 Bd6+ 48. Ke3 h2 49. Nxh2 Bxh2 50. Kf2 Bh1 51. b6 Kd6) 47... Bg1 {Byron Jacobs: '!' Byron Jacobs: 'The long range bishops can cover the white pawns whilst simultaneously assisting with the advance of their own passed pawns. Knights are not so nimble.'} 48. b6 Bxf3+ 49. Kxf3 h2 50. Kg2 {Byron Jacobs: 'The finale might have been'} f3+ 51. Kh1 f2 52. a7 f1=Q 53. a8=Q Be3+ 54. Kxh2 Bf4# {. Shirov's imaginative efforts to extract the maximum potential from the position were rewarded with the full point.} 0-1

