1. e4 {Polgar,J Polgar,J Schussler Polgar,J Schussler Hazai Polgar,J Schussler} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 (7... O-O {Hazai} 8. c3 {1-0 (44) Polgar,J-Van der Sterren,P Wijk aan Zee 1990 MAS C92 LH [Hazai]}) 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Nd7 10. d4 Bf6 {10...b6} 11. a4 Rb8 (11... Bb7 12. axb5 axb5 13. Rxa8 Qxa8 (13... Bxa8 14. d5 Ne7 15. Na3 Nc5 16. Bc2 c6 17. b4 Na6 18. dxc6 Bxc6 19. Qd3 Nc7 20. Rd1 $16 {Huebner,R-Short,N/Skeleftea WCup/1989/ -> CBM 14}) 14. d5 Ne7 15. Na3 Ba6 16. Nh2 $14 {Anand,V-Speelman,J/Thessaloniki ol/1988/ -> TD 1988/6}) 12. axb5 axb5 13. d5 Ne7 14. Nbd2 {N; the theory recommends 14.a3} (14. Be3 {Schussler} Nc5 15. Bc2 c6 16. b4 Na6 17. dxc6 Nxc6 18. Na3 Nc7 {And Black was ok in Nunn-Karpov, Rotterdam 1989.}) (14. Na3 {Hazai}) 14... Ng6 (14... c6 {Hazai: '?!'} 15. dxc6 Nxc6 {15...c5? 16.d5!} 16. Nf1 Nc5 17. Bd5 Ne7 18. Ne3 $14) (14... Nc5 {Hazai: '!?'} 15. Bc2 c6 {15...b4!?} (15... b4 {Hazai}) 16. b4 Na6 17. dxc6 Nxc6 18. Nf1 $14) (14... b4 $5) 15. Nf1 Nh4 {15...f4 is interesting} (15... Nf4 $5 {Hazai}) 16. N1h2 Nxf3+ 17. Nxf3 Nc5 18. Bc2 c6 $6 (18... b4 19. Be3 b3 (19... bxc3 20. bxc3 $14) 20. Bb1 $14) 19. b4 (19. dxc6 $2 Qc7 20. b4 Ne6 $1) 19... Na6 20. dxc6 Qc7 21. Bb3 $1 (21. Be3 {Hazai} Qxc6 22. Qd2 Nc7 { e6=}) 21... Qxc6 22. Bd5 Qxc3 (22... Qd7 23. Be3 $6 (23. Qd2 $1 Rd8 (23... Nc7 24. Ra7 Qd8 25. Rd1 Nxd5 26. Qxd5 Be7 27. Be3 Be6 28. Qc6 $14 {Hazai: 'Polgar,J'}) 24. Qa2 $1 {Hazai: ''} Nc7 $2 25. Qa7) 23... Rd8 { 24...b7}) 23. Be3 $1 Qc7 $8 (23... Nxb4 $2 24. Bd2 {Hazai: '+-'}) (23... Qxb4 $2 24. Qc2 $1 { 25.eb1  25.eb1  25.eb1 Hazai: ' eb1+-'}) 24. Qc1 $1 (24. Qd2 Bb7 25. Bxb7 Qxb7 26. Qxd6 Ra8 $10) 24... Bb7 (24... Qxc1 25. Rexc1 { 26.xc8} Nxb4 26. Ba7 Nxd5 (26... Rb7 27. Rxc8 $18) 27. Bxb8) (24... Qd7 25. Qa3 {Black has difficulties finding a move Black has difficulties finding a move Black has difficulties finding a move Hazai: '!'}) 25. Ba7 Bxd5 (25... Qxc1 {not better} 26. Rexc1 Bxd5 27. exd5 (27. Bxb8 $2 Nxb8 28. exd5 e4) 27... Nxb4 28. Bxb8 Rxb8 29. Rab1 Nxd5 $2 30. Rxb5 $18) 26. Qxc7 Nxc7 27. Bxb8 Rxb8 28. exd5 Nxd5 (28... e4 29. Rac1) 29. Rad1 Nxb4 30. Rxd6 Nc2 31. Re2 $1 (31. Rc1 $2 Nd4 32. Nxd4 exd4 33. Rb6 Rd8 34. Rxb5 d3 35. Rd1 d2 {with the black pawn at the second rank the win is much more difficult for white than in the game, if it is possible at all.}) 31... Nd4 32. Nxd4 exd4 33. Rb6 Rd8 34. Rxb5 g6 (34... d3 35. Rd2 Bc3 (35... g6 36. Rb3 $1 $18) 36. Rxd3 $1 $18) 35. Rd2 {to stop 35...d3} h5 {If black would take a passive set-up with g7,f8,h6, than I put both my rooks on the 7th rank ( b7,d7 ), push my pawns g4,f4, put my king on g3 - than h4,g5 is the winning plan.} 36. g3 Kg7 37. Rb7 Rd5 38. Kf1 Rd8 39. Ke2 Re8+ 40. Kd3 Re5 41. Ra2 Rf5 (41... h4 42. g4 { a2-a7, f2-f4}) 42. h4 Kg8 $2 {looses immediatly, but the black position is lost anyway.} (42... g5 43. hxg5 Bxg5 44. Ke4 Rf6 45. f4 Bh6 46. Rh2 $18) 43. Ra8+ Kg7 44. f4 {Black is in total Zugzwang} (44. f4 Bxh4 45. gxh4 Rxf4 46. Raa7 Kg8 47. Rd7 $18) 1-0

