1. e4 {Banusz,Tamas} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nge7 5. O-O g6 6. c3 Bg7 7. d4 exd4 8. cxd4 b5 9. Bb3 O-O 10. Nc3 (10. h3 {(Banusz,Tamas) Ü 111/155}) 10... Na5 (10... d6 $145 {Banusz,Tamas} 11. h3 Bb7 12. Re1 Na5 13. Bc2 Nc4 $1 $132 {Delchev,A}) 11. Bc2 d6 12. h3 (12. Bg5 {(Banusz,Tamas) Ü 111/(155)}) 12... c5 13. Bg5 {Banusz,Tamas: '!?' The most ambitious move.} ({The bishop development on f4 doesn't make problems for Black.} 13. Bf4 cxd4 {Banusz,Tamas: '!?'} (13... Nc4 {Banusz,Tamas}) 14. Nxd4 Bb7 ({Or} 14... Nc4 15. b3 Na3 16. Rc1 Bb7 17. Qd2 $6 (17. Nce2 $11) 17... Rc8 $36 {0-1 Rogic,D (2581)-Brkic,A (2588)/Stari Mikanovci CRO 2011/The Week in Chess 862 (35)}) 15. Re1 (15. Nde2 {Banusz,Tamas} Nc4 16. b3 Na3 17. Rc1 d5 $11) 15... Nc4 16. b3 Na3 17. Nce2 Qb6 $13 {1/2 Vedmediuc,S (2465)-Brkic,A (2605)/Porto Carras GRE 2011/[Microsoft] (38)}) ({After the queen exchange} 13. dxc5 dxc5 14. Qxd8 Rxd8 {White has no more reasons to hope to get an advantage.} 15. Be3 Nb7 {Banusz,Tamas: '!?'} 16. e5 Bf5 17. Be4 (17. Ne4 Nd5 18. Bg5 Re8 19. g4 Bd7 $13 {Smeets,J-Karjakin,S/Nice 2010}) 17... Bxe4 18. Nxe4 Rd5 (18... Nc6 19. Bg5 Rd3 $13) 19. Bg5 Nc6 20. Nf6+ Bxf6 21. Bxf6 Nd4 $11 {Smeets,J-Aronian,L/Nice 2010. The powerful position in the centre compensates for the weakness of the black squares.}) (13. Re1 {Banusz,Tamas} cxd4 $5 14. Nxd4 (14. Ne2 Nec6 15. Nexd4 Nxd4 16. Nxd4 Bb7) 14... Bb7 { c8, c4}) 13... h6 14. Bh4 $13 g5 ({Perhaps it's more secure to play without the kingside being weakened by the move g6-g5.} 14... cxd4 $5 15. Nxd4 (15. Ne2 $6 {is doubtful} Nc4 $15 16. Nexd4 g5 17. Bg3 Nxb2 18. Qe2 Nc4) 15... Bb7 16. Nd5 Bxd5 17. exd5 Rc8 $13) 15. Bg3 Nc4 (15... cxd4 $5 {Banusz,Tamas} 16. Nxd4 Nc4 17. b3 Na3 18. Rc1 Qb6 $1 19. Nde2 Rd8 20. Bd3 Bb7 $13 { d5}) 16. b3 $1 {This is the only way White can create problems to the opponent.} (16. Rb1 {was in vain:} Nc6 17. dxc5 (17. Ne2 $2 g4 $1 18. hxg4 Bxg4 19. e5 dxe5 20. dxc5 Bxf3 21. gxf3 Nd2 $17 {Wieczorek,O-Banusz,T/Krakow POL 2011}) 17... dxc5 18. Nd5 Ra7 19. b3 Nb6 {White should play with care.} 20. Ne3 $1 (20. Qd3 $2 {was followed by the energetic} f5 $1 $17 {0-1 Kislik,E (2320)-Banusz,T (2552)/Szombathely HUN 2011/The Week in Chess 891 (54)}) 20... Nb4 $11) 16... Na3 (16... cxd4 {Banusz,Tamas} 17. bxc4 $1 dxc3 18. Bxd6 Re8 19. c5 Bb7 20. e5 $14) 17. Bd3 {Banusz,Tamas: 'N!'} (17. Rc1 {Banusz,Tamas}) 17... Nc6 18. Nd5 $1 Nxd4 19. Nxd4 Bxd4 20. Qh5 {Banusz,Tamas: '!'} Bg7 $6 {A natural but inaccurate move.} (20... Kg7 {Banusz,Tamas: '!?' led to an unclear game:} 21. Rad1 Be6 {Banusz,Tamas: '!?'} 22. Kh1 f6 (22... Bxd5 $5 {Banusz,Tamas} 23. exd5 Bf6 $1 (23... c4 24. Bxc4 $1 bxc4 25. Rxd4 c3 26. f4 $1 $40) 24. f4 Rh8 $8 (24... b4 $2 25. fxg5 Bxg5 26. h4 Bf6 27. Qg4+ Kh8 28. Qf5 $18) 25. Qf3 b4 $13 { b5}) 23. f4 Ra7 $13 (23... Bf7 {Banusz,Tamas} 24. Qf3 Be6 25. Bf2 Bxf2 26. Qxf2 Ra7 $13) 24. fxg5 $1 {Banusz,Tamas} (24. Qf3 {Banusz,Tamas} Raf7 25. Bf2 Bxf2 26. Qxf2 $44) 24... fxg5 (24... hxg5 $4 25. e5 $18) 25. e5 Qe8 (25... Bxd5 $2 26. Qg6+ Kh8 27. Qxh6+ Kg8 28. e6 $1 Nc2 $1 (28... Rg7 $2 29. e7 Qxe7 30. Bxd6 Bxg2+ 31. Kxg2 $18) 29. Bxc2 Rg7 30. Rxf8+ (30. e7 $2 Qxe7 31. Bxd6 $140 Bxg2+ 32. Kh2 $8 (32. Kxg2 $4 Qe2+ 33. Kg3 Bf2+ 34. Kg2 Be1+ $19) 32... Bxf1 $1 33. Bxe7 Rf2+ 34. Kg3 (34. Kh1 $2 Bg2+ 35. Kg1 Rf6+ 36. Rxd4 Rxh6 37. Rd8+ Kf7 38. Bxc5 Bxh3 $15) 34... Rg2+ 35. Kf3 Rf2+ $11)) 26. Nf6 (26. Qxe8 Rxe8 27. Nf6 Rf8 28. Nh5+) 26... Qxh5 27. Nxh5+ Kg8 28. Rxf8+ Kxf8 29. exd6 $14) (20... Bxa1 $6 {Banusz,Tamas} 21. Rxa1 Ra7 $5 (21... Kg7 22. e5 $1 Re8 23. exd6 Ra7 (23... c4 24. Bf1 f5 (24... Ra7 25. Rd1 Bf5 26. Qf3 Be4 27. Qe3 $1 Rb7 28. Nc7 Rxc7 29. Qd4+ $1 f6 30. dxc7 Qxd4 31. Rxd4 $18) 25. f4 $1 (25. Ne7 $6 Rxe7 26. dxe7 Qxe7 27. Qf3 Bb7 28. Qxf5 Re8 $16) 25... Re6 (25... Bb7 26. Nc7 $18) 26. Nc7 Qxd6 27. fxg5 $1 (27. Nxa8 $2 Qd4+ 28. Bf2 Qxa1 $13) 27... Qc5+ 28. Kh2 Rg6 29. Nxa8 Rxg5 30. Qf3 $18) 24. f4 $1 Be6 $8 25. Nc7 Rxc7 26. fxg5 Qxg5 27. Qxg5+ hxg5 28. dxc7 $16) 22. Rd1 $1 (22. Qxh6 $6 f6) 22... f6 23. Ne3 $1 {( e2-g4)} b4 (23... Qe7 24. Be2 (24. Bxd6 $4 Qxd6 25. Bc4+ Nxc4 26. Rxd6 Nxd6 $19) 24... Rd8 25. Bg4 Qf7 26. Qxh6 Qg7 27. Qh5 Qf7 28. Rxd6 Rxd6 29. Bxd6 Qxh5 30. Bxh5 $14) 24. Qg6+ (24. Be2 Qe8 25. Bxd6 Qxh5 26. Bxh5 Rd8 27. Bxc5 Rxd1+ 28. Bxd1 $44) 24... Rg7 25. Qxh6 Rh7 26. Qg6+ Rg7 27. Qh5 $44) 21. Rad1 $36 {White has got more than enough compensation for the pawn.} c4 22. Be2 c3 {Banusz,Tamas: '?'} (22... cxb3 {Banusz,Tamas} 23. axb3 Nc2 24. f4 $1 $40) 23. Nxc3 {Banusz,Tamas: '!'} Bxc3 24. Bxd6 {Banusz,Tamas: ''} Nc2 {Banusz,Tamas: '?'} (24... Re8 {Banusz,Tamas} 25. e5 $1 (25. Bxa3 Qf6 26. Rd6 Be6 27. Rfd1 Be5 $14) 25... Nc2 26. Rd3 $1 Bb2 (26... Nd4 27. Bf3 Bf5 28. Rxc3 Rc8 29. Bd5 $1 (29. Rxc8 $6 Nxf3+ 30. Qxf3 Qxc8 $16) 29... Ne2+ (29... Be6 30. Rxc8 Qxc8 31. Qxh6 $1 Bxd5 32. Qxg5+ Kh8 33. Qh4+ Kg8 34. Qxd4 $18) 30. Kh2 Nxc3 31. Qxf7+ Kh8 32. Qxf5 Nxd5 33. Rd1 $1 $18 Nc3 $140 34. e6 $1 { e5}) (26... Bd4 27. Rf3 $1 Ra7 28. Bd3 Bxe5 29. Bxe5 Rxe5 30. Qxh6 f5 31. Bxc2 $16) 27. Rf3 $1 Ra7 $8 (27... Nd4 28. Qxf7+ Kh8 29. Rf6 Nxe2+ 30. Kh1 Re6 31. Bf8 $1 $18) (27... Be6 28. Qxh6 Nd4 29. Bd3 $1 Nxf3+ 30. gxf3 f5 31. exf6 Qd7 32. Qxg5+ Kh8 33. Qh5+ Kg8 34. Kh1 $18) 28. Bd3 Bxe5 29. Bxe5 Rxe5 30. Qxh6 f5 $8 31. Bxc2 $16) 25. Bxf8 Qxf8 26. Rc1 {Banusz,Tamas: '+-'} Ne3 27. fxe3 Be5 28. Bg4 Bxg4 29. Qxg4 Rd8 30. Rc6 Kg7 31. Qh5 f6 32. Rd1 Qb4 33. Rcc1 Qxe4 34. Qf3 Rxd1+ 35. Rxd1 Qc2 36. e4 Qxa2 37. Rd7+ Kg6 38. h4 Qa1+ 39. Rd1 Bd4+ 40. Kh1 Qc3 41. h5+ Kf7 42. Qf5 Bc5 43. Qh7+ Ke6 44. Qd7+ 1-0

