d3 17. Qxd3 (17. cxd3 Qc7 18. Qe3 d4 19. Qxd4 Bxg2 20. Rhg1 Bb7 $13) 17... Qc7 18. Ne2 Qc4 19. Nd4 $14) 16... Qc7 17. g4 f6 (17... Nxd3 $6 18. Qxd3 b5 19. Ne2 $14) (17... b5 18. f5 $11) 18. f5 $5 (18. exf6 Rxf6 (18... Nxd3 19. Rxe6 (19. cxd3 $6 Rxf6 20. Re5 Qc5 21. Qxc5 bxc5 $11) 19... Qxf4 20. Qxd3 $16) 19. f5 Nxd3 (19... Qxh2 20. g5 Rff8 21. fxe6 $16) 20. Qxd3 d4 $14) 18... Nxd3 (18... Rfe8 19. h3 $11) 19. cxd3 {Nijboer,Friso: '*'} ({Weaker is} 19. Qxd3 fxe5 20. fxe6 d4 $15) (19. Rxd3 $6 fxe5 20. Rxe5 exf5 21. gxf5 Rce8 22. Rxe8 Rxe8 $14) 19... exf5 20. gxf5 fxe5 (20... Qc5 21. Qxc5 Rxc5 22. d4 $14) 21. Rxe5 {Nijboer,Friso: ''} Qc5 22. Qg4 (22. Qxc5 bxc5 23. Nxd5 Bxd5 24. Rxd5 Rfd8 $16) 22... b5 (22... Rc7 23. d4 Qc4 24. Qg2 $11) 23. d4 (23. Rde1 Rc7 $14) 23... Qd6 $6 ({Better was} 23... Qc6 $1 24. Rxd5 b4 25. Rc5 Qg2 26. Qxg2 Bxg2 27. Na4 Be4+ 28. Kc1 Bxf5 $11 {with equal position}) 24. h4 (24. Rde1 Rf7 $14) 24... Rc7 (24... b4 25. Rg1 Rc7 26. Ne2 $14) 25. Re6 (25. Rde1 Rcf7 $14) 25... Qd8 26. Rf1 Rcf7 (26... b4 27. Nd1 $11) 27. Re5 (27. Nd1 Bc8 28. Re5 Re7 $11) 27... b4 28. Nd1 {[%cal Gd1e3]} (28. Na4 $6 Bc8 29. Nc5 g6 $15 {[%csl Rf5]}) 28... a5 (28... b3 29. a3 $11) 29. Ne3 Kh8 (29... b3 30. a3 $14) 30. h5 a4 31. Qg2 (31. h6 g6 $14) 31... b3 32. a3 (32. Nxd5 $2 {is no good because of} Rd7 33. Rg1 Re8 $19 (33... Bxd5 $6 34. Rxd5 Qf6 35. h6 gxh6 36. Rxd7 Qxf5+ 37. Ka1 Qxd7 38. d5 $14)) 32... Qh4 33. Rd1 h6 (33... Qxh5 $4 {the pawn is something Black will choke on} 34. Rh1 Qxh1+ 35. Qxh1 $18) 34. Qe2 (34. Nxd5 $4 {the pawn of course cannot be captured} Rxf5 35. Ne7 Qxe7 $19 (35... Bxg2 $6 {is clearly worse} 36. Ng6+ Kh7 37. Nxh4 Rxe5 38. dxe5 Be4+ 39. Kc1 $19)) 34... Rc7 35. Qb5 (35. Qf3 Qg5 $14) 35... Re7 {After this move game becomes extremly sharp and black doesn't stand a pressure.} (35... Rcf7 36. Qxa4 Qxh5 37. Qxb3 $16) (35... Bc6 {'!?' should be investigated more closely} 36. Qc5 (36. Qd3 Qxh5 $11) 36... Rcc8) 36. f6 $1 Rxe5 (36... Ref7 37. fxg7+ Kxg7 38. Qxa4 $16) (36... gxf6 37. Rxe7) 37. fxg7+ Kxg7 38. dxe5 Qe4+ 39. Ka1 Rf7 $2 {Losing in a few moves, while after correct} (39... d4 $1 40. Qd7+ (40. Nc4 Qc6 41. Qb4 Qf3 $132) (40. Rg1+ Kh8 41. Ng4 Qf4 $132) 40... Kh8 41. Qd6 (41. Qe7 Qf3 42. Rg1 Rg8 43. Rxg8+ Kxg8 44. Qd8+ Kf7 45. Qd7+ Kf8 46. Qxd4 $11) 41... Qf4 42. Rxd4 Rc8 43. Rd1 Qxe3 44. Qf6+ Kg8 45. Rd8+ Rxd8 46. Qxd8+ Kf7 47. Qd7+ Kf8 $11 {the position remains equal.}) (39... Qxe3 40. Qxb7+ Kh8 41. Qxd5 Rc8 $14) 40. Rg1+ Kh7 (40... Kf8 41. Qb6 $1 Qxe5 42. Qd8+ Qe8 43. Rg8+ Kxg8 44. Qxe8+ Kg7 45. Nf5+ $18) 41. Ng4 $1 $18 (41. Qb6 $5 {might be the shorter path} Bc6 42. Qxc6 Rg7 $18) 41... Bc6 $5 (41... Qd4 42. Nf6+ Rxf6 43. Qxb7+ $18) 42. Qxc6 Qxg4 43. Qg6+ $1 (43. Rxg4 $4 {White will choke on that} Rf1+ 44. Qc1 Rxc1#) 43... Qxg6 44. hxg6+ (44. Rxg6 $4 Rf1#) 44... Kg7 45. gxf7+ Kxf7 46. Rg4 $18 {1-0 (46) Polgar,J (2656)-Short,N (2677) Buenos Aires 2000 CBM 080 [Finkel,Alexander]} 1-0

