1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. g3 Bg7 7. Bg2 O-O 8. O-O Nc6 9. Nde2 Rb8 10. a4 a6 11. h3 b5 12. axb5 axb5 13. Bg5 h6 14. Be3 b4 15. Nd5 Nd7 16. Qc1 Kh7 17. Rd1 Bb7 18. Nd4 e6 19. Nxc6 Bxc6 20. Nf4 Ne5 21. Bd4 Qc7 22. b3 Ra8 23. Qe3 Rxa1 24. Rxa1 Ra8 25. Rxa8 Bxa8 26. Qd2 h5 27. Ne2 Nd7 28. Bxg7 Kxg7 29. Nf4 Nf6 30. Qxb4 Qxc2 31. Qxd6 Qxb3 {The position looks dead draw, so White goes for the last wave of pressure, which surprisingly pays off.} 32. e5 Ne4 {Only move!} (32... Bxg2 $4 33. exf6+) (32... Nd5 33. Nxe6+ $1 fxe6 34. Qd7+ Kh6 35. Qd8 Qb7 36. Qh8+ Kg5 37. Qf8 $18) (32... Qb1+ 33. Kh2 Ne4 34. Nxe6+ fxe6 35. Qe7+ Kh6 36. Qf8+ Kh7 37. Qxa8 Nxf2 (37... Ng5 $18 {doesn't change much.}) 38. Qa7+ $18 {, picking up the horse on one of the longest forks ever!}) 33. Qd4 Qb1+ 34. Kh2 Bc6 {'??'} (34... Bb7 35. Qd7 (35. Nxe6+ fxe6 36. Qd7+ {leads nowhere -} Kh6 37. Qxe6 Ng5 38. Qe8 Bxg2 39. Qf8+ Kh7 40. Qe7+ $11) 35... Qb6 36. Nxe6+ Qxe6 37. Qxb7 Nxf2 38. Qf3 Qxe5 $1 {not the only, but perhaps the easiest way to draw.} 39. Qxf2 h4 $11) 35. Nd3 {'!'} Qb7 36. Nb4 {'!'} Bd5 37. Nxd5 exd5 38. Bxe4 {'!'} dxe4 39. e6+ Kh6 (39... Kh7 40. Qd7 Qb2 41. Qxf7+ Qg7 42. Qd7 $1 $18) 40. Qh8+ Kg5 41. Qe5+ Kh6 42. e7 $18 1-0

