{Nigel Davies: '15...d5!? is an enterprising attempt to free Black's position. But does it work? This is the stem game in which Black seems to be OK after 16.exd5 - though the position is massively complicated.'} 1. e4 {Anand Anand: 'Beliavsky'} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Nb8 10. d4 Nbd7 11. Nbd2 Bb7 12. Bc2 Re8 13. Nf1 (13. a4 {(Anand) Beliavsky}) 13... Bf8 14. Ng3 g6 15. b3 d5 $1 $146 {Nigel Davies: '!?' Nigel Davies: '!?' Nigel Davies: '!?' Anand: '!'} (15... c5 $6 {Ü 14/297 Ü 14/297 Ü 14/297 Anand: 'Beliavsky'}) (15... Bg7 $6 {Ü 17/326 Ü 17/326 Ü 17/326 Anand: 'Beliavsky'}) 16. exd5 ({Nigel Davies: 'For'} 16. Bg5 {Nigel Davies: '!?' Nigel Davies: 'see Polgar - Spassky and Sherzer - Lesiege.'} h6 $1 17. Bxf6 Qxf6 18. exd5 exd4 $132) ({Nigel Davies: 'One of Black's ideas is that after'} 16. dxe5 Nxe5 17. Nxe5 Rxe5 18. f4 {Nigel Davies: 'he can sacrifice the exchange with'} (18. Bf4 Re6 $1 $132) 18... Rxe4 19. Nxe4 dxe4 $44 {Nigel Davies: 'etc.'}) 16... Nxd5 17. dxe5 Nxc3 18. Qd3 ({Nigel Davies: 'Black can meet'} 18. Qd4 {Nigel Davies: 'with'} Nxe5 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'because' Nigel Davies: 'because' Nigel Davies: 'because' Anand: ''} 19. Qxc3 $140 $2 {Nigel Davies: '?' Nigel Davies: '?' Nigel Davies: '?' Anand: '?'} Nxf3+ 20. gxf3 Bg7 $19 {Nigel Davies: 'wins the rook on a1.'}) 18... Nd5 19. Bg5 Qc8 20. Qd4 Bg7 21. Nf5 $5 {Nigel Davies: 'Trying to confuse matters.'} ({Nigel Davies: 'After'} 21. Rad1 c5 22. Qh4 Nxe5 23. Nxe5 Rxe5 {Nigel Davies: 'White doesn't get enough for the pawn. If he tries'} 24. Nh5 {Nigel Davies: 'there follows'} Rxe1+ ({Nigel Davies: 'and not the immediate'} 24... gxh5 {Nigel Davies: 'because of'} 25. Rxe5 Bxe5 26. Qe4 $40 {Nigel Davies: 'with dangerous threats.'}) 25. Rxe1 gxh5 26. Qxh5 Qc6 $1 27. Qxh7+ Kf8 $17 {Nigel Davies: 'when White's attack grinds to a halt.'}) 21... gxf5 22. Bxf5 {[ g4]} Re6 $8 {Anand: ''} 23. Qh4 Nf8 24. Nd4 c5 25. Rac1 Qc7 26. Nxe6 fxe6 27. Bb1 Rc8 28. Qg3 ({Nigel Davies: 'Perhaps'} 28. Re4 $5 $44 {Nigel Davies: '!?' Nigel Davies: 'would have been a better try.' Nigel Davies: '!?' Nigel Davies: 'would have been a better try.' Nigel Davies: '!?' Nigel Davies: 'would have been a better try.' Anand: 'Beliavsky'}) 28... Ng6 29. h4 Nxe5 $1 30. Bh6 Nf3+ $17 31. Qxf3 Bxh6 32. Rcd1 Qg7 33. Qe4 Re8 34. g3 Nf6 ({Nigel Davies: 'And not'} 34... Nc3 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'which allows White to fight on with'} 35. Qxh7+ $1 Qxh7 36. Bxh7+ Kxh7 37. Rd7+ Kg6 38. Rxb7 {etc.}) 35. Qc2 Qc7 36. Rf1 Kh8 37. Qc3 Bg7 38. Qd2 Nd5 39. Kh2 Bd4 40. Qd3 Nf6 $19 41. Qe2 Rg8 42. Rxd4 cxd4 0-1

