{[%mdl 2] Wedberg: 'Wedberg,Tom: 'Wedberg,T: 'This win certainly contributed a lot to the overall victory for the world team. In a sense it might have been the deciding game.'''} {This win certainly contributed a lot to the overall victory for the world team. In a sense it might have been the deciding game.} 1. e4 {Wedberg Wedberg Wedberg Wedberg: 'Wedberg,Tom Wedberg,Tom: 'Wedberg,T''} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 {Wedberg: 'Wedberg,Tom: 'Wedberg,T: 'Quite a surprise. Kasparov takes up the Berlin defence. The very weapon that robbed him of his crown.''' Quite a surprise. Kasparov takes up the Berlin defence. The very weapon that robbed him of his crown.} 4. O-O Nxe4 5. d4 Nd6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. dxe5 Nf5 8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 9. Nc3 h6 10. Rd1+ Ke8 11. h3 Be7 {Wedberg: 'Wedberg,Tom: 'Wedberg,T: 'The move Be7 in some position or another is the new fab. Kramnik has played it without h6. The idea is to set up an exchange with Nh4. One negative aspect of the move is that the often useful reprouping with Ne7-g6 is lost.''' The move e7 in some position or another is the new fab. Kramnik has played it without h6. The idea is to set up an exchange with h4. One negative aspect of the move is that the often useful reprouping with e7-g6 is lost.} 12. Ne2 (12. g4 Nh4 13. Nxh4 Bxh4 14. Kg2 h5 15. f3 {Wedberg: 'Wedberg,Tom: 'Wedberg,T: 'was tried succesfully in Kotronias,V-Nikolaidis,I/ Peristeri 1993/CBM 39 ext/[ChessBase] (66)''' was tried succesfully in Kotronias,V-Nikolaidis,I/Peristeri 1993/CBM 39 ext/[ChessBase] (66)}) 12... Nh4 {Wedberg: 'Wedberg,Tom: 'Wedberg,T: 'Should Black strive after exchanges at all costs in the Berlin? Im not so sure. There is also the question of time. Black is spending it here.''' Should Black strive after exchanges at all costs in the Berlin? Im not so sure. There is also the question of time. Black is spending it here.} (12... Bd7 13. b3 Rd8 (13... Nh4 14. Nxh4 Bxh4 15. Ba3 b6 16. Rd4 Bd8 17. Rad1 Bf5 18. R4d2 c5 19. g4 Be4 20. Ng3 Bc6 21. Nh5 g6 22. Nf6+ 