1. e4 {Baburin Baburin,Alexander Alexander Baburin: 'Baburin: 'Ftacnik ''} c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Qb6 5. Nb3 a6 (5... Nf6 {Ü 67/225}) (5... d6 {Ftacnik} 6. Bd3 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. Be3 Qc7 9. f4 Nc6 10. Nc3 Bd7 11. g4 h5 12. h3 hxg4 13. hxg4 g5 14. fxg5 Nh7 15. g6 fxg6 16. Nb5 Qb8 17. Bf4 Ng5 18. Kg2 Ne5 19. Be2 Bc6 20. Bxg5 Bxg5 21. Qd4 Bxb5 22. Bxb5+ Ke7 {0-1 Shetty,R-Vaidya,A/Calcutta (10)/1992 (33)}) 6. Nc3 d6 $146 (6... Qc7 {Ü 61/191 Alexander Baburin: 'Ftacnik '} 7. Be2 Nf6 8. O-O b5 9. Bf3 Nc6 10. g3 Bb7 11. Bg2 d6 12. Re1 Be7 13. a4 b4 14. Na2 O-O 15. Bf4 Rfd8 16. Qd2 Rab8 17. Rac1 Ne5 18. Nxb4 Bxe4 19. Nxa6 Qb7 20. Rxe4 Nxe4 21. Nxb8 Nxd2 22. Bxb7 Nxb3 23. cxb3 Rxb8 24. Rc8+ Rxc8 25. Bxc8 {1-0 Anand,V-Polgar,J/Monaco blind (02)/1995 (32)}) (6... Nc6 $5) 7. Bf4 $5 Nf6 8. Qd2 Be7 (8... Nbd7 9. O-O-O Ne5 10. Be3 Qc7 11. f4) 9. O-O-O O-O 10. g4 {Alexander Baburin: '!?' '!?' '!?' Baburin,Alexander: '!?'} (10. Bxd6 {Ftacnik} Bxd6 11. Qxd6 Qxf2 $13) 10... Nxg4 (10... e5 11. Be3 Qd8 12. f3 $16) 11. Rg1 Ne5 (11... e5 12. Nd5 Qd8 13. Nxe7+ Qxe7 14. Bg3 $5 {×d6} (14. Bg5 f6 15. Bh4)) (11... Nxf2 $2 {Ftacnik} 12. Be3 $18) (11... Nf6 {Ftacnik} 12. Bh6 Ne8 13. Bxg7 Nxg7 14. Qh6 $18) 12. Qe2 (12. Bxe5 $2 dxe5 13. Qh6 g6 14. Rd3 Qxf2 15. Rh3 Qf4+) (12. Rg3 $5) 12... Qc7 (12... Ng6 $5 13. Be3 Qd8 14. f4 $44 { h5, f5}) 13. Be3 b5 (13... Nbc6 14. f4 Ng6 15. h4 $5 $44 Bxh4 16. Qh5) 14. f4 Nc4 (14... Ng6 {Ftacnik} 15. f5 $40) 15. Bd4 g6 {Alexander Baburin: 'Some holes appear in the Black position.'} (15... e5 {Ftacnik} 16. Nd5 Qd8 17. Qg2 g6 18. fxe5 $16) 16. Qh5 {Alexander Baburin: '!?' '!?' '!?' Alexander Baburin: 'The queen is getting close to Black's king and the promising h6-square.' Baburin,Alexander: '!?'} (16. Rd3 d5 $1 {} 17. exd5 Qxf4+ 18. Kb1 e5) 16... Nd7 $8 {Alexander Baburin: '?' '?' '?' Baburin,Alexander: '?'} ({Alexander Baburin: 'More critical would have been'} 16... Nc6 {Alexander Baburin: '!' '!' Alexander Baburin: 'hitting the dangerous d4-bishop, as GM Seirawan correctly pointed out in 'Inside Chess' magazine. Then the play may continue:' Baburin,Alexander: '!'} 17. Rd3 {Alexander Baburin: '!' '!' Alexander Baburin: 'Ftacnik ' Baburin,Alexander: '!'} (17. f5 Nxd4 18. fxg6 (18. Nxd4 $6 Bf6 {is slow and therefore is not satisfactory for White.}) 18... Nxb3+ 19. axb3 fxg6 20. Rxg6+ $1 {It looks to me that this sharp line should result in a draw:} (20. Bxc4 $2 {is not good because of} Bf6 $1 ({but not} 20... bxc4 $2 {when White transposes into a favourable line:} 21. Rxg6+ Kh8 22. Qh6)) {After the inferior move} 20... Kh8 $2 {White's attack is indeed very dangerous:} (20... hxg6 $1 {Strangly enough Seirawan did not consider this move, although the text makes a lot of sense - grabbing as much material as possible and giving some of it back later can be a good defensive technique in such positions.} 21. Qxg6+ Kh8 22. Qh6+ Kg8 {and now White has to settle for a draw by perpetual check -} 23. Qg6+ ({as after} 23. Bxc4 $2 Bf6 {White has insufficient compensation for the rook.})) 21. Bxc4 bxc4 22. Qh6 Rf7 23. Rdg1 Bb7 24. Rg7 Bg5+ 25. R7xg5 {for example:} cxb3 26. Qxe6 bxc2 27. Nd5 Bxd5 28. Qxd5 $16) (17. Qh6 $6 Nxd4 18. Nxd4 Bf6) 17... e5 (17... Nxd4 18. Rh3 Nxb3+ 19. axb3 Kg7 20. Qh6+ Kf6 21. e5+ dxe5 22. Ne4+ Kf5 23. Bd3 $18) 18. Nd5 Qd8 (18... Qb7 19. f5 Kh8 20. Qh6 Rg8 21. Rh3 Rg7 22. Bf2 $40) 19. f5 Kh8 20. Qh6 Rg8 21. Rh3 Rg7 22. Bf2 $16) 17. Qh6 (17. Rd3 $5 {Alexander Baburin: 'appears to be more direct. Black has only one defence:'} e5 {Alexander Baburin: '(Seirawan)'} (17... Bf6 $2 18. Rh3 Rd8 19. Rxg6+ fxg6 20. Qxh7+ Kf8 21. Bxf6 $18 Nxf6 22. Qxc7 $18) (17... Nf6 18. Bxf6 Bxf6 19. Rh3 Re8 20. Qxh7+ Kf8 21. Rxg6 $18) (17... Re8 $4 18. Qxh7+ $1 $18) (17... Rd8 18. Qxh7+ $1 Kxh7 19. Rh3+) 18. Nd5 Nf6 $8 {Alexander Baburin: 'However, after'} (18... Qd8 19. Rh3 $18) 19. Nxc7 Nxh5 20. Nxa8 exd4 21. Nc7 {Alexander Baburin: 'Ftacnik '} (21. f5 {White keeps the advantage.}) 21... Bb7 $13 (21... Nxf4 $14)) 17... Bf6 (