1. e4 {Ftacnik,L Petrov,Marian Ftacnik Petrov,Marian Hellers} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 e6 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. Qf3 g6 {Petrov,Marian: 'Sometimes Black tries this Dragon-like setup. The pawn on e6 makes the d6-pawn more fragile compared to the Dragon, but the white setup is also very different so it can work.'} (8... Qb6 $5 9. a3 Nc5 10. b4 $1 Nxd3+ 11. Qxd3 Be7 12. Bb2 O-O 13. O-O-O e5 14. Nf5 Bxf5 15. exf5 exf4 16. g4 $1 h6 17. h4 Nxg4 18. Nd5 Qd8 19. Rhg1 Ne5 $1 20. Qe4 Kh8 $8 {Ftacnik: ''} 21. Rxg7 $2 (21. f6 $1 Bxf6 22. Nxf6 Qxf6 23. Rxd6 Qxd6 24. Bxe5 $18) 21... Kxg7 22. Rg1+ Kh8 23. Qxf4 Kh7 24. Nxe7 $17 {Mokry,K-Arnason,J/Manila ol/1992/}) (8... Nc5 9. O-O (9. f5 {Petrov,Marian} e5 10. Nb3 b5 $6 (10... Nxd3+ 11. cxd3 b5 12. Bg5 Bb7 $11) 11. Bg5 Be7 12. Nxc5 dxc5 13. O-O-O Qa5 14. Qg3 $1 c4 15. Be2 b4 16. Nd5 Qxa2 17. Qxe5 $18 Nxd5 18. Rxd5 f6 19. Bh5+ {1-0 (19) Sokolov,A (2585)-Sakaev,K (2570) Tivat 1995}) 9... Nxd3 10. cxd3 Be7 11. Be3 O-O 12. g4 Kh8 13. g5 Nd7 14. Qh5 g6 15. Qh6 Rg8 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Bd4+ Nf6 18. Qh4 Rf8 19. Nd5 e5 20. fxe5 Nxd5 21. e6+ Kg8 22. exd5 Rf5 23. Rxf5 gxf5 24. Qh5 $18 {Takk-Turke/corr/1968/}) (8... e5 $5 {Petrov,Marian} 9. Nf5 (9. Nb3 Be7 10. O-O O-O 11. a4 exf4 12. Qxf4 Ne5 13. a5 Be6 14. Nd4 b5 15. Nf5 Re8 16. Be3 Bxf5 17. Qxf5 Qc8 18. Bd4 Bd8 $11 {1/2 (30) Patterson,L (2195)-Norkin,A (2200) ICCF email 2008}) 9... g6 10. Ne3 exf4 11. Qxf4 Ne5 12. O-O Bg7 $11 {0-1 (43) Markzon,G (2280)-Oll,L (2585) Benidorm 1993}) 9. Nb3 (9. g4 Bg7 10. Be3 e5 11. Nde2 exf4 12. Qxf4 Ne5 13. h3 O-O 14. Ng3 Be6 15. O-O Bxg4 16. hxg4 Nfxg4 17. Kg2 Bh6 18. Qxh6 Nxh6 19. Bxh6 Re8 20. Nd5 Re6 21. Nf4 Re8 22. Nd5 Re6 $13 {0,5/Bronstein,L-Giardelli,S/Argentina ch (4)/1989/}) 9... Bg7 10. Be3 O-O 11. g4 Rb8 $5 {Petrov,Marian: '?!' '?!'} (11... b5 12. e5 Nxg4 $5 13. Qxg4 (13. Qxa8 Nxe3 $132) 13... dxe5 14. O-O f5 15. Qg2 e4 16. Be2 Bb7 $44) (11... Qc7 {Hellers  b5} 12. h4 {Petrov,Marian} b5 13. h5 Bb7 14. hxg6 hxg6 15. Qh3 (15. g5 N