1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. c4 Nb6 5. Nf3 g6 (5... Bg4 {is the alternative.}) 6. Be2 Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. Nc3 Nc6 9. d5 $1 $146 {Alexander Volzhin: '!' Alexander Volzhin: 'The only way to fight for an opening advantage.'} (9. Be3 Bg4 $1 {it is White who has to fight for equality! In Janetsch - Larsen, 1977, he failed to achieve this:} 10. d5 Bxf3 11. gxf3 $6 ({The natural} 11. Bxf3 {looks better} Ne5 12. c5 Nbc4 {with mutual chances.}) 11... Na5 $1 12. c5 Nbc4 13. Bf4 e6 $1 {sacrificing a pawn in order to penetrate to the 7th rank} 14. dxe6 fxe6 15. Qxd8 Raxd8 16. Bxc7 Rd2 {with a clear advantage for Black.}) 9... Ne5 (9... Na5 {Alexander Volzhin: '?!' Alexander Volzhin: 'leads to a clear advantage for White after'} 10. c5 Bxc3 11. cxb6 (11. bxc3 Nxd5 12. Bh6 Re8 (12... Nxc3 $2 13. Qe1 Nxe2+ 14. Qxe2 Re8 15. Rad1 Bd7 16. Qd2 $18) 13. Qa4 $44 Nxc3 $140 (13... c6 $140 $2 14. Rad1 Qc7 15. Rxd5 $18) 14. Qxa5 Nxe2+ 15. Kh1 $18) 11... Bg7 12. Bf4 $1 Bxb2 (12... axb6 13. b4 Bxa1 14. Qxa1 Nb3 15. Qb2 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: 'winning'}) 13. bxc7 $16) 10. Nxe5 (10. c5 $5 Nbd7 11. Be3 Nxf3+ 12. Bxf3 Ne5 13. Be2 c6 14. f4 $1 Nd7 15. Bf3 Qa5 $2 {A ridiculous move.} (15... cxd5 {should be preferred, after} 16. Qxd5 Qc7 17. Rac1 Nf6 18. Qd1 Rd8 19. Qe2 {White is slightly better, but Black easily held the position in Vlad - Prudnikova, Romania, 1992.}) 16. dxc6 Nxc5 17. Nd5 $1 {and Black is in trouble.}) 10... Bxe5 11. Bh6 Bg7 {Alexander Volzhin: '?!' Alexander Volzhin: 'A clear inaccuracy. After the exchange of dark-squared Bishops White obtains a huge space advantage.'} ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Black has a playable position after'} 11... Re8 12. Qd2 $16 (12. c5 {leads White nowhere after} Bxc3) 12... e6 $1 {and White couldn't obtain any advantage in Dmitriev - Volzhin, Russia,1990:} 13. Rad1 exd5 14. cxd5 Bd7 15. Rfe1 Nc8 16. Bg5 Bf6 17. Bxf6 Qxf6 18. Bb5 Bxb5 19. Nxb5 Nd6 20. Qb4 Nxb5 21. Qxb5 Rxe1+ 22. Rxe1 b6 23. g3 Qd6 $11) 12. Bxg7 Kxg7 13. Qd4+ $16 f6 $6 (13... Kg8 14. c5 Nd7 {was also not much fun.}) 14. c5 e5 $8 15. Qd2 Nd7 16. b4 f5 17. Rad1 a5 18. a3 axb4 19. axb4 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Black's position is very difficult. His pieces are passive and cannot be activated due to White's powerful pawn mass, his king is also not safe.'} f4 $6 ({Alexander Volzhin: 'This pawn advance makes things worse.'} 19... Nf6 $16 {Alexander Volzhin: 'was more tenacious.'}) 20. d6 $1 Nf6 21. Nb5 $1 cxd6 22. Qb2 $1 Bf5 23. Nxd6 Qe7 24. Bf3 e4 {Alexander Volzhin: 'This is losing but Black had no choice.'} 25. Bxe4 $1 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: '!'} Bxe4 26. Rde1 ({Although there was nothing wrong with} 26. Rfe1 {the text move is good as the rook could be useful on the f-file as we'll see.}) 26... Kh6 27. f3 b6 28. fxe4 bxc5 29. bxc5 Nh5 (29... Ng4 30. Rf3 {Alexander Volzhin: 'winning'}) 30. e5 Qe6 31. Rf2 Ra5 32. c6 Rc5 33. Qb7 {Alexander Volzhin: 'The quickest way to win as the pawn on e5 cannot be taken.'} Qd5 (33... Rxe5 34. Rxe5 Qxe5 35. Nf7+ Rxf7 36. Qxf7 Qe1+ 37. Rf1 {Alexander Volzhin: 'winning'}) 34. Qe7 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Black resigned.'} 1-0

