1. e4 {Notes by Judit Polgar Notes by Judit Polgar C16: French: 3 Nc3 Bb4 4 e5: Lines without ...c5} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 Ne7 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 b6 {One of L.B.Hansen's pet lines} 7. Qg4 (7. Nh3 Ng6 8. a4 Ba6 {8...c5!?} 9. Bxa6 Nxa6 10. O-O Nb8 11. f4 Qd7 12. f5 $16 {Nunn,J-Hansen,LB/Lugano/1989/   TD 1989/1}) 7... Kf8 {7...g6 is more usual} 8. Nf3 (8. h4 Ba6 9. Bxa6 Nxa6 10. h5 h6 11. Ne2 c5 12. Rh3 Rc8 13. a4 cxd4 14. Ba3 dxc3 15. Rf3 $13 {Lgumina-Hansen,LB/Lugano/1989/  TD 1989/1}) 8... Ba6 9. Bd3 c5 10. dxc5 Bxd3 11. cxd3 bxc5 12. O-O Nd7 13. a4 Nc6 14. Ba3 h6 {14...g8!?  h6 14...g8!?  h6 Consolidates g5} 15. c4 $1 Ncxe5 $8 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. Qg3 (17. Qd4 Nd7 18. cxd5 Kg8 19. Bxc5 Nxc5 20. Qxc5 Qxd5 $10) 17... Nc6 (17... Ng6 18. Bxc5+ Kg8 19. Rab1 Qd7 20. Qd6 {/}) 18. Bxc5+ Kg8 19. Rab1 Kh7 $1 (19... Qd7 20. Qd6 $1) (19... Rc8 20. Ba3 $14) 20. Rb7 Qf6 21. cxd5 (21. Bd6 Nd4) 21... exd5 22. Qg4 $5 {against 22...ab8 23.c7 hc8} Rhd8 23. h3 Kg8 24. d4 $6 (24. Rfb1 Re8 $14) 24... Re8 $1 {× e4} 25. Qh5 Rad8 (25... Nxd4 26. Bxd4 Qxd4 27. Qxf7+ Kh8 $10) 26. Rd1 Re4 27. Rd3 $5 {Start of an interesting plan} (27. Bxa7 $5 {and White has air to breath} Rde8 28. g3 $11) 27... Re1+ {''} ({Weaker is} 27... Nxd4 28. Bxd4 Rxd4 29. Rxd4 Qxd4 30. Qxf7+ Kh7 31. Rxa7 $16) 28. Kh2 Qxf2 29. Rf3 {Do you see the mate threat?} Qg1+ 30. Kg3 g6 $8 31. Qxh6 Re2 32. Kh4 $1 (32. Rbxf7 Rxg2+ 33. Kh4 Qe1+ 34. Rf2 Qe4+ 35. R7f4 g5+ 36. Qxg5+ Rxg5 37. Rxe4 dxe4 38. Kxg5 Nxd4 $10) 32... Qxg2 $4 {Black overlooks a pretty combination in a heavy timetrouble Black overlooks a pretty combination in a heavy timetrouble spoils everything} (32... Re4+ 33. g4 (33. Kg3 Re2 34. Kh4 Re4+ 35. Kg3 $10 Qe1+ 36. Kh2) 33... Qe1+ 34. Rg3 Rde8 $13) (32... Qe1+ {was a good chance to save the game} 33. g3 Re4+ 34. Rf4 Ne7 35. Bxe7 Rxe7 $11) 33. Qg7+ $3 {Judit Polgar Judit Polgar a sacrifice to finish the game} (33. Qg7+ Kxg7 34. Rfxf7+ Kh8 (34... Kg8 35. Rg7+ Kh8) 35. Rh7+ Kg8 36. Rbg7#) (33. Rbxf7 $6 {is not possible} Re4+ 34. R3f4 Rxf4+ 35. Rxf4 Re8 $16) (33. Rfxf7 $6 {is easily refuted} Re4+ 34. Rf4 Qf2+ 35. Kg4 Qg1+ 36. Kh4 Qf2+ 37. Kg4 Qg1+ 38. Kh4 Qf2+ $11) 1-0

