1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. Nce2 c5 6. c3 cxd4 7. cxd4 f6 8. f4 fxe5 9. fxe5 {Polgar,Judit: 'N'} (9. dxe5 Nc6 10. Nf3 Bb4+ 11. Nc3 (11. Bd2 Nc5 12. Bxb4 Nxb4 13. Nc3 (13. Ned4 Qa5 $36) 13... O-O 14. a3 (14. g3 d4 $36) 14... Nc6 15. g3 Qb6 16. b4 Nxb4 17. axb4 (17. Rb1 Ncd3+ 18. Bxd3 Qe3+ $19) 17... Qxb4 18. Rc1 Nb3 $17) 11... Nc5 12. Be3 Qa5 13. Qc2 O-O 14. Rc1 $2 (14. a3 Ne4 (14... d4 15. Nxd4 Nxd4 16. Bxd4 Rxf4 17. O-O-O Bxa3 18. g3 $1 $16 (18. bxa3 Qxa3+ 19. Qb2 Nb3+ $19)) 15. Rc1 Bxc3+ 16. bxc3 $13) 14... d4 $1 $17 {Shirov,A-Ivanchuk,V/Tilburg 1993}) 9... Bb4+ (9... Qh4+ {Polgar,Judit: '!?'} 10. Ng3 Bb4+ 11. Kf2 O-O+ 12. Nf3 Nc6 13. Be3 $14 (13. Kg1 Rxf3 $5 14. gxf3 Nxd4 15. f4 g5 16. Be3 Nc6 17. fxg5 Ndxe5 18. Qh5 Qxh5 19. Nxh5 Ng4 20. Bf2 e5 21. Be2 Nxf2 22. Nf6+ Kg7 23. Kxf2 Be6 24. Rad1 Rd8 25. h4 $13)) 10. Kf2 (10. Bd2 $2 Qh4+ $17) 10... O-O+ 11. Nf3 Nc6 12. a3 (12. Be3 $13) (12. Kg3 $5 Ne7 13. h3 Nf5+ 14. Kh2) 12... Ndxe5 $6 {This sacrifice,wich is typical for many variations in french defense now is not so strong that's why black should prefer simple Polgar,Judit: '!?'} (12... Ba5 13. Nf4 (13. h4 Qe7 14. Kg3 (14. g4 Ndxe5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Bg2 Nxg4+ $13) 14... Bc7 15. Kh3 Qf7 16. Nf4 Nf6 17. Bd3 Ne4 18. Rf1 $14) 13... Qe7 14. h4 $6 Bb6 $1 15. Kg3 (15. Be3 Ndxe5 $1 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. dxe5 Rxf4+ $19) 15... g5 16. hxg5 Nxd4 $1 17. Nxd4 Qxg5+ $40 {in all the cases with complicated struggle.}) 13. axb4 (13. dxe5 Bc5+ 14. Ke1 Nxe5 $44 15. Nxe5 $140 Bf2+ 16. Kd2 Qg5+ 17. Kc2 Qxe5) 13... Qh4+ 14. Kg1 $6 {For some reason white decides to give up a pawn on f3,which is very important one.Better was} (14. Ng3 $5 Nxd4 15. Be2 (15. Ra3 Nexf3 16. gxf3 e5 $44) 15... Nexf3 16. gxf3 e5 17. Be3 $16) 14... Nxf3+ (14... Rxf3 15. gxf3 (15. g3 Qe4 (15... Qd8 16. dxe5 Qb6+ 17. Kg2 Rf2+ 18. Kh3 Nxe5) 16. dxe5 Rd3 17. Qa4 Rf3) 15... Nxf3+ 16. Kg2 Ne1+ $11) 15. gxf3 Rxf3 16. Ng3 Nxd4 17. Bg2 {Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (17. Ra3 $5 Rf7 18. Bg5 Qxg5 19. Qxd4 $13) 17... Rf7 $6 {Missing a chanse to get strong counterplay after} (17... Ne2+ $1 18. Qxe2 Qd4+ 19. Be3 Qxe3+ (19... Rxe3 20. Qf2 Rd3 $13 (20... Bd7 $5 21. Ne2 Qb6 22. Ra3 Rxa3 23. bxa3 Qc7) 21. Qxd4 Rxd4 22. b5 Rb4 23. Ra2 Rxb5 24. Kf2 $44) 20. Qxe3 Rxe3 21. Kf2 Rb3 $132) 18. Be3 $14 {Despite of material balance white has muh better chanse,mainly because of paralised queenside of black.} Nf5 $6 (18... Nc6 19. b5 Ne5 20. Bd4 Nc4 21. b3 Nd6 (21... Rf4 22. Ne2 $18) 22. b6 a6 23. Be5 $14) (18... Nb5 $5) 19. Nxf5 Rxf5 20. b5 $1 {[%cal Ga1a4,Ga4g4] Polgar,Judit: ''} Bd7 21. b6 a6 (21... Bc6 22. Qd4) 22. Qd4 Qh5 (22... Qxd4 23. Bxd4 Raf8 (23... Rc8 24. h3 Rc2 25. Rh2) 24. Re1 Rf4 25. Be3 R4f5 26. h4 Bc6 27. Bh3 R5f6 28. Bg5 $16) 23. h3 $1 Bc6 24. Kh2 e5 25. Qg4 Rd8 {Polgar,Judit: '?'} ({Deserved attention} 25... Qf7 26. Rhf1 Rf8 27. Rxf5 Qxf5 28. Qxf5 Rxf5 29. Ra5 $1 e4 30. Rc5 Rf6 31. Bd4 Re6 32. Kg1 $14 {and it's not so easy for white to breakthrough.}) (25... d4 26. Qxh5 Rxh5 27. Bxc6 bxc6 28. Bd2 (28. Bf2 c5 29. Rhe1 Rh6 30. Rxe5 Rxb6 31. Ra2 Rc8) 28... e4 29. Ra5) 26. Qxh5 Rxh5 27. Rhf1 g6 $6 (27... e4 $5) 28. Bf3 $1 {Now the bishop makes hs way to e6 with decisive effect.} Rf5 29. Bg4 $1 Rxf1 30. Rxf1 Kg7 (30... Re8 31. Bh6) 31. Be6 $1 $18 Be8 (31... Rf8 32. Bh6+ Kxh6 33. Rxf8 $18) 32. Bc5 1-0

