1. e4 {Nor,I Nor Gershon} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be2 e5 7. Nb3 Be7 8. O-O O-O 9. Kh1 b6 $6 {[!] After the game Shirov-Gelfand everybody plays 9.Kh1! 9...b6 can't be a good chessmove,but it is a smart decision! Gelfand wants to see how deep Polgar understands this position without theory.} 10. Be3 $6 {After this move white will not be better.If 10.f4 is the main move after 9...b5,it sertently is after 9...b6.} (10. a4 $6 Nbd7 11. Bc4 $6 Bb7 12. Qe2 Nxe4 $6 13. Nxe4 d5 14. Bd3 dxe4 15. Bxe4 Bxe4 16. Qxe4 f5 17. Qc4+ Kh8 18. Rd1 Qe8 19. c3 Rd8 20. Re1 f4 21. Nd2 $6 Nc5 22. Ne4 $2 Nd3 23. Rf1 f3 $1 24. Qe6 fxg2+ 25. Kxg2 Qh5 $19 {0-1 Ivanov,A-Vera,R/Cienfuegos 1980 (28)}) (10. Nd5 $6 Nxd5 (10... Nxe4 $2 11. Bf3 f5 (11... Bf5 12. Qe2 $18) 12. Nxe7+ Qxe7 13. Bxe4 fxe4 14. Qd5+ $18) 11. Qxd5 Qc7 $1 $132 12. Qxa8 $140 $2 Bb7 13. Qa7 Nc6) (10. f4 $5 Bb7 11. Bf3 $5 $14 (11. fxe5 $6 dxe5 (11... Nxe4 12. Nxe4 Bxe4 13. Bf3 Bxf3 14. Qxf3 Nd7 15. exd6 Bxd6 $11) 12. Bd3 Nc6 $1 $13 (12... Nbd7 $6 13. Bg5 $36))) 10... Bb7 11. Nd5 $6 {White continues her plan - playing on the queen flank.Good plan... in other positions!She had to stop and play more carefully [11.f3!?].} (11. f3 $5 Nbd7 12. a4 (12. Qd2 Rc8 13. Rfd1 Qc7 14. Rac1 Rfd8 $13 {1-0 Francis Vasquez-Abdullah Ali Mahmoud/Ch World cadets unde 1993 (35)}) 12... Qc7 13. Rf2 $5 h6 14. Bf1 Rfc8 $6 15. Nc1 Nc5 16. N1a2 $5 a5 $2 17. Rd2 Ne8 18. Nb5 Qc6 19. Nac3 $16 {1-0 Solozhenkin,E-Saulin,D/RUS-ch Elista 1995 (40)}) 11... Nxd5 (11... Nxe4 $2 12. Nxb6 Ra7 13. Nd7 Nxd7 14. Bxa7 $18) 12. exd5 Bg5 $1 $15 13. Qd2 $6 (13. Bd3 $142 $5 Bxe3 (13... f5 $2 14. f4 $1 $14) 14. fxe3 Qh4 15. e4 {It is better then in game.}) 13... Bxe3 14. fxe3 Qh4 $6 (14... f5 $142 $5 15. Bd3 $5 g6 (15... Qg5 $6 16. e4 f4 17. Qb4 $1 Qd8 18. Na5 Bxd5 $140 19. Bc4 Bxc4 20. Nxc4 $14) 16. e4 $140 f4 $15) (14... Nd7 15. Bd3 Nc5 16. Nxc5 $140 dxc5 $6 (16... bxc5 $142) 17. d6 $1 (17. c4 $2 Qd6 $17) 17... e4 18. Bc4 $14) 15. Bd3 $5 Nd7 16. e4 a5 $6 {Black's position should be better,but it is not easy to use this "better"! Gelfand sees it and starts worrying.} 17. Qe3 $1 { Nb3-d2-c4} f5 $6 {Too early.} 18. exf5 $2 (18. Bb5 $1 f4 (18... Nc5 $6 19. Nxc5 bxc5 20. exf5 Bxd5 21. Rad1 {And white is not worse.}) 19. Qe1 $1 (19. Qg1 Nc5 20. Nxc5 bxc5 $17) 19... Qxe1 20. Raxe1 Nf6 21. Nd2 $1 Rac8 $8 22. Nc4 (22. Bd3 $6 Nd7 23. Nc4 Rf6 $17) 22... Nxe4 (22... Rfd8 $6 23. b3 $1 $16) 23. Nxb6 (23. Rxe4 $2 Bxd5) 23... Rc5 24. c4 Nf6 $13) 18... Bxd5 $15 19. Rad1 Rf6 $1 20. Kg1 (20. Bb5 $143 $6 Rh6 21. h3 $6 (21. Qg1 Nf6 $40) 21... Nf6 $1 $40 (21... Qxh3+ $2 22. Qxh3 Rxh3+ 23. Kg1 $18)) 20... Rh6 21. Qg3 (21. h3 $143 $6 a4 22. Nc1 Bc6 23. c4 Nc5 $17) 21... Bc6 $2 (21... Qxg3 $142 22. hxg3 a4 23. Nc1 Nc5 $17) 22. Qxh4 Rxh4 23. g3 $1 Rh6 $6 (23... Ra4 $5 {Was black's last chance.}) 24. Bc4+ Kf8 (24... Kh8 $6 25. Be6 $1 $16) 25. f6 $1 $11 {Understanding=Fighting} Rxf6 26. Rxd6 Rc8 27. c3 Rxf1+ 28. Kxf1 Nf6 29. Nd2 b5 30. Be6 Ke7 31. Bxc8 Kxd6 32. Ke2 g6 1/2-1/2

