{ChessCalisthenics: 'C18: French: 3 Nc3 Bb4: Main line: 7 h4 and 7 Qg4'} {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'A wonderful game which shows how Black can blow his opponent away in a seemingly solid position. '} 1. e4 {Ftacnik,L Moskalenko,Viktor Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir ChessCalisthenics Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'ChessCalisthenics Ftacnik'} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 Kf8 (7... O-O 8. Nf3 Nbc6 9. Bd3) 8. Bd3 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'This pseudo-active bishop placement is quite wrong in many sub-Winawer lines.'} Qa5 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '!' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'Once again using Black's most important motif in the Winawer system.'} 9. Bd2 Qa4 10. c4 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'Trying to open up the game.'} ({Moskalenko,Viktor: 'After'} 10. Kd1 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '?!' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'White lost almost all the games.'} b6 $5 {Moskalenko,Viktor}) ({Moskalenko,Viktor: 'It was the same story with'} 10. Ra2 Nbc6 (10... b6 $5 {Moskalenko,Viktor} 11. Nf3 Ba6 12. O-O h6 $5 13. h3 Nd7 14. Bxa6 Qxa6 15. a4 Kg8 16. Rfa1 Nc6 17. Be3 Rc8 18. Rb1 Ne7 19. a5 Kh7 20. Bd2 Rhe8 21. Rba1 b5 22. Rb1 Rb8 23. Qh5 Rf8 24. Rab2 Rb7 25. dxc5 Nxc5 26. Nd4 Nc6 27. Be3 Ne4 28. c4 Nxd4 29. Bxd4 Nd2 30. cxb5 Qxa5 31. Rd1 Rfb8 32. Kh2 Nc4 33. Rb3 Qc7 34. Ra1 Rxb5 35. Rxa7 R5b7 36. Raxb7 Rxb7 37. Rg3 Rb1 {0-1 (37) Totorat,U (2208)-Dos Santos,M (2275) LSS email 2011})) (10. Nf3 {ChessCalisthenics} Nbc6 11. Qh5 h6 12. O-O (12. dxc5 Qa5 13. O-O Qxc5 14. Rfb1 Qa5 15. c4 Qc7 16. cxd5 Nxd5 17. c4 Nde7 18. Bb4 Nxb4 19. axb4 Bd7 20. Nd4 Rd8 21. Qe2 a6 22. Rd1 Nc6 23. Nxc6 Bxc6 24. Qe3 g6 25. Be4 Rxd1+ 26. Rxd1 Qxe5 {Hasan,M (2307)-Drozdovskij,Y (2562)/New Delhi 2007/CBM 116 ext/0-1 (34)}) 12... c4 13. Be2 Qxc2 14. Bd1 Qg6 15. Qh3 Bd7 16. Rc1 f5 17. exf6 gxf6 18. Bc2 Qg7 19. Rce1 h5 20. Rxe6 Bxe6 21. Qxe6 Qf7 22. Qd7 Ng6 23. Qd6+ Kg7 24. Qg3 Rag8 {Sutovsky, E (2624)-Drozdovskij,Y (2509)/playchess.com INT 2006/EXT 2007/1-0 (39)}) (10. Qd1 {Moskalenko,Viktor} b6 $5 11. Nf3 Ba6 {transposes to the next Games 10}) ({A curious line is} 10. Qh5 {Moskalenko,Viktor} c4 11. Bxh7 Qe8 12. Qh3 Ng6 13. Bg5 Qd7 14. Nf3 Ke8 15. Bc1 Nf8 16. Ng5 Qe7 17. a4 Kd7 18. Qh5 Nxh7 {½-½ (18) Keuter,K (2494)-Galanov,S (2536) ICCF 2014}) 10... dxc4 {ChessCalisthenics: 'N'} (10... Bd7 {ChessCalisthenics} 11. dxc5 Bc6 12. Ne2 Nd7 13. Nc3 Nxe5 14. Qe2 Nxd3+ 15. cxd3 Qb3 16. O-O dxc4 17. dxc4 Qc2 18. Rac1 Qg6 19. f3 h5 20. Nb5 h4 21. Bf4 Nf5 22. h3 Ng3 23. Bxg3 Qxg3 24. f4 Rh5 25. Nd6 {Apicella,M (2560)-Legky,N (2540)/France 1996/CBM 055 ext/0-1 (47)}) 11. dxc5 Bd7 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '!?'} (11... Nd7 $5 {Moskalenko,Viktor} 12. Ne2 Nxe5 $1 (12... Nxc5 13. Bxc4 b6 $11 {Corrales Jimenez,F (2599)-Barria Zuniga,D (2419) Parla 2010}) 13. Qd4 Nxd3+ 14. cxd3 f6 $15) 12. Be2 $6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Ftacnik: '?!''' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'White does not worry too much about the pawns.'} (12. Qxc4 {Moskalenko,Viktor: ''} Qxc4 13. Bxc4 Bc6 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'and ...d7'} 14. Nf3 Nd7 15. O-O Bxf3 16. gxf3 Nxe5 17. Be2 $13) 12... Bc6 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '!' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'And Black won in 31 moves.'} 13. f4 (13. Nf3 $2 c3 $1 14. Bf4 (14. Qxa4 cxd2+ $19) 14... Ng6 15. g3 Nd7 $17) (13. c3 {ChessCalisthenics} Nd7 14. Nf3 Nxc5 $11) 13... h5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Ftacnik: '!'''} 14. Qg3 (14. Qg5 Nd7 15. Nf3 Nf5 { f6}) (14. Qh3 c3 15. Bxc3 Qxf4 $17) 14... h4 15. Qg4 Qxc2 16. Rc1 Qf5 17. Kf2 (17. Qxf5 Nxf5 18. Nf3 (18. Kf2 Ng3 $1 19. hxg3 hxg3+ 20. Kxg3 Rxh1 $19) 18... h3 $1 19. g3 Nd4 20. Kf2 Nxe2 21. Kxe2 Bd5 $17) 17... Qxg4 18. Bxg4 Bd5 19. Be2 Nd7 20. Bxc4 Nxc5 21. Bxd5 $6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Ftacnik: '?!'''} (21. Nf3 Rc8 22. Be2 $17) 21... Nd3+ 22. Ke3 Nxc1 23. Be4 Nb3 24. Bb4 Rc8 25. Nf3 Nc5 26. Rd1 (26. Rc1 b6) 26... Ke8 27. Nd4 (27. Bxc5 $5 {ChessCalisthenics} Rxc5 28. Nd4 $19) 27... Nxe4 28. Kxe4 a6 29. Bxe7 Kxe7 30. Rb1 b5 31. a4 (31. f5 $19 {ChessCalisthenics}) 31... Rc4 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'Later, in 1997 in a game between the same players, White opted for 8.d2!? - see line in Game2.'} (31... Rc4 32. axb5 Rd8 $19) 0-1

