itions}) 11... O-O 12. Be3 $14) ({More natural, and an attempt to justify the (temporary) omission of a6 is} 10... Qc7 $5 11. Be3 (11. Ndb5 {gives Black a choice between} Qb8 {and} (11... Qc6 $5 $13 {Stohl: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I''})) (11. b3 {Stohl: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I''} Rc8 $5 12. Bb2 O-O 13. Rc1 Qb8 14. Rc2 Rfe8 15. Rd2 a6 16. f4 Bf8 17. Bf3 h6 18. h4 h5 $1 19. Bxh5 Nxh5 20. Qxh5 Nf6 21. Qd1 b5 $44 {Ruck,R-Prusikhin,M/Griesheim/2003/}) 11... Rc8 12. Rc1 Qb8 13. b3 Nc5 {Stohl: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I''} (13... O-O {(Stohl) ChessCalisthenics} 14. f4 a6 15. g4 Qa8 16. Bf2 g6 17. g5 Nh5 18. Qg4 Rc7 19. h4 Qc8 20. f5 Ne5 21. Qd1 b5 22. f6 Bd8 23. Nf3 Ng4 24. Bb6 Rxc4 25. Bxd8 Qc5+ {Van Wely,L (2681)-Shipov,S (2588)/chessassistantclub.com INT 2004/CBM 104 ext/0-1}) 14. f4 $5 (14. f3 a6 15. Bf2 O-O 16. f4 Qa8 17. Qe2 Rfe8 18. g4 g6 19. f5 $6 exf5 20. gxf5 Bf8 21. fxg6 hxg6 22. Nd5 Bxd5 23. cxd5 Nfxe4 $17 {Garcia Paolicchi,R-Marin,M/Andorra la Vella/2002/}) 14... Ncxe4 15. Nxe4 Bxe4 16. Bxe4 Nxe4 17. f5 e5 18. Qg4 Qb7 19. Nb5 g6 20. Qf3 gxf5 21. Qxf5 a6 22. Nd4 $44 {Cacho Reigadas,S-Suba,M/ESP-chT/2001/}) 11. b3 $6 $146 {Stohl: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I: 'N?!''' Too soft, but one has to realize this is a 5 minute game. Stohl: 'Too soft, but one has to realize this is a 5 minute game. ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I: 'Too soft, but one has to realize this is a 5 minute game.'''} (11. f4 {Stohl: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I''} O-O 12. Ndb5 a6 13. Nxd6 Bxd6 14. Qxd6 Nc5 15. Qxd8 Rfxd8 16. e5 Bxg2 17. Kxg2 Ne8 18. Be3 $16 {Christiansen,L-Wallace,J/Internet/2001/}) (11. Ndb5 $1 {Stohl: 'ChessCalisthenics: 'Stohl,I''} Ne5 (11... O-O 12. Nxa7 Qc7 13. b3 $16) 12. Nxa7 O-O 13. b3 $16 {and White seems to have a healthy extra .}) 11... a6 12. Bb2 O-O 13. h3 Qc7 {Now despite Black's 10...b8 we have a normal Hedgehog position with a full board of pieces and the typical possibilities for both sides. Ponomariov doesn't have too much experience with the White side 