6 $16) (23. Qe3 c5 (23... Bh6 24. Bf4 (24. Qxh6 Qxe5 25. Qg5+ Qxg5+ 26. hxg5 $14) 24... Bg7 (24... Bxf4 25. Qxf4 c5 (25... Bf5 26. Bf1 Qa5 27. Qg5+ Kf8 28. Bd3 $18) 26. Qg5+ Kf8 (26... Kh8 27. Re1 $18) (26... Kh7) 27. Nxc5 $1 Qxc5 (27... Rxc5 28. Rd8+ Ne8 29. Qh6+ Kg8 30. Be4 Bf5 31. a4 $18) 28. Rd8+ Ne8 29. Qh6+ Kg8 30. Be4 Bf5 (30... Qe5 31. Bh7+ Kh8 32. Rxc8 Bxc8 33. Bg6+) 31. Qg5+ Kf8 32. Bxf5 $18) 25. c4 Qb4 (25... Bxc4 26. Nb6 $18) (25... Qf5 26. Nc5 $16) 26. Qc5 $16) 24. c4 $5 (24. Nc3 Qb4 25. Kb2 $14) 24... Qb4 (24... Qa5 25. Bc3 Qc7 26. Qg5 $16) 25. Qc3 $14 Qa3+ $140 26. Qb2 Qb4 27. a3 Qa5 28. Qc3) (23. Qe1 Bh6+ (23... c5 24. c4 Bh6+ (24... Bxc4 $2 25. Nc3) 25. Kc2 Bf5+ 26. Kb2 Qe8 27. Bb7 $16) 24. Kb1 c5 25. Nc3 $14) 23... Bc4 $1 24. Qxc4 (24. Qe1 Bxf1 25. Bxf6 Bxf6 26. Qxf1 e6 $15) 24... Qxe5 25. c3 (25. Qxa6 Qa1+ 26. Kd2 Rd8+ 27. Bd3 Ne4+ 28. Ke1 Qe5 $17) (25. Qc3 Qf5 (25... Qc7 26. Bxa6 Ra8 27. Bb5) 26. Bxa6 Rb8 27. Qxc6 Qxf2 28. Qc7 $13) 25... Qf5 26. Qc5 (26. Qxa6 Bh6+ 27. f4 gxf3+ 28. Kb2 Rc7 29. Qd3 Qxd3 30. Rxd3 f2 $15) 26... Qf3 27. Bd3 Bh6+ 28. Kc2 Ne4 29. Qe5 $2 {The centralization of the strongest piece is not necessarily always the best move, much more promising was 29.xh5!} (29. Qxh5 $1 Qxf2+ (29... Nxf2 30. Nb2 Nxd1 31. Qxh6 Ne3+ 32. Kc1 Nf5 33. Qg5+ Ng7 34. Qh6 $11) 30. Kb1 Qf3 31. Bc2 Bg7 32. Rd3 Qe2 33. Qa5 Rf8 34. Kb2 $13) 29... Nxf2 (29... Qxf2+ $5 30. Kb1 Qf3 31. Bc2 Nxg3 32. Qxe7 Rf8 $17) 30. Be2 Qg2 (30... Nxd1 31. Bxf3 Ne3+ 32. Kb2 gxf3 33. Qxh5 f2 34. Qxh6 f1=Q (34... Nd1+ 35. Kc2 f1=Q 36. Qg5+ Kf8 37. Qh6+ Ke8 38. Qh8+ Kd7 39. Nb6+ $16) 35. Qxe3 Qg2+ 36. Ka3 $11) 31. Re1 (31. Bf1 Qh2 32. Re1 Nh1+ 33. Kb1 Nxg3 $17) 31... Rd8 32. Qxe7 (32. Bf1 Rd2+ 33. Kb1 Qd5 34. Qxd5 cxd5 35. Bxa6 Ne4 $19) 32... Rd2+ 33. Kb1 Qd5 34. Ka1 (34. Nb2 Rxb2+ 35. Kxb2 Qd2+ 36. Ka3 Bf8 $19) (34. Bc4 Rd1+ 35. Kb2 Bc1+ 36. Kc2 Qd2+ 37. Kb1 Ba3+ 38. Rxd1 Qxd1#) 34... Ne4 {The FIDE world champion is in real trouble, as black pieces are clearly dominating the board.} 35. Qe8+ Kg7 36. Nb2 (36. Bxg4 hxg4 37. Qxe4 Rd1+ 38. Kb2 Bc1+ 39. Kc2 (39. Ka1 Be3+ 40. Kb2 Rd2+ 41. Ka3 Qxe4 $19) 39... Qd2+ 40. Kb1 Ba3+ 41. Rxd1 Qxd1#) 36... Rxb2 (36... Nd6 37. Bc4 Nxe8 38. Bxd5 cxd5 39. Rxe8 Rg2 40. Na4 Rxg3 $19) 37. Kxb2 (37. Bc4 $1 Rxa2+ 38. Kxa2 Qa5+ (38... Nxc3+ 39. Kb2 Qd2+ 40. Ka3 Nb5+ 41. Bxb5 axb5 42. Qe2 Qd6+ 43. Ka2 Qxg3 $17) 39. Kb2 (39. Kb1 Nxc3+ 40. Kc2 Qa2+ 41. Kxc3 Qd2#) 39... Qxc3+ 40. Ka2 Qa5+ 41. Kb2 Qd2+ 42. Ka3 Nd6 43. Qe2 Nxc4+ 44. bxc4 Qc3+ 45. Ka2 Kg8 $17) 37... Qd2+ 38. Ka3 Nf6 $1 {Ponomariov,Ruslan; Komarov,D: '0-1 (38) Ponomariov,R (2743)-Polgar,J (2685) Benidorm 2002 CBM 93 [Ftacnik]'} (38... Nf6 $1 39. Rd1 Qxd1 40. Bxd1 Nxe8 $19) 0-1

