{ChessCalisthenics: 'E71: King's Indian: 4 e4 d6 5 h3'} 1. d4 {ChessCalisthenics} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. h3 O-O 6. Bg5 Na6 7. f4 {ChessCalisthenics: 'N'} (7. Nge2 {ChessCalisthenics} e5 (7... Qe8 8. Ng3 e5 9. d5 h5 10. Be2 Nh7 11. Be3 h4 12. Nf1 f5 13. a3 Nc5 14. Nd2 Bd7 15. Qc2 Na4 16. Ndb1 a6 17. Nxa4 Bxa4 18. b3 Bd7 19. Nc3 Qe7 20. Qc1 Rae8 21. Ra2 Bf6 22. O-O {Van Wely,L (2635) -Damljanovic,B (2555)/Elista 1998/CBM 066 ext/0-1 (50)}) 8. d5 c6 9. g4 cxd5 10. cxd5 Bd7 11. Ng3 Qb6 12. Qd2 Rfc8 13. Be2 Qd4 14. Be3 Qxd2+ 15. Kxd2 Nc5 16. b4 Na4 17. Nb5 a5 18. a3 Ne8 19. Rhc1 Bf6 20. Rxc8 Rxc8 21. Rc1 Rxc1 {Gyimesi,Z (2571)-Beliavsky,A (2638)/Ohrid 2001/CBM 084/1/2-1/2 (31)}) 7... Nh5 $6 {This move seems to be too risky. Black wants to fight against the weaknesses on f4 and g3, but loses time, and his  may get trouble.} (7... Qe8 {is the theoretical continuation preparing for the standard push e7-e5.} 8. Nf3 (8. e5 Nh5 {is already not the same!}) 8... e5 $1 {This nice move is well-known also from the 4  Attack!} 9. fxe5 dxe5 10. Nxe5 c5 $1 {blowing up White's mighty .}) 8. Nge2 h6 9. Bh4 f5 {This is again an original idea, but it is not in the spirit of the position.} (9... c5 $142 $5 {ChessCalisthenics} 10. d5 Bxc3+ 11. bxc3 Nf6 $11) 10. exf5 {ChessCalisthenics: ''} gxf5 11. g3 {Completing the development with the  fianchetto. Suddenly all white pieces work together harmoniously.} Qe8 { e5} 12. Bg2 e5 13. dxe5 {This gives up the tension in the  a bit.} (13. O-O exd4 (13... exf4 14. Nxf4 Qe3+ 15. Kh2) 14. Nd5 c5 15. Re1 {was an interesting option.}) 13... dxe5 14. fxe5 Qxe5 15. Qd5+ Qxd5 16. Bxd5+ (16. Nxd5 {looks more agressive, for example:} Bxb2 17. Rb1 Bg7 18. Ne7+ Kh7 19. Nxc8 Raxc8 20. Bxb7 Rb8 21. O-O Nc5 22. Bf3 $14) (16. cxd5 $6 {ChessCalisthenics} f4 17. O-O fxg3 $11) 16... Kh7 17. Bf3 Nf6 18. O-O-O Nc5 19. Nf4 Nfe4 20. Be7 Re8 21. Ncd5 Be5 22. Rhe1 c6 23. Bxc5 cxd5 24. Rxd5 Bxf4+ 25. gxf4 Be6 26. Re5 Bxc4 ({White can still continue the game after} 26... Bxc4 27. Rxe8 Rxe8 28. b3 Bd5 29. Kb2 $14 {}) 1/2-1/2

