1. e4 {Postny,E} c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nc3 Qc7 6. Be3 a6 7. Qd2 Nf6 8. O-O-O Bb4 9. f3 Ne5 10. Nb3 b5 11. Qe1 Be7 12. f4 Nc4 13. e5 Ng4 (13... Nxe3 $2 14. Qxe3 $16) 14. Bd4 Bb7 {Judit Polgar had this position twice in the same tournament.} (14... f5 $6 15. h3 Nh6 16. Qf2 {[%csl Rh6] It is important to control the diagonal g1-a7.} Bb7 17. Bxc4 $1 bxc4 18. Bb6 Qc6 19. Na5 Qxg2 20. Qd4 $1 Bc8 21. Bc5 Bxc5 22. Qxc5 $18 {1-0 Grischuk,A (2719)-Geller,J (2489)/Sochi 2004/CBM 101 (27)}) (14... Nh6 15. Qf2 Nf5 (15... Bb7 16. Bxc4 bxc4 17. Bb6 Qc8 18. Na5 $14) 16. Bxc4 Qxc4 17. Na5 Qc7 18. Bb6 Qb8 19. g4 $16) (14... O-O 15. h3 Nh6 16. g4 f6 (16... Bb7 17. Rg1 d6 18. Bxc4 bxc4 19. Nd2 $14) 17. exf6 Bxf6 18. Bxf6 Qxf4+ 19. Nd2 Qxf6 20. Bxc4 bxc4 21. Rf1 Qd8 22. Nxc4 $14) 15. Bxc4 (15. Rg1 d6 16. exd6 Bxd6 17. g3 O-O $11 {½-½ Motylev,A (2640)-Makarov,M (2530)/Sochi 2004/EXT 2005 (44)}) (15. Qg3 h5 16. Bd3 (16. h3 Nh6 17. Qxg7 $6 O-O-O {[%csl Rg7][%cal Gd8g8]} 18. Qg3 $8 d6 $1 19. exd6 Bxd6 $15 {[%csl Rf4]}) 16... d6 17. h3 dxe5 18. fxe5 Nh6 19. Kb1 (19. Qxg7 $6 O-O-O 20. Qg3 Rhg8 $15 {[%csl Rg2]}) 19... g6 20. Qf2 Nf5 $11 {1-0 Vokarev,S (2529)-Geller,J (2484)/Alushta 2004/CBM 102 ext (35)}) (15. Kb1 O-O 16. Ne4 Nce3 $1 17. Bxe3 Bxe4 18. Bd3 Bxd3 19. Rxd3 Rac8 $11 {1-0 Najer,E (2663)-Polgar,J (2687)/Netanya 2009/CBM 131 Extra (78)}) 15... bxc4 (15... Qxc4 $2 16. Na5 Qc7 17. Nxb7 Qxb7 18. h3 Nh6 19. g4 $16) 16. Nd2 Nh6 (16... d5 $5 {This is a possible improvement for Black.} 17. exd6 Qxd6 18. Bxg7 (18. Nxc4 Qxf4+ 19. Kb1 O-O 20. Qe2 Rad8 21. Rhf1 Qg5 22. h3 Nf6 $13) 18... Rg8 19. Be5 Nxe5 20. fxe5 Qd4 21. Rg1 O-O-O {Black has sufficient compensation for the pawn thanks to the pair of powerful bishops.}) 17. Qe2 Rc8 (17... Nf5 18. Nxc4 ({The following line illustrates well the potential of the pair of bishops:} 18. Qxc4 $6 Qxc4 19. Nxc4 Bxg2 20. Rhe1 Bh4 $1 21. Rg1 Bf3 22. Rd2 Nxd4 23. Rf1 (23. Nd6+ Kf8 24. Rf1 f5 25. Rxd4 Bg2 26. Rfd1 g5 $15) 23... Nb5 24. Rxf3 Nxc3 25. bxc3 (25. Rxc3 $2 Be1 $19) 25... Be7 $15) 18... Rc8 19. b3 Qc6 20. Rhg1 $14) 18. Nde4 Nf5 (18... O-O 19. g4 $14) 19. g4 Nxd4 20. Rxd4 $14 O-O (20... f6 21. Rhd1 fxe5 22. Rxd7 Qxd7 23. Rxd7 Kxd7 24. fxe5 $36 {[%csl Rd7] 1-0 Volokitin,A (2685)-Macieja,B (2618)/Bermuda 2005/CBM 106 (44)}) 21. g5 Bxe4 22. Nxe4 Qa5 23. Kb1 c3 24. Rhd1 Rb8 25. b3 Rfc8 26. Qd3 Bb4 27. Rc4 Rxc4 28. Qxc4 d5 29. exd6 Qa3 30. Nxc3 Bxd6 31. Ne4 Bf8 32. Rd7 Qa5 33. a4 Qe1+ 34. Ka2 Rb4 35. Qc8 Rxe4 36. Rb7 Qc1 37. b4 Re3 0-1

