1. e4 {Sutovsky,E Sutovsky Van Wely,Loek Boensch Sutovsky: 'Sutovsky,E Boensch'} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be2 e6 7. f4 (7. O-O {Van Wely,Loek} Be7 8. f4 O-O {1-0 (22) Sutovsky,E (2565)-Polgar,J (2665) Tilburg 68/(212) 1996 CI1-130 [Van Wely,Loek]}) 7... Be7 8. Be3 O-O 9. O-O Qc7 $6 {Once again!I didn't expect this move from Judith just two rounds after my victory over L.Van Wely.I understood that black prepared something,but believing in my own analysis,I played: Sutovsky: 'Once again!I didn't expect this move from Judith just two rounds after my victory over L.Van Wely.I understood that black prepared something,but believing in my own analysis,I played: Sutovsky,E: 'Once again! I didn't expect this move from Judith just two rounds after my victory over L. Van Wely. I understood that black prepared something, but believing in my own analysis, I played:''} 10. g4 $1 Nc6 $5 {Intereseting attempt.Other moves-10...Re8,10...d5,10...b5 I analized in commentaries to the game E.Sutovsky-L.Van Wely,Tilburg,1996 ,which you could see earlier,so this time I won't analize these moves. Sutovsky: 'Intereseting attempt.Other moves-10...Re8,10...d5,10...b5 I analized in commentaries to the game E.Sutovsky-L.Van Wely,Tilburg,1996 ,which you could see earlier,so this time I won't analize these moves. Sutovsky,E: 'Interesting attempt. Other moves - 10...Re8, 10...d5, 10...b5 - I analysed in commentaries to the game E.Sutovsky-L.Van Wely, Tilburg 1996, which you could see earlier, so this time I won't analyse these moves.''} (10... b5 {Boensch} 11. g5 Nfd7 12. Bd3 $1 Re8 13. Qh5 g6 14. Qh4 b4 15. Nce2 Bb7 $2 16. Rf3 h5 17. Ng3 Bf8 18. Nxh5 $1 $18 {1-0 Sutovskij,E-Van Wely,L/Tilburg Fontys 1996 (23) -CBM 56}) (10... Re8 {Boensch} 11. f5 Bf8 12. g5 Nfd7 13. Nxe6 $3 $16 {1-0 Shirov,A-Polgar,J/Tilburg Fontys 1996 (29) -CBM 56}) (10... d5 $5 {Boensch} 11. exd5 $1 Nxd5 12. Nxd5 exd5 13. Bf3 Rd8 14. Qd2 $14 {Sax,G-Eising/GER/1972/}) 11. g5 Nd7 12. f5 {White has to play f4-f5 immediately,otherwise black solves all his problems;for example: Sutovsky: 'White has to play f4-f5 immediately,otherwise black solves all his problems;for example: Sutovsky,E: 'White has to play f4-f5 immediately, otherwise black solves all his problems; for example:''} (12. Bd3 Nxd4 13. Bxd4 e5 14. Nd5 (14. Be3 exf4 15. Nd5 (15. Bxf4 $2 Bxg5 $1 16. Bxg5 Qc5+ 17. Kh1 Qxg5 $17) 15... Qd8 16. Bxf4 Ne5 {and black hasn't any problems.}) 14... Qd8 15. Nxe7+ (15. Be3 {Boensch} exf4 16. Bxf4 Ne5 (16... Bxg5 $4 17. Bxd6 Re8 18. Bc7 Be3+ 19. Kh1 Qg5 20. Qf3 $18) 17. Qd2 Be6 $15) 15... Qxe7 16. Be3 exf4 17. Bxf4 Ne5 {and black stands very good.}) 12... Nde5 {Another possible move is 12...Nd4,but on my opinion,white is better after that;let's see the games: Sutovsky: 'Another possible move is 12...Nd4,but on my opinion,white is better after that;let's see the games: Sutovsky,E: 'Another possible move is 12...Nd4, but in my opinion white is better after that; let's see the games:''} (12... Nxd4 13. Qxd4 Re8 (13... Rd8 $6 14. a4 Ne5 15. f6 Bf8 16. Qb6 Qxb6 17. Bxb6 Re8 18. Rad1 Bd7 19. Bc7 $16 {1-0 Ivanchuk,V-Hellers,F/Tilburg 1993 (44)}) 14. f6 $5 (14. fxe6 fxe6 15. Bh5 Rf8 (15... g6 16. Nd5 $1 exd5 17. Qxd5+ Kh8 18. Qf7 Qd8 19. Bxg6 (19. Bd4+ Ne5 20. Bxg6 $1 hxg6 21. Qxg6 $18) 19... hxg6 20. Qxg6 { f7  f1-f7} Ne5 21. Qh6+ Kg8 22. g6 $18 {N.Short}) 16. Rxf8+ Bxf8 17. Rf1 Ne5 (17... g6 18. Nd5 exd5 (18... Qc5 19. Rxf8+ Nxf8 20. Ne7+ Kf7 21. Qf6+) 19. Qxd5+ Kh8 20. Bd4+ {Short/}) 18. Nd5 Qd8 19. Nb6 Rb8 20. Bf4 Nc6 (20... Nd7 21. Nc4 d5 22. Kh1 Bc5 23. Qd2 Ra8 24. Bf7+ Kh8 25. exd5 b5 26. Na5 $16 {Short,N-Ljubojevic,L/Novi Sad(ol)/1990/1:0/43/} (26. Na5 {Boensch} Nf8 27. Be5 $1 $18 {1-0 Short,N-Ljubojevic,L/Novi Sad olm 1990 (42)})) (20... Bd7 21. Bxe5 (21. Nxd7 Nxd7 22. Bf7+ $2 Kxf7 23. Bxd6+ Kg8 24. Bxb8 Bc5 $19) 21... dxe5 22. Qxd7 Qxb6+ 23. Kh1 Qd6 24. Bf7+ Kh8 25. Bxe6 Qxd7 26. Bxd7 { f7  f1-f7} Be7 27. h4 Rf8 28. Rxf8+ Bxf8 29. Bc8 {Short/}) 21. Qf2 g6 (21... g6 22. Bg4 Bg7 23. c3 e5 24. Bxc8 exf4 25. Be6+ Kh8 26. h4 Nd4 27. cxd4 Qxb6 28. Rd1 Re8 29. Bd5 Rf8 30. b3 Qa7 31. Rd3 $16 {Lanka,Z-Vera,R/Luzern WchT(LAT-CUB)/1993/1:0/58/}) (21... e5 22. Be3 Be6 23. Bf7+ Bxf7 24. Qxf7+ Kh8 25. Nd7 $18 {Short})) (14. Rad1 Ne5 15. f6 Bf8 $2 (15... gxf6 16. gxf6 Bf8 17. Kh1 b5 18. Rg1+ Kh8 19. Rg3 Bb7 20. Rdg1 Ng6 21. h4 d5 22. h5 (22. e5 Bc5 $1 $19) 22... Bd6 $13) 16. fxg7 Bxg7 (16... Kxg7 17. Bh5 Kg8 18. Bf4 $1 $16) 17. Qxd6 Qxd6 18. Rxd6 $16 {Zagrebelny,S-Tratar,M/Ljubljana op 1994/0-1 (69)}) 14... Bf8 15. fxg7 Bxg7 16. Qd2 Ne5 17. Rad1 Rd8 18. a4 b6 19. Qe1 Rb8 20. Qg3 Qc6 21. Bd3 b5 22. axb5 axb5 23. Ne2 Nc4 24. Nd4 Qc7 25. Bxc4 Qxc4 26. Qh4 Bb7 27. b3 Qc5 28. Nf5 Qc3 29. Rd3 Qe5 30. g6 $1 $18 {Bologan,V-Ginsburg,G/Nikolaev(zt)/1993/1:0/37/}) 13. f6 Bd8 14. Bd3 $146 {[%cal Gd1h5] Novelty. Before,white played 14.fg,but black managed to defend his king and to get good counterplay,like it was in the next game: Sutovsky: 'Novelty. Before,white played 14.fg,but black managed to defend his king and to get good counterplay,like it was in the next game: Sutovsky,E: 'Novelty. Before white played 14.fg, but black managed to defend his king and to get good counterplay, like it was in the next game:''} (14. fxg7 {Van Wely,Loek: 'Ü 23/467'} Kxg7 (14... Re8 $6 {Boensch} 15. Qd2 b5 16. Bh5 Ne7 17. b3 N7g6 18. a4 $1 $14 {1-0 Kholmov,R-Spassky,B/Moscow zt 1964 (56)}) 15. Qd2 b5 16. g6 hxg6 17. Bh6+ Kg8 18. Bxf8 Kxf8 19. Nxc6 Qxc6 20. Bd3 Kg7 21. Ne2 Bb7 22. Nf4 Bb6+ 23. Kh1 Rh8 {and black has more than enough compensation for the exchange:Sax,G-Stean,J/Moscow/1976/0:1/36/ With the move 14.Bd3 white keeps the tension and preparing to continue the attack with Qd1-h5,but all this Sutovsky: 'and black has more than enough compensation for the exchange:Sax,G-Stean,J/Moscow/1976/0:1/36/ With the move 14.Bd3 white keeps the tension and preparing to continue the attack with Qd1-h5,but all this Sutovsky,E: 'and black has more than enough compensation for the exchange: Sax,G-Stean,J/Moscow/1976/0:1/36/ With the move 14.Bd3 white keeps the tension and preparing to continue the attack with Qd1-h5, but all this''}) 14... Nxd4 {Another idea was:14...gf 15.gf Kh8,but probably,it doesn't work: Sutovsky: 'Another idea was:14...gf 15.gf Kh8,but probably,it doesn't work: Sutovsky,E: 'Another idea was 14...gf 15.gf Kh8, but probably it doesn't work:''} (14... gxf6 15. gxf6 Kh8 (15... Nxd4 $5 16. Bxd4 Kh8 {will be analized later.}) (15... Qb6 {Boensch Dieser selbstmörderisch anmutende Zug stammt von "Herrn Fritz". Wie die nachstehenden Beispielvarianten zeigen,ist es mir nicht gelungen Schwarz matt zu setzen.} 16. Na4 (16. Kh1 Nxd4 17. Na4 Qc6 18. Bxd4 Ng6 (18... Kh8 $2 19. Bxe5 dxe5 20. Qh5 $18) 19. Qh5 Kh8 20. Nc3 (20. Rf3 e5 21. Rg1 exd4 22. Qh6 Rg8 23. Rg5 Bxf6 24. Rxf6 Be6 $17) 20... Bb6 21. Qh6 Rg8 $13) (16. Nf5 Qxb2 17. Na4 (17. Qe1 exf5 18. Rb1 Qa3 19. Rb3 Qa5 20. Qg3+ Ng4 21. exf5 h5 $17) 17... Qa3 18. Nh6+ Kh8 19. Nb6 Bxb6 20. Bxb6 $13) 16... Qa5 17. c3 (17. Qh5 Qxa4 (17... Kh8 $2 18. Nxc6 Rg8+ 19. Kh1 bxc6 20. Rg1 Rg6 21. Rxg6 Nxg6 22. Bg5 $1 $18) 18. Qh6 (18. Nxc6 Qxc6 19. Qh6 Bxf6 20. Qxf6 Ng4 $1 $13) 18... Bxf6 19. Qxf6 Ng4 $13) 17... Bd7 $13) 16. Bh6 Rg8+ (16... Re8 $2 17. Nxc6 bxc6 18. Qh5 Qb6+ 19. Kh1 Qxb2 20. Qg5 Ng6 21. Bg7+ Kg8 22. Qh6 Qxc3 23. Bh8 $18) 17. Bg7+ Rxg7+ 18. fxg7+ Kxg7 19. Nxc6 bxc6 20. Kh1 {and black hasn't enough compensation,due to his unsave king. Sutovsky: 'and black hasn't enough compensation,due to his unsave king. Sutovsky,E: 'and black hasn't enough compensation due to his unsave king.''}) 15. Bxd4 Qa5 $2 {Black made this move almost immediately,showing that it was prepared at home.But actually,it's a mistake!During the game,I expected 15...gf 16.gf Kh8;let's see the variations: Sutovsky: 'Black made this move almost immediately,showing that it was prepared at home.But actually,it's a mistake!During the game,I expected 15...gf 16.gf Kh8;let's see the variations: Sutovsky,E: 'Black made this move almost immediately,showing that it was prepared at home. But actually it's a mistake! During the game I expected 15...gf 16.gf Kh8; let's see the variations:''} (15... gxf6 {Van Wely,Loek: ''} 16. gxf6 Kh8 {Sutovsky: 'Sutovsky,E: 'will be analysed later.'' Sutovsky: 'will be analized later.'} 17. Kh1 Rg8 18. Bxe5 $1 {This knight was the best black defender,now white's attack became very strong;but also natural 18.Qh5 was strong: Sutovsky: 'This knight was the best black defender,now white's attack became very strong;but also natural 18.Qh5 was strong: Sutovsky,E: 'This knight was the best black defender, now white's attack became very strong; but also natural 18.Qh5 was strong:''} (18. Qh5 Nxd3 $5 (18... Rg6 19. Bxe5 $1 {-18.Be5} (19. Qh4 $6 Nxd3 $1 20. cxd3 e5 21. Be3 Be6 $13)) 19. cxd3 e5 (19... Rg6 20. Rg1 Bxf6 21. Rxg6 Bxd4 22. Rh6 f6 23. Ne2 $18) 20. Rg1 $1 Rg6 $8 21. Nd5 Qd7 22. Ne7 $1 Qe8 (22... Bxe7 23. Rxg6 fxg6 24. Qh6 {and mating on the next move.}) 23. Nxg6+ fxg6 24. Qh6 Qf7 25. Be3 $16) 18... dxe5 19. Qh5 Rg6 20. Qh4 Qb6 (20... Qc5 21. Rf3 Bb6 22. Rg3 $16) (20... b5 {Boensch} 21. Rf3 Qc5 22. Rh3 h6 23. Qxh6+ (23. b4 Qf8 (23... Qxb4 $4 24. Qxh6+ Rxh6 25. Rxh6+ Kg8 26. Rg1+ Kf8 27. Rh8#) 24. Rf1 Kh7 $13 25. Z0 Qh8 $140) 23... Rxh6 24. Rxh6+ Kg8 25. Rg1+ Qxg1+ 26. Kxg1 Bb7 $13) 21. Rf3 $1 Qxb2 22. Rb1 Qxc3 23. Rh3 h6 24. Qxh6+ $1 Rxh6 25. Rxh6+ Kg8 26. Rg1+ Kf8 27. Rh8#) 16. fxg7 Kxg7 {ATTACK} (16... Re8 17. Kh1 {and now 17...Bb6 is losing:} Bb6 18. Bxe5 Qxe5 19. Rxf7 $1 Kxf7 20. Qh5+ Kxg7 21. Rf1 $1 $18) 17. Kh1 $1 {Only this move was unexpected for black.After the game Judith told me that she analized only 17.Qh5.But the prophylactic move in the game is much stronger.White doesn't change the bishops,he wants to move out the knight Sutovsky: 'Only this move was unexpected for black.After the game Judith told me that she analized only 17.Qh5.But the prophylactic move in the game is much stronger.White doesn't change the bishops,he wants to move out the knight Sutovsky,E: 'Only this move was unexpected for black. After the game Judith told me that she analysed only 17.Qh5. But the prophylactic move in the game is much stronger. White doesn't change the bishops, he wants to move out the knight.''} (17. Qh5 Bb6 18. Bxb6 Qxb6+ 19. Kh1 Rg8 $1 20. Rf4 Kh8 $13) 17... Bb6 {It's very difficult to give any advices in this position,but this move is losing almost by force; probably black has to play Sutovsky: 'It's very difficult to give any advices in this position,but this move is losing almost by force; probably black has to play Sutovsky,E: 'It's very difficult to give any advices in this position, but this move is losing almost by force; probably black has to play''} (17... Bxg5 $5 18. Rg1 h6 (18... Kh6 $2 19. Rxg5 $1 Kxg5 20. Qd2+ $1 Kh5 (20... Kf6 21. Nd5+ {winning a queen.}) 21. Be2+ Ng4 22. Bxg4+ Kxg4 23. Rg1+ {and mating in a couple of moves.}) 19. h4 f6 20. hxg5 hxg5 {and white still has a big technical problems,because black's king is save and the knight on e5 placed very good.} (20... hxg5 {Boensch} 21. Kg2 $16)) 18. Bxe5+ Qxe5 19. Qh5 {It's hard to believe,but now black's position is lost!White is just playing Rf6,Raf1,Qh6,and,finally,g5-g6;black can't do anything against this.  f1-f6, a1-f1, h5-h6, g5-g6 Sutovsky: 'It's hard to believe,but now black's position is lost!White is just playing Rf6,Raf1,Qh6,and,finally,g5-g6;black can't do anything against this.  f1-f6, a1-f1, h5-h6, g5-g6 Sutovsky,E: 'It's hard to believe, but now black's position is lost! White is just playing Rf6,Raf1,Qh6 and finally g5-g6; black can't do anything against this.  f1-f6, a1-f1, h5-h6, g5-g6''} Be3 {All other moves also didn't save,but the best chanse was: Sutovsky: 'All other moves also didn't save,but the best chanse was: Sutovsky,E: 'All other moves also didn't save, but the best chanse was''} (19... Bd7 20. Rf6 Be3 (20... Bd8 21. Qh6+ Kg8 22. Raf1 Be7 23. R1f3 {and then 24.Rh3 and mating.}) (20... Rac8 21. Raf1 Be8 22. Qh6+ Kg8 23. g6 $18) 21. Raf1 Be8 22. Qh6+ Kg8 23. Nd5 $1 exd5 24. exd5 Qxd5+ 25. R1f3 Qxd3 26. cxd3 Bc6 27. Kg2 {and white should win,but he has some technical problems.}) (19... Bd8 {Boensch} 20. Rf3 b5 21. Raf1 Ra7 22. Rf6 (22. Rh3 $2 Rh8 23. Qh6+ Kg8 $13) 22... Kg8 23. Qh6 Re8 24. R1f3 b4 25. Rh3 bxc3 26. Qxh7+ Kf8 27. Rhf3 $18) (19... Bd4 $6 {! Gutman,L: bietet Rettungschancen.} 20. Rf3 (20. Rf6 $1 $18 {Fritz z.B.} b5 21. Raf1 Ra7 22. Qh6+ Kg8 23. g6 $1 hxg6 24. Rxg6+ Qg7 25. Rxg7+ Bxg7 26. Rg1 $18) 20... b5 21. Raf1 Ra7 22. Nd1 $1 (22. Nd5 $2 exd5 23. exd5 f5 $1 24. gxf6+ Kh8 25. Qh6 Rg8 26. f7 Rxf7 27. Rxf7 Qxd5+ 28. R7f3 Qxf3+ 29. Rxf3 Rg1#) 22... Rc7 23. c3 Bb6 24. Nf2 Bxf2 25. R1xf2 Bb7 26. Rf4 $36) 20. Rf3 {Now black is losing immediately.} Bxg5 21. Rg1 f6 22. h4 {and in a view of variation 22...h6 23.hg hg 24.Rh3,black resigned. Sutovsky: 'and in a view of variation 22...h6 23.hg hg 24.Rh3,black resigned. Sutovsky,E: 'and in a view of variation 22...h6 23.hg hg 24.Rh3 black resigned.''} (22. h4 {Boensch} h6 23. hxg5 hxg5 24. Rh3 Rg8 25. Qh7+ Kf8 26. Qc7 Qc5 27. Qd8+ Kf7 28. Rh7+ Rg7 29. Rh8 $18) 1-0

