{Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'In the quiet positional 6.Be2 e5 Najdorf, Svidler has tried the 10.Nd5 and 11. Qd3 line. After Judith's energetic 13...Nfe4 it became clear that the queenside will be closed and Black has chances on the kingside in the long run. This is a fine illustrative game showing Black's blockade strategy on the queenside and her attacking possibilities on the kingside. White's whole plan received a severe blow in this game.'''} 1. e4 {Ftacnik,L Polgar,Judit Ftacnik'Ftacnik,Lubomir Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit Hazai Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik'''} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be2 e5 7. Nb3 Be7 8. O-O O-O 9. Be3 Be6 10. Nd5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'The idea is to put pressure on the queenside. Black has to take the N, and after exd5 White has a queenside pawn majority. However to build up the ideal set of pawns a5-b4-c4-d5 is far from easy. The breakthrough on c5 can easily be stopped, while in the meantime Black can advance in the centre with the ... f5 advance.'''} Nbd7 11. Qd3 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'Now c4 is already threatened.'''} Bxd5 12. exd5 Nc5 13. Qd2 (13. Nxc5 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Hazai: '?!' Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} dxc5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: 'leads to a successful blockade for Black on d6, and the defended passed P on d5 is useless.''} 14. c4 (14. Rad1 {(Polgar,Judit) Hazai} e4 15. Qd2 Bd6 16. a4 Qc7 17. g3 Rae8 18. a5 Nd7 19. Bf4 Ne5 20. c4 f5 {and Black ca n mobilize his kingside pawns, but White cannot do the same on the other flank, King-Browne, Reykjavik 1990.}) 14... Bd6 15. b4 $5) 13... Nfe4 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: '!' Hazai: 'This is the best continuation.'''} (13... Qc7 {(Polgar,Judit) Ü 56/278} 14. f3 {(Ftacnik,Lubomir) controlling the e4 square.} Nfd7 (14... Nxb3 15. axb3 Nd7 (15... a5 16. c4 {and b4 will come again.}) 16. c4 {followed by b4.}) (14... h6 15. c4 Nh7 {Black wants to exchange the B through ...Bg5.} (15... Nfd7 16. Na5 $1 {discouraging ...b6, when there is no good defence against b4.}) (15... b6 16. Nxc5 dxc5 17. Bd3 {with only a small advantage for White because of the weakened kingside.}) 16. Nxc5 dxc5 17. Bd3 {preventing Bg5, Apicella-Brunner, EU-chT Debrecen 1992.}) 15. Nxc5 Nxc5 16. b4 Nd7 17. c4 b6 {The key square is c5.} 18. a3 a5 19. Rfc1 Ra7 $11 {with the idea of Rfc8 and Black has equalized, Galkin-Voitsekhovsky, RUS-cup Tomsk 1997.}) (13... Nce4 $6 {(Polgar,Judit) (Ftacnik,Lubomir) (Hazai) is met by} 14. Qb4 $1 {and the pressure on the queenside is increasing.} a5 15. Qxb7 Rb8 16. Qc6 a4 17. Nd2 Rxb2 18. Nxe4 Nxe4 19. Bd3 {and Black's position is a bit worse.}) (13... Nxb3 {(Polgar,Judit) (Ftacnik,Lubomir) Hazai} 14. axb3 a5 15. c4 {threatening b4 with a fine game for White.}) 14. Qb4 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'While the knight is on c5, this is not dangerous any more.'''} a5 (14... b6 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 15. f3 Nf6 16. Qd2 Qd7 17. f4 Nfe4 18. Qb4 Rfb8 19. Nxc5 Nxc5 20. fxe5 dxe5 21. Rad1 Bd6 22. Qh4 Rf8 23. g4 Qa4 24. c4 Qc2 25. Rd2 Qe4 26. Qh3 a5 27. b3 {Shirov,A-Topalov,V/Sarajevo/1999/ 1-0 (76)}) 15. Qb5 Qc7 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'Black has to blockade the dark squares.'''} 16. Rfd1 {Polgar,Judit: 'N''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'N'''} (16. Nxc5 dxc5 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 17. Qc4 Nf6 {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: 'The B is also strong now on d6.''} 18. Rfd1 Bd6 19. a3 Nd7 20. Rab1 Rac8 21. g4 {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: 'This is directed against ...f5, but weakening the dark squares is not a sensible strategy.''} Qd8 22. Kh1 Qh4 {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: 'Here is the punishment!''} 23. Rg1 e4 24. Rg2 Rce8 {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: 'with chances for a kingside attack, Nikolenko-Voitsekhovsky, Zepter op Minsk 1998.''} 25. g5 Ne5 26. Qa4 Nf3 27. Qd7 Bxh2 {0-1 Nikolenko,O-Voitsekhovsky,S/Minsk/1998/ (50)}) 16... b6 17. Qc4 (17. a3 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} f5 18. Nxc5 bxc5 $13) (17. Nxc5 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'} bxc5) 17... f5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'Black's pawns can easily be mobilized.'''} 18. Bd3 Qd8 {Black must get some counterplay on the kingside, since white's two bishops and domination on queenside make his position vulnerable. 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Black must get some counterplay on the kingside, since white's two bishops and domination on queenside make his position vulnerable. Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: 'Black must get some counterplay on the kingside, since white's two bishops and domination on queenside make his position vulnerable. ''''} (18... f4 $6 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 19. Bxe4 (19. Bxc5 Nxc5 20. Nxc5 Qxc5 21. Qe4 g6 $14) 19... fxe3 20. fxe3 b5 21. Qc3 b4 22. Qc4 Bg5 23. Re1 Rac8 24. Nxc5 Qxc5 25. Qd3 h6 26. Bf5 $16) 19. Nxc5 Nxc5 20. a3 Rc8 (20... a4 $5 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'}) 21. Qb5 {Polgar,Judit: '?''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '?'''} (21. b4 {Polgar,Judit: '!''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '!'''} Nxd3 (21... Na4 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'} 22. Qb3 Nc3 23. bxa5 bxa5 24. Re1 $13) 22. Qxd3 f4 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} (22... Qc7 $15 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'}) 23. Bd2 f3 $1 $15) 21... e4 22. Bf1 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'This light-squared B has no future in this pawn structure.'''} Bf6 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'activating the B.'''} (22... f4 $5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir'} 23. Bd4 Bf6 24. Bxf6 (24. b4 $5) 24... Rxf6 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} 25. b4 Nd7 26. Re1 e3 $1 27. fxe3 f3 28. gxf3 Ne5 29. Bg2 Nxf3+ 30. Bxf3 Rxf3 $17) 23. Rab1 (23. Bd4 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} f4 (23... Bxd4 24. Rxd4 Nd7 $15) 24. b4 $5 {Ftacnik: '!?''Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!?'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!?''} (24. Bxf6) 24... Nd7 25. Bxf6 Nxf6 26. c4 e3 $15) 23... Be5 {Polgar,Judit: '''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: ''''} 24. b4 axb4 25. Rxb4 $2 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '?' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '?'''' Svidler is making a move, that equals positional bancrupcy. Black seems to be having a good game, but after this move all white pawns on the queenside are of lesser quality.'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Svidler is making a move, that equals positional bancrupcy. Black seems to be having a good game, but after this move all white pawns on the queenside are of lesser quality. Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: 'Svidler is making a move, that equals positional bancrupcy. Black seems to be having a good game, but after this move all white pawns on the queenside are of lesser quality.''''} ({Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'or'''} 25. axb4 {Polgar,Judit: '!?''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '!?'''} Nd7 26. c4 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} f4 27. Bd4 Bxd4 28. Rxd4 Nf6 $15) 25... Nd7 26. Rc4 (26. c4 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} f4 $40) (26. Bxb6 Nxb6 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} (26... Qe8 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'}) 27. Qxb6 Qg5 $17) 26... Rxc4 27. Qxc4 Qe8 28. Re1 (28. h3 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Qg6 $17) 28... Nf6 $1 {Polgar,Judit: '?''Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '?' Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!''''} (28... Qg6 $1 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'}) 29. h3 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: '?!' Hazai: 'This is the beginning of a faulty plan.'''} (29. Bxb6 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Bxh2+ 30. Kxh2 Qh5+ 31. Kg1 Ng4 32. Bd3 Qh2+ 33. Kf1 Qh1+ 34. Ke2 exd3+ $17) 29... Nd7 $1 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!''''} 30. Qc7 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: '?'''} (30. Qb4 $5 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''}) 30... f4 $1 {[%mdl 128] 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'Now the avalanche of the black pawns cannot be stopped.' Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!'''' Polgar plays her cards very skilfully, white has problems to hold his endangered kingside. 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar plays her cards very skilfully, white has problems to hold his endangered kingside. Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: 'Polgar plays her cards very skilfully, white has problems to hold his endangered kingside. ''''} 31. Bc1 {Polgar,Judit: '?''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: '?'''} (31. Bxb6 {Polgar,Judit: '''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: ''''} Nxb6 (31... e3 $2 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '?' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '?''''} 32. Bb5 $1 $16 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!''''}) (31... Nf6 $1 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'} 32. c4 Qg6 $36 33. c5 $140 f3 34. Qc6 fxg2 35. Bxg2 Nh5) 32. Qxb6 Qg6 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} (32... e3 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'destroying White's defence.'''} 33. fxe3 f3 $17 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'and the opposite coloured B is the decisive factor in the attack.' Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '''''} 34. gxf3 Qg6+ 35. Bg2 Qg3 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} (35... Rxf3 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'} 36. Rf1) 36. Kf1 Rxf3+ 37. Bxf3 Qxf3+ $11) 33. c4 e3 $40) 31... e3 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: '!'''} 32. Bb5 {Polgar,Judit: '?''Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: '?' Hazai: 'This loses outright.' Polgar,Judit: '?'''} (32. fxe3 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'was the persistent defence, although Black has a fierce attack anyway.'''} f3 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: '!' Hazai: 'Again this motif crushes White's defence.'''} 33. gxf3 Qg6+ {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} (33... Rxf3 $19 {(Polgar,Judit) Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit'}) 34. Bg2 (34. Kh1 $2 {(Polgar,Judit) Hazai} Qg3 35. Re2 (35. f4 Qxe1) 35... Qxf3+ {and wins.}) 34... Qg3 35. Kf1 ({or} 35. Re2 {(Polgar,Judit) Hazai} Rxf3) 35... Nc5 $1 (35... Rxf3+ {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: '!''} 36. Bxf3 Qxf3+ 37. Kg1 Nf8 {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: '!''} (37... Bh2+ 38. Kxh2 Qf2+ 39. Kh1 Qxe1+ 40. Kg2 Nf6 41. Qc8+ Kf7 42. Qe6+ Kg6 43. Bb2 $11) 38. Bd2 (38. Qxb6 $2 {(Polgar,Judit) Hazai} Bh2+ $1) 38... Qg3+ 39. Kf1 Qxh3+ 40. Ke2 Bg3 41. Rb1 Qg2+ 42. Kd3 Qxd5+ {Polgar,Judit: 'Hazai: 'and Black is much better.''} 43. Ke2 $13) 36. f4 g5 37. Qe7 gxf4 38. exf4 Bd4 $1 39. Qe2 Qh2 40. Qg4+ Kh8 $19) 32... exf2+ 33. Kxf2 f3 $1 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hazai: 'followed by Bg3, winning.' Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!''''} (33... f3 $1 {'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik: '!''''} 34. Qxd7 (34. gxf3 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Bg3+ 35. Kxg3 Qxe1+ $19) 34... Bg3+ 35. Kxg3 Qxe1+ 36. Kh2 {'(Ftacnik,Lubomir) Polgar,Judit: 'Ftacnik''} Qxc1 $19) 0-1

