1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Qb6 5. Nb3 Nf6 6. Bd3 {This is what I call the Eros variation subline - a big survey was published in CBM 140. By choosing the text move White retains the possibility of a well-timed c4, but Black should face no problems if she reacts at the right moment with the typical ...d5 advance.} e6 (6... d5 {is also a good alternative:} 7. exd5 Nxd5 8. O-O e5 $1 {and Black is doing well according to my extensivly published analysis.}) 7. O-O Be7 8. c4 (8. Nc3 d6 9. Be3 Qc7 10. f4 a6 {transposes to more 'main' lines, where White can choose between: a)} 11. a4 {- the Hermes variation} ({b)} 11. a3 {- the Hestia variation}) ({c)} 11. Qe2 {- the Athena variation}) ({d)} 11. Qf3 {- the Zeus variation.})) 8... d5 ({This is objectively the best continuation. Black has also tried} 8... Ne5 9. Nc3 a6 10. Be2 d6 11. Be3 Qc7 12. Rc1 b6 13. f4 Ned7 14. Bf3 Bb7 15. Qe2 O-O 16. Nd4 $14 {Milos,G-Morozevich,A Internet 2000.}) 9. cxd5 exd5 10. Nc3 ({The main alternative is} 10. Be3 Qc7 11. exd5 Nxd5 12. Bc5 Be6 13. Na3 (13. Bxe7 Qxe7 $1 (13... Ncxe7 14. Nd4 Bd7 15. Na3 O-O 16. Re1 Qf4 17. Re4 Qf6 $11 {Wehmeier, S-Illner,A Germany 2008}) 14. Qf3 O-O $15) 13... O-O 14. Nb5 Qd7 (14... Qf4 15. Bxe7 Ndxe7 $13 {Dworakowska,J-Arakhamia Grant,K Leon 2001}) 15. Rc1 Nf4 16. Bc4 Qxd1 17. Rfxd1 Rfd8 $11 {.}) 10... Be6 $6 ({A novelty. Simpler is} 10... dxe4 11. Nxe4 O-O 12. Qe2 Nd4 (12... Rd8 $5 13. Be3 Qc7 14. Nxf6+ Bxf6 15. Rfd1 Qe5 $11) 13. Nxd4 Qxd4 {and Black is fine, as in Timoshenko,G-Epishin,V Tbilisi 1989.}) 11. exd5 Nxd5 12. Nxd5 Bxd5 13. Be3 $6 ({I think here White could gain the upper hand with} 13. Re1 Qd8 14. Qg4 $1 (14. Bg5 O-O $11) 14... O-O 15. Bh6 Bf6 16. Rad1 {.}) 13... Qb4 $1 {Probably White missed this strong and energetic move, which allows Black to obtain even play.} 14. Qc2 ({An invitation to a draw. If White wanted to continue he should go for} 14. Re1 O-O-O (14... O-O $2 15. Qh5 $18) 15. Bd2 Qh4 {when a sharp battle is on the cards.}) 14... Bxg2 {Accepted!} 15. Kxg2 Qg4+ 16. Kh1 Qf3+ 17. Kg1 Qg4+ 1/2-1/2

