n adventurous route of the king starts.} a5+ 31. Kc5 Qd3 32. b7 Ra6 (32... Qxc3+ 33. Kb5 Qd3+ (33... Qb2+ 34. Ka4 Rad8 35. Qe4+ f5 36. Bxf5+ Kf6 (36... Rxf5 37. g4 Kf7 38. Qxf5+ Kg8 39. Qc8) 37. Bxh7 $18) 34. Qc4 Qxc4+ 35. Bxc4 $18) 33. Qd7 Qxc3+ 34. Bc4 {Finally the bishop shelters the monarch from further, annoying checks.} f5 (34... Qxa3+ 35. Kd5 $18) (34... h5 35. Qd3+ Qxd3 36. Bxd3+ $18) 35. g4 $3 {Another stunning, silent move and the only way for the victory.} Raf6 (35... f4 36. b8=Q {is one of the main motifs.} Rxb8 37. Qf5+ Kh6 38. Qh5#) (35... Qxa3+ 36. Kd5 {It is so unique to see a king dancing in the middle of the board between the enemy heavy pieces, while the position is just winning!} Raf6 37. gxf5+ Kh5 (37... Rxf5 38. Qe6+ R5f6 (38... Kh5 39. b8=Q) 39. Qg4+ Kf7 40. Bc5 $18) 38. Qxg7 Qd6+ 39. Ke4 Qc6+ 40. Kd3 Rd6+ 41. Kc3 $18) 36. gxf5+ Rxf5 37. Qe6+ Kh5 (37... R8f6 38. Qe8+ Rf7 39. b8=Q $18) 38. b8=Q e4+ 39. Kd6 $18) 27... Be4 28. Rd2 Qb5 (28... Rac8 $1 {Ribli,Zoltan Hera,Imre A very nice diverting idea.} 29. Qe7 (29. Bxc8 $4 Qb3 $19) 29... Qa5 (29... Rcd8 30. g4 $8 Rxd2 31. Kxd2 Qc2+ 32. Ke1 Qc1+ $11) 30. Bb4 Qxb6 31. Rd7 Kh5 32. Qxg7 Qxe6 33. f3 $1 Bg6 $8 34. Bxf8 Rxf8 35. Qxf8 Qxd7 36. Qxf6 Kh6 37. Qxe5 $11) 29. Rd7 Qb1+ 30. Kd2 Qc2+ 31. Ke3 {Ribli,Zoltan Hera,Imre: '?'} (31. Ke1 {Ribli,Zoltan Hera,Imre} Qxc3+ 32. Kf1 Qc1+ 33. Ke2 Qc2+ $11) 31... Rfc8 $17) 26... Bxd5 27. Qxd5 Qxd5 (27... Qa4 {Timman,Jan H} 28. Qd3+ $1 (28. Kb2 Rad8) 28... e4 29. Qc2 Qxa3+ 30. Kb1 $16) 28. Rxd5 $14 {[%csl Gb6,Ge3] Timman,Jan H: '' '' '' Timman,Jan H: 'Ribli: ''' Weiss hat einen gefährlichen Bauern (auf b6) für die Qualität. Weiss hat einen gefährlichen Bauern (auf b6) für die Qualität. Timman,Jan H: 'Ribli: 'Weiss hat einen gefährlichen Bauern (auf b6) für die Qualität.''}) (25... Rac8 $5 {Timman,Jan H: 'Ribli: '!?'' Timman,Jan H: 'TonyK: 'although the line''} 26. Kb2 $40 {[%cal Re6b3,Rb3c2,Rc2g6] Timman,Jan H: '+-' '+-' '+-' Timman,Jan H: 'Ribli: '''} (26. c4