1. e4 {Psakhis,L Psakhis,Lev Psakhis,Lev Psakhis,Lev Psakhis,Lev: 'Psakhis'} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Qxd7 5. O-O g6 {Deviating from the main lines at very early stage} 6. c3 Bg7 7. d4 Nf6 8. Re1 (8. Qe2 O-O 9. Re1 Na6 10. Nbd2 cxd4 11. cxd4 d5 12. e5 Ne4 $1 13. h3 (13. Nxe4 dxe4 14. Qxe4 Nb4 {[%csl Gd5][%cal Gb4d5]}) 13... Nxd2 14. Bxd2 Rac8 $13 {½-½ Timman,J-Van Wely,L/Breda m rapid 1998 (45)}) 8... O-O (8... cxd4 9. cxd4 d5 10. Ne5) 9. dxc5 $146 {The simpliest way to small advantage} (9. b3 cxd4 10. cxd4 Nc6 11. Nc3 Rac8 12. Bb2 $14 {1-0 Xu Hanbing-Berczes,D/Balatontourist op 2000/The Week in Chess 294 (50)}) (9. h3 Qc7 10. Bf4 Nfd7 11. Nbd2 cxd4 12. cxd4 Nc6 13. Nb3 Qb6 14. Be3 Qa6 $11 {Utegaliev,A-Berczes,D/Wch B10 Oropesa del Mar 2000/InfoXadrez/0-1 (51)}) (9. d5 $5) (9. e5 dxe5 10. Nxe5 Qd5 $11) 9... dxc5 10. Qe2 (10. e5 Nd5 $13 (10... Qxd1 11. Rxd1 Nfd7 12. e6 $5 fxe6 13. Ng5 $14)) 10... Qc6 11. Na3 (11. e5 $5 Nd5 12. Qe4 $36 {[%cal Ge4h4]}) 11... a6 12. e5 Nd5 13. Qe4 ({Worth considering} 13. e6 $5 $14) 13... Nd7 14. Nc4 (14. Bg5 {[%cal Ga1d1]}) (14. Qh4 $5 {[%cal Gc1h6] Leads to very nice game for white.}) 14... Rad8 15. Na5 Qc7 16. Qxd5 Nxe5 $1 ({Judit rightly avoided the line} 16... Qxa5 17. Qxb7 Nxe5 18. Nxe5 Bxe5 19. Bh6 $16) 17. Qxb7 Nxf3+ 18. Qxf3 Qxa5 19. Bg5 (19. Rxe7 Qb5 $132) 19... f6 20. Be3 e5 21. Qc6 (21. Qg4 $5 {[%cal Gg4c4,Gg4e6]}) 21... Rc8 22. Qd5+ Kh8 23. b4 ({Maybe} 23. Red1 Qb5 $140 24. c4 Qxb2 $140 25. Bxc5 Rfe8 26. Bd6 {[%csl Gc4] gives more chances for advantage.}) 23... Rfd8 $1 24. Qe6 (24. Qb3 cxb4 25. cxb4 Qd5 26. Qxd5 Rxd5 $11) 24... cxb4 25. Bb6 Qd5 26. Qxd5 Rxd5 27. cxb4 1/2-1/2

