{[%evp 0,65,17,29,52,49,71,73,48,37,37,30,67,41,56,42,38,21,38,6,80,75,57,17,29,0,38,22,73,54,56,56,64,43,35,45,25,-89,-6,-108,-116,-113,-113,-302,-328,-302,-313,-395,-448,-425,-448,-406,-320,-328,-290,-387,121,227,789,716,724,722,29989,29990,29991,29992,29993,29994]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 e6 7. O-O b5 8. Bb3 Be7 9. Qf3 Qb6 (9... Qc7 $5 {is another way to prevent e5, also with the idea to answer it with ...Bb7.}) 10. Be3 Qb7 11. a3 $5 (11. Qg3 {is the main line.}) 11... O-O 12. Rae1 {One move amongst many others, 12.g4 being the most sensible in my opinion.} Bd7 (12... Nbd7 $5) (12... Nc6 $5) 13. g4 $1 Nc6 (13... h6 14. h4 {is never a good inclusion for Black, unless there's a concrete reason for it. With the black king standing on g8, it only accelerates White's attack.}) 14. g5 Ne5 15. Qg2 Nh5 16. f4 Nc4 17. Bxc4 bxc4 18. f5 {White continues her attack. However the position is unclear.} g6 19. Nce2 {It was probably better to avoid any endgame, playing something like 19.Qf2, with an unclear position.} e5 (19... exf5 20. exf5 Qxg2+ 21. Kxg2 f6 $1 {would be more than decent for Black.}) (19... Rae8 {is possible too - not touching the pawn structure.}) 20. f6 Bd8 21. Nf5 $2 {In the style of M. Tal! Just throw all the pieces and make your opponent blunder!} gxf5 22. Nc3 Kh8 {It seems like many moves were winning for Black, but this is one of the strongest.} 23. Qh3 Nf4 (23... Nxf6 24. gxf6 f4 {followed by ...Rg8, ...fxe3, seemed to be the clearest win. But hey, this is a rapid game!}) 24. Bxf4 exf4 25. Rxf4 Rg8 $2 {Black starts going wrong.} (25... fxe4 26. Qh6 Rg8 27. Rh4 Bb6+ 28. Kf1 Bf5 {and White's attack is over.}) 26. Rh4 Rxg5+ 27. Kf1 Bxf6 $4 (27... Kg8 $1 28. Rxh7 Bxf6 29. Nd5 Bg7 {and Black was still winning.}) 28. Nd5 $1 {No longer allowing the black king to escape!} Qxb2 (28... Bg7 29. Ne7 $3) (28... Rg1+ $1 29. Kxg1 Rg8+ 30. Kf1 Bxh4 31. Qxh4 fxe4 {was apparently only a draw.}) 29. Rxh7+ Kg8 30. Qh6 Bd8 (30... Bg7) 31. e5 $1 {Cutting the long queen's diagonal. Game over!} Rg1+ 32. Kxg1 Qd4+ 33. Kf1 1-0

