1. d4 {Krasenkow,M Krasenkow,Michal Krasenkow,Michal Krasenkow Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Nc3 Ne4 8. Qc2 Nxc3 9. Qxc3 c5 10. Rd1 d6 11. b3 Nd7 (11... Bf6 {Krasenkow is the main theoretical move, quite sufficient for equality. GM Judit Polgar tries another plan, condemned by theory... and fails to rehabilitate it.}) 12. Bb2 Nf6 {Krasenkow: 'Quite logical. White must react energetically, otherwise Black's control of the e4 square will be an important factor.'} ({However,} 12... Bf6 $142 {Krasenkow transposing to the 11...f6 system.}) 13. d5 {Krasenkow: '!' Krasenkow,Michal: '!' '!' Krasenkow,M: '!'} (13. dxc5 {Krasenkow} bxc5 14. Ne1 Qb6 15. e4 Rfd8 16. Nd3 Bf8 $6 (16... a5 $1 $132) 17. Qe1 Be7 18. e5 dxe5 19. Nxe5 Bxg2 20. Kxg2 Qb7+ 21. f3 $14 {/= 1-0 Lombard,A-Scholz Solis,G/Buenos Aires 1978/EXT 2000 (75)}) (13. Ne1 {Krasenkow} Bxg2 14. Nxg2 Qc7 15. dxc5 bxc5 16. Rd3 a5 17. a4 Rfd8 18. Rad1 Ne8 19. Qd2 Qb7 20. Ne3 Ra6 21. Bc3 Rb8 22. Rb1 Qa8 23. Nc2 d5 $1 24. cxd5 c4 25. Rf3 cxb3 26. dxe6 Rxe6 27. Nd4 Re4 28. Nf5 Bf8 29. Bxa5 Rxa4 30. Qd7 Qxf3 31. exf3 Rxa5 $44 {0-1 Kraidman,Y-Smyslov,V/Hastings 1976/Inf 23 (35)}) (13. Qd3 {Krasenkow} Qc7 14. dxc5 bxc5 15. Ng5 e5 16. Bxb7 Qxb7 17. f4 Rad8 18. Nh3 e4 19. Qc3 Nh5 20. Rab1 Bf6 $13 {1-0 Kuerten,D-Westerlund,B/ICCF 1997/ICCF tele 1/2002 (64)}) 13... exd5 (13... e5 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'is perhaps a lesser evil:'} 14. Nd2 $14 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} (14. Nxe5 dxe5 15. d6 Bxg2 16. Qxe5 Re8 17. dxe7 Qxe7 18. Qxe7 Rxe7 19. Bxf6 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} (19. Kxg2 {Krasenkow} Rxe2 20. Bxf6) 19... gxf6 20. Kxg2 Rxe2 $11 21. Rd7 {Krasenkow} Rb2 (21... a5 22. Rd6 a4 23. Rxb6 axb3 24. Rxb3 Rc2 25. Rb6 Kg7 26. a4 Rxc4 27. a5 $16 {1-0 Anikaev,Y-Yuferov,S/USSR 1977/Inf 24 (41)}) 22. Re1 Rxa2 23. Ree7 Rf8 24. Rxa7 Rxa7 25. Rxa7 Rd8 26. Rb7 Rd6 27. g4 Kg7 28. f3 Kg6 29. Kg3 h5 30. gxh5+ Kxh5 31. Rxf7 Rd3 32. Rxf6 Rxb3 33. Kf4 $14 {½-½ Petrosian,T-Karpov,A/Moscow 1976/URS-ch (63)})) 14. cxd5 Re8 (14... Ne8 {Krasenkow} 15. e4 Bf6 16. Qc2 Bxb2 17. Qxb2 Qf6 18. Qd2 Rd8 19. Ne1 Nc7 20. a4 Rfe8 21. Nc2 a5 $6 22. Ne3 Rb8 23. f4 $16 {1-0 Schinzel,W-Boehlig,H/Warsaw 1978/EXT 2002 (29)}) 15. e4 (15. Nh4 $5 {Krasenkow is tempting. After} Bf8 (15... Nh5 $5) 16. Qf3 Nd7 17. e4 b5 18. Qe2 b4 19. f4 a5 20. a3 Ba6 21. Qf3 Be7 22. axb4 axb4 23. Nf5 Bf6 24. Qf2 {0-1 Thorbergsson,F-Hecht,H/Siegen 1970/EXT 2002 (45) White eventually managed to build up an attacking position but lost the game after all.}) 15... Bf8 (15... b5 $5 {Krasenkow Here is how the great Ulf Andersson defended this position:} 16. Re1 ({a prophylactic approach is interesting:} 16. Nd2 Qd7 17. a3 Bd8 18. Qf3 a6 19. Rdc1 Qg4 20. Qxg4 Nxg4 21. Bc3 Bf6 22. h3 Bxc3 23. Rxc3 Nf6 24. f4 h6 25. Kf2 Kf8 26. Rc2 g5 27. Bf3 Rad8 28. Re1 gxf4 29. gxf4 Bc8 30. h4 $14 {1-0 Salai,J-Shields,G/IECC 2000/81 telechess (55)}) 16... Bf8 17. Nh4 a5 18. Nf5 a4 19. Rad1 axb3 20. axb3 b4 21. Qc1 Nd7 22. f4 g6 23. Ne3 Ba6 24. Ba1 Bb5 25. Qb2 Rxa1 $1 26. Qxa1 Bg7 27. Qa7 Bc3 28. Bf1 Bxf1 29. Nxf1 Bxe1 30. Rxe1 Nf6 31. e5 dxe5 32. fxe5 Qxd5 33. exf6 Qd4+ 34. Kg2 Qd5+ {½-½ Lakic,N-Andersson,U/Banja Luka 1976/MCL}) 16. Nd2 b5 17. a4 b4 $146 {Krasenkow: '?!' Krasenkow,Michal: '?!' '?!' Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: 'N'' Krasenkow,M: '?!' Krasenkow: 'An unsuccessful attempt to improve on the following game. Black just weakens the c4-square.'} (17... Ba6 {Ü 24/577 Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: 'Ü 24/577''} 18. axb5 {Krasenkow} Bxb5 19. Re1 a5 20. Qc2 Qd7 21. Nc4 Ra6 22. e5 dxe5 23. Nxe5 Qc7 24. Bc3 Rd8 25. Red1 Re8 26. Nc4 a4 27. Ne3 Qd7 28. bxa4 Bxa4 29. Qd3 Bb5 30. Qc2 Ba4 31. Qf5 Qxf5 32. Nxf5 Rea8 33. Re1 R8a7 34. Bf1 Rb6 35. d6 $18 {1-0 Tukmakov,V-Kuzmin,G/Leningrad 1977/URS-ch (41)}) (17... a6 {Krasenkow} 18. axb5 axb5 19. Rxa8 Qxa8 20. Ra1 Qb8 21. f4 $36) 18. Qc2 g6 (18... a5 $5 {Krasenkow}) 19. a5 Ba6 20. Bf1 {Krasenkow: 'A typical move exchanging the defender of the light squares in Black's camp. After the bishop exchange the white knight will be comfortably placed on c4.'} (20. Nc4 $143 {Krasenkow} Bxc4 21. Qxc4 $14) 20... Bxf1 21. Rxf1 Bh6 (21... Bg7 {Krasenkow: '!?' Krasenkow,Michal: '!?' '!?' Krasenkow,M: '!?' Krasenkow: 'was probably more accurate but didn't solve Black's problems:'} 22. Rfe1 {Krasenkow} (22. f4 $2 {Krasenkow} Nxe4) 22... Nd7 23. Bxg7 Kxg7 24. f4 $16 {[%cal Yd2c4]}) 22. f4 Bg7 23. Rfe1 Qd7 (23... Qe7 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'}) 24. Nc4 {Krasenkow: 'Black is now totally passive and can't prevent White preparing a decisive break.'} Nh5 25. Rad1 Bxb2 26. Qxb2 Ng7 27. Qg2 (27. e5 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Nf5) 27... Rad8 28. g4 (28. e5 $5 {Krasenkow} Nf5 29. g4 {but White needn't hurry.}) 28... f6 29. h3 (29. Qg3 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} g5 30. Re3 Qe7 31. Rf1 $16) 29... g5 30. fxg5 fxg5 31. e5 {Krasenkow: '!' Krasenkow,Michal: '!' '!' Krasenkow,M: '!' Krasenkow: 'Still!'} dxe5 32. d6 Qf7 (32... e4 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 33. Rxe4 (33. Rd5 h6 34. Rxe4 Ne6) 33... Ne6 34. Re5 h6 (34... Kh8 35. Rde1) 35. Qd5 $18) 33. Qd5 e4 34. Qxg5 Qf3 35. Qd5+ (35. Qe3 $1 $16 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'}) 35... Re6 36. Re3 Rdxd6 37. Rxf3 (37. Qxd6 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Rxd6 38. Rxd6 Qf4 39. Rd8+ Kf7 40. Rd7+ Kg6 41. Re7 $16) 37... Rxd5 38. Rxd5 exf3 39. Kf2 {Krasenkow: 'The complications have ended in a gloomy endgame for Black. His pawns are falling like ripe apples and his g7 knight is still out of play.'} Re2+ (39... Rh6 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 40. Rd8+ Kf7 41. Rd7+ Kf8 42. Rxa7 Rxh3 43. a6 $18) 40. Kxf3 Rc2 (40... Ne6 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 41. Kxe2 Nf4+ 42. Kf3 Nxd5 43. Ke4 $18) 41. Rd8+ {Krasenkow: 'It is essential to capture the a7 pawn and not c5. White's passed a5 pawn becomes extremely formidable.'} Kf7 42. Rd7+ Kg6 (42... Kf8 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 43. Rxa7 Rc3+ 44. Ke4 Rxb3 45. a6 $18) 43. Rxa7 Ne6 44. Ke4 Nd4 45. h4 {Krasenkow: 'The principle of two weaknesses: a threat to move the a5-pawn forward is combined with an attack on the black king.'} (45. Ne5+ {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} Kf6 46. Nd7+ Kg5 47. Nxc5) 45... Rh2 (45... Re2+ {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 46. Kd5 Nxb3 47. Ne5+ $18) 46. a6 (46. Ne5+ $1 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: '!''} Kf6 47. Nd7+ Kg6 (47... Ke6 {Krasenkow} 48. Nxc5+) 48. Nf8+ $18 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny: '+-''} Kf6 {Krasenkow} 49. g5# {was simpler}) 46... Nxb3 47. Kd5 Kf6 (47... Rxh4 {Krasenkow,Michal: 'Bareev,Evgeny'} 48. Ne5+ Kh6 49. g5+ $18) 48. Rxh7 Ra2 49. a7 Nc1 50. Ne5 Rd2+ 51. Kxc5 Ra2 52. Nd7+ Kg6 53. Nf8+ Kf6 54. Kxb4 1-0

