1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. d4 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. Nd2 a5 {Joe Gallagher: 'Against 9 Nd2 Black does best to hold up White's queenside play. If he gets involved in a direct race (kingside v queenside attack) then he usually comes out second best as the knight on d2 can be extremely powerful when it emerges on c4 (after White has played c5 of course).'} 10. Rb1 Bd7 {Joe Gallagher: 'Played to further slow down White on the queenside as now a3 is met by a4.10. . . Nd7 is the other mainline'} 11. b3 Ne8 (11... c6 $5) 12. a3 f5 13. b4 axb4 14. axb4 Nf6 (14... Bh6 {is the other possibility in order to exchange off the 'bad bishop'. After} 15. c5 fxe4 16. Ndxe4 Bxc1 17. Rxc1 Nf5 {Black is thought to be Ok}) 15. c5 fxe4 16. Ndxe4 Nf5 17. Bg5 h6 18. Nxf6+ $146 {Joe Gallagher: 'This looks like a new move. Normally White plays'} (18. Bxf6 {Ü 64/556} Bxf6 19. b5 b6 20. c6 Bc8 $13) 18... Bxf6 19. Bd2 (19. Bxf6 Qxf6 20. Ne4 Qf7 21. Bc4 b5 $11) 19... Bg7 20. Bd3 Qe7 (20... Qh4 21. Ne4 Ra3 22. Bc3 $11) 21. Qc1 (21. Qg4 Kh7 (21... Qf7 22. Qc4 Ra3 23. Rbe1 $14) 22. Qc4 Nd4 23. Be3 Nf5 $11) 21... g5 $6 (21... dxc5 $6 22. bxc5 (22. Ne4 $1) 22... Qxc5 23. Rxb7 $14) (21... Kh7 22. Qc2 Qf6 23. Rbe1 Nd4 24. Qb2 $11) 22. Ne4 Nd4 {Joe Gallagher: 'The game is about level with each side having one excellent central White now heads for complications he would have been well advised to steer clear of.'} 23. cxd6 (23. Be3 Nf5 24. Ra1 $14) 23... cxd6 24. Qc7 {Joe Gallagher: '?!'} (24. Be3 Nf5 25. Qd2 $14) 24... Ra3 $1 25. Bc3 $2 {Joe Gallagher: '!' Joe Gallagher: 'Ftacnik must have planned'} (25. Bc4 {Joe Gallagher: 'here but then realised that the reply'} b5 {Joe Gallagher: 'is awkward for him. For example,'} (25... Rc8 26. Qxd6 Qd8 27. b5 Ra4 28. Bd3 Nf5 29. Qg6 Nh4 30. Qh5 Bf5 31. Qe2 Qxd5 $14) 26. Bc1 Raa8 (26... Ra6 27. Nc5 (27. Bd3 Rc8 28. Qb7 Rca8) 27... bxc4 28. Nxa6 Rc8 29. Qb7 Qf7 $17) (26... bxc4 27. Bxa3 Nb5 28. Qa5) 27. Bd3 Nf5 $11) 25... Rc8 26. Qxb7 Raxc3 27. Nxc3 Rxc3 28. Be4 {Joe Gallagher: 'The b-pawn and the fact that the bishop on g7 is so passive gives White hope'} (28. Rfd1 e4 (28... Qe8 29. Ra1 Bc8 30. Qb6 e4 $17) 29. Bxe4 Qxe4 30. Qxd7 Ne2+ 31. Kh1 Nf4 32. Qg4 Rc2 $17) 28... Qe8 (28... Kf7 29. Rfe1 Bb5 30. Qa8 Qe8 $17) (28... Bf8 29. b5 $1 Rc5 30. b6 Ne2+ 31. Kh1 Nc3 32. Bf5 $3 Bxf5 (32... Nxb1 $2 33. Qxd7 Nd2 34. b7 Qxd7 35. Bxd7 Nxf1 36. b8=Q Rc1 37. Be6+ Kg7 38. h4 gxh4 39. g4 $16) 33. Qxe7 Bxe7 34. b7 Nxb1 35. b8=Q+ Kg7 36. Rxb1 Bxb1 37. Qxb1 Rxd5 $11) (28... Qd8 $5 29. Ra1 (29. b5 Ne2+ $1 30. Kh1 Rc8 31. Rb4 Nc3 32. Qa6 Bxb5 33. Rxb5 Nxe4 $19) 29... Qc7 30. Qa8+ Bc8 31. Qa4 Qf7 $17) 29. Ra1 Bc8 30. Qb6 (30. Qb8 Qf8 (30... Bf8 31. Ra7 Qb5 32. Qxb5 Nxb5 33. Ra8 Bd7 $15) 31. Ra8 g4 32. Rd1 Bf6 $15) 30... Bf8 31. Ra8 $6 (31. Ra7 $5 Be7 32. Rfa1 Qf8 33. Qb8 $15) 31... Qf7 32. Qd8 Qf4 (32... Qb7 33. Qa5 (33. Qf6 $2 Ne2+ 34. Kh1 Nf4 35. Raa1 Qc7 36. b5 Bg7 $19) 33... Nb3 34. Qa4 Rc4 $15) (32... Ne2+ 33. Kh1 Qxf2 $4 34. Raa1 $1 {is a trap that had to be sidestepped}) 33. f3 (33. Bh7+ Kxh7 34. Rxc8 Rxc8 35. Qxc8 Kg8 $17) (33. Rxc8 Rxc8 34. Qxc8 Qxe4 $17) 33... Qe3+ $2 (33... Rc1 $1 34. Ra1 (34. g4 Qe3+ 35. Kg2 Qd2+ 36. Kh3 Ne2 $19) 34... Rxf1+ 35. Rxf1 Bf5 36. Bxf5 (36. Qf6 Bg7 37. Qd8+ Kh7 38. Bxf5+ Nxf5 39. Qb6 Qc4 40. Qf2 e4 $19) 36... Nxf5 37. Qe8 Ne3 38. Qg6+ Kh8 39. Rb1 Qd4 40. Kh1 Qd2 41. Rg1 Qxb4 $17) 34. Kh1 Rc1 (34... Qf2 $2 35. Rfa1 Qb2 (35... Re3 36. Qxf8+ $1 Kxf8 37. Rxc8+ Ke7 38. Ra7+ Kf6 39. Rf8# {#}) 36. Rg1 Qc1 37. Ra7 $18) 35. Ra1 Rxf1+ (35... Rxa1 36. Rxa1 Qc3 37. Rb1 Kf7 38. h3 $11) 36. Rxf1 Bf5 (36... Ba6 $2 37. Qc7 $1 Qxe4 38. fxe4 Bxf1 39. Qc3 $14) (36... Qe2 37. Rc1 $1 (37. Kg1 $6 Ba6 $1 38. Ra1 Bd3 $17) 37... Bh3 38. Rg1 Bf5 39. Qe8 $11) 37. Qe8 $1 (37. Qf6 Bg7 38. Qxd6 Bxe4 39. fxe4 Qxe4 $15) 37... Qe2 38. Kg1 (38. Ra1 Bxe4 39. fxe4 Nb3 40. Qg6+ Kh8 41. Qf6+ Kg8 42. Rf1 Bg7 43. Qe6+ Kh8 44. Qc8+ Kh7 45. Qf5+ $11) 38... Qe3+ 39. Kh1 Qe2 40. Kg1 Qe3+ {Joe Gallagher: 'Ftacnik was a little lucky after he mishandled the early middlegame but it is not unusual for a rook to be an equal of two minor pieces in the King's Indian.'} 1/2-1/2

