1. c4 {[%emt 0:00:02] Notes by Judit Polgar Notes by Judit Polgar A21: English Opening: 1...e5 Nc3} e5 2. Nc3 c5 3. g3 Nc6 4. Bg2 g6 5. a3 (5. Nf3 Bg7 6. d3 Nge7 7. Nd2 (7. Bg5 O-O 8. O-O h6 9. Bxe7 Nxe7 10. Nd2 d6 11. Rb1 Rb8 12. a3 Be6 13. Qa4 a6 14. Rfc1 {Lobron,E-Polgar,J/TV-match/Cologne/1989/}) 7... d6 8. Nf1 Be6 9. Ne3 O-O 10. O-O Rb8 11. Rb1 a6 12. Ned5 b5 13. b3 Qd7 {Hansen,LB-Schussler,H/Vejstrup/1989/ played in the same round and black was fine}) 5... a5 6. Nf3 {The knight intends Ng1-f3-d2-f1-e3-d5} Bg7 7. d3 Nge7 8. Nd2 (8. O-O d6 9. Rb1 Rb8 10. Nd5 O-O 11. Bg5 f6 12. Bd2 Be6 13. Ne1 b5 14. Nc2 f5 15. b3 $13 {Gelfand,B-Polgar,Zsu/New York op/1989/  CBM 12}) 8... d6 9. Nf1 {A popular manouver nowdays} Be6 10. Ne3 O-O 11. Ned5 $14 {The knight feels good on d5} Rb8 12. O-O {White is behind in development.} h6 {Consolidates g5} (12... f5 13. Bg5 h6 $2 14. Bxe7 Nxe7 15. Nxe7+ Qxe7 16. Bd5 $16) 13. Rb1 Kh7 14. Bd2 f5 15. b4 axb4 16. axb4 cxb4 17. Nxb4 f4 $5 {Black gains space} (17... Nxb4 18. Rxb4 d5 19. cxd5 Nxd5 20. Rb5 Nxc3 21. Bxc3 Qc7 22. Qa1 $16) 18. Ncd5 $6 { 18.bd5  18.bd5 A beautiful square!} Nd4 19. Bc3 $6 (19. Nxe7 Qxe7 20. Nc2 $14) 19... Nef5 $1 $10 20. Nc2 (20. e4 f3 21. exf5 fxg2 22. fxg6+ Kh8 23. Kxg2 Nf3 $11) 20... Nxc2 21. Qxc2 h5 $1 (21... b5 22. cxb5 Rc8 23. Qd2 $14) 22. e4 $2 {Anything else would have been better} (22. gxf4 Bxd5 23. Bxd5 exf4 24. Bxg7 Kxg7 $16) 22... Nh4 $5 {22...h6} (22... fxe3 23. Nxe3 Nxe3 24. fxe3 Rxf1+ 25. Bxf1 $11) 23. f3 $8 {Covers g4} (23. gxh4 f3 $19) (23. Bh1 Bh3 24. Qd1 f3 $14) 23... Nxg2 {'=' '='} 24. Qxg2 (24. Kxg2 Qc8 { ...h3, ...g5}) 24... Qc8 $1 $17 25. gxf4 Bxd5 $1 (25... Bh3 $2 26. Qg5 Bxf1 27. f5 $44) 26. exd5 Rxf4 { ...b5  ...b5 An ideal square for the black rook.} 27. Rb5 {The rook dominates} (27. Bd2 Rd4 28. Rb3 Bh6 $11) 27... Ra8 $2 (27... Qf5 $1 28. Qe2 $6 e4 $1 29. Bxg7 exf3 30. Qe7 Qg4+ 31. Kf2 Qg2+ 32. Ke1 Rf7 $1 $19) 28. Bb4 Ra6 29. Kh1 Qa8 (29... h4 30. Qe2 $11) 30. Rg1 {'=' The mate threat is Qxg6 '='} Rf6 31. f4 {White had only 5 minutes for 9 moves left.} Ra2 32. Qg5 Ra1 $2 (32... Qc8 $1 33. fxe5 (33. f5 Qxf5 34. Qxf5 Rxf5 35. Bxd6 Rff2 36. Rd1 Rxh2+ 37. Kg1 h4 38. Rxb7 h3 39. Rxg7+ Kh6 $19) 33... Qh3 34. Qg3 Qxg3 35. Rxg3 Rf1+ 36. Rg1 Rff2 $19) (32... Qa7 33. Bc5 dxc5 34. fxe5 Qb8 $17) 33. fxe5 {'' ''} Rxg1+ (33... dxe5 34. Bc5 $13) 34. Qxg1 dxe5 35. Rb6 $1 (35. Bc5 $5 $14 {might be a viable alternative}) 35... Rxb6 {'=' '='} 36. Qxb6 Qa1+ (36... Qa4 37. Qxb7 Qd1+ 38. Kg2 Qxd3 39. d6 $15) 37. Qg1 {'=' '='} Qb2 38. Qe1 { 39.c3} e4 $1 39. dxe4 Be5 {The bishop likes it on e5. Do you see the mate threat?} 40. Bd2 Qc2 41. Qe3 $1 g5 $1 42. Qe2 $5 {42.f2!} Kg6 {Threatening Bf4} (42... Kg7 43. Qe3) 43. Qe3 Kf7 44. Qf3+ $1 (44. Qe2 $2 g4 $1 $17) (44. Qxg5 $4 {that pawn is deadly bait and will cause White grave problems} Qd1+ 45. Qg1 Qxd2 $19) 44... Kg7 45. Qe3 Kh7 46. Qf3 (46. Qxg5 $4 {the pawn must remain untouched} Qd1+ 47. Qg1 Qxd2 $19) 46... Kg8 47. Qxh5 $1 Qxe4+ 48. Kg1 Bd4+ 49. Kf1 Bf6 50. Qe2 Qh1+ {Judit Polgar} 1/2-1/2

