{Alexei Shirov: 'This annotations are based on my notes published in 'Informator 60'. This was the best tournament in my career (so far), but I started with ½/3. Fortunately it didn't kill my fighting spirit and I won the next four games. This one is the last in the series. Despite shaky play after that, my luck held and I somehow made it. Something to remember. '} 1. e4 {Shirov Shirov} g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 c6 4. Nf3 d6 (4... d5) 5. Bg5 $5 {Alexei Shirov: 'Quite an interesting set-up against the Pirc Defence. Eight months after this game I played it myself against David Norwood (Bundesliga 1994/95).'} Qb6 $5 ({Norwood continued} 5... Bg4 {.}) 6. Rb1 $146 {Alexei Shirov: 'I was very surprised by this move.'} ({Alexei Shirov: 'but I was completely sure that with her attacking style Judit was going to sacrifice a pawn with'} 6. Qd2 $5 Qxb2 7. Rb1 Qa3 8. Bd3 $44 {Alexei Shirov: '. Black might then continue'} (8. Bc4 {Ü 14/180}) 8... h6 9. Be3 Nf6 10. O-O Nbd7 11. h3 Qa5 $13 {Alexei Shirov: 'with an unclear game.'}) (6. a3 Bg4 7. Be3 Nd7 $10 {Alexei Shirov: 'would also have been fine for Black'}) 6... Bg4 7. Be3 Bxf3 8. gxf3 Qc7 $11 {Alexei Shirov: 'Curiously enough Judit repeated the same line against me in a blindfold game in Monaco in 1996.'} ({Unable to remember our previous encounter properly I continued} 8... Nd7 {and won again.}) 9. h4 e6 $1 10. h5 d5 11. Qd2 ({Alexei Shirov: 'I was more afraid of'} 11. Qe2 {Alexei Shirov: ', a direct attempt to use White's lead in development. But I think that Black is still solid after the precise'} Nf6 $1 (11... Ne7 $6 {Alexei Shirov: 'leaves Black's position too passive after'} 12. h6 Bf8 13. Bh3 Nd7 14. Bg5 $36 {Alexei Shirov: '!'}) 12. h6 Bf8 13. Bg5 Be7 $10 {Alexei Shirov: ', as'} 14. Bxf6 $140 Bxf6 15. exd5 cxd5 16. Nxd5 Qa5+ 17. Nc3 Bxd4 18. Qb5+ Nc6 $1 {Alexei Shirov: 'is good for him.'}) 11... Nd7 12. b4 (12. exd5 exd5 13. Bf4 Qb6 14. Qe3+ {Alexei Shirov: 'looks dangerous but can be answered by'} Ne7 $11 {Alexei Shirov: ', since'} 15. Bd6 $140 $2 O-O $1 {Alexei Shirov: '!!'} 16. Bxe7 Rfe8 $17 {Alexei Shirov: 'is playable for Black, for example'} (16... Bxd4 17. Na4 $1 Qa5+ 18. Qd2 Qxa4 19. Bxf8 $13) 17. Ne2 (17. hxg6 Qxd4 $1 {allows Black to win back the piece with a strong position}) 17... Qa5+ $1 (17... Bf8 18. hxg6 hxg6 19. Bc5 Nxc5 20. dxc5 Bxc5 21. Qh6 Bd4 22. Kd1 Bg7 23. Qh4 Re5 $1 {with an initiative to compensate for White's extra piece.}) 18. c3 Qxa2 19. Rd1 Bf8 $19) 12... Ngf6 13. h6 $5 Bf8 14. Bf4 Qd8 $6 {Alexei Shirov: 'Although Black is not worse after this move, he certainly becomes very passive.'} (14... e5 $142 {Alexei Shirov: 'was called for, as Black needs to open the centre to show that White's position is vulnerable and full of weaknesses. White then has to try to swap some pieces, for example'} 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Bxe5 Qxe5 17. f4 Qe6 18. e5 {Alexei Shirov: 'and after'} Ne4 {Alexei Shirov: '(other knight moves might also be interesting)'} 19. Nxe4 dxe4 20. Bh3 Qd5 21. c4 $1 Qxd2+ 22. Kxd2 a5 $5 (22... Bxh6 23. Ke3 f5 24. exf6 Kf7 25. Bg4 Bf8 $13 {Alexei Shirov: 'is also okay for Black'}) 23. bxa5 Bc5 $1 24. Rxb7 O-O $10 {Alexei Shirov: 'the position should be about equal.'}) 15. Bd3 {Alexei Shirov: 'The plan chosen by Judit seems too slow and Black soon gets the upper hand.'} ({Alexei Shirov: 'Critical was'} 15. Be2 $142 {Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: ', when Black can choose between'} {Alexei Shirov: ', or'} Nb6 (15... Be7 16. e5 {Alexei Shirov: 'not'} Nh5 $2 (16... Ng8 { f8} 17. Nd1 b5 {with a slow but solid plan of ...Bf8 and ...Ne7}) 17. Be3 {xh5  f4 Alexei Shirov: 'threatening 18 f4'}) (15... Z0) 16. a4 Be7 17. a5 Nc8 $15 {Alexei Shirov: 'which seems equal to me.'}) 15... Be7 16. Ne2 $6 ({Alexei Shirov: 'Now'} 16. e5 {Alexei Shirov: 'would have been less strong but still preferable to the text-move. I intended to reply'} Nh5 17. Be3 Nxe5 $1 18. dxe5 d4 {Alexei Shirov: 'with an equal position after'} 19. Ne2 ({Alexei Shirov: 'or'} 19. Ne4 dxe3 20. fxe3 $13) 19... dxe3 20. Qxe3 $13 {Alexei Shirov: '.'}) 16... O-O 17. c3 b5 $1 $15 {Shirov: '!' '!' Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: 'Here, holding a slight advantage, I began feeling very ambitious, but as usual I had to be prepared for a fight against the clock.'} 18. Kf1 a5 19. a3 Nb6 20. Re1 Ne8 $5 {Alexei Shirov: 'A natural plan but one that allows White some curious counterplay for which Judit, of course, immediately goes.'} ({Alexei Shirov: 'Another possibility would have been'} 20... axb4 21. axb4 Ra3 $5 { a8 Alexei Shirov: ', intending'} 22. Z0 Qa8 {.}) 21. Be5 Nd6 22. Bg7 {Alexei Shirov: '!'} Ndc4 23. Qc1 ({Alexei Shirov: 'The correct decision as the 'active''} 23. Qf4 {Alexei Shirov: 'would also have been answered by'} Re8 {xa3 ×a3 Alexei Shirov: ', when the a3 pawn is hanging.'}) 23... Re8 24. e5 axb4 25. axb4 Ra2 26. Qf4 Rd2 27. Bb1 $1 Na4 $5 {[ץb1] Alexei Shirov: 'Fighting against the bishop on b1.'} 28. Kg2 Nab2 (28... Rxe2 29. Rxe2 Nxc3 30. Ree1 Bxb4 {Alexei Shirov: 'would smash White's pawn structure, but allows him a powerful initiative with'} 31. Bd3 $1 $13 {Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: '.'}) 29. Qg4 $1 ({Alexei Shirov: 'Avoiding'} 29. Ng3 $2 Bg5 30. Qg4 Nd1 $1 $19 {Shirov: '-+' '-+' Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: 'and wins.'}) 29... Na3 {Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: 'The bishop must be taken before it can be sacrificed on g6.'} 30. Nf4 Nxb1 31. Rxb1 Nd3 32. Nxd3 ({Alexei Shirov: 'White has to exchange another active piece as'} 32. Nh3 $6 {Alexei Shirov: 'fails to'} Qa8 $1 33. Ra1 Ra2 34. Rad1 Nb2 $17 {Alexei Shirov: ', with a clear advantage for Black.'}) 32... Rxd3 {Alexei Shirov: 'This is the position I had been aiming for. Black's pawns are still much better but the passivity of some of his pieces make the chances roughly equal. Now White commits hara-kiri.'} 33. Ra1 $2 {Alexei Shirov: 'Giving up one, then another pawn, and not getting anything in return.'} ({Alexei Shirov: 'The right idea was'} 33. Rhc1 $8 f5 $1 34. exf6 Bxf6 35. Ra1 $1 $15 {Shirov: '!' '!' Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: 'with an unclear game.'} Bxg7 36. hxg7 $15) 33... Rxc3 34. Ra7 Rc4 $1 $19 {Shirov: '!' '!' Alexei Shirov: '!' Alexei Shirov: 'Now Black is winning. White can only hope for time-trouble tricks.'} 35. Rha1 Rxb4 36. Qf4 c5 37. Rxe7 $5 Qxe7 38. Bf6 {Alexei Shirov: 'The purpose of'} Qc7 $1 {Alexei Shirov: 'is to meet'} 39. Ra6 (39. Bg5 {Alexei Shirov: 'with'} f5 {Alexei Shirov: '.'}) 39... Rxd4 40. Qg5 Ra4 41. Rd6 Raa8 42. Rc6 $5 {Alexei Shirov: 'Beautiful but insufficient.'} ({Alexei Shirov: 'or'} 42. Qh4 $5 Qb7 $1 43. Bd8 f5 44. Qf6 c4 45. Rb6 Qd7 46. Rd6 Raxd8 $1 47. Rxd7 Rxd7 $19 {Alexei Shirov: '.'}) ({Alexei Shirov: 'Black also wins after'} 42. Bd8 $2 f6) 42... Qa7 $1 ({Alexei Shirov: 'Not'} 42... Qxc6 $4 43. Be7 { f6  f6+- Alexei Shirov: ', intending Qf6 winning.'}) 43. Bd8 {Alexei Shirov: 'Offering another poisoned piece.'} ({Alexei Shirov: 'The rook sacrifice'} 43. Ra6 {Alexei Shirov: 'would now fail to'} Qxa6 44. Be7 f5 45. Qf6 Rxe7 46. Qxe7 Qa7 $19 {Alexei Shirov: 'winning.'}) 43... f6 44. Bxf6 c4 45. Qg4 Qf7 46. Qd4 Rec8 47. Qb6 Rxc6 48. Qxc6 Rb8 0-1

