{Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,J: '67/99 ''} 1. c4 {Polgar,J Shipov Polgar,J Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,J Polgar,Judit' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S Shipov,S: 'Polgar,J''} Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. e4 d6 4. d4 Bg7 5. f3 O-O 6. Be3 c5 7. Nge2 (7. d5 {leads to another version of the same kind of lines. White's idea is to play Nh3-f2, something Black should never allow. But as White will have to develop his knight from g1 before Black will have to play ...Nbd7, this should not be a big problem.}) 7... Nc6 8. d5 (8. Qd2 {is a true Sämisch King's Indian and beyond the scope of this book.}) 8... Ne5 9. Ng3 e6 10. Be2 exd5 11. cxd5 a6 12. a4 h5 ({Another option is the pawn sacrifice} 12... Bd7 13. O-O b5 $5 {which is very sharp, but probably OK:} 14. Z0 (14. axb5 axb5 15. Bxb5 ({or} 15. Rxa8 Qxa8 16. Bxb5 Bxb5 17. Nxb5 Qa6 {followed by ...Rb8 with full compensation}) 15... Bxb5 16. Nxb5 Qb6 {and Black regains the pawn:} 17. Qe2 Rab8 18. Na7 Qxb2 19. Qxb2 Rxb2 20. Rfb1 Rc2 21. Ra6 (21. Nb5 Nc4 22. Bf4 Nh5 $1 23. Nxh5 Bxa1 24. Rxa1 gxh5 {would favour Black}) 21... Nc4 22. Bf4 Ra8 23. h4 Nd7 24. Kh2 h5 25. Kh3 Nde5 26. Rb7 $4 Nd3 $1 {won a piece in Seirawan-Ivanchuk, Roquebrune (blitz) 1992.}) (14. h3 Rb8 $1 15. b3 ({or} 15. axb5 Bxb5 $1 16. Nxb5 axb5 17. b3 Ned7 18. Ra6 {with unclear play in B.Lalic-Timoshchenko, Piestany 1996; there was no reason for the players to agree a draw just yet}) 15... Ne8 $1 {(this is good in most lines here)} 16. Rc1 bxa4 $1 {(the standard reaction)} 17. bxa4 (17. f4 axb3 18. fxe5 Bxe5 {gives Black far more than enough for the piece}) 17... Rb4 $5 18. Bxa6 Qa5 19. Bb5 Bxb5 20. axb5 Nc7 21. Kh1 Nxb5 22. Nxb5 Qxb5 {and Black was better in Reilly-Nunn, Islington 1990.})) 13. O-O Nh7 14. Qd2 h4 15. Nh1 f5 (15... g5 {Shipov,Sergei} 16. Nf2 Qf6 17. h3 Bd7 18. Rab1 Rac8 19. Nfd1 Ng6 $1 $13 20. b4 $2 cxb4 21. Rxb4 Qxc3 $1 22. Nxc3 Bxc3 23. Qa2 Bxb4 $17 {Haba,P-Rasik,V/CZE/1994/0:1/34/}) 16. Nf2 Re8 (16... Bd7 $5 {is another possibility. Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S'} 17. Kh1 {Shipov,Sergei} Re8 18. exf5 gxf5 19. Nh3 Ng6 20. Rfe1 Qf6 21. f4 Re7 22. Bh5 Bh6 $132 {Vyzmanavin,A-Georgiev,Ki/Burgas/1993/0:1/55/}) 17. Kh1 Rb8 18. Rg1 Rf8 $146 {Shipov,Sergei: '!' '!' '!' Shipov,Sergei: ' 19.g3?! fe!/' Shipov,Sergei: ' 19.g3?! fe!/ Polgar,J: 'N'' Shipov: '!' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S: '!' Shipov,S: ' 19.g3?! fe! Polgar,J.''} (18... Kh8 {Ü 59/99 Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 59/99'' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 59/99' Polgar,J: '- 59/99 Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 59/99''' Polgar,J: '- 59/99 Shipov,S: '(Polgar,J) - 59/99''} 19. g3 {Shipov,Sergei} b5 20. axb5 axb5 21. gxh4 $1 Qxh4 22. Rg3 b4 23. Ncd1 Bd7 24. f4 $1 $16 {Vyzmanavin,A-Georgiev,Ki/Groningen/1993/1:0/41/}) 19. exf5 Bxf5 20. g4 (20. Nfe4 {Shipov,Sergei} h3 21. g3 Bxe4 22. fxe4 Nf3 23. Bxf3 Rxf3 $15) 20... hxg3 21. hxg3 (21. Rxg3 $5 {Endre Vegh: 'was worth considering.' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S: 'Polgar,J''}) 21... Qe7 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S: 'Polgar,J''} (21... b5 {Polgar,J: '!' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S'} 22. axb5 axb5 23. Kg2 $6 {0-1 (55) Gulko,B-Polgar,J Yerevan Olympiad 1996 [Endre Vegh] Polgar,J: '0-1 (55) Gulko,B (2615)-Polgar,J (2665) Yerevan 1996 CBM 101 theory [Shipov,S]'} (23. f4 $5 Nf7 24. g4 Bd7 25. Rg3 {looks better.}) (23. Nxb5 $6 {Shipov,Sergei} Rxb5 24. Bxb5 Nxf3 $17)) 22. Kg2 $6 (22. f4 $5 Nf7 23. g4 Bd7 24. Rg3) 22... b5 23. axb5 {Shipov,Sergei: '0-1 (55) Gulko,B (2615)-Polgar,J (2665) Yerevan (ol) 67/99 1996 CI1-130 [Polgar,Judit]'} axb5 {Shipov,Sergei: '' '' '' Shipov: ''} 24. Bh6 {Shipov,Sergei: '?!' '?!' '?!' Shipov: '?!'} (24. g4 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S: 'Polgar,J''} Bd3 $1 25. Bxd3 Nxf3 26. Qe2 Bxc3 27. bxc3 Rbe8 $44 {Endre Vegh: 'is dangerous for White,'}) (24. f4 {Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Judit' Polgar,J: 'Shipov,S: 'Polgar,J''} Nc4 25. Bxc4 bxc4) ({Endre Vegh: 'but'} 24. Rh1 $5 {Endre Vegh: 'was a possibility.' Shipov,Sergei: 'Polgar,Jud