1. e4 {Psakhis Psakhis,L Psakhis,Lev Psakhis,Lev Psakhis Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 O-O 8. Bd3 f5 9. Qh3 {Psakhis: 'Rare, double-edged move. Usual continuation is something like'} (9. exf6 {Psakhis} Rxf6 10. Bg5 Rf7 11. Qh5 g6 12. Qd1 Qa5 13. Bd2 Nbc6 14. Nf3 c4 15. Be2 Nf5 {with complicated game.}) 9... Qa5 (9... Qe8 {Ü 72/292 Psakhis,Lev: '(Polgar,Judit) Ü 72/292'}) 10. Bd2 Nbc6 {Psakhis: 'deserves attention'} (10... Qa4 {Psakhis} 11. dxc5 Nd7 {for example} 12. Nf3 Nxc5 13. O-O b6 14. Be3 Ng6 15. Rfd1 Ne4 16. Bd4 Ba6 17. Nd2 Rac8 18. Bxe4 dxe4 19. Qe3 Ne7 {0-1 Bragin,A-Rychagov,A/RUS t-ch Orel 1997 (24)}) 11. Nf3 Qa4 12. Rg1 (12. g4 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} c4 13. Be2 fxg4 14. Qxg4 Qxc2 15. Rg1 Qg6 16. Qh4 Nf5) ({White could play also} 12. Kd1 {Psakhis} Bd7 13. g4 cxd4 14. Rg1 {1-0 Ginzburg,M-Robledo,N/Buenos Aires FMDA tt 1992 (24) with big complications, but Judit never worried too much about pawns.}) 12... c4 13. Be2 Qxc2 14. Rc1 Qb2 15. g4 Na5 {Psakhis: '!' '!' Psakhis,Lev: '!' '!' Psakhis,L: '!'} 16. Bd1 Nb3 17. Rc2 Qxa3 {Psakhis: 'Judit sucrificed ( lost?) two pawns and only her chance for survival is just to give checkmate to oppenent. With real astonishment I found, that this crazy position came to life not in the first time , ant instead of Polgars,'} 18. Bh6 $146 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit: 'N''} ({Psakhis: 'Velimirovic played'} 18. Ng5 $5 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit: '!?''} h6 19. Nf3 (19. Nh7 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} Kxh7 20. Bxh6 gxh6 21. g5 Rf7) 19... Nxd2 20. Kxd2 fxg4 21. Rxg4 (21. Qxg4 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} Rf7) 21... Nf5 22. Nh4 Bd7 23. Nxf5 exf5 24. Rg1 Kh7 25. Qg2 Qe7 26. Qxd5 b5 $44 {Psakhis: '' '' Psakhis: '½-½ Velimirovic,D-Drasko,M/YUG t-ch 1996 (71)' Psakhis,Lev: '' '' Psakhis,Lev: '½-½ Velimirovic,D-Drasko,M/YUG t-ch 1996 (71) Polgar,Judit: ''' Psakhis,L: '' Psakhis: 'just one thing is interesting for me: did Judit know about this game?'}) 18... Ng6 (18... gxh6 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} 19. Qxh6 (19. gxf5+ Kh8 20. Qxh6 Nxf5) 19... Ng6 (19... f4 $2 20. Ng5 Rf7 21. Qh5) 20. gxf5 (20. Nh4 f4 21. Nxg6 hxg6 22. Qxg6+ Kh8) 20... Rxf5 21. Nh4 Qf8 22. Nxf5 Qxf5 23. h4 Qf8 24. Rxg6+ (24. Qg5 Kh8 25. h5 Ne7 26. Qf6+ Qxf6 27. exf6 Nf5) 24... hxg6 25. Qxg6+ Qg7 26. Qe8+ Kh7 27. Qh5+ Qh6 28. Qf7+ $11) ({White has dangerous attack after} 18... Na1 $6 {Psakhis} 19. Rd2 $1 (19. gxf5 $143 $2 Nxc2+ 20. Bxc2 Qxc3+ 21. Kd1 Nxf5 22. Bxf5 Rxf5 23. Rxg7+ Kf8 24. Rxh7+ Ke8 25. Be3 $13) 19... Qxc3 20. Bxg7 Kxg7 21. gxf5+ Kh8 (21... Ng6) 22. Qh6 Rf7 23. Ng5 $18) ({everithing is more complicated in the case of} 18... f4 {Psakhis} 19. Ng5 $1 Rf7 $8 (19... gxh6 20. Qxh6 Rf7 21. Qh5 $1 (21. Nxf7 Kxf7 22. Qxh7+ Ke8 23. g5 Na1 $5) 21... Ng6 22. Nxf7 $18) (19... Nxd4 20. Bxg7 $1 Nxc2+ 21. Kd2 $18) 20. Qh5 (20. Nxf7 Nxd4 $1 21. Rd2 Nb3) 20... Ng6 (20... g6 21. Qh4 {[%csl Rf6,Rg7,Rg8]}) 21. Nxf7 Na1 (21... Kxf7 22. Bxf4 $16) 22. Rd2 Kxf7 23. Bxf4 Kg8 $1 $132) 19. gxf5 Rxf5 (19... exf5 {Psakhis} 20. Rxg6 hxg6 21. Bf4 Na1 22. Rc1 (22. Ng5 Nxc2+ 23. Bxc2 Re8 24. Qh7+ Kf8 25. Qh8+ Ke7 26. Qxg7+ Kd8) 22... Kf7 23. Qh7 $40) 20. Be3 (20. Nh4 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} Nxd4 21. Nxg6 (21. Rd2 Rxe5+ 22. Kf1 Nf5) 21... Nxc2+ 22. Kf1 (22. Bxc2 Qa1+ 23. Bd1 hxg6 24. Rxg6 Rxe5+ 25. Kd2 Qb2+ 26. Bc2 Re2+) 22... hxg6 23. Rxg6 Qa1 24. Rxg7+ Kh8 25. Qg4 Ne3+ 26. Bxe3 Qxd1+ 27. Qxd1 Kxg7) 20... Bd7 (20... Na1 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} 21. Rc1 Nb3 22. Rc2) 21. Ng5 Nf8 {Psakhis: 'Black organized tough defence, but Judit found way to increase preasure on the black king'} (21... Rxg5 $5 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} 22. Rxg5 a5 23. Qg4 $13) 22. f4 {Psakhis: '!' '!' Psakhis,Lev: '!' '!' Psakhis,L: '!'} Na1 $2 {Psakhis: '?!' '?!' Psakhis,Lev: '?!' '?!' Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit: '?'' Psakhis,L: '?!' Psakhis: 'Knight moves too far.'} (22... Rxg5 $5 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} 23. Rxg5 Qe7 24. Rcg2 g6 25. Bc2) ({It,s funny what white will do after} 22... Qa1 $1 {Psakhis}) 23. Rcg2 Qxc3+ 24. Kf2 g6 {Psakhis: '?' '?' Psakhis,Lev: '?' '?' Psakhis,L: '?' Psakhis: 'Decisive mistake, it was obligatory to sucrifice exchange'} (24... Nb3 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} 25. Ne4 Rxf4+ 26. Bxf4) (24... Rxg5 $142 {Psakhis} 25. Rxg5 (25. fxg5 Nc2 $19) 25... g6 {with unclearconsequences.}) 25. Nxh7 {Psakhis: '+-!' '+-!' Psakhis,Lev: '+-!' '+-!' Psakhis,L: '+-!'} Rxf4+ (25... Nxh7 26. Rxg6+ Kh8 27. Qh6 Rf7 (27... Rxf4+ {Psakhis} 28. Bxf4 Qxd4+ 29. Be3 Qxe5 30. Qxh7+ $1 $18) 28. Rg7 Rxf4+ {Psakhis} 29. Qxf4 $18) 26. Bf3 Qc2+ (26... Nxh7 {Psakhis} 27. Rxg6+ Kh8 28. Bxf4 Qxd4+ 29. Be3 Qb2+ 30. Be2 Rf8+ 31. Kg2 $1 Qxe2+ 32. Kh1 Qxe3 $8 33. Qxe3 d4 34. Qxd4 Bc6+ 35. R6g2) 27. Kg3 Rxf3+ (27... Rf5 {Psakhis} 28. Rxc2 (28. Nf6+) 28... Nxc2 29. Qh6 $18) 28. Kxf3 Qe4+ (28... Nxh7 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} 29. Rxg6+ Kh8 30. Qxh7+ Kxh7 31. Rh6# {#}) 29. Kf2 (29. Kf2 Qc2+ (29... Qf5+ {Psakhis} 30. Qxf5 exf5 31. Nxf8 Kxf8 32. Rxg6 $18) 30. Kg3 Qd3 {Psakhis,Lev: 'Polgar,Judit'} (30... Nxh7 {Psakhis} 31. Rxc2 Nxc2) 31. Nf6+ Kf7 32. Qh6 Nc2 33. Rxc2 Qxc2 34. Rf1) 1-0

