1. e4 {Hansen,Cu Hansen,Cu Hansen,Cu Hansen,Cu} e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. d4 Nxe4 4. Bd3 d5 5. Nxe5 Nd7 6. Nxd7 Bxd7 7. O-O Be7 8. c4 Nf6 9. Nc3 Be6 10. c5 $14 { White is slightly better because of his spaceadvantage on the -side.} O-O 11. Bf4 c6 12. b4 Qd7 {[%cal Ye6f5] Le6-f5 Just like in many other openings where black places his s on white - Ortodox Queensgamit or French Defence for instance - the exchange of whitesquared bishops would make things easier for him. Hansen,Cu: 'Just like in many other openings where black places his s on white - Ortodox Queensgamit or French Defence for instance - the exchange of whitesquared bishops would make things easier for him.'} 13. Qc2 g6 14. b5 {Blacks problems has to do with the combination of white been able to open the b, and at the same time control the square b8. Making it impossible for blacks s to oppose whites in the open line.} Rfe8 15. a4 (15. Rab1 $5) 15... Nh5 16. Be3 Bd8 {[%cal Yd8a5] This move improves blacks position but that could also have been done by:} (16... Ng7 $5 {[%cal Ye6f5,Yg7f5] e6-f5/g7-f5}) 17. a5 {[%cal Ya5a6] a5-a6} a6 $8 18. bxa6 bxa6 19. Na4 {White has to sacrifice something to make progress. Another idea would be to play: Hansen,Cu: 'White has to sacrifice something to make progress. Another idea would be to play:'} (19. Rfb1 $5 {[%cal Yb1b6] Tb6}) 19... Bxa5 20. Nb6 Bxb6 21. cxb6 Bf5 $2 {Now white will regain her  with a big advantage.} (21... Qb7 $8 22. Rfb1 Ng7 $14) 22. Bxf5 Qxf5 23. Rfc1 (23. Qxc6 $5 $16) 23... Qxc2 24. Rxc2 a5 25. Rxc6 Reb8 26. Bh6 $1 Ng7 {Van der Sterren had to keep an eye both on the dangerous b6- and his backrank. It does not seem that blacks position could be defended: Hansen,Cu: 'Van der Sterren had to keep an eye both on the dangerous b6- and his backrank. It does not seem that blacks position could be defended:'} (26... f5 27. h3 a4 (27... Rb7 28. Rac1 Rab8 29. g4 Ng7 30. R1c5 $16) 28. g4 Ng7 29. Bxg7 $1 Kxg7 30. Rc7+ Kf6 31. Ra7 $18) (26... a4 27. g4 Ng7 28. Rac1 $16 {[%cal Yb6b7,Yh6f4] b7/f4}) 27. Rac1 Ne8 28. Bf4 Rb7 29. Rc8 Rxc8 30. Rxc8 Kf8 31. Bd6+ Kg7 32. Rxe8 Rxb6 33. Bf8+ Kf6 34. g3 1-0

