re from far too many directions. Hansen,Cu: 'The exchanges has taken the dynamic out of White's position. His centre is under attack and because of the misplaced b3 there is no active continuation. The conclusion of the opening battle seems to me to be: From a strategic point of view the build-up of the white -centre f3-e4-d5 was a good idea. However that was only possible by an extremely slow build-up a1-c1, f3-d2, e2-e3-e4. Black has just gained too much extra time and is tactically able to stop White from getting a harmoniously setup of his minor-pieces.' Now White's position comes under pressure from far too many directions.   Hansen,Cu: 'The exchanges has taken the dynamic out of White's position. His centre is under attack and because of the misplaced b3 there is no active continuation. The conclusion of the opening battle seems to me to be: From a strategic point of view the build-up of the white -centre f3-e4-d5 was a good idea. However that was only possible by an extremely slow build-up a1-c1, f3-d2, e2-e3-e4. Black has just gained too much extra time and is tactically able to stop White from getting a harmoniously setup of his minor-pieces.'  Tisdall,Jonathan D: 'Now white's position comes under pressure from far too many directions.   Hansen,Cu: 'The exchanges has taken the dynamic out of whites position. His center is under attack and because of the misplaced b3 there is no active continution. The conclusion of the opening-battle seems to me to be: From a strategical point of view the build-up of the white -center f3-e4-d5 was a good idea. However that was only possible by a extremely slow build-up a1-c1, f3-d2, e2-e3-e4. Blacks just gained to much extra time and was tactically able to stop white from getting a harmoniously setup of his minor-pieces.''} 20. Nd2 Qa4 (20... Bxd5 {was possible; was possible;} 21. Qd3 (21. a4 $5 {Tisdall,Jonathan D: 'Polgar,Judit: '''}) 21... Be6 22. a4 {creates some counterchances so Black rules even here. cre