1. e4 {Dautov Dautov Dautov Dautov Dautov Lukacs} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. f4 {Lukacs: 'From time to time this aggressive plan attracts the attacking players, who want to avoid the solid positional main lines.'} (6. h4 {Lukacs is the popular main line.}) 6... e6 7. Nf3 {Lukacs: 'White has an enormous pressure on e5, but after the inevitable c6-c5 sometimes he regrets the weakening of the g1-a7 .'} Bd6 8. Be2 $146 {Lukacs: 'White wants to keep his , although the  on g6 is well-posted.'} (8. Bd3 Ne7 9. O-O Nd7 10. Kh1 (10. Ne5 {Lukacs} Qb6 $6 (10... Qc7 {is the usual plan.}) 11. Nc4 Qc7 12. Bxg6 hxg6 13. Ne4 Nc8 {Now the  is badly placed here.} 14. a4 Be7 15. b3 {in order to activate the  on the a3-f8 .} Nd6 16. Ncxd6+ Bxd6 17. Nxd6+ Qxd6 18. Ba3 Qc7 19. Qd2 $14 {and suddenly the  becomes strong, Socko-Burmakin, Pardubice op 1993.}) (10. Ne4 Bc7 {and it is not easy for White to go ahead.}) 10... Qc7 11. Ne5 Rd8 {Lukacs: 'c6-c5 will come soon.'} 12. Qe2 Bxd3 13. Nxd3 O-O 14. Bd2 c5 15. Ne4 Nf5 $11 {Marshall,F-Capablanca,J/New York 1927} (15... Nf5 16. dxc5 Nxc5 $11 {and it is time to regret f4, Marshall-Capablanca, New York 1927.})) (8. Bc4 Ne7 9. O-O Nd7 10. Ne5 Nf6 11. c3 Qc7 {Lukacs: 'It is not easy for White to continue his march ahead because Black can fully blockade the light squares.'} 12. Qe2 O-O 13. Be3 c5 {Lukacs: 'Soon or later this comes, and White's  becomes shaky.'} 14. dxc5 Bxc5 15. Bxc5 Qxc5+ 16. Kh1 Rad8 $11 {Stoltz,G-Flohr,S/Bled 1931 Lukacs: 'Stoltz-Flohr, Bled 1931'}) 8... Ne7 (8... Nd7 {Lukacs} 9. O-O Qc7 10. Ne5 Ne7 11. c3 (11. h4 $6 {is illogical, when White has already castled .} O-O-O 12. Qe1 (12. h5 $4 {is only a dream, because after} Nxe5 13. fxe5 Bxe5 $19 {White has to wake up.}) 12... f6 13. Nd3 Nf5)) 9. Ne5 $2 {Ein grober Fehler im Sinne des Spiels auf Gewinn (J.Polgar lag mit 0:1 zurück und mußte diese Partie unbedingt gewinnen, um auszugleichen). Schwarz kann nun direkt ins Endspiel übergehen, ein Partie