1. e4 {Ftacnik Ftacnik Ftacnik,L Ftacnik} c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Be2 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. Be3 O-O 9. f4 Bd7 10. Qe1 Nxd4 11. Bxd4 Bc6 12. Qg3 g6 13. Bd3 {The lines with early Qe1-g3 manouver are coming back, black must refresh some dfensive ideas.} Nd7 14. Kh1 Bh4 (14... e5 15. fxe5 (15. Be3 exf4 16. Bxf4 Bh4 17. Qh3) 15... Bh4 16. Qh3 (16. Qf4 Bg5 17. Qf2 dxe5 18. Bxa7 $2 b6 $17) 16... dxe5 17. Be3 $14) 15. Qh3 e5 16. Be3 (16. fxe5 dxe5 17. Be3 $14) 16... exf4 17. Bxf4 Ne5 (17... Be7 18. Rad1 $14) 18. Bxe5 dxe5 19. Rad1 Bg5 20. Bc4 Qc8 $6 (20... Qc7 21. Bb3 Rad8 22. Nd5 Bxd5 23. exd5 $14) 21. Rxf7 $1 {The charms of Sicilian defense! Black must always be prepared to be assaulted in an unexpected way. Fortunatelly for him the matter is not so serious here.} Qxh3 (21... Rxf7 22. Bxf7+ Kg7 (22... Kxf7 23. Qxh7+ Ke6 24. Qxg6+ Bf6 25. Nd5 Bxd5 26. exd5+ Ke7 27. Rf1 Qh8 28. d6+ Ke6 29. Qf5+ Kf7 30. g4 $18) 23. Be6 $16) 22. Rxf8+ Kxf8 23. gxh3 Rb8 (23... Rd8 24. Bd5 $14) 24. Kg2 (24. a4 a6 25. Bd5 Be8 $14) 24... b5 25. Bd5 Be8 26. Rf1+ Kg7 27. a3 a5 28. Ne2 Rb6 {Black has managed to prove, that white's main claim to advantage - a spare double pawn on h file- is not so critical.} (28... Rc8 29. c3 a4 30. Nc1 $1) 29. Nc1 $1 Bf4 30. Nd3 g5 31. h4 (31. b4 axb4 32. axb4 Ra6 33. h4 Rh6 34. hxg5 Rxh2+ 35. Kg1 Rxc2 36. Nxf4 exf4 37. Rxf4 Rd2 $14) 31... Rh6 $1 32. hxg5 (32. Nxf4 gxf4 33. b4 axb4 34. axb4 Rxh4 35. c4 bxc4 36. Rc1 $11) 32... Rxh2+ 33. Kg1 Rxc2 34. Nxf4 exf4 35. Rxf4 Rxb2 36. Rf6 Rb1+ (36... b4 $1 37. Ra6 (37. axb4 axb4 38. Rb6 Ba4 39. Rb8 Kg6 40. Rg8+ Kh5 41. e5 Kg4 $17) 37... bxa3 38. Rxa5 Kg6 39. Rxa3 Kxg5 $11) 37. Kf2 Ra1 $2 {[%mdl 8192] A bit reckless move in an equal position, black misses the mating idea.} (37... b4 $11) 38. Ra6 Rxa3 (38... Rc1 39. Ra8 Kf8 40. Rxa5 $16) 39. Ra8 $1 Kg6 (39... Bf7 40. Ra7 $18) (39... Bg6 40. Rg8#) 40. Rxe8 Kxg5 41. e5 b4 42. e6 Rd3 43. Rg8+ Kf6 44. Rf8+ (44. Rf8+ Ke7 45. Rf7+ Kd6 (45... Kd8 46. Bc6 $18) 46. Rd7+ Ke5 47. e7 $18) 1-0

