1. d4 {Golod,V Golod,V Golod,V} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 O-O 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. Qxc3 b6 7. Bg5 Bb7 8. e3 d6 9. Ne2 {White's plan is: c2,e4(control over point e4).Besides,white has two principales moves: Golod,V: 'White's plan is: c2, e4 (control over the e4-square). Besides this, White has two main moves:' Golod,V: 'White's plan is: c2, e4 (control over the e4-square). Besides this, White has two main moves:'} (9. f3 $5 {See comments to Kasparov,G-Karpov,A/ Frankfurt,1999/CBM 72(1-0)(Golod,V)(43)}) ({and} 9. Nf3 $5 {See comments to Dreev,A-Razuvaev,Y/St. Petersburg,1998/CBM 67(1-0) (Golod,V)(40)}) 9... Nbd7 {c5(×d4) and so on. Golod,V: 'c5(×d4) and so on.'} 10. Qc2 {[%csl Re4][%cal Ge2c3]} h6 $5 $146 ({Good enough:} 10... c5 {(was checked in the previous games).} 11. Nc3 cxd4 12. exd4 Qc7 13. Bd3 Rac8 (13... h6 $5 14. Bh4 Rfc8 15. O-O d5 16. Bg3 Qc6 17. cxd5 Nxd5 18. Be4 N7f6 19. Nxd5 Qxc2 20. Nxf6+ gxf6 21. Bxc2 Rxc2 22. b4 Rd8 $15 {½-½ Sokolov,I-Timman,J/Amsterdam,1996 (22) Golod,V: '½-½ Sokolov,I-Timman,J/Amsterdam,1996 (22)'}) 14. O-O Ba6 15. Qa4 (15. Rfc1 $5 Bxc4 $140 16. Nd1 $11) 15... Bxc4 16. Nb5 Bxb5 17. Bxb5 $44 {Ivanchuk,V-Topalov,V/Linares,1999(½-½) (60) Golod,V: 'Ivanchuk,V-Topalov,V/Linares,1999(½-½) (60)'}) 11. Bh4 $140 c5 {Just so!} ({After:} 11... e5 $2 12. d5 {white has a big positional advantage. Golod,V: 'White has a big positional advantage.'}) 12. dxc5 $6 {[%mdl 16384]} ({In my opinion better is:} 12. Rd1 $11) 12... bxc5 {This move better than: Golod,V: 'This move is better than:'} (12... dxc5 13. Rd1 Qe7 14. Nc3 Rfd8 $11) ({or} 12... Nxc5 $6 13. Rd1 Qe7 $140 (13... g5 14. Bg3 Nce4 15. f3 Nxg3 16. hxg3 Kg7 17. Nd4 $14) 14. Bxf6 $1 Qxf6 (14... gxf6 $14) 15. b4 $1 $14 {[%csl Rd6]} (15. Rxd6 $4 Ne4 $19 {[%csl Rd6,Rf2]})) 13. Nc3 ({Another alternative is:} 13. Rd1 Qb6 (13... d5 $5 14. cxd5 exd5 15. Bxf6 Qxf6 16. Nf4 {[%csl Rd5]} d4 (16... Nb6 $5) (16... Rab8 $5 {[%csl Rb2]}) 17. Bb5 $13) 14. Nc3 d5 {Golod,V: '-transfer to 13.d1' Golod,V: '-transfer to 13.d1'} 15. cxd5 exd5 16. Qd2 {[%csl Yd1,Yd2] e2,0-0 with equal game. Golod,V: 'e2,0-0 with a level game.' Golod,V: 'e2,0-0 with a level game.'}) 13... d5 14. O-O-O $6 {[%mdl 16384] Again strategical blunder. Much better is: Golod,V: 'Again, a strategical blunder. Much better is:'} (14. Rd1 Qb6 {-transfer to 13.d1}) 14... Qb6 $15 15. Bg3 ({Can be recommended: Golod,V: 'What can be recommended is:'} 15. cxd5 exd5 16. Bd3 $15) 15... Bc6 $5 {[%cal Yc6a4] 16...d4 Golod,V: '16...d4'} ({Badly right away: Golod,V: 'Playing'} 15... d4 {because of: Golod,V: 'right away is bad, because of:'} 16. exd4 cxd4 17. Na4 {[%csl Rd4]}) 16. f4 $6 {[%mdl 16384] ×e4;g4 Golod,V: '×e4;g4'} ({Also dubious: Golod,V: 'Also dubious is:'} 16. f3 {in view of:} d4 17. exd4 cxd4 18. Bf2 e5 $36) ({Probably better is:} 16. Bd3 d4 17. Ne4 Nxe4 18. Bxe4 Bxe4 19. Qxe4 f5 20. Qc2 e5 $15) 16... Ng4 $1 {[%csl Re3]} ({Dubious: Golod,V: 'Dubious is:'} 16... d4 $2 {because of:} 17. exd4 cxd4 18. Bf2 {[%csl Rb6,Rd4]} Nc5 19. b4 (19. Bxd4 $4 Nb3+) 19... Qa6 {[%csl Ra3,Rc3]} 20. Bxd4 (20. Qa2 dxc3 21. Bxc5 Rfd8 $13) 20... Qxa3+ 21. Qb2 Nb3+ 22. Kc2 Nxd4+ 23. Rxd4 Qxb2+ 24. Kxb2 Rfd8 $11) 17. Bf2 ({Very weakly:} 17. Qe2 {because of: Golod,V: 'is very weak, because of:'} d4 18. exd4 cxd4 19. Qxg4 dxc3 $19) ({After:} 17. Qd2 $6 Rab8 {[%csl Rb2,Yd2,Re3][%cal Gg4e3,Yd2b2,Yd2e3] black has a strong initiative. Golod,V: 'Black has a strong initiative.'}) 17... Ndf6 {With the idea:18...xf2 19.xf2 g4 and 20...d4 Golod,V: 'With the idea:18...xf2 19.xf2 g4 and 20...d4'} 18. Bg1 (18. h3 $143 Nxf2 19. Qxf2 Rfd8 {20...ab8(קb2) and 21...d4 Golod,V: '20...ab8(קb2) and 21...d4'}) 18... Rfd8 $5 19. h3 $140 Nxe3 $1 20. Bxe3 d4 {[%csl Rc3,Re3]} 21. Bd3 $2 ({It is necessary:} 21. Bd2 dxc3 22. Bxc3 Rxd1+ 23. Qxd1 Ne4 $15) 21... dxe3 $17 22. Rde1 (22. Qe2 $2 Rab8 $19 {[%csl Rb2,Rg2]}) ({More stubborn resistance after: Golod,V: 'More stubborn resistance is put up after:'} 22. Rhe1) 22... Nh5 $1 {[%csl Rf4]} 23. Rxe3 ({Loses right away:} 23. Rhf1 Ng3 24. Rg1 Qc7 {[%csl Rf4]} 25. Rxe3 Qxf4 26. Rge1 Rd4 $19) ({and} 23. f5 Nf4 {[%csl Rd3,Ge3,Rg2]} 24. Rxe3 $140 Nxg2 25. Rg3 Ne3 $1 26. Rxe3 Bxh1 $19) 23... Nxf4 {[%csl Rg2]} 24. Bh7+ Kh8 25. Rf1 ({Slightly better is:} 25. Be4) 25... Nxg2 26. Rg3 Qc7 $19 {[%csl Rg3,Rh7][%cal Yc7f7]} 27. Ne2 Qe5 ({Also win: Golod,V: 'Also winning is:'} 27... f5) 28. Qc3 {[%csl Rg7]} (28. Rxf7 {is refuted by:} Ba4 $1 29. Qxa4 (29. b3 Ne3 30. Qc3 Rd1+ 31. Kb2 Nxc4+ $1 32. bxc4 Rb8+ {[%csl Rb2,Re2] and mate in 5 moves.}) 29... Qxe2 30. Rfxg7 (30. Rd3 Ne3 $19 {[%csl Rc1,Rd3,Rh7][%cal Ge2e1]}) 30... Qe1+ 31. Kc2 Ne3+ 32. Rxe3 (32. Kb3 Qd1+ {[%csl Ra4]}) 32... Rd2+ 33. Kb3 Rb8+ 34. Ka2 Rbxb2#) ({Also loses: Golod,V: 'Nother losing move is:'} 28. Rg1 Rab8 $1 29. R3xg2 $140 Qe3+ 30. Kb1 Bxg2 31. Rxg2 Rd2 $19) 28... Qxc3+ 29. Nxc3 Kxh7 30. Rxf7 Rg8 {[%csl Rg7,Yg8][%cal Yg8g7] The rest it is of no importance. Golod,V: 'The rest is of no importance.'} 31. Rc7 Rac8 32. Rgxg7+ Rxg7 33. Rxc8 Bf3 {Whole this game despite the white's mistakes Judit Polgar conducted very strong. Golod,V: 'White's mistakes notwithstanding, Judit Polgar conducted the whole of this game very strongly.'} 0-1

