1. e4 {Lukacs Lukacs Lukacs Lukacs Lukacs: 'Lukacs,Peter Lukacs,Peter: 'Lukacs''} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 {This is the old main line.} (7... Nf6 {is more and more popular these days.}) 8. h5 {White's main advantage is his space advantage on the  thanks to his h5 . However in some situation it may also become weak.} Bh7 9. Bd3 {White has to change the strong h7 .} Bxd3 10. Qxd3 Ngf6 11. Bf4 (11. Bd2 Qc7 {- 11.f4}) 11... Qa5+ {trying to force back the .} 12. Bd2 (12. c3 $5) 12... Qc7 {Lukacs: '- 11.f4''Lukacs,Peter: 'Lukacs: '- 11.f4'''} 13. O-O-O e6 14. Ne4 {White wants to bring his passive  into action.} (14. Qe2 { e5 is the other possibility.}) 14... Bd6 {Seirawan's idea. Black is not afraid of exchanging his  for the .} (14... O-O-O 15. g3 Nxe4 16. Qxe4 Bd6 {is the usual move order here.}) 15. g3 (15. Kb1 $5) 15... Nxe4 16. Qxe4 O-O-O {Lukacs: 'is the usual m'Lukacs,Peter: 'Lukacs: 'is the usual move order here.''' ove order here.'} 17. Qe2 {Pure prophylactic against f6.} (17. c4 c5 18. d5 {Arakhamia-Van der Sterren, Sydney Mercantile 1991CBM 23} (18. Bc3 {Thipsay-Prakash, Chalapathi GM 2000 CBM 77})) 17... Rhe8 { e5} 18. Kb1 b5 $6 {This is a regular positional mistake. Black wants to secure his 's position on d5, but after c2-c4 the c6  and the  becomes weak.} (18... e5 {was the consequent continuation.} 19. dxe5 Nxe5 20. Nxe5 Bxe5 21. Be3 b6 22. a3 Kb7 23. Rhe1 Bf6 24. Qc4 Rd7 25. Ka2 Qd8 26. Qg4 Re6 27. Rxd7+ Qxd7 $11 {Liu Dede-Adianto, Yangon zt playoff 1998}) (18... a6 19. c4 c5 20. Bc3 cxd4 21. Rxd4 Be7 22. Rg4 Bf6 23. Bxf6 gxf6 {Black's  structure is a bit corrupted, but it is not easy to exploit it.} 24. c5 (24. Rg7 Nc5 25. Rh7 Rh8 26. Rxh8 Rxh8 27. Rd1 Rd8 $11 {and White's advantage would be significant only in a  .}) 24... Ne5 25. Rf4 {(Watson-Van der Sterren, Budapest 1989)} Nxf3 $1 26. Rxf3 Qc6 27. Re1 f5 $11) (18... Nf6 19. c4 (19. Ne5 $6 c5 20. Bf4 Nd5) 19... c5 (19... e5 $6 {now is already late:} 20. c5 Bf8 21. dxe5 ({but not} 21. Nxe5 $2 Rxd4) 21... Bxc5 22. Qc4 Nd7 23. Qxf7 Re7 24. Qc4 Bxf2 25. Bf4 $16 {with a strong  on e5.}) 20. Bc3 $14) (18... Re7 19. c4 c5 20. Bc3 Nf6 21. Ne5 cxd4 22. Rxd4 Bxe5 23. Rxd8+ Qxd8 24. Bxe5 Rd7 25. Bc3 Qb6 26. g4 $16 {Kasparov-Vukic, EU-chT Skara 1980}) 19. c4 $5 {White immediately attacks the targets on the c .} (19. Rhe1 Nb6 (19... Nf6 20. Ne5) 20. Ba5 $14) 19... bxc4 20. Qxc4 Nb6 21. Qc2 Nd5 ({On} 21... Kb7 {follows} 22. Ba5 $14 {with a nasty pin.}) 22. Rc1 (22. Ne5 $5 Bxe5 (22... Kb7 23. Nc4 {× a5} Ka8 24. Ba5 Nb6 25. Rc1 $16 {× c6}) 23. dxe5 Qxe5 (23... Kb7 24. f4 $16 {with a better  structure.}) 24. Qxc6+ Kb8 (24... Qc7 25. Qa6+ $1 (25. Qa8+ $4 Kd7) (25. Qxc7+ Nxc7 26. Bc3 f6 $14 {is an only slightly worse .}) 25... Qb7 (25... Kb8 26. Ba5 $14) 26. Qe2 Qb6 (26... Kb8 27. Qe5+) 27. Rc1+ Kb7 $14) 25. Qb5+ Ka8 26. Ka1 Rc8 27. Rc1 $14) 22... Kb7 23. Ne5 $1 Bxe5 24. dxe5 Rc8 25. Rhe1 Qb6 26. Be3 $1 $16 {White is happy to exchange his  for the wonderful  on d5.} (26. f4 Qf2 $132) 26... Qb5 (26... Nxe3 $2 {brings only the enemy  into action.} 27. Rxe3 Ka8 28. Rc3 $18) 27. Bc5 Red8 28. Re4 Rd7 29. Rd4 (29. Rc4 $16) 29... Ka8 (29... Rcd8 30. Bd6 $16 {and the  kills the rooks.}) 30. Qd2 ({Or} 30. Bd6 Rb7 31. Rc4) 30... Rb7 31. f4 Rcb8 32. b3 Qa6 33. Kb2 {White can strengthen his position slowly but surely.} Rb5 34. Qd3 (34. Bd6 R8b7 (34... Rc8 35. a4) (34... Ra5 $2 {puts the  to an inferior place.} 35. a4 Rc8 36. Rdc4) 35. Qd3 $16) 34... Qa5 35. Bd6 Rc8 36. Rdc4 Nb6 {Finally Black cannot defend his weak  anymore.} ({On} 36... Rb6 {follows the unexpected breakthrough by} 37. f5 $1) 37. Rxc6 $18 Rxc6 38. Rxc6 Rd5 39. Qc3 Rd2+ 40. Kc1 (40. Kb1 $1 {was simpler.} Qxa2+ (40... Qd5 41. Rc8+ $18) (40... Rd1+ 41. Kc2 $18) 41. Kc1 $18) 40... Qxc3+ 41. Rxc3 Rxa2 42. Rc7 Rg2 43. Rxf7 Rxg3 44. f5 $1 {creating a decisive .} exf5 45. e6 Rg1+ (45... Rc3+ 46. Kb2 ({or} 46. Kd2 Rc6 47. Rf8+ Kb7 48. e7 Rxd6+ 49. Kc2 Rc6+ 50. Kb2 Re6 51. e8=Q Rxe8 52. Rxe8 $18) 46... Re3 47. e7 Nc8 48. Bc5 $18) 46. Kd2 Rg2+ 47. Kd3 Nc8 48. Be5 1-0

