1. e4 {Lukacs Lukacs Lukacs} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Ng5 Ngf6 6. Bd3 e6 7. N1f3 Bd6 8. Qe2 h6 9. Ne4 Nxe4 10. Qxe4 Qc7 11. Qg4 Kf8 {This is Karpov's favourite line against the modern variation.} 12. Nd2 {There are certainly many other tries here. White wants to activate his  on c4.} e5 13. Nc4 Nb6 $1 $146 {This is an important novelty here.} (13... Nc5 {- Anand-Karpov, Dos Hermanas 1999 CBM 71}) 14. Qh4 (14. Qe4 Nxc4 ({In case of} 14... f5 $6 15. Qh4 {is already stronger, because White has created some weaknesses on the .} Nxc4 (15... e4 16. Be2 $14) 16. Bxc4 $36) 15. Bxc4 exd4 16. Qxd4 {Lukacs: '- 14.e4'} Bf5 (16... Be5 17. Qh4 Bf5 {- 14.h4}) 17. Bb3 Re8+ 18. Be3 c5 19. Qc4 Be6 20. Qc3 Bxb3 21. axb3 b6 22. O-O-O Be5 23. Qd3 g6 24. Qd7 Kg7 $11) 14... Nxc4 15. Bxc4 Bf5 $1 {Now Black is playing for an advantage!} (15... exd4 16. Qxd4 {- 14.e4}) 16. dxe5 Bxe5 {Lukacs: '- 14.h4'} 17. O-O $2 {White gives a  for some activity, but this is not quite sufficient.} (17. Bb3 Rd8 18. O-O Rd4 19. f4 Re4 20. c3 Qb6+ 21. Kh1 Bf6 $15 {and suddenly White has problems with his development.}) 17... Bxc2 (17... g5 $5 18. Qh5 Bxc2 {is also interesting.}) 18. Re1 Bg6 (18... Re8 19. Be3 (19. Bd2 g5 $1) 19... g5 $1 $19 {with a healthy  up.}) 19. f4 $5 {White has to play actively.} (19. Re2 Kg8 20. Be3 Kh7 $17 {and connecting the rooks on the eights rank, Black can begin to convert his  advantage.}) 19... Bd4+ (19... Bf6 {was also tempting.} 20. Qh3 (20. Qf2 Qb6 21. Be3 Qxb2 $19) (20. Qg4 h5 21. Qg3 h4) 20... Qa5 21. Be3 Kg8) 20. Be3 Qb6 (20... Bxb2 21. Rad1 Bf6 22. Qg4 Qa5) 21. Qf2 Bxe3 (21... c5 22. Rad1 Rd8 23. Bxd4 cxd4 24. Re5 $44) (21... Rd8 22. Rad1) 22. Rxe3 {White has to keep the queens on the board.} (22. Qxe3 $6 Qxe3+ 23. Rxe3 Re8 24. Rae1 Rxe3 25. Rxe3 h5 26. Kf2 h4 27. b4 Rh5 $17) 22... Re8 23. Rae1 Rxe3 24. Rxe3 {and Black is still suffering because of his undeveloped .} Bf5 25. Kf1 $6 {This is a serious inaccuracy.} (25. Kh1 Qd8 26. Re5 g6 27. Qxa7 {gets back the .} Kg7 $11) 25... Qd8 26. Qe1 (26. Re5 Bd3+ 27. Bxd3 Qxd3+ 28. Kg1 b6) 26... b6 27. Qb4+ c5 (27... Kg8 {allows the penetration after} 28. Qe7) 28. Qa4 (28. Qc3 Kg8 29. h3) 28... g5 $2 {Black gives back the material without any fight.} (28... a5 {was the last chance to fight for an advantage in the .} 29. Qc6 (29. Bd5 g5 $1 30. Qc6 gxf4 31. Rf3 Kg7 32. Rxf4 Qg5 33. g3 Rd8 $17) 29... g6 30. Bd5 (30. Qb7 Qd1+ 31. Kf2 (31. Re1 Bd3+) 31... Qc2+ 32. Be2 Qxb2 $19) 30... Bd7 (30... Kg7 31. Qb7 Bd7) 31. Qd6+ Kg7 32. Kf2 Ba4 33. Qe5+ Qf6 $17) 29. fxg5 hxg5 30. Qxa7 {Now materially it is equal again.} Bg6 (30... Qd1+ 31. Re1 Bd3+ 32. Bxd3 Qxd3+ 33. Re2 $11) 31. h3 Kg7 32. Qe7 Qd4 33. Qe5+ Qxe5 34. Rxe5 Rh4 35. b3 g4 36. hxg4 Rxg4 37. Re7 Rf4+ 38. Kg1 Rf6 39. a4 Bf5 40. a5 1/2-1/2

