 $5 {See comments to Ahlander,B-Wedberg,T/Stockholm,1999/ CBM 73(1-0) (Golod,V)(43)}) 8... f5 (8... Nc6 $5 9. cxd5 exd5 {/= Golod,V: '/='}) 9. cxd5 $146 {Except of this move white have also.} (9. a3 $5 Ba5 (9... Qa5 10. Rb1 Bxc3+ 11. bxc3 cxd4 12. Rb5 $14) 10. Bxe4 (10. cxd5 $2 Nxc3 11. bxc3 Qxd5 $17 {[%csl Rg2][%cal Gc5c4]}) 10... fxe4 11. O-O (11. dxc5 $2 d4 12. b4 Bc7 13. Nxe4 d3 $17) 11... Nc6 12. cxd5 exd5 13. dxc5 Bxc3 14. Nxc3 Nxe5 15. Qb3 Nc4 16. Nxe4 Qe7 $132) (9. exf6 $5 Qxf6 (9... cxd4 $1 10. Nxd4 Nxf6 11. Nb3 $132) 10. O-O cxd4 11. cxd5 (11. Nxe4 dxe4 12. Bxe4 $14) 11... Nxf2 12. Bxh7+ Kh8 13. Nf4 $36 {[%cal Gf4g6]}) 9... cxd4 10. Bxe4 $1 ({Badly:} 10. a3 $2 Ba5 $140 11. Nxd4 {because of:} Qxd5 $17 {[%csl Rc3,Rd4]}) (10. Nxd4 $6 Qxd5 11. Nf3 Nc6 $15) 10... fxe4 11. Nxd4 $1 (11. Qxe4 $2 exd5 12. Qxd4 Nc6 13. Qd1 d4 14. a3 Be7 $15) 11... Qxd5 (11... exd5 12. O-O Bc5 (12... Nc6 13. Nxc6 bxc6 14. Nxe4 $1 $14) 13. Nb3 Bb6 14. Be3 Nc6 (14... Bxe3 15. fxe3 $14 {[%cal Gf1f8,Gb3d4]} Rxf1+ 16. Rxf1 Nc6 17. Rd1 $14) 15. Bxb6 axb6 $132) 12. Be3 {White solved opening problems and equalized.} Nd7 13. O-O {[%csl Re4]} Bxc3 14. Qxc3 Nxe5 $44 {Black with  over, but white have enough compensation.} 15. Rfd1 (15. Rad1 $5) 15... Qc4 ({It deserves attention:} 15... Nd3 16. f3 Qe5 17. fxe4 Nf4 18. Qc2 (18. Bxf4 Qxf4 19. Rf1 Qxe4 20. Rxf8+ Kxf8 21. Rf1+ Kg8 22. Nb5 Bd7 23. Rf7 Qb1+ 24. Rf1 Qg6 $17) 18... Nd5 19. Bf2 Nf6 20. Rac1 Qxe4 21. Re1 Qd5 (21... Qxc2 22. Rxc2 $44 {[%csl Re6]}) 22. Qc4 {[%csl Re6]} Ne4 23. Nxe6 $1 $11) 16. Qxc4 Nxc4 17. Nb5 b6 (17... a6 18. Nc7 Nxe3 (18... Rb8 $2 19. Ba7 $18) 19. fxe3 (19. Nxa8 Nxd1 20. Rxd1 e5 21. Nb6 Be6 22. b3 Kf7 $15) 19... Ra7 20. Rac1 $11) 18. Nc7 Rb8 19. b3 Rb7 (19... Nxe3 20. fxe3 e5 21. Rd5 Bb7 (21... Rb7 22. Rc1 $44) 22. Rxe5 Rbc8 23. Nb5 $132) 20. Nb5 (20. Rac1 Rxc7 21. Rxc4 Rxc4 22. bxc4 $11) 20... Nxe3 21. fxe3 {White keep enough compensation.} Rd7 (21... e5 22. Nd6 Rd7 23. Nxe4 Rfd8 24. Rxd7 Rxd7 25. Rc1 Bb7 26. Ng3 (26. Ng5 Rd2 27. e4 h6 28. Rc7 hxg5 29. Rxb7 Rxa2 $15) 26... Kf7 (26... Rd2 27. e4 $1 $11) 27. Rc2 Ke6 28. Kf2 $11) 22. Rxd7 Bxd7 23. Nd6 Bc8 (23... Bc6 24. Rc1 $44) 24. Rc1 Ba6 25. Nxe4 {The material equality is restored.} Rf5 26. b4 Re5 27. Nd6 Rd5 {Avoiding a trap:} (27... Rxe3 $2 28. b5 Rd3 29. Rc6 Rxd6 30. Rxd6 Bxb5 31. Rxe6 $16) 28. b5 Rxd6 29. bxa6 (29. bxa6 Rd7 30. Kf2 Kf7 31. Kf3 $11) 1/2-1/2

