1. e4 {Psakhis Psakhis,L Khalifman,Alexander} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 cxd4 7. Qg4 Ne7 8. bxa5 dxc3 9. Qxg7 Rg8 10. Qxh7 Nbc6 11. Nf3 Qc7 12. Bf4 Bd7 13. Bd3 O-O-O 14. Bg3 Qxa5 15. O-O Rh8 $1 {Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '!'' It is interesting why Judit decided to repeat this line - just two round ago Khalifman won nice game against Galkin - without preparing real improvement. Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'It is interesting why Judit decided to repeat this line - just two round ago Khalifman won nice game against Galkin - without preparing real improvement.''} 16. Qg7 $146 {Neil McDonald: '?' Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'N''} ({Neil McDonald: 'White will soon regret sparing the life of the f7 pawn. Instead the crucial line is'} 16. Qxf7 Rdf8 17. Qg7 Rhg8 18. Qh6 Rxf3 {Neil McDonald: 'etc. as in Galkin-Khalifman.'} 19. gxf3 Nd4 20. Qf4 Nef5 21. Kh1 Bb5 22. Rfd1 Bxd3 23. Rxd3 Qc5 24. Qc1 Kb8 $15 {0-1 Galkin,A-Khalifman,A/Hoogeveen Essent 2000/ (37)}) 16... d4 (16... f5 $6 {Khalifman,Alexander} 17. exf6 Rdg8 18. Qf7 Rf8 19. Ne5 $1 Nxe5 (19... Rxf7 20. Nxf7 $18) 20. Qxe7 Nc6 21. Qd6 $16) 17. Qg4 Nf5 $1 {[%mdl 4] Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '!'' Black manage to keep material balance ( rare achievement in this variation! ) and I think that his position already better. Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'Black manage to keep material balance ( rare achievement in this variation! ) and I think that his position already better.''} 18. Rfb1 {Khalifman,Alexander: '?!'} (18. Bxf5 {Khalifman,Alexander: '?!'} exf5 19. Qf4 Be6 {[%cal Ga5a4] Khalifman,Alexander: ''}) (18. Rfe1 {Khalifman,Alexander} Rhg8 (18... Nxg3 $5) 19. Qf4 Nxg3 20. hxg3 Qc5 $13) 18... Nxg3 {Eliminating main defender of e5 pawn. Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'Eliminating main defender of e5 pawn.''} (18... Rdg8 19. Qf4 Nxg3 20. hxg3 $13 (20. fxg3 $1 {Khalifman,Alexander} f5 21. exf6 e5 22. Qe4 Rg4 23. Qe2 $16) 20... f5 $1 {Khalifman,Alexander} 21. exf6 (21. Nxd4 Rg4 22. Nxc6 Bxc6 23. Qe3 f4 $17) 21... Qh5 $44) 19. Qxg3 {What else? Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'What else?''} (19. hxg3 $2 Nxe5 20. Qxd4 Nxf3+ 21. gxf3 Qh5 $17 {lose almost by force}) (19. fxg3 {Khalifman,Alexander} Nxe5 20. Qxd4 Nxf3+ 21. gxf3 Bc6 22. Qe3 Rh5 $36) 19... Qc7 $1 {[%cal Gc7g3] Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '!''} 20. Kf1 {Trying to escape fronm the dangerous zone. Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'Trying to escape fronm the dangerous zone.''} (20. Qf4 {Khalifman,Alexander: '!?'} f5 (20... f6 {Khalifman,Alexander} 21. Qxf6 Rdf8 22. Qg5 (22. Qg7 Rfg8) 22... Rhg8 (22... Rxf3 23. gxf3 Nxe5 24. Be4 $14) 23. Qh5 Rh8 $11) 21. Nxd4 {Khalifman,Alexander} Nxe5 22. Rb3 $132) (20. Qg7 {Khalifman,Alexander} f5 (20... Rdg8 21. Qf6 Qd8 22. Qxd8+ Rxd8 23. Be4) 21. exf6 Rdg8 (21... Ne5 22. Nxe5 Qxe5 23. Qg3 (23. h3 $2 Rdg8 24. Qf7 Bc6 25. Bg6 Qd5 26. f3 Be8 $19) 23... Qxf6 24. Rxb7 $1 Kxb7 25. Rb1+ $16) 22. Qf7 (22. Bh7 Rxg7 23. fxg7 Rd8 24. g8=Q Rxg8 25. Bxg8 Qf4 $15) 22... Rf8 (22... Ne5 23. Nxe5 Qxe5 24. g3) 23. Qg6 Qf4 $36) (20. Qg5 {Khalifman,Alexander} f5 $1 21. exf6 Rdg8 22. Qb5 (22. Qc5 Qf4 $36) 22... Rf8 $44) 20... Rhg8 {Neil McDonald: '!' Neil McDonald: 'The correct rook. The other one is needed to defend the d4 pawn, even if indirectly- see the note to move 23.'} 21. Qf4 (21. Qh4 Nxe5) 21... f5 $1 {[%cal Gg8g4] Neil McDonald: 'Khalifman borrows a trick from the McCutcheon Variation to assert control of the position. Of course, taking en passant now drops White's queen- apologies if you think I'm stating the obvious, but the first time someone played this move against me- it was the veteran American player Dan Mayers- it took me a little while to realise what was happening! As the pawn is immune, it is therefore transformed from a weakling on f7 to a monster on f5, where it controls the e4 square and supports the idea of Rg4 followed by doubling rooks on the g file. And indirectly it helps Black's attack by clearing the second rank so that his queen and rooks can cooperate together.'} ({Worth consideration and} 21... f6 $5 22. Qxf6 Rdf8 23. Qh4 {Khalifman,Alexander: ''} Nxe5) 22. h3 ({Not} 22. Nxd4 Rg4) 22... Kb8 $5 {Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '!?'' Khalifman hasn't reasons to hurry up and find  time to improve position of the king Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'Khalifman hasn't reasons to hurry up and find  time to improve position of the king''} 23. Re1 ({Neil McDonald: 'If'} 23. Nxd4 $2 {Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '?''} Nxd4 24. Qxd4 {Neil McDonald: 'when Black has the pleasant choice between'} Bc6 $19 {Neil McDonald: 'and Psakhis: '-+''} (24... Rxg2)) 23... Bc8 {[%cal Gb7b6]} 24. Ng5 {Khalifman,Alexander: '?!'} (24. Rad1 {Khalifman,Alexander} Qa5 $15) 24... Rd5 (24... Qg7 25. h4 Ne7 $5 $17 {[%cal Ge7d5,Ge7g6]}) 25. Nf3 $8 {Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '''} (25. Bc4 {Khalifman,Alexander} Rxe5 26. Rxe5 Nxe5 27. Bb3 Rg6 28. Re1 d3 $1 29. cxd3 (29. Rxe5 d2 30. Ke2 Rxg5 31. g3 b6 $19) (29. Re3 d2 30. Ke2 Rxg5 31. Qxg5 Qd6 $19) (29. Qxe5 d2 30. Qxc7+ Kxc7 $19) 29... Nxd3 30. Qxc7+ Kxc7 31. Re3 b6 $1 $17) 25... Ne7 {Khalifman,Alexander: '!'} (25... Qg7) 26. Rab1 ({Maybe} 26. Nxd4 $5 {Khalifman,Alexander: '?' was better, at least after posiible continuation} Ng6 27. Qe3 f4 28. Qe4 Rxe5 29. Qf3 Nh4 {Khalifman,Alexander: '-+'} 30. Rxe5 $8 Nxf3 31. Nxf3 $17 {White have chances for successful defence.}) 26... Ng6 27. Qh2 (27. Qg5 Rg7 $1 {[%csl Re5]}) (27. Qg3 $5 {Khalifman,Alexander} Rg7 28. Qh2) 27... Qh7 {Black's pieses coming to the king's fland one after another. Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'Black's pieses coming to the king's fland one after another.''} 28. Rb4 (28. Rb5 $5 Rd7 $5 {[%cal Gd7g7]}) (28. h4 {Khalifman,Alexander} Qh6 $17) 28... Nh4 $19 {Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '-+''} 29. Nxd4 {Neil McDonald: 'Judith Polgar tries to use her tactical prowess to save herself, but the FIDE World Champion doesn't let the win escape.'} (29. Nxh4 Qxh4 {[%csl Rf1,Rh2,Gh4] looks terrible for White} 30. a4 {Khalifman,Alexander} b6 31. Ra1 Bb7 $17) 29... Nxg2 30. Reb1 (30. Rd1 {Khalifman,Alexander} Nh4 31. Be2 Qh6 $17) 30... Qd7 {Khalifman,Alexander: '!'} 31. Ne2 (31. Bb5 Qd8 {Khalifman,Alexander: '!'} (31... Rxb5 {Khalifman,Alexander} 32. Nxb5 Qd2 33. Qxg2 Rxg2 34. Kxg2 $13) 32. Nc6+ (32. Rd1 {Khalifman,Alexander} a5 33. Rc4 Bd7 34. a4 (34. Bxd7 Qxd7 35. Rd3 f4 36. a4 f3 $19) 34... f4 $1 35. Rd3 f3 $19) (32. Bc6 {Khalifman,Alexander} Rxd4 33. Rxd4 Qxd4 34. Bxg2 b6 $19) 32... bxc6 33. Bxc6+ (33. Ba6+ {Khalifman,Alexander} Kc7 34. Rb7+ Bxb7 35. Rxb7+ Kc8 $19) 33... Kc7 34. Bxd5 Qxd5 $19) 31... Rxd3 $1 {Nice end of good game! Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: 'Nice end of good game!''} (31... a5 $5 {Khalifman,Alexander} 32. R4b3 Rxd3 $1 33. cxd3 Qxd3 34. Rc1 Nf4 $1 $19) 32. cxd3 Qxd3 {[%csl Rf1,Rh2][%cal Rd3f1]} 33. Rc1 c2 {[%cal Gb7b6,Gc8a6]} 34. Rd4 $8 {Neil McDonald: 'Psakhis: '''} Qf3 {Khalifman,Alexander: '-+'} 35. Nf4 (35. h4 b6) (35. Ng3 {Khalifman,Alexander} b6 $1 36. Qxg2 Qxa3 37. Ne2 Rxg2 38. Kxg2 Bb7+ 39. Kf1 Be4 $19) (35. Ng1 {Khalifman,Alexander} Qxa3 36. Ne2 b6 $1 37. Rxc2 (37. Rd2 Ba6 38. Rdxc2 Qf3 39. Rd2 Nf4 $19) 37... Ba6 38. Rcd2 f4 39. Rd8+ Rxd8 40. Rxd8+ Kc7 $19) 35... b6 $1 {Neil McDonald: '!!' Neil McDonald: 'A wonderful way to finish the attack- the entrance of the bishop will be decisive. I wonder at what point in the attack Khalifman noticed this move? Psakhis: '!''} (35... Nxf4 $2 {Khalifman,Alexander} 36. Qxf4 Qxh3+ 37. Ke2 $13) 36. Nxg2 Ba6+ 37. Kg1 Bb7 {Neil McDonald: '!'} 0-1

