'This is the only move to have been tested; presumably most players would reason that if one is going to face a strong attack regardless, then one may as well grab some material and hope for the best. Other possibilities fail to equalize.' Houdini 1.5a w32 (2s): '=''' '='} ({Andrew Greet: 'Black is certainly not helped by' Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Andrew Greet: 'Black is certainly not helped by''' Andrew Greet: 'a) Black is certainly not helped by'} 12... Nb4 $6 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A'} 13. hxg6 hxg6 14. Bc4 Rc8 15. Bb3 $16 {[%csl Rg8][%cal Gd2f2,Gf2g3] Andrew Greet: 'followed by Qf2-g3 with strong pressure, as noted by Finkel.' Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Andrew Greet: 'followed by Qf2-g3 with strong pressure, as noted by Finkel.'''}) ({b)} 12... gxh5 {is not ridiculous, as the bishop on g4 helps to glue the black kingside together. The line} 13. Nd5 Bg7 14. Bb5 {was mentioned by Polgar, who presumably believes White is doing well here. Extending this line a little further, play might continue Polgar,Judit: '' '' James Vigus: '(Polgar) gives White the initiative.'} Rc8 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,Alexander'} 15. e5 $5 e6 ({if} 15... dxe5 16. Bxc6 Rxc6 17. Nf6+) 16. Bxc6 Rxc6 {and from here} 17. Nb4 (17. Ne3 $1 {looks like the right way to preserve White's initiative}) 17... Rc4 18. b3 Rc7 19. Qxd6 Qxd6 {leads to a murky endgame.}) 13. Rxh5 $1 (13. Bb5 $5 Rc8 14. Nd5 $11) 13... gxh5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Houdini 1.5a w32 (2s): 'Black wins the exchange''' ''} 14. Qd5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Andrew Greet: 'White has sacrificed a considerable amount of material, but in return she has succeeded in wrecking the opposing king's protective barrier. Her last move wins a tempo to transfer the queen to the danger zone.' Houdini 1.5a w32 (2s): 'White threatens to win material: Qd5xc6''' Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Andrew Greet: 'White has sacrificed a considerable amount of material, but in return she has succeeded in wrecking the o