ar position. White is starting an actions on the kingnside without preliminary preparations. Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'White is starting an actions on the kingside without preliminary preparations. A new move in very popular position. White is starting an actions on the kingnside without preliminary preparations.'} ({Neil McDonald: 'The slower'} 11. h4 {Neil McDonald: 'gives Black time to mobilise his queenside pieces and counterattack in the centre:' Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'is the another even more popular continuation.'} Bb7 12. Rh3 (12. Qe2 Nf6 13. Neg5 Bxf3 14. Nxf3 Qd6 15. Ne5 c5 16. dxc5 Qxc5 17. Kb1 Bd6 18. Nc4 Rfd8 19. g4 Bf8 20. Nd2 $14 {Van den Doel,E-Sakalauskas,V/Bled 2002}) (12. c3 c5 13. Neg5 (13. dxc5 Qc7 14. Neg5 Nf6 15. Qe2 Qf4+ 16. Kb1 Bxc5 17. g3 Bxf3 18. Nxf3 Qc7 $11 {Al Modiahki,M-Arizmendi Martinez,J/Biel 2002}) 13... Nf6 (13... h6 14. Bh7+ Kh8 15. Bc2 Bxf3 16. Nxf3 Nf6 {and Black held the draw against a renowned French killer in Anand,V-Bareev,E/ Monte Carlo MNC 2003.}) 14. Qc2 g6 15. h5 Nxh5 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Bxg6 Nf4 18. Bxh7+ $40 {Ivanchuk,V-Radjabov,T/Moscow 2002} Kg7 19. Be4 Bxe4 20. Qxe4 {½-½ (49) Ivanchuk,V (2711)-Radjabov,T (2610) Moscow 2002 CBM 090 [Finkel,A]}) 12... c5 13. Rg3 Qc7 14. dxc5 Rfd8 15. Nfg5 $1 bxc5 16. Nd6 Bxd6 17. Bxh7+ Kf8 18. Qxd6+ Qxd6 19. Rxd6 $16 {Gashimov,V-Dizdar,G/Dubai 2003}) (11. Qf4 $5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A'} Bb7 12. h4 Nf6 13. Neg5 Qd6 14. Ne5 Rad8 15. Rh3 h6 16. g4 c5 17. Ngxf7 Qxd4 18. Qxd4 Rxd4 19. g5 $36 {Guliev,L-Gouliev,N/Baku 2001}) 11... h6 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'This is not a mistake yet, but it shows Black reluctance to exchange his bishop for the g5-knight, an attitude that will soon makes problems for him.' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): 'LiveBook: 3 Games'} ({White has a very dangerous initiative after both} 11... Nf6 12. Ne5 {and}) (11... g6 12. h4) (11... Bxg5 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian was the safer answer,} 12. Nxg5 Nf6 13. 