looked Judit's reply, otherwise he wouldn't dare to take the knight which was beging to be taken.'' My guess is that black overlooked Judit's reply, otherwise he wouldn't dare to take the knight which was beging to be taken. Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'The decisive mistake. Probably Black saw White's reply, but he could underestimated that. My guess is that black overlooked Judit's reply, otherwise he wouldn't dare to take the knight which was beging to be taken. '} ({Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'In case of'} 13... Rb8 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'White would keep the initiative with'} 14. h4 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: ''} Ba6 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A'} (14... Nf6 15. Ne5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A'} (15. Bd3 {Polgar,Judit} Bb7 16. Ne5 Kg8 17. Qe2 $40) 15... Nxe4 16. Ngxf7+ Kg8 17. Nxd8 Nxd2 18. Ndc6 $18) 15. Qf4 $36) ({The best response was Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'The best reply was'} 13... Bxg5 {when White maintains some initiative after Polgar,Judit: '!' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '=' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): 'remains equal.'} 14. Nxg5 Rb8 15. h4 (15. Nf3 {Polgar,Judit} Nf6 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '=' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'with an approximately equal position, Volokitin,A (2652)-Nielsen,P (2663) Germany 2004.'} 16. Bd3 Bb7 $11) 15... Nf6 {Polgar,Judit}) 14. g4 $3 $40 {Neil McDonald: '!!' Neil McDonald: 'The point. White fixes the pawn on g5 so that she can lever open the h file with h2-h4.Ifinstead' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '!!' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: ''!!'' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '!' Finkel,A: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'Brilliant move! White's idea is to open an h-file and deliver a mate. For this purpose white is ready to waste a precious tempo. However this tempo doesn't help black to build up a defensive line up on the kingside since his rook is attacked and he has to move it.'' Brilliant move! White's idea is to open an h-file and deliver a mate. For this purpose white is ready to waste a precious tempo. However this tempo doesn't help black to build up a defensive line up on the kingside since his rook is attacked and he has to move it. Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'What a brilliant move! White's idea is to open the h-file and create a mating attack against the black king. Black has to spend a tempo to save his rook, allowing White to play h4. Brilliant move! White's idea is to open an h-file and deliver a mate. For this purpose white is ready to waste a precious tempo. However this tempo doesn't help black to build up a defensive line up on the kingside since his rook is attacked and he has to move it.'} ({Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'The greedy'} 14. Bxa8 $2 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'could have been met by'} g4 $15 {[%cal Ge7g5] Neil McDonald: 'leaves White in deep trouble as' Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A: ''' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '-+' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'followed by ...g5 and suddenly Black is winning.'} 15. Ne5 $2 Bg5 {drops the queen. Polgar,Judit: '-+'}) 14... Rb8 {Neil McDonald: 'More or less forced as White might really have taken the rook now.'} (14... Ba6 {Polgar,Judit Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): 'keeps fighting.'} 15. h4 gxh4 (15... f5 16. hxg5+ Kg8 17. gxf5 Rxf5 18. Bxf5 exf5 19. Qc3 $1 (19. Qe3 Bc4) 19... Bxg5+ 20. Nxg5 Qxg5+ 21. Kb1 Rf8 (21... c5 22. Qb3+ c4 23. Qa4 $18) (21... Kf7 22. Qb3+ Kf6 23. Qd5 Rd8 24. Rde1 $18) 22. Qb3+ Rf7 23. Rh8+ Kxh8 24. Qxf7 $18) (15... g6 16. hxg5+ Kg7 17. Qf4 Rh8 (17... Bd6 18. Ne5 Be7 19. Nxf7 Bd6 20. Qf3 Qe7 21. Rh7+ Kxh7 22. Qh3+ Kg8 23. Rh1 Kxf7 24. Bxg6+ Kxg6 25. Qh5+ Kg7 26. Qh7# {#}) 18. Rxh8 Qxh8 19. Ne5 Nxe5 20. Qxe5+ Kg8 21. Qxh8+ Kxh8 22. Rh1+ Kg7 23. Bxa8 $18) (15... Kg8 16. hxg5 Re8 17. Bh7+ Kf8 18. Bd3 $18) 16. g5 Kg8 17. Qf4 f5 18. Qxh4 fxe4 19. Qh7+ Kf7 20. Qh5+ g6 (20... Kg8 21. g6 $18) 21. Qh7+ Ke8 22. Qxg6+ Rf7 