t square for the queen transfer. On the way to the h-file, it also puts some pressure on the queenside. White’s attack may seem a bit slow, but Black’s development is even slower! He has a wide choice, but no saving move. Ftacnik: 'It is almost sure that white had this very position on the board during preparation, black pieces are too passive for the sucessful coping with the threats along the open h file.''} Bb7 {Neil McDonald: 'Black has an extra piece but he has no way to organise a successful defence. The problem is that the f7 square collapses if he contests control of the h file. For example' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '[#]' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Black continues the development and hoping to exchange at least one of White's attacking pieces - the bishop.'} ({Finkel,A: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'An only move not to lose on the spot was'' An only move not to lose on the spot was Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'With Black's major pieces incompletely coordinated, Black would not be successful in his fight for the h-file: An only move not to lose on the spot was'} 17... Rh8 $8 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '''' Finkel,A: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'however it wouldn't influence an outcome of the game.'' however it wouldn't influence an outcome of the game. Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'however it wouldn't influence the outcome of the game. however it wouldn't influence an outcome of the game.'} 18. Rxh8 (18. Rh6 $6 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A'} Bxg5 19. Nxg5 Rxh6 20. Qxf7+ Kh8 21. Qf4 Qf8 22. Nf7+ Kh7 $17) 18... Qxh8 (18... Kxh8 {Polgar,Judit} 19. Qxf7) 19. Ne5 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '!' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Despite being a piece down, White keeps attacking with quiet moves. This is possible only because Black is seriously behind in development.'} Qe8 ({The rook is trapped after} 19... Nxe5 20. Qxe5+ Kg8 21. Qxc7 Bxg5+ 22. Kb1 {Polgar,Judit: '+-' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '+-' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'unexpectedly traps the rook. This line illustrates the lack of communication between Black’s opposite wings.'}) (19... Qg8 {Polgar,Judit} 20. Rh1 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Another apparently peaceful move. It may seem that Black can neutralize the attack with:'} Bd6 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Black's position seemt to be just okay, but White is ready with some new tactical fireworks.'} 21. Rh7+ $3 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'It is quite a beautiful one, moreover the only winning move!'} Qxh7 (21... Kxh7 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'leads to forced mate:'} 22. Qh2+ Kg7 23. Qh6# {#}) (21... Kf8 22. Rh8 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '!' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'and White wins the queen, since'} Qxh8 23. Qxf7# {#}) 22. Qxf7+ Kh8 23. Nxg6+ {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '+-'} Qxg6 24. Bxg6 Nf8 25. Qf6+ Kg8 26. Bf7+ Kh7 27. g6+ $18) (19... f6 {Polgar,Judit} 20. gxf6+ Bxf6 21. Rh1 Bxe5 (21... g5 22. Qf3 Qg8 23. Nxd7 Bxd7 24. Rh7+ $18) 22. dxe5 Qg8 23. Rh6 Nf8 24. Rh3 $18) (19... Bxg5 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian happened in a game,} 20. Qxg5 Qh6 21. Qxh6+ Kxh6 22. Nxf7+ Kg7 23. Ne5 $18 {and White had a clear pawn up, Kim,J (2058)-Vignesh,B (2317) Ho Chi Minh City 2019.}) 20. Rh1 $18 {[%cal Gf4h2] Finkel,A: 'Finkel,Alexander: 'and black is helpless against h2.'' and black is helpless against h2. Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A: 'and black is helpless against h2.'' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'and Black faces with undefendable threats. and black is helpless against h2.'} Bd6 ({If} 20... Bb7 21. Nxd7 Qxd7 22. Qe5+ f6 23. Qh2 {looks decisive.}) 21. Qh2 Bxe5 22. Qh6+ Kg8 23. dxe5 f5 24. Qh8+ Kf7 25. Rh7#) ({Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Another apparently logical try which would fail because of Black’s lack of development is:'} 17... Bd6 {Polgar,Judit Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): ''} 18. Ne5 Bxe5 (18... Be7 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian could have been met by} 19. Nxf7 $1 (19. Qh2 $2 Rh8 $19) 19... Bxg5 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): ' Decoy'} (19... Rxf7 20. Rh7+ $1 Kxh7 21. Qxf7+ $18 {and 22.h1 mate.}) 20. Qxg5 Qxg5+ (20... Qf6) 21. Nxg5 $18 {and White wins again.}) 19. dxe5 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Threatening with 20.h7 xh7 21.h2 g7 22.h6 g8 23.h1+-.'} Rh8 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'and'} 20. Rxh8 (20. Rh6 $1 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian White maintains the tension, leaving Black completely paralyzed.} c5 (20... Bb7 21. Rxd7 $1 {Another nice tactical blow!} Qxd7 22. Qf6+ $18) 21. Bc6 Rxh6 22. gxh6+ Kf8 23. g5 $18 {There is no adequate defence against 24.xd7 followed by 25.f6.}) ({However the smart} 20. Qf6+ $18 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian}) 20... Qxh8 21. Bc6 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '+-' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'are also winning.'} Qd8 22. Kb1 $1 a5 23. a4 Kf8 24. Rh1 $18) (17... Rg8 {Polgar,Judit Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'allows the smart finish by'} 18. Rh7+ {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '!'} Kxh7 19. Qxf7+ $18 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'followed by 20.h1 mate.'}) 18. Rh7+ $1 {Neil McDonald: 'A very elegant finish.' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '!!' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: ''!'' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '!!' Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): ' Decoy' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Another fantastic tactical blow, which made possible by the fact that the white bishop is still alive and ready to sacrifice on g6 when required.'} Kxh7 {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '[#]'} ({Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'Obviously'} 18... Kg8 {Polgar,Judit: 'Finkel,A' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'is hopeless, because of'} 19. Rdh1 {Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: '+-' Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'and mate soon.'} f5 20. gxf6 Bxf6 21. Rh8+ Bxh8 22. Rxh8+ Kxh8 23. Qh6+ Kg8 24. Qxg6+ Kh8 25. Qh7#) 19. Qh2+ {Tactical Analysis 2.10 (12s): '!'} Kg8 ({Finkel,Alexander Szabo,Krisztian: 'The bishop’s lethal action is revealed after:'} 19... Kg7 {Polgar,Judit} 20. Qh6+ Kg8 21. B