1. c4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. a3 Bc5 7. Nb3 Be7 8. e4 O-O 9. Be2 b6 10. O-O Bb7 11. Bf4 d6 12. Rc1 Rc8 13. Re1 Ne5 14. Nd2 Nfd7 15. Be3 {15. b4 Kh8 16. Bg3 g5 17. Nb3 a6 18. Bf1 Rg8 19. Na4 Bc6 20. Nd4 Bb7 21. Nb3 Bc6 22. Nd4 Bb7 23. Nb3 1/2-1/2 Van Wely,L (2692)-Gashimov,V (2761)/ Wijk aan Zee 2012} Qc7 16. b4 Qb8 {Magnus wasn't sure about this. "It's always a bit committal."} 17. f4 Ng6 18. g3 Rfe8 19. Bf3 Qa8 20. Bf2 Ngf8 21. Qe2 Qb8 22. Red1 g6 $6 {This seemed awkward to Carlsen. 22... g5} 23. e5 Bc6 {23... Bxf3 24. Nxf3 dxe5 25. fxe5 Qb7 26. Ne4} 24. Bd4 Red8 {Black didn't really have any other useful moves.} 25. Bxc6 Rxc6 26. Nf3 dxe5 {26... Rdc8 27. exd6 Bxd6 28. Ne4 Be7 29. Ba1 intending Nd4 (Carlsen)} 27. fxe5 Rdc8 28. Ne4 Qc7 29. Nfd2 a6 {29... Nxe5 30. b5} 30. Nf2 Bg5 $2 {30... h5 and 31...Nh7 (Carlsen)} 31. Rf1 $1 Bxd2 {Otherwise Nf3} 32. Qxd2 Nxe5 {32... Rxc4 33. Rxc4 Qxc4 34. Ng4} 33. Bxe5 Qxe5 34. Ng4 Rd6 {"Sort of the best chance." (Carlsen)} 35. Nh6+ Kg7 36. Rxf7+ Kh8 37. Qf2 Qd4 38. c5 bxc5 39. Qxd4+ Rxd4 40. Rxc5 Rcd8 {40... Rdd8 41. Rxc8 Rxc8 42. Ra7 Rc6 43. Kf2 and again White is dominating completely.} 41. Rcc7 Rd1+ 42. Kg2 R1d2+ 43. Kh3 R2d5 44. Ng4 Rh5+ {44... Nd7 45. Re7! h6 46. a4! Carlsen} 45. Kg2 Rd2+ 46. Kf3 Rf5+ 47. Ke3 Rxf7 48. Rxf7 Rd8 49. Nf6 Rb8 50. Kf4 h6 51. Ke5 a5 52. bxa5 Ra8 53. a6 1-0

