1. e4 {Schulz,A Boensch} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f4 Nc6 7. Nf3 Bg7 8. Bd3 O-O (8... Qb6 {Boensch} 9. Qe2 O-O 10. Rb1 Ng4 11. Nd5 Qd8 12. O-O b6 13. Bd2 e6 14. Ne3 Nxe3 15. Qxe3 Bb7 $10 {Kolar,S-Baric,D/Ljubljana op (07) ;EXP 53 1996/1-0 (43)}) 9. O-O Bg4 (9... b5 10. Qe1 b4 11. Nd5 Bb7 (11... Rb8 12. Kh1 Bg4 13. Nxf6+ Bxf6 14. e5 Bg7 $14 {Kuijf,M-Banas,J/Mitropa Cup (09) SVK-NED ;EXP 46 1995/½-½ (55)}) 12. f5 Nxd5 13. exd5 Ne5 14. fxg6 fxg6 15. Qe4 Qa5 16. Nxe5 Rxf1+ 17. Bxf1 Bxe5 18. Be3 Bxb2 19. Qe6+ Kh8 20. Rd1 Bf6 21. Bc4 Qc7 22. Bb3 a5 23. Rf1 Qc3 24. Bh6 Ba6 25. Rb1 Bb5 26. a4 bxa3 27. h4 Qd4+ 28. Be3 Qxh4 29. c4 Bxc4 {0-1 Hector,J-Smirin,I/Antwerp op(4) 1994}) (9... a6 10. Qe1 Nb4 (10... b5 11. Qh4 e6 12. Kh1 Nd7 13. Qh3 Nb4 14. f5 Ne5 15. fxg6 Nxg6 $14 {Kolar,S-Krasevec,A/Ljubljana op (3/26) 1992/0-1 (56)}) 11. Qh4 Nxd3 12. cxd3 e6 13. f5 exf5 14. Bg5 h6 15. Nd5 $2 (15. Bxh6 Qb6+ 16. Kh1 Qxb2 $13) 15... hxg5 16. Nxg5 Re8 $19 {0-1 Masserey,Y-Gurevich,D/Genf op (4) 1992 (33)}) 10. Qe1 Bxf3 (10... Rc8 {Boensch} 11. Kh1 Qa5 12. Qg3 Bxf3 13. Qxf3 Nd4 14. Qh3 d5 15. Bd2 dxe4 16. Nxe4 Qd5 $10 {Klinger,J-Lobron,E/Munich zt 1987/½-½ (75)}) 11. Rxf3 e6 12. Kh1 Rc8 {Schulz: Das ist nun eher ein Stellungstyp der Scheveninger Variante als des Drachen. Wenn man die üblichen Stellungen des Drachen nicht mag, kann man mit 6.f4 und 7.f3 ganz andere Stellungsbilder erzeugen.} 13. Rf1 (13. Bd2 Nd7 14. Rd1 Nc5 15. Bc1 d5 16. Rh3 Nxd3 17. cxd3 f5 18. e5 Rf7 19. d4 Bf8 20. Qg1 a6 21. g4 fxg4 22. Qxg4 Qd7 23. Ne2 Ne7 24. Ng1 Nf5 25. Nf3 Be7 26. Ng5 Bxg5 27. fxg5 Qa4 28. Ra3 Qc2 29. Rad3 Qb1 {0-1 Roofdhooft,M-Tukmakov,V/Antwerp op(04) 1993}) (13. f5 {Boensch} Ne5 14. Rh3 Nfg4 $15) 13... Re8 (13... d5 14. e5 Nd7 {with the idea ...f6}) 14. Qf2 a6 15. f5 Nd7 16. Qg3 Qb6 17. Nd1 (17. Qxd6 Nde5 {Leaves White's queen awkwardly placed. Black threatens 18...f8. Also possible is 17...e5!? when 18.xd7?? loses to 18...cd8} (17... Nde5 {Boensch} 18. fxg6 hxg6 19. Be2 Red8 20. Qa3 Nd4 21. Be3 Qc6 $44) (17... Be5 18. Qxd7 (18. Qa3 Nb4 $44) 18... Rcd8 19. fxe6 Rxd7 20. exd7 Rd8 21. Nd5 $10)) 17... Nce5 18. Be3 Qa5 19. Bg5 h6 $6 (19... exf5 20. exf5 Nxd3 {with counterplay e.g.} 21. cxd3 (21. Qxd3 Re1 22. Ne3 Rxa1 23. Rxa1 Bxb2) 21... Qe5 $1 {and now} 22. fxg6 (22. Bf4 Qxf5) (22. Qh3 Qxf5 $1) (22. Qf3 Qxf5) 22... fxg6 23. Bf4 Qe2 24. Nf2 Bxb2 25. Rad1 (25. Rab1 Rc1 $3 $19) 25... Be5 $17) 20. Be3 Kh7 21. Qh3 exf5 (21... Nc5 {Boensch} 22. f6 Bf8 23. g4 Ncxd3 24. Bxh6 (24. cxd3 Nxd3 25. Bxh6 Bxh6 26. Qxd3 Qg5 $17) 24... Bxh6 25. g5 Ng4 $19) 22. exf5 Qb4 23. Nf2 (23. fxg6+ fxg6 24. Bxg6+ Nxg6 (24... Kxg6 $2 25. Qf5#) 25. Qxd7 Rcd8 $44 (25... Rf8 $17 {Schulz,A})) 23... Nc5 (23... Qxb2 $2 24. fxg6+ fxg6 25. Bxg6+ Nxg6 (25... Kxg6 {Boensch} 26. Nd3 Nxd3 27. Qf5#) 26. Qxd7 $36) 24. a3 Qa4 (24... Qxb2 25. Rab1 Qa2 (25... Qxa3 26. fxg6+ fxg6 27. Bxh6 Kg8 28. Bxg7 Kxg7 29. Ne4 {looks equal}) 26. Bxc5 Rxc5 27. fxg6+ fxg6 28. Rxb7 {with complications and equal chances}) 25. Rae1 Ncxd3 26. cxd3 h5 27. Bd2 Ng4 28. Ne4 (28. Nxg4 {Boensch} Qxg4 29. Qxg4 (29. fxg6+ Kxg6 30. Qxg4+ hxg4 $17) 29... hxg4 30. fxg6+ Kxg6) 28... Qc2 29. Rc1 (29. Nxd6 $4 Qxd2 30. Rxe8 Nf2+ $19) 29... Qxb2 30. Qf3 Ne5 31. Qe3 Qxa3 {Black is collecting pawns while White's last few moves seem rather aimless. Time trouble perhaps? White certainly doesn't appear to have enough compensation for two pawns} 32. Bc3 Kg8 (32... Ng4 {Schulz,A} 33. fxg6+ fxg6 34. Ng5+ Kg8 (34... Kh8 $2 35. Bxg7+ Kxg7 36. Rc7+ Rxc7 37. Qxe8 Nf2+ 38. Kg1 Nh3+ 39. Nxh3 $18 (39. gxh3 $2 Qc5+ 40. Kh1 Qxg5 41. Qf8+ Kh7 42. Rf7+ Rxf7 43. Qxf7+ Kh8 $10)) 35. Qf3 Qb3 36. Bxg7 Rxc1 (36... Kxg7 $4 37. Rb1 $18) 37. Rxc1 Kxg7 $19) 33. fxg6 fxg6 34. Qb6 Rf8 35. Qxb7 $2 {A blunder which should lose instantly. 35.fd1 appears to be the best chance to survive a bit longer but White has a lost position anyway} (35. Nxd6 {Boensch} Rxc3 $19) 35... Qa2 $4 {And now Black returns the blunder!} (35... Rxf1+ 36. Rxf1 Rxc3 37. Nxc3 Qxc3 {is winning easily for Black}) (35... Rxc3 $19) 36. Bxe5 $1 {Black must allow mate or lose a rook. I suspect that both players were short of time during the last few moves} (36. Bxe5 Bxe5 (36... Rxc1 37. Qxg7#) 37. Rxc8 $18) 1-0

