1. e4 {Huzman Ftacnik} d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 e5 4. Nf3 Nbd7 5. Bc4 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 c6 8. a4 b6 9. d5 {Huzman: 'This central advance is a typical motif for White in the Philidor Defence.' Huzman: ''Dieser Vorstoß im Zentrum gehört zu den typischen Weißmotiven in der Philidor-Verteidigung.''} cxd5 (9... c5 {Huzman} 10. a5 a6 11. axb6 Nxb6 12. Bf1 Ne8 13. Nd2 Nc7 14. Nb3 Bg5 15. Na5 Bxc1 16. Qxc1 Bd7 17. Qe3 Nb5 18. Nxb5 axb5 19. Nc6 Bxc6 20. dxc6 b4 21. c3 $16 {Jansa,V-Lawson,D/Gausdal AC (04) ,TD 92\08 1992 (32)}) (9... Bb7 {Huzman} 10. dxc6 $1 Bxc6 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bxf6 Nxf6 13. Qd3 g6 14. Nd2 Kg7 15. Bd5 Nxd5 16. Nxd5 $14 {Kindermann,S-Plachetka,J/Trnava 43/(386) 1987}) 10. Bxd5 {Huzman: '!?' Huzman: 'Taking with the knight (10.d5) is an alternative here.' Huzman: ''Das Nehmen mit dem Springer (10.d5) stellt hier eine Alternative dar.''} (10. Nxd5 {Huzman} Bb7 (10... Nxd5 11. Bxd5 Rb8 12. c3 (12. Qd3 Qc7 (12... Nf6 13. Bb3 h6 14. Bd2 Bb7 15. Rad1 Qc7 16. Nh4 d5 17. Nf5 Rfd8 18. Qg3 g6 19. Bxh6 Bb4 20. c3 Nh5 21. Qg5 Bc5 22. exd5 Kh7 23. Ng3 {1-0 Jansa,V-Hesse,P/BL2-O 1992}) 13. Be3 Nf6 14. Bb3 h6 15. Bd2 Nd7 16. Bb4 Nc5 17. Bxc5 dxc5 18. Bd5 $14 {½-½ Kindermann,S-Schmidt Schaeffer,S/Munich op9293 1993 (41)}) (12. Nd2 Nf6 13. Nc4 Nxd5 14. Qxd5 Be6 15. Qd3 Rc8 16. Ne3 Bg5 17. c3 Bxe3 18. Bxe3 Qc7 19. f3 Rfd8 20. Qe2 d5 $132 {0-1 Koscielski,J-Blauert,J/Dortmund op 1995 (35)}) 12... Nf6 13. Bb3 Bb7 14. Qd3 h6 15. h3 Rc8 16. Nh2 Rc5 17. Ng4 Nxg4 18. hxg4 Bg5 19. Be3 Bxe3 20. Rxe3 Qg5 $15 {1-0 Kaiumov,D-Panchenko,A/Cheliabinsk 1993 (40)}) 11. Bg5 (11. b3 Rc8 12. Ba3 (12. Ra2 Nxd5 13. Bxd5 Bxd5 14. exd5 f5 15. c4 a5 $15 {Iordachescu,V-Rowson,J/WchJM-U20 Halle (09) ,EXP 48 1995 (44)}) 12... Nxd5 13. Bxd5 Bxd5 14. Qxd5 Rxc2 15. Bxd6 Bxd6 16. Qxd6 Nc5 $13 {Yandemirov,V-Abramovic,B/EUCup f Ljubljana 1995/½-½ (47)}) 11... Nxd5 (11... Rc8 12. Bxf6 Nxf6 13. Nxf6+ Bxf6 14. Qd3 $14 {½-½ Koch,J-Chabanon,J/FRA-ch 1994 (21)}) 12. Bxd5 Bxd5 13. Bxe7 Qxe7 14. Qxd5 Rac8 {½-½ Rodriguez,A-Jansa,V/Andorra 1996}) 10... Nxd5 (10... Rb8 {Huzman With this move Black is intending to prepare the advance b6-b5-b4 after something like 10..a6, 11..b5. 'Schwarz beabsichtigt damit den Vorstoß b6-b5-b4 nach etwa 10..a6, 11..b5 vorzubereiten.'} 11. b3 (11. Ba2 $5) (11. Nd2 a6 12. Qe2 Qc7 13. Nf1 Nc5 14. Bg5 Ne8 15. Bd2 Ne6 16. Be3 Qd8 17. Red1 $14 {½-½ Koskela,N-Agrest,S/Helsinki 1999/(69)}) 11... a6 (11... Nc5 12. Ba3 Be6 13. Bxc5 bxc5 14. Qd3 Nh5 15. Ne2 Kh8 16. Nd2 Bc8 17. Rad1 g6 18. Nc4 $14 {½-½ Jurkiewicz,K-Dworakowska,J/Zakopane 2000/(77)}) 12. Ba3 (12. Bc4 Bb7 13. Bg5 {White is threatening to secure control of the d5-square with the exchange on f6. Weiß droht durch Tausch auf f6 die Kontrolle über das Feld d5 zu sichern.} Ne8 $6 {Here Black has the choice between 13...c8, 13...c7 and 13...h6. The game move is an obvious attempt to weaken the black squares in White's camp by exchanging off the black-squared bishop. Schwarz hat hier die Wahl zwischen 13...c8 sowie 13...c7 und 13...h6. Der Partiezug ist offenbar ein Versuch durch den Tausch der schwarzfeldrigen Läufer die schwarzen Felder im Lager des Weißen zu schwächen.} (13... Rc8 $5 14. Bxf6 (14. Qd3 $6 Nc5) (14. Qd2 h6 15. Bxf6 Nxf6 16. Nd5 Nxd5 17. Bxd5 Bxd5 18. exd5 f5 $132) 14... Nxf6 15. Qd3 Qc7 16. Rac1) (13... h6 $6 14. Bxf6 Nxf6 15. Qd3 $36) 14. Bxe7 Qxe7 15. Bd5 (15. Qd2 Kh8 16. Rad1 f5) 15... Ndf6 16. Bxb7 Qxb7 17. Qd3 Rc8 18. Na2 {19.c4 followed by c3} (18. Re2 Qc7 $132) 18... Nd7 (18... d5 $5 19. Nxe5 (19. exd5 $2 e4) 19... dxe4 20. Qe2 Nd6 $132) 19. Rad1 (19. Nb4 Nc5 20. Qe3 Nf6 $132) (19. c4 Nc5 20. Qc2 {c3} b5 21. cxb5 axb5 $132) 19... Nc5 20. Qe2 a5 {On the queenside and in the centre Black is obviously playing for a blockade on the dark squares. But he has to accept in return White's pressure down the d-file. Am Damenflügel und im Zentrum spielt Schwarz offenbar auf die Blockade auf den schwarzen Feldern. Der weißen Druck auf d-Linie muss er allerdings in Kauf nehmen.} (20... f5 21. exf5 Rxf5 22. Nb4 $14) (20... Nf6 21. Nd2 b5 $132) 21. Nd2 {c4 with pressure on d6. c4 mit Druck auf d6.} Ne6 (21... f5 22. exf5 Rxf5 23. c4 $14) 22. Nc4 {White is pursuing a clever strategy; he is logically making efforts to secure the white squares and attack the dark squares, e.g. d6. Weiß verfolgt eine geschickte Strategie, er ist nämlich konsequent bemüht, die weißen Felder zu sichern und die schwarzen Felder, u.a. das Feld d6, anzugreifen.} Nd4 (22... f5 23. Nc3 Nf4 24. Qe3 fxe4 25. Nxd6 Nxd6 26. Rxd6 $14) 23. Qd3 f5 24. Nc3 f4 {Black is attempting to seize the initiative on the kingside. Schwarz ist bemüht, am Königsflügel die Initiative zu ergreifen.} 25. Nb5 (25. Nd5 $5 {This would be a good alternative. White's trumps include the c4, secure control of the white squares, the pressure down the d-file, e.g. Dies wäre eine gute Alternative. Zu den Trümpfen des Weißen gehören der c4, die sichere Kontrolle über die weißen Felder, der Druck auf der d-Linie, z.B.} f3 $5 26. Ndxb6 Rd8 27. Nd5 fxg2 28. Kxg2 Qf7 29. Rf1 Nf3 30. Nd2 $16 {White is now clearly better. Weiß steht nun klar besser.}) 25... Nxb5 26. axb5 Rc5 $6 {leads to the loss of the important d6 and e5 pawns. Führt zum Verlust der wichtigen Bauern d6 und e5.} (26... f3 $5) 27. Nxd6 Nxd6 28. Qxd6 Rxc2 29. Qxe5 $16 {1/2 Carlsson,P (2330)-Agrest,E (2532)/Linkoping 2001 (40)}) 12... b5 13. axb5 axb5 14. Bb4 Qc7 15. Ra5 Nc5 16. Nxb5 Qb6 17. c4 Nxd5 18. exd5 $13 {Bode,W-Schmidt Schaeffer,S/Baden-Niedersachsen 1993/½-½ (45)}) 11. Nxd5 (11. Qxd5 {Huzman} Ba6 12. Be3 Rc8 13. a5 Bc4 14. Qd2 bxa5 15. b3 Be6 16. Nb5 Nc5 17. Nxa7 Nxe4 18. Qd3 Nc5 19. Qb5 Rc7 20. Nc6 Qd7 21. Nxe7+ Qxe7 22. Qxa5 Rfc8 $15 {0-1 Hnydiuk,A-Pedzich,D/Czestochowa 1998/EXT 2000 (32)}) 11... Nf6 $1 (11... Bb7 12. a5 $36 (12. b3 {Huzman} Rc8 (12... Nf6 13. Nxf6+ Bxf6 14. Ba3 (14. c4 Be7 (14... Qc7 15. Qd3 (15. Ba3 Be7 16. Qe2 a6 17. Nd2 Bc6 18. Nb1 Rab8 19. Nc3 $14 {1-0 Afek,Y-Ellenbroek,T/Hoogeveen 2001/CBM 84 ext (52)}) 15... Bc6 16. Be3 Rfd8 17. Nd2 Qb7 18. f3 a6 19. Nf1 Be7 20. Red1 b5 21. a5 Rdc8 22. Bb6 bxc4 23. bxc4 Bd7 24. Ne3 $14 {1-0 Landa,K-Kasparov,S/Senden 2002/CBM 90 ext (42)}) 15. Qd3 (15. Ba3 f5 (15... g6 16. Ra2 Qc7 17. Rd2 Rad8 18. Rd3 Kh8 19. Nd2 f5 20. f3 a6 21. Kh1 Bc6 22. Bb4 Qb7 $14 {½-½ Lobron,E-Rebers,E/Amsterdam 2002/CBM 89 ext (47)}) 16. Nd2 Qd7 (16... Bh4 17. Ra2 Qf6 18. Nf3 Bxf2+ 19. Rxf2 fxe4 20. Qxd6 exf3 21. Qxe5 Qxe5 22. Rxe5 Rfe8 {½-½ Gyimesi,Z-Ruck,R/HUN-ch 1996/CBM 57}) 17. Ra2 Rad8 $132 18. f3 fxe4 19. Nxe4 d5 $1 20. Bxe7 Qxe7 21. cxd5 Rxd5 $15 {0-1 Kalod,R-Jansa,V/Zlin 1997/ (43)}) 15... f5 16. exf5 Bf6 17. Rb1 e4 18. Rxe4 Bxe4 19. Qxe4 Qe7 20. Qd3 Rfe8 21. Ba3 Rad8 22. Kf1 Qb7 23. Rd1 Re4 24. Qd5+ Qxd5 25. Rxd5 h5 26. Bxd6 $16 {1-0 Acs,P-Conquest,S/Bled 2002/EXT 2003 (42)}) 14... Be7 15. Qd3 Qc7 16. c4 g6 17. Rad1 Rad8 18. Nd2 f5 19. f3 Bc6 20. Nb1 Qb7 21. Nc3 $14 {½-½ Roeder,M-Odendahl,R/Germany 1998/EXT 99 (58)}) 13. c4 Nc5 (13... Nf6 14. Ba3 Nxd5 15. exd5 f5 16. Ra2 Bf6 17. Rae2 a6 18. Qd2 Rf7 $15 {½-½ Bentsen,H-Adnoy,H/Oslo 2002/ (39)}) 14. Ba3 (14. Rb1 f5 15. exf5 Rxf5 16. Nd4 Rf7 17. Nb5 Qd7 18. Be3 Rcf8 19. f3 Bh4 20. Rf1 Qe6 21. Nbc3 Qg6 $132 {½-½ Voloshin,L-Neumann,P/CZE 2001/EXT 2003 (29)}) (14. Ra2 Bxd5 15. exd5 a5 16. Rae2 Rc7 17. Be3 f5 18. Qc2 g6 19. Nd2 Bg5 $15 {0-1 Mazi,L-Kiss,A/St Veit 1998/ (40)}) (14. b4 Ne6 15. Qe2 Ba6 16. b5 Bb7 17. a5 Bxd5 18. cxd5 Nc5 19. axb6 axb6 20. Ba3 $14 {½-½ Van de Oudeweetering,A-Philippe,C/Paris 2001/CBM 83 ext (20)}) 14... Re8 15. Bxc5 $6 {strangely enough, White proves his eagerness to swap his own well-positioned pieces for ones that are less useful for his opponent. Due to these bizarre tactics, Black takes over the initiative.} (15. Ra2 $5 Bg5 16. Nxg5 Qxg5 17. Re3 $14) 15... bxc5 16. Nxe7+ Qxe7 17. Nd2 Qg5 18. Re3 (18. Nf1 Re6 19. Qd2 Qg6 20. f3 f5 $36) 18... Re6 19. Nf1 Rf8 20. f3 Rg6 (20... f5 $5 21. exf5 Rxf5 22. Ra2 Ref6 $36) 21. Ra2 f5 22. exf5 Rxf5 {0-1 Berthelot,Y (2311)-Bauer,C (2579)/France 2003 (28)}) (12. c4 {Huzman White has succeeded in securing control of the c4-, d5- and e4-squares. 'Es dem Weißen gelungen, die Kontrolle über die Felder c4, d5, e4 zu sichern.'} Bxd5 (12... Nc5 13. b4 Ne6 14. a5 bxa5 15. Rxa5 a6 16. Be3 $16 {1-0 Zufic,M-Kiss,A/Szentgotthard 2001/EXT 2002 (66)}) (12... f5 13. exf5 Rxf5 14. Nd4 Rf7 15. Ne6 Qc8 16. Nxe7+ Rxe7 17. Qxd6 $16 {1-0 De Vreugt,D-Ellenbroek,T/Breda 2001/CBM 82 ext (71)}) 13. Qxd5 Qc7 14. b3 a6 15. Be3 Rab8 16. Nd2 Rfd8 17. Rec1 Nc5 18. b4 a5 19. b5 h6 20. Rc3 Bg5 21. Nf1 Qb7 {½-½ Cheparinov,I-Hoffman,A/Mondariz ESP 2002/ (21)})) (11... Nc5 {Huzman} 12. Be3 Nxe4 13. Bxb6 axb6 14. Rxe4 Bb7 15. Rb4 Ra5 16. Nxe7+ Qxe7 17. Rxb6 $16 {1-0 Vallejo Pons,F-Bellini,F/Mondariz 2000/CBM 79 (29)}) 12. c4 {Ftacnik: 'A new move, that can hardly aspire for an advantage. Relatively the most promissing continuation is 12.xf6+, but with an exact play black should be able to equalize.' Huzman: 'A new move, that can hardly aspire to an advantage. Relatively the most promising continuation is 12.xf6+, but with precise play Black should be able to equalize.''} (12. Nxe7+ Qxe7 13. Bg5 h6 14. Bxf6 {½-½ De la Riva Aguado,O-Magem Badals,J/Manresa 1996/EXT 98 (14)} (14. Bxf6 Qxf6 15. Qd3 (15. Nd2 {Ftacnik} Be6 16. Nf1 Rfd8 17. Ne3 Rac8 18. Qd3 Qe7 19. c4 Qc7 20. b3 a6 21. Red1 Qc5 22. Nd5 $14 {Khruschiov,A-Strikovic,A/Internet section 16-B/2003/}) 15... Bb7 16. c4 Qe7 17. Nd2 f5 18. exf5 Qg5 19. Ne4 Qxf5 $11 {½-½ Bitalzadeh,A-Ellenbroek,T/Dieren NED 2003/(76)})) (12. Nxf6+ Bxf6 13. c4 {Huzman: ''×d5''} (13. Ra3 {Huzman} Ba6) (13. b3 $2 {Huzman} d5 14. exd5 e4) 13... Bb7 (13... Be6 {Huzman} 14. b3 Be7 15. Ba3 $14) 14. b3 (14. Qd3 {(Huzman) d2}) 14... Be7 (14... Qc7 {Huzman} 15. Qd3 (15. Ba3) 15... Bc6 16. Be3 Rfd8 17. Nd2 Qb7 18. f3 a6 19. Nf1 (19. Nb1 $2 d5 $1 20. cxd5 Bxd5 21. exd5 e4 $15) 19... Be7 20. Red1 b5 $132 21. a5 (21. cxb5 axb5 22. a5 d5 $36) 21... Rdc8 22. Bb6 bxc4 23. bxc4 Bd7 24. Ne3 {Huzman: '' Huzman: '1-0 Landa,K-Kasparov,S/Senden 2002/CBM 90 ext (42)'} Be6 25. Nd5 $14 {Landa,K (2632)-Kasparov,S (2439)/Senden 2002}) 15. Qd3 (15. Ba3 f5 (15... g6 16. Ra2 Qc7 17. Rd2 Rad8 18. Rd3 Kh8 19. Nd2 f5 20. f3 $14 {½-½ Lobron,E-Rebers,E/Amsterdam 2002/CBM 89 ext (47) Huzman: '½-½ Lobron,E-Rebers,E/Amsterdam 2002/ (47)'}) 16. Nd2 Qd7 (16... Bh4 17. Ra2 Qf6 18. Nf3 Bxf2+ 19. Rxf2 fxe4 20. Qxd6 exf3 21. Qxe5 Qxe5 22. Rxe5 Rfe8 {½-½ Gyimesi,Z-Ruck,R/Budapest 1996/CBM 57 (22) Huzman: '½-½ Gyimesi,Z-Ruck,R/Budapest 1996/ (22)' Huzman: '½-½ Gyimesi,Z-Ruck,R/HUN-ch 1996/CBM 57'}) 17. Ra2 Rad8 $15 {0-1 Kalod,R-Jansa,V/Zlin 1997/CBM 61/[Blatny,P] (43) Huzman: ''} 18. f3 {Huzman} fxe4 19. Nxe4 (19. fxe4 Bh4 20. Re2 Qg4 $132) 19... d5 $1 20. Bxe7 Qxe7 21. cxd5 Rxd5 {0-1 Kalod,R (2455)-Jansa,V (2490)/Zlin 1997 (43) Huzman: '' Huzman: '0-1 Kalod,R-Jansa,V/Zlin 1997/ (43)'}) 15... f5 (15... Qc7 $1 {Huzman} 16. Ba3 (16. Bb2 $5 g6 17. Rad1 f5 $13) 16... f5 17. Nd2 $5 (17. exf5 Qc6 $1 18. Rad1 Rae8 $132)) 16. exf5 Bf6 (16... Qc7 {Huzman} 17. Ng5) (16... e4 {Huzman} 17. Rxe4 $1 Bxe4 18. Qxe4 Qd7 (18... Bf6 19. Rb1 {Inf.16...f6}) 19. Bb2 (19. Ba3 $5) 19... Rae8 20. Qd5+ Kh8 21. g4 Bf6 22. Bxf6 Rxf6 23. Rd1 $14) 17. Rb1 e4 18. Rxe4 Bxe4 19. Qxe4 {Huzman: 'Inf.16...f6'} Qe7 (19... Qe8 {Huzman} 20. Qd3) 20. Qd3 (20. Qd5+ $6 {Huzman} Qf7) 20... Rfe8 21. Ba3 Rad8 22. Kf1 $14 {1-0 Acs,P-Conquest,S/Bled 2002/EXT 2003 (42)} (22. Rd1 {Huzman} Qe2 23. h3 h5 24. Qd5+ Kh8 25. Rd2 Qe4 26. Qxe4 Rxe4 27. Kf1 $16 (27. g3 $5)) 22... Qb7 {Huzman} (22... Qe4 {Huzman} 23. Rd1) 23. Rd1 Re4 24. Qd5+ (24. Bxd6 $2 Be7 $19) 24... Qxd5 25. Rxd5 h5 (25... Kf7 26. Bxd6 Be7 27. Re5 $1 $18) (25... Rde8 26. Bxd6 (26. h3 h5) 26... Re2 27. g4 Rb2 28. Rb5 $1 (28. Rd3 $6 Rd8 29. Nd2 Be5) 28... Rd8 (28... Ree2 29. Bg3 $16) 29. c5 $16) 26. Bxd6 $1 {1-0 Acs,P (2591)-Conquest,S (2537)/Bled olm 2002 (42) Huzman: '' Huzman: '1-0 Acs,P-Conquest,S/Bled 2002/EXT 2003 (42)'} (26. g3)) (12. b3 $5 {Huzman}) 12... Nxd5 13. exd5 $6 (13. Qxd5 Be6 14. Qd3 Qc8 15. b3 f5 $132) 13... Bg4 $15 {The position of Black is much better due to the pair of bishops and the possibility of the pawn advances f5 and e4.} 14. a5 Qd7 {[%cal Yb6b5]} (14... Qc7 15. Qa4) (14... bxa5 {Ftacnik} 15. Bd2 Qb6 16. Ra2 $11) 15. Qa4 $2 {This move doesn't prevent the planned break of pawns chain c4-d5 but helps it. Huzman: 'This move doesn't prevent the planned break-up of the pawn chain c4-d5 but helps it.'} (15. h3 $142 Bf5 (15... Bh5 $2 16. Nxe5 $18) 16. Be3 $132) 15... b5 $1 {Ftacnik: 'A very impressive small combination. Azmaiparashvili is not satisfied with simple equality and instead tries for an active play. ' Huzman: 'A very impressive little combination. Azmaiparashvili is not satisfied with simple equality and instead tries for active play. '} (15... Qb7 $5) 16. Qxb5 (16. cxb5 Rfb8 17. b6 axb6 $17 {[%csl Rd5]}) 16... Qxb5 17. cxb5 Rfb8 18. b6 (18. Nd4 $1 Kf8 (18... Bf6 {Ftacnik} 19. Nc6 Rxb5 20. h3 Bd7 21. Rd1 a6 $15) 19. Nc6 Rxb5 $17 {[%csl Rd5]}) 18... axb6 19. a6 {'?' Ftacnik. Huzman: '?'} (19. Nd4 $5 {Ftacnik} Bd7 (19... exd4 20. Rxe7 bxa5 21. Re4 Bd7 22. Rxd4 a4 23. h3 $11) 20. a6 Rc8 21. Bd2 Kf8 $15) 19... Bc8 $17 20. a7 (20. Nd4 $142 Bxa6 (20... Rxa6 21. Rxa6 Bxa6 22. Nc6 Rb7 23. Be3 $44) 21. Nc6 Re8 22. Be3 Bf6 23. Bxb6 Bc4 $17) 20... Rb7 21. Be3 Rbxa7 22. Rac1 (22. Rxa7 Rxa7 23. Bxb6 Rb7 24. Rc1 Bf5 25. Rc6 Kf8 $5 (25... Be4 26. Rc8+ Bf8 27. Nd2 Bxd5 28. Bc7 Be6 29. Rxf8+ Kxf8 30. Bxd6+ Ke8 31. Bxe5 f6 $17) 26. b4 Bd7 27. Ba5 Rb5 28. Rc7 Rxd5 $19) 22... Bb7 23. Bxb6 Ra6 24. Bc7 Bxd5 $19 25. b4 Bc6 26. Nd4 exd4 $1 27. Rxe7 d3 28. Rd1 Ra1 $1 29. Ree1 Rxd1 30. Rxd1 Ra2 31. f3 d2 32. Kf2 Ba4 33. Ke2 Bxd1+ 34. Kxd1 d5 35. Be5 f6 36. Bd4 Kf7 37. g4 Ke6 38. h4 Ra3 39. f4 Rd3 40. f5+ Kd7 41. Bc5 Rg3 0-1

