1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f3 e5 7. Nb3 Be6 8. Be3 Nbd7 9. g4 Nb6 10. g5 Nh5 11. Qd2 Be7 12. O-O-O Rc8 13. Rg1 O-O 14. Kb1 g6 15. Qf2 Nc4 16. Bc1 $5 {[%mdl 4] Svidler opened a new plan with this game, white is insisting on keeping white squared bishop.} (16. Bxc4 Bxc4 17. Qd2 Qc7 18. Rg2 f5 19. Nd5 Bxd5 20. Qxd5+ Kh8 21. c3 Qc6 22. Na5 Qxd5 23. Rxd5 b5 {½-½ Leko,P-Anand,V/Monte Carlo 2003/ (23)}) 16... Na3+ (16... f6 17. Nd5 Bxd5 18. gxf6 Rxf6 19. exd5 Nf4 20. Rg4 Qb6 21. Qe1 Bf8 22. h4 Qc7 23. h5 {1-0 Tiviakov,S-Shneider,A/Istanbul 2003/ (27)}) (16... b5 17. Nd5 Bxd5 18. exd5 f6 19. gxf6 Bxf6 20. c3 Bh4 21. Qc2 Rxf3 22. Qe4 Rf2 23. Nd2 Nxd2+ 24. Bxd2 Qf6 25. a4 bxa4 26. Bxa6 {1-0 Spasov,V-Grischuk,A/Plovdiv 2003/ (43)}) 17. Ka1 (17. bxa3 $6 Rxc3 18. Bb2 Rc6 19. Bxe5 Bxg5 20. Rxd6 Rxd6 21. Bxd6 Qxd6 22. Rxg5 Rd8 $15) 17... b5 18. Bd3 Qc7 (18... f5 19. gxf6 Rxf6 20. Nd5 Bxd5 21. exd5 Nc4 22. Rg4 $13) 19. Rg2 a5 (19... Nc4 20. Nd5 Bxd5 21. exd5 a5 $132) 20. Nd5 (20. Nxb5 Nxb5 21. Bxb5 a4 22. Bxa4 Rb8 23. a3 Rb7 24. Nd2 Nf4 25. Rg3 Ra8 26. Bb3 d5 27. exd5 Bxd5 28. Bxd5 Rxa3+ 29. Kb1 Nxd5 $40) 20... Bxd5 21. exd5 Nc4 (21... a4 $5 22. bxa3 (22. Nd4 exd4 23. bxa3 Qc5 24. Rg4 f6 $13) 22... axb3 23. axb3 b4 24. a4 f6 $44) 22. Rg4 a4 23. Nd2 Qb6 $6 {Polgar is playing very passively, in this moment the timely 23...f5! would promise fair chances for an advantage.} (23... f5 $1 24. Rxc4 (24. gxf6 Nxf6 25. Rg3 a3 (25... Kh8 26. Nb1 Nxd5 27. Bxg6 Bh4 28. Bxh7 Qxh7 29. Rxd5 Bxg3 30. hxg3 Qh1 $19) 26. Nxc4 bxc4 27. Bf5 axb2+ 28. Bxb2 Rb8 $17) 24... bxc4 25. Nxc4 f4 (25... Rb8 26. f4 Rb4 27. b3 axb3 28. cxb3 Nxf4 29. Bxf4 exf4 30. Qxf4 Ra8 31. Kb2 Qa7 32. Bb1 Qc5 $17) 26. h4 Rb8 $17) 24. Qxb6 Nxb6 25. Bxb5 Nxd5 $2 {Another important moment, when 25...f% would have been a more viable option.} (25... f5 26. gxf6 (26. Rb4 Nxd5 27. Rxa4 Ne3 28. Rh1 Bxg5 $11) 26... Nxf6 27. Rxa4 Rxc2 28. Ra7 Rfc8 29. Kb1 Nfxd5 $11) 26. Ne4 $1 Ndf4 (26... f5 27. gxf6 (27. Nxd6 $5 Bxd6 (27... fxg4 28. Nxc8 Rxc8 29. Rxd5 gxf3 30. Kb1 Rc5 31. Bxa4 Rxd5 32. Bb3 f2 33. Bxd5+ Kf8 34. Bc4 Bc5 35. c3 $14) 28. Rxa4 Nb6 29. Rxd6 Rxc2 30. Bd2 Rfc8 31. Kb1 Nxa4 32. Bxa4 $14) 27... Nhxf6 28. Bc4 Nxg4 29. Bxd5+ Kg7 30. fxg4 Rxc2 31. Bd2 $16) 27. Bxa4 d5 28. Ng3 (28. Nc3 d4 29. Ne4 h6 30. h4 hxg5 31. hxg5 Rfd8 32. Kb1 $16) 28... Rfd8 (28... f5 29. gxf6 Nxf6 30. Rg5 (30. Nf5 Bd8 31. Rxf4 exf4 32. Nd4 $14) 30... Nd7 31. Bxd7 Bxg5 32. Bxc8 Rxc8 33. Kb1 $16) (28... Nxg3 29. hxg3 Ne2 30. Be3 Bc5 31. Bxc5 Rxc5 32. Re1 Nd4 33. Rxe5 Nxf3 34. Re3 $16) 29. Nxh5 gxh5 (29... Nxh5 30. Bb3 d4 31. Re4 $16) 30. Rgg1 Ng6 (30... Ne2 31. Rge1 Nxc1 32. Rxe5 Bd6 33. Rexd5 Ra8 34. Bc6 (34. Rxc1 Rxa4 35. c4 Be7 $14) 34... Rxa2+ (34... Nxa2 35. Bxa8 Rxa8 36. Kb1 Be7 37. Rd7 Kf8 38. f4 $18) 35. Kb1 Rb8 36. b3 Ba3 37. Rxc1 Rb2+ 38. Ka1 R2xb3 39. cxb3 Bxc1 40. Bb5 Kg7 41. Bc4 $16) 31. Bb3 d4 32. Kb1 Kg7 33. Rge1 {Svidler has no problems playing a position with two bishops and an extra pawn.} Bd6 (33... f6 34. gxf6+ Kxf6 35. Re4 $18) 34. Re4 h4 35. h3 Rf8 (35... f5 36. gxf6+ Kxf6 37. Rg1 $18) 36. c3 Bc5 (36... f5 37. Ree1 Bc5 38. f4 $1 dxc3 39. Rd7+ Be7 40. fxe5 $18) 37. cxd4 exd4 (37... Bxd4 38. a4 f5 39. gxf6+ Rxf6 40. f4 $18) 38. Bd2 Rce8 (38... f5 39. gxf6+ Rxf6 40. Rc1 Rxf3 41. Bb4 Rf5 42. Be6 $18) 39. Rde1 Rxe4 40. Rxe4 f5 41. gxf6+ Rxf6 42. f4 Ne7 (42... Bd6 43. Rxd4 Bxf4 44. Bc3 Be5 45. Rd7+ $18) 43. a4 Rg6 (43... Nf5 44. a5 Ne3 45. Ba2 Nf1 46. Be1 Ng3 47. Re8 Bf8 48. b4 Rxf4 49. a6 $18) 44. Re5 Bd6 (44... Rg2 45. a5 Rxd2 46. Rxc5 $18) 45. Rg5 Rxg5 46. fxg5 {Polgar is helpless against bishops.} Nc6 47. Bd5 Nb4 (47... Bb4 48. Kc2 Bxd2 49. Kxd2 Nb4 50. Be4 $18) 48. Be4 Be7 49. a5 Bc5 50. b3 Bd6 51. Kb2 Bc5 52. Ka3 Nd5+ 53. b4 Ne3 54. bxc5 Nc4+ 55. Kb4 Nxd2 56. Bg2 1-0

