1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. Nc3 Bb7 5. a3 d5 6. cxd5 Nxd5 7. Qc2 Nxc3 8. bxc3 Be7 9. e4 O-O 10. Bd3 c5 11. O-O Qc8 12. Qe2 Ba6 13. Rd1 Rd8 14. h4 (14. Bf4 cxd4 15. cxd4 Bxd3 16. Rxd3 Nd7 17. Rb3 Qb7 18. h3 Rac8 19. Rd1 Qc6 20. Rbd3 Qc2 21. Qe3 b5 22. Ne1 Qa4 23. Qg3 Bf8 24. d5 e5 25. Bxe5 Qxe4 26. Bc7 {1-0 Strating,S-Werle,J/Netherlands 2000/ (52)}) (14. Bb2 Bxd3 15. Rxd3 cxd4 16. cxd4 Nd7 17. Rad1 Qa6 18. h4 h6 19. Bc1 Qb7 20. Nh2 Bxh4 21. Qg4 Bxf2+ 22. Kxf2 Nf6 23. Qf3 Qxe4 24. Qxe4 Nxe4+ 25. Kf3 $11 {Bunzmann,A-Sax,G/Saint Vincent/2000/}) 14... cxd4 15. cxd4 Bxd3 16. Rxd3 Nd7 17. Bg5 f6 {White has only a tiny advantage in this line, but black must play very carefully.} (17... Bxg5 18. hxg5 Qc7 19. Qe3 Rac8 20. Rad1 $13) 18. Bf4 Qb7 19. h5 (19. Rc1 Rac8 20. Rxc8 Rxc8 21. h5 Qa6 22. Qd1 Qb7 23. Nd2 $14) 19... Rac8 20. Rad1 Qa6 21. e5 (21. Qa2 Qc4 22. Qxc4 Rxc4 23. Be3 (23. d5 Nc5 24. Rd4 Rxd4 25. Nxd4 Rd7 $13) 23... Rdc8 24. Kf1 $14) 21... f5 $6 (21... Qc4 $5 22. exf6 Bxf6 23. Re1 b5 24. Re3 Nf8 $11) 22. d5 $1 {Sokolov opens up the fight for the kingside attack with some great tactical shots.} (22. h6 g6 23. d5 Nc5 24. d6 Nxd3 25. Qxd3 (25. dxe7 $2 Rd5 $17) 25... Qxd3 26. Rxd3 $44) 22... exd5 (22... Nc5 23. d6 Nxd3 24. Qxd3 Qxd3 25. Rxd3 Rd7 (25... Bf8 $2 26. Ng5 $18) 26. Nd4 Kf7 27. dxe7 Rc4 28. Rg3 Rxe7 29. Bg5 $16) 23. Nd4 (23. Qa2 Nf8 (23... Nc5 24. Rxd5 Kf8 25. e6 $16) 24. Rxd5 Rxd5 25. Qxd5+ Kh8 26. Qf7 Qa4 27. Re1 Qe8 28. Qxf5 Bxa3 29. Ra1 Bc5 30. Rxa7 $16) 23... Rf8 (23... Nc5 24. Nxf5 Bf8 25. Qg4 Nxd3 26. Nh6+ Kh8 27. Nf7+ Kg8 28. Qe6 Be7 29. Nh6+ Kh8 30. Qg8+ Rxg8 31. Nf7#) 24. Qf3 Nc5 25. h6 (25. Qxd5+ Kh8 26. Rc3 Qa4 27. Rd2 Ne4 28. Rxc8 Rxc8 29. Rd3 Nc5 $11) 25... g5 (25... Nxd3 26. hxg7 $1 Rf7 (26... Kxg7 27. Rxd3 Kh8 28. Bh6 Qa5 29. Kh2 $40) 27. Rxd3 Bc5 28. Ne6 (28. e6 Rf6 29. e7 Qb7 30. Bg5 Bxd4 31. Rxd4 Qxe7 32. Bxf6 Rc1+ 33. Kh2 Qxf6 34. Qxd5+ Kxg7 35. Qd7+ $11) 28... Qc4 29. Rxd5 Bxa3 30. Nd4 Qa2 31. e6 $14) 26. Bxg5 $5 {[%mdl 128] A magnificient attacking idea, that was played partly on calculation and to a great deal on tactical feeling. Polgar's queen on a6 is the main reason behind black's defensive problems.} Bxg5 (26... Nxd3 $2 27. Bxe7 Nxe5 28. Qxd5+ Nf7 29. Qxf5 $18) 27. Qh5 (27. Qxd5+ Kh8 28. Ne6 Nxe6 29. Qxe6 Rce8 $19) 27... Bf4 (27... Nxd3 $2 28. Qxg5+ Kf7 29. e6+ Ke8 30. Nxf5 Rxf5 31. Qxf5 $18) (27... Bd8 28. Nxf5 Qa4 (28... Nxd3 $2 29. Qg4+ Kf7 30. Qg7+ Ke6 31. Nd4#) (28... Kh8 29. Nd6 $3 Nxd3 (29... Rc7 30. Rf3 Rg8 31. Rf7 Be7 32. Qf5 Rg6 33. Rf8+ Bxf8 34. Qxf8+ Rg8 35. Qf6+ Rgg7 36. hxg7+ Rxg7 37. Qf8+ Rg8 38. Nf7#) 30. Nf7+ Kg8 (30... Rxf7 31. Qxf7 $18) 31. Nxd8 Rcxd8 (31... Rfxd8 32. e6 Qb7 33. Qg5+ Kf8 34. Qf6+ Ke8 35. Qh8+ Ke7 36. Qxh7+ $18) 32. Qg5+ Kf7 33. Qf6+ Ke8 34. Qe6#) (28... Rxf5 29. Qxf5 (29. Qe8+ Rf8 30. Rg3+ Bg5 31. Qe7 Ne6 32. Qxe6+ Kh8 33. Rxg5 $18) 29... Nxd3 30. Rxd3 $18) 29. Rd4 Qc6 30. Nd6 Rc7 31. Rxd5 $16) 28. Rf3 (28. Nxf5 Rxf5 $1 29. Qxf5 Nxd3 30. Qe6+ Kf8 31. Qf6+ Ke8 32. Qe6+ $11) 28... Bxe5 29. Nxf5 (29. Rxf5 Rxf5 (29... Bf6 30. Qg4+ Kh8 31. Rxf6 Rg8 32. Qf5 $16) 30. Nxf5 Nd7 $1 (30... Kf8 31. Rxd5 Nd3 32. Ng3 $1 (32. Rxe5 $6 Nxe5 33. Nd6 Qxa3 34. Qf5+ Ke7 35. Nxc8+ Kd8 36. Nxa7 Qc1+ 37. Kh2 Qxh6+ $11) 32... Ke7 33. Qf5 $18) (30... Qb7 31. f4 $1 Bf6 (31... Bh8 32. Nd6 Qd7 33. Qg5+ Kf8 34. Rxd5 $18) 32. Qg4+ Kh8 33. Nd6 Rg8 34. Qh5 $18) (30... Kh8 31. Ne7 Bb2 32. Rxd5 Ra8 33. Qf7 $18) 31. f4 (31. Ne7+ Kf8 32. Nxd5 (32. Nxc8 Qxc8 33. Qf5+ Ke7 34. Qxh7+ Kd6 35. Qf7 Qc4 $13) 32... Qb5 33. Qf3+ Ke8 34. Qh5+ $11) 31... Qxa3 (31... Bf6 32. Nd6 Rf8 33. Qxd5+ Kh8 34. Nf7+ Rxf7 35. Qxf7 $18) 32. Qg4+ Kh8 33. fxe5 Qc5+ 34. Kh1 Rg8 35. Qh4 Qc2 36. Ne3 $13) 29... Qb7 (29... Kh8 30. Ne7 Bb2 (30... Nd7 31. Nxc8 Rxc8 (31... Qxc8 32. Rxf8+ Qxf8 33. Rxd5 Qe7 34. Rxd7 $18) 32. Re3 $18) 31. Nxc8 Qxc8 (31... Rxc8 32. Rf7 $18) 32. Rxf8+ Qxf8 33. Qxd5 $16 Qxh6 $140 34. Qd8+ Kg7 35. Qe7+ Kg6 36. Rd6+ $18) 30. Rxd5 Rce8 (30... Rxf5 $2 31. Qxf5 Qxd5 32. Qxc8+ $18) (30... Bf6 31. Nd6 Qd7 32. Nxc8 Qxc8 33. Rxf6 Rxf6 34. Qg5+ Kf7 35. Qg7+ Ke6 36. Qg4+ Kxd5 37. Qxc8 $18) (30... Nd7 31. Ne7+ Kh8 32. Rxe5 Rxf3 (32... Rc1+ 33. Kh2 Rxf3 34. Qg5 $18) 33. Nxc8 Qc7 34. Qxf3 Qxe5 35. Qf7 $18) 31. Qg5+ Kh8 32. Rxe5 Rxe5 33. Ne7 $3 {The final touch of a tactical magician, Sokolov has managed to create an attacking masterpiece.} (33. Qg7+ Qxg7 34. hxg7+ Kg8 35. gxf8=Q+ Kxf8 36. Nd6+ Ke7 37. Nc8+ Kd7 38. Nxa7 $16) 33... Re1+ (33... Rxg5 34. Rxf8+ Rg8 35. Rxg8#) 34. Kh2 Qb8+ (34... Qc7+ $2 35. g3 $18) 35. Rg3 $1 (35. g3 Ne6 $19) 35... Rxe7 (35... Ne6 36. Qg7+ $1 Nxg7 37. hxg7#) 36. Qxe7 Ne6 37. Qxe6 Qf4 38. a4 a6 (38... Rd8 39. Kh3 Qd4 40. Rg4 $18) 39. Qxb6 Rb8 40. Qe3 Qh4+ 41. Rh3 Qf6 42. Qc3 1-0

