1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 b6 3. d4 e6 4. g3 Ba6 5. Qb3 $5 {This is the sharpest of all the alternatives at White's disposal.} Nc6 {[%cal Rc6a5] a5 The most usual and best move.} (5... d5 6. cxd5 Qxd5 (6... exd5 7. Nc3 $14) 7. Qc2 c5 8. Nc3 Qc6 9. dxc5 Bxc5 10. Bg2 Bb7 11. O-O Nbd7 12. Bd2 O-O 13. Rac1 Rfc8 14. Qb1 a5 15. Nh4 Qc7 16. Nb5 Qb8 17. Bf4 e5 18. Bg5 Bxg2 19. Nxg2 $14 {Piket,J-Karpov,A/Amber blind/1995/}) (5... c6 6. Bf4 d5 7. cxd5 Nxd5 (7... cxd5 $2 8. Bxb8 $1 Bc4 9. Qa4+ $1 b5 10. Qc2 Rxb8 11. b3 $18) 8. Bg5 Be7 9. Bxe7 Qxe7 10. Nbd2 O-O 11. Rc1 Rc8 12. e4 Bxf1 13. Kxf1 Nf6 14. e5 Ne8 15. Kg2 Qb7 16. Ne4 Na6 17. Rc4 Rc7 18. Rhc1 Rac8 19. a3 h6 20. Qe3 c5 21. dxc5 bxc5 22. R1c2 Qd5 23. Qc3 $16 {Stohl,I-Danailov,S/Leipzig/1986/}) (5... c5 6. d5 exd5 7. cxd5 d6 8. Bg2 g6 9. O-O Bg7 10. Nc3 O-O 11. Bf4 Re8 12. Rfe1 {In a Benoni-like position the queen on b3 seems strangely placed, but it has prevents immediate counterplay with b5. This together with White's potential central play speaks in his favour:} Ne4 13. Nxe4 $1 (13. Qc2 Qe7 14. Nxe4 Qxe4 15. Qxe4 Rxe4 16. Bxd6 Nd7 17. Rab1 Rxe2 18. Rxe2 Bxe2 19. b3 c4 20. bxc4 Bxc4 21. Nd2 Bxa2 22. Rc1 Nf6 23. Be5 Re8 24. Bxf6 Bxf6 25. Ne4 Bb2 26. Rd1 f5 $17 {Fominyh,A-Epishin,V/RUS-ch Elista/1997/}) 13... Rxe4 14. Qc2 Rc4 15. Qd2 Qe7 16. e4 $1 $16) 6. Bd2 ({The older move is} 6. Nbd2 {[%csl Rc4,Ge4] White not only protects the c4-pawn, but prepares e4 as well.} {More ambitious is} d5 $5 (6... Na5 7. Qa4 Bb7 8. Bg2 c5 9. dxc5 bxc5 10. O-O Qc7 $5 (10... Be7 11. Ne5 Bxg2 12. Kxg2 O-O 13. Ndf3 d6 14. Bd2 $1 dxe5 15. Bxa5 Qb8 16. Bc3 Bd6 17. Rfd1 $14 {Sorin,A-Almasi,Z/Buenos Aires/1996/}) 11. Rd1 Nc6 $132) 7. Qa4 Bb7 8. Bg2 (8. Ne5 Bd6 $1 9. Nxc6 Qd7 $15) 8... Bd6 9. O-O O-O 10. a3 a5 11. e3 Ne7 $13) 6... Bb7 {[%cal Rc6d4] d4} (6... Rb8 7. Bg2 b5 8. c5 $5 b4 9. a3 bxa3 10. Qxa3 Bc4 11. Nc3 Rb3 12. Qa4 Rb4 13. Qc2 Bb3 14. Qd3 Bc4 $11) (6... Na5 $143 7. Qa4 $1 $14) 7. Bc3 (7. d5 $6 Ne7 $1 (7... exd5 8. cxd5 Ne7 9. d6 cxd6 10. Bg2 $44) 8. dxe6 fxe6 9. Bg2 Nf5 10. O-O Bc5 11. Bc3 (11. Nc3 O-O 12. Qc2 Qe8 13. Bg5 Ng4 14. h3 Nxf2 15. Rxf2 Nxg3 16. Qd2 Nf5 17. Re1 Qh5 18. Bf4 Bxf2+ 19. Kxf2 Nh4 $17 {,Fominyh,A-Sakaev,K/Moscow/1999/}) 11... Ne4 12. Nbd2 O-O 13. Nxe4 Bxe4 14. Rad1 a5 15. Qa4 d6 16. a3 Qc8 17. Ng5 Bxg2 18. Kxg2 h6 19. Nf3 Qb7 20. Qc2 a4 21. Qd3 Rf7 22. Kg1 Raf8 $15 {Fominyh,A-Poluljahov,A/RUS-ch Samara/ 2000/}) 7... Ne4 8. a3 {White must waste some more precious time due to the threats against d4. It's curious he will never get to play g2 anymore.} (8. Bg2 $2 Nxc3 9. bxc3 (9. Nxc3 Nxd4 $19) 9... Na5 $17) 8... Nxc3 9. Qxc3 Be7 (9... Qf6 $6 10. d5 $1 Ne7 11. e4 Qxc3+ 12. Nxc3 a6 13. Bg2 g6 14. O-O Bg7 15. Rfe1 h6 16. h4 O-O 17. Rad1 exd5 18. cxd5 d6 19. e5 Rae8 20. exd6 cxd6 21. Nd4 Nf5 22. Nc6 b5 23. a4 $36 {Epishin,V-Ehlvest,J/New York op/1998/}) 10. Qd3 $1 {[%csl Rb7,Gc4,Gd4,Ge4] White wants to occupy the centre and thus limit the scope of the Bb7.} (10. e4 $6 f5 $1 {attacks the centre immediately.} (10... Bf6 11. e5 $2 (11. Qd3 {-10.d3}) 11... Nxd4 12. Nxd4 Bxe5 $19) 11. d5 (11. Bd3 $143 Bf6 $36) (11. exf5 $143 $2 Nxd4 $17) 11... Bf6 12. Qe3 Ne5 $5 13. Nxe5 Bxe5 14. f4 (14. exf5 Qf6 $1 $15) 14... Bxb2 15. Ra2 Bf6 16. exf5 O-O $44 {[%csl Re1] ,עe1}) (10. Bg2 {is natural, but not ideal either:} Bf6 11. e3 (11. O-O Nxd4 12. Nxd4 Bxg2 13. Kxg2 c5 14. Nxe6 dxe6 $15) 11... Ne7 $1 12. Qd3 c5 13. Nc3 cxd4 14. exd4 Rc8 15. Nb5 d5 16. cxd5 a6 17. d6 (17. Nc3 $6 Nxd5 18. Ne4 Be7 19. O-O Qc7 20. Ne5 f6 21. Nf3 Qc2 (21... Qc2 22. Qxc2 Rxc2 23. Rab1 Kf7 24. Rfe1 Rhc8 25. Bf1 h6 26. h4 b5 $17 {Ehlvest,J-Ivanchuk,V/President's Cup/1998/})) 17... Nf5 $15 {and White doesn't even have full equality.}) (10. d5 Bf6 11. Qc2 (11. Qd2 $2 Na5) 11... Ne5 $15 {[%cal Gf6a1]}) 10... d5 (10... Bf6 11. e4 e5 12. d5 Nd4 13. Nxd4 exd4 14. f4 $1 (14. Nd2 c5 15. h4 O-O 16. Bh3 d6 17. Kf1 $6 b5 $1 18. cxb5 a6 19. Kg2 axb5 20. Qxb5 Ba6 21. Qc6 Bd3 22. b3 Ra6 23. Qd7 Qa5 24. Ra2 Qc3 $17 {Epishin,V-Rodriguez Lopez,R/Linares op/1998/}) 14... Qe7 15. Be2 (15. Bh3 b5 $13) 15... d6 16. Nd2 c5 17. Bg4 $13 {/ Here the  is closed and the  don't have that much scope. White has chances for an advantage.}) 11. cxd5 Qxd5 $32 12. e4 $2 $146 {[%csl Rd4,Re1,Re4] White is not sufficiently developed to maintain a broad pawn centre and should have paid more attention to his uncastled king.} (12. Nc3 $142 Qh5 13. Bg2 O-O 14. O-O Rfd8 15. Rad1 Bf6 16. Qe3 Ne7 17. Ne4 Bxe4 18. Qxe4 Qb5 19. Rd2 c5 20. dxc5 bxc5 21. Rc2 Rab8 22. e3 Qd3 23. Qxd3 Rxd3 24. Rxc5 Rxb2 25. a4 Ra3 26. Ra5 Rb4 27. Rxa7 Rbxa4 28. Rxa4 Rxa4 {½,Epishin,V-Razuvaev,Y/RUS-ch St Petersburg/1998/}) 12... Qa5+ 13. Nbd2 (13. Nc3 {closes the c for White.} O-O-O (13... Bf6 $143 14. e5 $5 {} Nxd4 $2 15. Qxd4 $1 Bxf3 16. Bb5+ c6 17. b4 $18) 14. Qc4 (14. Qe3 f5 $17) 14... f5 $5 (14... Bf6 15. O-O-O Rd7 16. d5 $1 $13 {h3}) 15. Bd3 Nb4 $40 {[%csl Rd4,Re4] ה}) 13... O-O-O 14. Rc1 (14. O-O-O Nxd4 $1 15. Nxd4 Qc5+ 16. Nc4 Bf6 $17) 14... f5 $5 {[%mdl 64]} (14... Nxd4 $2 15. Nxd4 Qe5 (15... Bf6 16. Qc2 $18) 16. N2f3 Qxe4+ 17. Qxe4 Bxe4 18. Ba6+ $18) ({Polgar's thematic blow will lead to interesting complications, but very strong was the direct} 14... Bf6 $1 15. b4 (15. Qc2 Bxd4 16. b4 Qxa3 17. Nxd4 Rxd4 18. b5 Rxd2 $1 19. Kxd2 Rd8+ 20. Bd3 Qd6 21. bxc6 Ba6 $19 {}) 15... Qa4 (15... Qh5 $6 16. Qc3 $13 {[%cal Gc1c8] /,c}) 16. Rc4 (16. Qc4 Rd7 17. e5 Be7 {[%cal Rc6d4,Ra4a3] a3, d4!}) (16. Qc3 Bxd4 17. Nxd4 Rxd4 18. b5 $2 Rxe4+ $1 $19) 16... Nxd4 $1 (16... Ba6 $6 17. b5 Qxb5 18. Qc2 Bb7 19. Rc5 $14) (16... b5 17. Rxc6 $1 Bxc6 18. Bg2 $15 {/}) 17. Nxd4 (17. Rxd4 Bxd4 18. Nxd4 Qd7 19. N2f3 e5 $19) 17... b5 18. Qc2 Qxc2 19. Rxc2 Rxd4 $17 {} 20. Bxb5 Rxe4+ $1) 15. b4 $8 (15. Bg2 $2 fxe4 16. Qxe4 Nxd4 $19) 15... fxe4 16. Qc3 $1 {} (16. Qxe4 Qxa3 17. Rxc6 Bxb4 $19 {[%cal Rd8d6] d6}) (16. Nxe4 Qf5 {b4,d4-+}) 16... Qd5 {Polgar wants to keep the queens on.} (16... Bxb4 17. axb4 Qxb4 18. Nxe4 Qxc3+ (18... e5 19. Qxb4 Nxb4 20. d5 $1 Bxd5 21. Nfd2 $132 {/ is similar.}) 19. Rxc3 Nxd4 20. Nfd2 $13) (16... Qf5 $143 17. Ne5 Rhf8 (17... Bc5 18. Nxc6 Bxc6 19. bxc5 e3 20. fxe3 Bxh1 21. cxb6 c6 22. e4 $1 Bxe4 23. Bd3 $1 $18) 18. f4 $1 (18. Nxc6 Qxf2+ 19. Kd1 e3 $1 20. Nxd8 Bxd8 $19) 18... e3 19. Ndf3 $16) 17. Ne5 $8 (17. Bc4 Qf5 18. Ba6 Bxa6 19. Qxc6 Kb8 $1 20. Qxc7+ Ka8 21. Qxe7 Rc8 $1 $40) (17. b5 exf3 18. bxc6 Ba8 {[%cal Rd8d6] d6-+}) 17... e3 18. Ndf3 exf2+ {Now White's king escapes into relative safety, but the alternatives were unconvincing} (18... Rhf8 19. Be2 (19. Bg2 $2 exf2+ 20. Kf1 Ba6+ 21. Kxf2 Qxd4+ $19) (19. fxe3 $2 Rxf3 20. Bg2 Rxe3+ $19) 19... exf2+ 20. Kf1 (20. Kd1 Bc5 21. bxc5 Nxd4 $1 22. Qxd4 Qb3+ $19) 20... Bg5 (20... Rd6 $2 21. b5 $16) 21. b5 $142 $1 (21. Rc2 Bd2 $1 22. Nxc6 (22. Rxd2 $2 Nxe5 23. dxe5 Rxf3 $19) 22... Bxc3 23. Ne7+ Kb8 24. Nxd5 Rxf3 $1 25. Bxf3 Bxd4 26. Rxc7 Bxd5 $17 {[%csl Gf2] ,f2}) 21... Bd2 22. Qc2 $1 Bxc1 23. bxc6 $132) (18... Bc5 19. Bc4 (19. bxc5 Nxe5 20. Nxe5 exf2+ $1 21. Ke2 Qxh1 22. cxb6 Qe4+ $19) 19... exf2+ 20. Kf1 Qe4 21. Bd3 Qe3 $5 (21... Qd5 $11) 22. bxc5 Nxe5 23. Nxe5 Rxd4 (23... Bxh1 $2 24. Ba6+) 24. c6 Qxe5 25. cxb7+ Kb8 26. Be2 $13) 19. Kxf2 Rhf8 20. Kg2 $8 (20. Kg1 Bc5 $1 $19) (20. Nxc6 $2 Bxc6 21. Bg2 Qd6 $19 {} 22. Qxc6 Qxd4+ 23. Ke2 Qd3+ 24. Kf2 Bc5+ $1 25. Rxc5 Qd2+ 26. Kf1 Qd1+ 27. Kf2 Rd2+ 28. Ke3 Qe2#) 20... g5 $2 {[%mdl 128] A misguided move, after which the advantage changes hands. Black could have continued the attack more effectively:} (20... Bc5 21. Bc4 Qe4 (21... Nxe5 22. Bxd5 Bxd5 23. dxe5 Rxf3 (23... Bxf3+ $2 24. Kh3) 24. Qxf3 Bxf3+ 25. Kxf3 Bd4 26. b5 $5 $14) 22. Rhe1 (22. Bd3 Qxd4 23. Nxd4 Nxe5+ 24. Kh3 Rf6 $1 $19 {}) 22... Nxe5 23. Rxe4 Bxe4 24. dxc5 (24. Bxe6+ Kb8 25. dxe5 Rxf3 26. Qxf3 Rd2+ $17) 24... Nxf3 $40) (20... Rxf3 21. Nxf3 b5 $1 $17 {[%cal Ga8h1] d7,d4}) 21. Nxc6 Rd7 $8 (21... Bc5 $2 22. Ne7+ $18) 22. g4 $2 {[%csl Rf4,Rg4,Rh4] ׻} (22. Nxa7+ $142 $1 Kb8 23. Nc6+ $16 {grabbing an extra pawn and deciding how to proceed later on.}) (22. h3 {} h5 (22... Bc5 23. b5 $5) 23. Nxa7+ Kb8 24. Nc6+ Kc8 25. Be2 g4 26. hxg4 hxg4 27. Rh7 $14) 22... Bc5 $1 23. Bb5 (23. b5 $6 Bxd4 $1 24. Qd3 (24. Ncxd4 Qxd4 $19) 24... e5 $40 {e4, df7}) (23. bxc5 Qxc6 24. Be2 (24. d5 Rxd5 25. Be2 Re5 $1 26. Qxe5 Rxf3 27. Qxc7+ Qxc7 28. c6 Rc3 $1 29. Rxc3 Bxc6+ $17 {gives Black very good winning chances.}) 24... Rxd4 (24... h5 $5) 25. cxb6 (25. Qxd4 $2 Rxf3 $19) 25... Qxb6 $17 {}) 23... Bxc6 24. Bxc6 Qxc6 25. Rhf1 $6 {[%mdl 4096] A solid move, White's king finally wants to leave the long diagonal and free his knight from the annoying pin. But in the resulting endgame Black is already better.} (25. bxc5 $142 $5 Rxd4 (25... h5 $5 26. cxb6 Qe4 27. Rhe1 $1 (27. b7+ $2 Kb8 28. Rhe1 Qxg4+ 29. Kf2 Qh3 $1 $17 {loses the piece back.}) 27... Qxg4+ 28. Kf2 axb6 29. Re3 $132 {[%csl Rc7] ×c7}) (25... Qe4 26. Rhf1 $1 Qxg4+ 27. Kh1 $16 {enables White to consolidate.}) 26. h3 (26. Qxd4 $2 Qxf3+ 27. Kg1 bxc5 $19) (26. cxb6 $2 Rxg4+ 27. Kf2 Qxb6+ 28. Qc5 Rgf4 $19 {}) 26... Qd5 (26... h5 27. Rhf1 $5 {} hxg4 28. Qxd4 Rxf3 29. cxb6 $1 Rc3+ 30. Kg1 Rxc1 (30... Rg3+ 31. Kf2 $18) 31. b7+ $1 Kb8 32. Qh8+ Kxb7 33. Qb2+ $18) 27. cxb6 Rc4 28. Qe3 Rxf3 $1 29. Qxf3 Qd2+ 30. Qf2 Qd5+ $11) (25. dxc5 $2 h5 $1 $40 {hg4, d2!, f3!}) 25... h5 26. Kg1 (26. h3 $2 hxg4 27. hxg4 Qe4 28. bxc5 (28. dxc5 Qxg4+ 29. Kf2 Rd2+ $1 30. Ke1 Qe4+ $1 31. Kxd2 Rd8+ $17 {/-+}) 28... Qxg4+ 29. Kf2 Rdf7 30. Ke2 Rxf3 $1 $17 {/-+}) 26... Rxf3 (26... Bxd4+ $6 27. Qxd4 $1 Rxd4 28. Rxc6 Rxg4+ 29. Kf2 $11) 27. Qxf3 Qxf3 (27... Bxd4+ $2 28. Kg2 Qxf3+ 29. Kxf3 {activates White's .}) 28. Rxf3 hxg4 29. Rg3 Bxd4+ 30. Kh1 $15 {/} (30. Kg2 Be5 31. Rxg4 Bf4 32. Rc2 (32. Rf1 e5 $17) 32... e5 33. b5 Kb7 $36 (33... Rh7 $17 {[%csl Ra3,Rb5,Rg4,Rh2] White's task is far from easy, as the Rg4 is out of play and his pawns are weak.})) 30... Be5 31. Rxg4 Bf4 32. Rc2 $6 (32. Rc3 $142 e5 33. Rg2 {[%cal Yg2c2,Yh1g2,Yg2e2] c2, e2, g2}) 32... e5 (32... Rd3 33. Kg2 e5 $17 (33... Rxa3 $6 34. h4)) 33. Rc3 (33. Kg2 $5) 33... e4 34. Rc4 (34. Rg2 $142 $1) 34... e3 35. Re4 c5 $2 (35... Rd1+ $142 36. Rg1 Rd2 37. Rg2 c5 $1 38. bxc5 bxc5 39. Rc4 (39. h4 Rd4 $19) 39... Kd7 {[%cal Rd7d5] d6-d5-+}) 36. bxc5 bxc5 37. h4 $2 (37. Rc4 Re7 $1 38. Rxc5+ Kb7 39. Rc1 (39. Rg1 e2 40. Rb1+ Ka6 $19) 39... e2 40. Re1 Bd2 $19) (37. Rg2 Rd1+ 38. Rg1 Rd4 $1 39. Re7 Kd8 $19 {loses as below.}) (37. Re8+ $1 {} Kc7 38. h4 Rd1+ (38... Rd4 $2 39. hxg5 Kd7 40. g6 $1 Bh6 41. Ree4 $18) 39. Kg2 Rd2+ 40. Kf1 (40. Kg1 $5 Rd4 41. Kf1 $15 {/=}) 40... Rf2+ 41. Ke1 gxh4 42. Rxh4 Bg3 43. Rhe4 $15 {/=}) 37... Rd4 $1 $19 {[%csl Ge3] e} 38. Rxd4 $8 (38. Re7 Kd8 39. Re6 Kd7 {[%cal Re3e2] e2-+}) 38... cxd4 39. Kg2 d3 40. Kf3 (40. Kf1 e2+ 41. Ke1 Be5 $19) 40... e2 (40... e2 41. Rg1 gxh4 42. Kxf4 d2 $19) 0-1

