1. e4 {Hecht Baburin} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Ndb5 d6 7. Bg5 a6 8. Na3 b5 9. Nd5 Be7 10. Bxf6 Bxf6 11. c3 O-O 12. Nc2 Bg5 13. a4 bxa4 14. Rxa4 a5 15. Bc4 Rb8 16. b3 Kh8 17. O-O g6 18. Kh1 (18. Qd3 Bd7 19. Raa1 f5 20. Rfd1 Bh6 21. Nde3 Rf6 22. f3 Ne7 23. Kh1 Bf4 {Shirov,A-Kramnik,V/Monaco blind 1995/EXP 46/1-0 (54)} (23... Bf4 {Baburin} 24. b4 a4 25. Nd5 Nxd5 26. Bxd5 Qf8 27. g3 Bg5 28. c4 f4 29. g4 h5 30. gxh5 Qh6 31. b5 Qxh5 32. Rxa4 Bh4 33. Rda1)) 18... Bh6 19. Qe2 Bd7 {Baburin: With many pieces on the board it's usually a lot easier for Black to deal with White's knight on d5 in the Sicilian Defence. That knight is not doing much right now, while Black's pieces are moving 'around' it.} 20. Raa1 (20. Ra2 f5 21. exf5 gxf5 22. f4 Bg7 {½-½ Dani,P-Kocsis,G/Zalakaros op 1996/EXP 52 (43)}) 20... f5 {Challenging White's control in the centre.} 21. exf5 gxf5 22. f4 Bg7 23. Rad1 Ne7 24. Nce3 Ng6 25. Qh5 Qe8 26. fxe5 Qxe5 27. Be2 f4 28. Nc4 Qxh5 29. Bxh5 Bb5 {Ich vermute, daß sich beide Spieler hier schon in Zeitnot befinden. In Zeitnot entscheiden die besseren Nerven, und die hatte hier Kramnik.} 30. Bxg6 hxg6 31. Rf3 (31. Ne7 $5 Kh7 32. Rxd6 Bxc4 33. bxc4 g5 34. Rd5) (31. Rxf4 $2 {Baburin} Rxf4 32. Nxf4 Bxc4 33. bxc4 Bxc3 $19) 31... Be5 (31... Bxc4 $5 32. bxc4 g5) 32. Nxe5 dxe5 33. c4 Bc6 34. Re1 Rfe8 35. g3 g5 36. gxf4 exf4 37. Rxe8+ Rxe8 { Hecht: Hauptmotiv: Fesselung} 38. h4 (38. Kg1 $1 {Hecht}) 38... a4 39. bxa4 $2 {Erst danach kommt Schwarz in Vorteil.} (39. hxg5 $142 a3 {Baburin} 40. Rf2 f3 (40... Rb8 {Hecht} 41. Ra2 Rxb3 42. Ra1 $13) 41. Nb4 Re2 42. Kg1 Rb2 $19) 39... Re4 40. Kg1 (40. Rc3 {Hecht} Rxc4 41. Rxc4 Bxd5+ 42. Kg1 Bxc4 43. hxg5 Kg7 44. Kf2 Bd5 $19) 40... Rxc4 41. Rd3 g4 $19 42. a5 g3 43. Rd1 f3 44. Ne7 f2+ 45. Kf1 Bb5 46. Kg2 Rc2 0-1

