1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 {Judit won match already, so why not to play finally Panov attack!?} cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Nf3 Be7 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Bd3 Nc6 9. O-O O-O 10. Re1 Nf6 11. a3 b6 12. Bg5 (12. Bc2 $5 Bb7 13. Qd3) 12... Bb7 13. Bc2 h6 $6 {Rare and not the best move, but any case White keep initiative, for example:} (13... Rc8 14. Qd3 g6 15. Rad1 (15. Bh6 Re8 16. Rad1 $14) 15... Nd5 (15... Re8 16. h4 Nd5 17. Nxd5 exd5 18. b4 Bxg5 19. hxg5 $14) 16. Bh6 Re8 17. Ba4 a6 18. Nxd5 Qxd5 19. Qe3 Bf6 20. b3 (20. Bb3 Qd7 21. d5 exd5 22. Qxb6 Rxe1+ 23. Rxe1 Bxb2 24. Bxd5 Bg7 25. Bxg7 Kxg7 26. h4 $14 {½-½ Beliavsky,A-Karpov,A/Trud-CSKA 1986 (42)}) 20... Qh5 21. d5 Nd8 22. d6 Rc5 23. d7 Re7 24. Qf4 Bg7 25. Qb8 Qxh6 26. Qxd8+ Bf8 27. Re3 Bc6 28. Qxf8+ Qxf8 29. d8=Q {1-0 Smyslov,V-Karpov,A/USSR-39ch Leningrad 1971}) (13... Re8 14. Qd3 g6 15. h4 Rc8 16. Rad1 (16. Rac1 Nd5 17. Ne4 f5 18. Nc3 Bxg5 19. Nxg5 Nf4 20. Qe3 Qxd4 21. Nb5 Qxe3 22. fxe3 Nxg2 23. Kxg2 Nd4+ 24. Be4 $1 $16 {0-1 Reshevsky,S-Fischer,R/New York-Los Angelos 1961 (57)}) 16... a6 17. Bb3 Na5 18. Ba2 b5 19. Ne5 Nd5 20. Bxd5 Bxd5 21. Bxe7 Rxe7 22. Nxd5 Qxd5 23. Ng4 $36 {1-0 Kavalek,L-Larsen,B/Solingen m 1970 (37)}) (13... Nd5 14. Qd3 g6 15. h4 (15. Bh6 $5) 15... Bxg5 16. hxg5 Nxc3 17. Qxc3 Rc8 18. Qe3 Na5 $11 {½-½ Pavlovic,M-Machulsky,A/Belgrade-Moscow m 1998 (42)}) 14. Bh4 {[%cal Rd1d3,Rd3h7]} (14. Bf4 Bd6 15. Be5 Rc8 16. Qe2 Na5 17. Qd3 g6 18. Bxd6 Qxd6 19. Ne5 Rc7 20. Rad1 Rfc8 $11 {0-1 Dolmatov,S-Epishin,V/Moscow PCA Qual 1995 (45)}) 14... Nh5 {N} (14... Nd5 15. Qd3 g6 {} 16. Re4 $1 {[%cal Re4g4]} Rc8 17. Rg4 {[ g6]} Qe8 18. Nxd5 exd5 19. Re1 Rc7 20. Re6 $1 Bc8 (20... fxe6 21. Rxg6+ Kh7 22. Rg7+ $1 Kxg7 23. Qh7#) 21. Rexg6+ fxg6 22. Rxg6+ Kf7 23. Bg3 Bd8 24. Rxh6 {1-0 Pyrich-Jenkins,D/corr 1992}) 15. d5 $1 (15. Qd3 g6 16. Re4) 15... Bxh4 (15... exd5 16. Qd3 f5 17. Bxe7 (17. Qxd5+ Qxd5 18. Nxd5 Bxh4 (18... Bd6 19. Rad1 $16 {[%csl Yc2,Yh4,Rh5][%cal Rd1d6,Re1e7]}) (18... Bd8 19. Bxd8 Raxd8 20. Rad1 $36) 19. Nxh4 Nd4 $1 (19... Rad8 20. Rad1) 20. Ne7+ Kf7 21. Bxf5 Nf4 $13) 17... Nxe7 18. Nd4 Rf7 (18... Re8 19. Ba4) 19. Ne6 $44 (19. Rad1 $5 $36)) 16. dxc6 Bxc6 17. Ne5 $1 Bxf2+ {What else? Black position is desperate after} (17... Qf6 18. g3 {or}) (17... Qxd1 18. Bxd1 Bxg2 19. Bxh5 Bb7 20. Rad1 $18) 18. Kxf2 Qh4+ 19. Kg1 Rad8 20. Nxc6 $5 {Interesting anf good, but maybe even stronger was to play} (20. Bh7+ $5 {and White getting big advantage in any case, for example:} Kxh7 (20... Kh8 21. Qc2 Bb7 22. Be4 $18) 21. Qc2+ g6 22. Nxc6 Rd6 23. Ne4 Rd5 24. Qf2 Qxf2+ 25. Nxf2 $18) ({From other point, Black is compleatly OK after} 20. Qg4 Qxg4 21. Nxg4 Bxg2 $1 $13 (21... Rd2 22. Re2 Rfd8 23. Rd1 $1) 22. Kxg2 $140 Rd2+ 23. Re2 $2 Nf4+ $19) 20... Rxd1 21. Raxd1 $16 {White has clear advantage, but it is not still to transfere this advantage to the point.} Nf6 22. Ne5 (22. h3 Nh5 $1) 22... Ng4 $1 23. Nxg4 Qxg4 24. Rd7 Qg5 $1 25. h3 (25. Rxa7 Qd2 26. Re2 Qc1+ 27. Nd1 $6 Rd8) 25... Qc5+ 26. Kh1 b5 {[%cal Gb5b4]} 27. Rb7 a6 (27... Qf2 $5 28. Re2 Qf1+ 29. Kh2 a6) 28. Rf1 Qc4 29. Rd1 Qc5 {It is not clear how White can improve there position.} 30. Rd2 Qe3 31. Rbd7 a5 $5 32. R7d3 (32. Nxb5 $2 Qe1+ 33. Kh2 Qe5+ $19) 32... Qe1+ 33. Kh2 Qe5+ 34. g3 b4 35. axb4 axb4 36. Nd1 g5 37. Re3 Qc7 38. Nf2 Rd8 39. Rde2 (39. Rxd8+ Qxd8 40. Re2 Qd4 $11) 39... Rd4 40. Ng4 Kg7 41. Ne5 (41. Rf2 $5 {[%cal Gg4f6]}) 41... h5 42. Nf3 Rd5 43. Bb3 Rc5 (43... Rf5 44. Nd4) 44. h4 (44. Bxe6 fxe6 (44... h4 45. Nd4 hxg3+ 46. Rxg3 Qf4 47. Nb3) 45. Nd4 Qa7 46. Nxe6+ Kf6 47. Nxc5 Qxc5 $14) 44... gxh4 45. Nxh4 Rc1 46. Re5 Qc6 47. Ng2 Qf3 48. R5e3 Qf1 49. Ne1 (49. Re1 Rxe1 50. Rxe1 Qf2 51. Re4 $11) 49... Kh6 50. Ba4 Kg7 51. Re4 Kh6 52. Bd7 Kg7 53. Re5 Kh6 54. Bb5 Qf6 55. Bd3 h4 56. R5e4 hxg3+ 57. Kxg3 Kg7 58. Rf2 (58. Rxb4 $1 $16) 58... Qd8 59. Rf3 Qd6+ 60. Kg2 f5 61. Re2 Kf6 62. b3 Qd4 63. Bc4 Qg4+ 64. Kf2 Qh4+ 65. Kf1 Qh1+ 66. Kf2 Qh4+ 67. Kf1 Qh1+ 68. Kf2 Qh4+ 1/2-1/2

