{[%mdl 2080]} 1. e4 {Bangiev. McShane.} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. f4 c5 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. Be3 cxd4 8. Nxd4 Bc5 9. Qd2 O-O {'!' Bangiev.} 10. O-O-O a6 11. h4 Nxd4 12. Bxd4 b5 13. Rh3 {McShane: 'This looks a little slow. Pushing on with 13.h5 or 13.g4 may be better.'} b4 14. Ne2 {Bangiev: 'Ein neuer Zug in dieser Stellung. Der weiße Plan ist allerdings nicht neu. Die Überführung des Springer nach d4 ist für Weiß in der französischen Verteidigung eine Herausforderung.'} (14. Na4 Bxd4 15. Qxd4 Qa5 (15... f6 16. Qxb4 $5 fxe5 17. Qd6 Qf6 18. f5 $5 Qh6+ 19. Kb1 Rxf5 20. Rf3 $1 $36 {Kasparov,G-Short,N/Amsterdam VSB 1994}) (15... a5 16. b3 $6 {'!?' Bangiev.} (16. Bb5 Rb8 (16... Ba6 $2 17. Bxd7) 17. Bd3 (17. Bxd7 Bxd7 18. Nc5 Bb5 19. f5 Qc7 $16 {fc8}) 17... Qc7 (17... f6 $5) 18. Re1 {'!?' Bangiev. Bangiev: 'f5'} (18. h5 Bb7 19. g4 Rfc8 20. Rh2 Qc6 21. b3 Ba6 $132 {Fogarasi,T-Luther,T/Kecskemet 1993}) 18... Qc6 19. b3 Ba6 20. Bxa6 Qxa6 21. Rg3 (21. f5 exf5 22. Qxd5 Nb6 $13) 21... Rbc8 (21... Qc6 22. f5) 22. f5 Qc6 (22... exf5 $2 23. e6) 23. Re2 $14 {Arakhamia,K-Matveeva,S/Kishinev izt-W 1995} (23. Re2 {Bangiev} Kh8 $132 {1-0 Arakhamia,K-Matveeva,S/Kishinev 1995/(61)})) 16... Ba6 17. Kb1 Bxf1 18. Rxf1 Qc7 19. h5 Ra6 20. Re3 Rc6 21. Rf2 f6 {Bangiev: '0-1 Kulish,I-Matveeva,S/Rostov 1995/(39)'} 22. Ree2 h6 $15 {Kulish,I-Matveeva,S/Rostov on Don-W 1995}) 16. b3 Bb7 17. Rg3 $5 (17. c3 Rfc8 18. Kb2 (18. Kb1 bxc3 19. Rxc3 Rxc3 20. Qxc3 Qxc3 21. Nxc3 Rc8 22. Kb2 $14 {Herrera,I-Ramas,L/CUB-ch 1993}) 18... bxc3+ 19. Rxc3 Rxc3 20. Qxc3 Qxc3+ 21. Nxc3 Kf8 22. a4 Ke7 23. a5 $14 {Nijboer,F-Luther,T/Leeuwarden op 1992}) 17... Rfc8 18. Rd2 Bc6 19. f5 Qc7 20. f6 g6 21. Qf4 $5 $40 {Arakhamia,K-Gurevich,M/Helsinki op 1992}) (14. Na4 {(McShane) may be better, as Shirov's attack came very fast. The problem is that the knight is prone to being attacked by a black bishop.}) 14... a5 15. Qe3 (15. Bxc5 {Bangiev} Nxc5 16. Nd4 Ba6 17. Bxa6 Rxa6 18. Qe3 a4 $36) 15... Qc7 16. Bxc5 Nxc5 17. Nd4 a4 (17... Ba6 {Bangiev} 18. Bxa6 Rxa6 19. h5 (19. f5 $6 Ne4) 19... a4 20. h6 g6 21. Kb1) 18. Kb1 $6 {Serious inaccuracy passing the initiative into black's hands.It was nessasary to prevent black from playing 18...a3.The only way to do it was to play 18.a3!:} (18. a3 $1 Nb3+ (18... b3) (18... bxa3 19. Qxa3 Qb6 (19... Ba6 20. Rc3 Rfc8 21. Bxa6 Rxa6 22. Nb5 Qb6 23. Nd6 Rc7 24. Kb1 $14) 20. h5 Ba6 21. Bxa6 Rxa6 22. h6 g6 23. g4 Ne4 24. Rf3 $13) 19. Kb1 $1 (19. Nxb3 axb3 20. Qxb3 bxa3 21. bxa3 Ba6 22. Qc3 Qb6 $36) 19... Nxd4 20. Qxd4 bxa3 21. Rxa3 Bd7 22. h5 h6 23. g4 $14) (18. h5 {Bangiev} b3 $1) 18... a3 $1 {[%csl Rc3] McShane: 'Shirov's attack is already creating concrete threats and Polgar's attack is barely off the ground.'} (18... b3 $2 {Bangiev} 19. cxb3 axb3 20. Nxb3) 19. b3 Ba6 {'!' McShane. McShane: 'The black bishop has no better role than to exchange off its counterpart.' '!' Bangiev.} 20. Bxa6 (20. Bd3) 20... Rxa6 $15 21. Qe1 (21. h5 {Bangiev} Ne4 22. Rd3 Rc8 $40) 21... Rb6 $1 {'' Bangiev. Bangiev: 'Der weiße Eröffnungsplan ist gescheitert. Der Nachziehende steht deutlich besser.'} 22. c3 $6 {White tries to deprive black the control over the square c3,but opens the king,which proves to be crucial. McShane: 'Otherwise Black will play Ne4, threatening Nc3+ and, if need be, break with f6!' '?' Bangiev.} (22. g4 Ne4 23. Rdd3 Rc8 (23... f6 24. exf6 Rxf6 25. Ne2 Qc5 26. Rhe3 $13) 24. h5 f6 $1 25. exf6 gxf6 $15) (22. Ka1 {Bangiev} Ne4 23. Rhd3 $15 {Weiß steht schlechter, verfügt aber über recht feste Stellung.}) 22... Qb7 {'!' Bangiev.} 23. Rc1 Ne4 24. cxb4 Rxb4 25. Rd3 {McShane: 'The knight on e4 is White's main problem, as it stops him doubling his rooks on the c-file and posting his queen on a better square'} (25. Nc2 {Bangiev} Rc4 26. Nxa3 Rxc1+ (26... Ra4 $5) 27. Qxc1 Rc8 28. Qe1 (28. Nc2 d4 $19 { d3, a6}) 28... Qa7 29. Nc2 Qc5 $19) 25... Rc4 $1 $17 {Very strong move revealing white's problems. '!' McShane. McShane: 'Now Shirov attacks the c-file with his rooks and Judit's position crumbles.' '!' Bangiev.} 26. Rxc4 {'?!' Bangiev.} (26. g4 Rfc8 27. Rc2 Rxc2 28. Nxc2 Qb5 29. Qe3 Nf2 $1 $17 {[%csl Rd3,Rg4]}) (26. Rdd1 {McShane} Rfc8 {threatening Nc3+} 27. Ka1 Qb6 $1 {is no better, as the d4 knight must now retreat}) (26. g3 $142 {Bangiev}) 26... dxc4 {[%csl Rb1][%cal Gb7b1]} 27. Rd1 $6 ({It was possible to put up some rsistance after} 27. Re3 $5 Nc5 28. Qe2 cxb3 29. Nxb3 Qb4 30. g3 Rc8 $17) 27... Nc5 {'-+' Bangiev.} 28. Qc3 Qxg2 {McShane: 'The diagonal opens for the queen.'} 29. b4 (29. Qxc4 {McShane} Qb2#) 29... Nd3 $19 30. Qxa3 Ra8 {'!' McShane.} 31. Rxd3 cxd3 (31... Rxa3 32. Rxa3 Qg1+ 33. Kc2 Qf2+ 34. Kb1 Qe1+ 35. Kc2 Qe4+ $19) {McShane: But Shirov's move wipes out all counterchances...} 32. Qxd3 Qxa2+ 33. Kc1 Qa1+ 34. Kd2 Rd8 35. Ke3 Qe1+ 0-1

