1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Be7 6. Bxf6 Bxf6 7. Nf3 O-O 8. Bc4 Nc6 9. Bb5 {Harmless continuation.} (9. c3 e5 10. d5 Na5 (10... Nb8 $5 11. O-O Bg4 12. h3 Bxf3 13. Qxf3 Be7 14. Bb5 a6 15. Ba4 Nd7 $11 {Ivanchuk,V-Ehlvest,J/Reggio Emilia8990}) 11. Bd3 b6 12. Qc2 g6 (12... Kh8 13. O-O Nb7 14. Rfe1 Qxd5 $6 15. Nxf6 gxf6 16. Be4 $36 {Garcia Martinez,S-Braga,F/Havana-B 1983}) 13. Nxf6+ Qxf6 14. O-O Bg4 15. Nd2 Nb7 16. Rae1 Nd6 17. Qa4 Bf5 $11 {Levenfish,G-Bondarevsky,I/Leningrad/Moscow 1939}) (9. Nxf6+ Qxf6 10. O-O e5 11. Nxe5 Nxe5 12. dxe5 Qxe5 13. c3 {½-½ Balashov,Y-Dreev,A/RUS-ch 1995}) 9... Bd7 10. Qd2 Be7 11. O-O (11. Be2 $5 Nb4 12. Ne5 Bc6 (12... Be8 13. O-O Nd5 14. Rfe1 Nf6 15. Bf3 $14) 13. Nxc6 Nxc6 14. c3 e5 15. d5 Nb8 $13) 11... Ne5 12. Nxe5 ({May be better was} 12. Be2 Nxf3+ 13. Bxf3 Bc6 14. Qe3 Bxe4 15. Bxe4 c6 $11 {with balance.}) 12... Bxb5 13. c4 Ba6 (13... Be8 $5 14. Rad1 f6 (14... Bd6 $5) 15. Nf3 b5 16. b3 Rb8 17. Qe2 bxc4 18. bxc4 Bh5 19. Ng3 Bf7 $13) 14. Rac1 c5 $1 $36 {Shirov plays this game at his best:now he sacrifices a pawn and in the endgame doesn't take it back till the right moment.} 15. dxc5 Qxd2 16. Nxd2 Rfd8 (16... Bxc5 $6 17. Nd7 Rfd8 18. Nxc5 Rxd2 19. b4 Rc8 20. a3 $14) 17. Nb3 Rac8 18. f4 b6 $1 ({Of course not} 18... f6 19. Nf3 Bxc5+ 20. Nxc5 Rxc5 21. b3 b6 22. Rfd1 $11 {with equality.}) 19. Rfd1 (19. cxb6 axb6 20. Rfd1 f6 $1 (20... Rxd1+ $6 21. Rxd1 f6 22. Rd7 Bf8 23. Ra7 $1 Bxc4 24. Nxc4 Rxc4 25. Ra6 Rc2 26. Rxb6 Rxb2 27. Rxe6 $11) 21. Nd7 Bxc4 22. Rd4 (22. Nxb6 $2 Rxd1+ 23. Rxd1 Bxb3 24. axb3 Bc5+ $19) 22... Bxb3 23. Rxc8 Rxc8 24. axb3 Rc2 $17) 19... Rxd1+ 20. Rxd1 Rc7 $1 {[%csl Gd7] Covering square d7.} 21. Rd6 ({Deserved attention} 21. cxb6 $5 axb6 22. Rd7 Rxd7 23. Nxd7 Bxc4 24. Kf2 Bxb3 25. axb3 h5 26. Ke3 b5 $15 {[%cal Gg8h7,Gh7f5]}) 21... Kf8 (21... Bxd6 $6 22. cxd6 Rc8 23. c5 $1 f6 (23... bxc5 24. d7 Rd8 25. Nxc5 Bb5 26. a4 Bxa4 27. Nxa4 f6 28. Nd3 Rxd7 29. Nac5 $14) 24. Nc6 $1 Rxc6 25. d7 Rc8 26. dxc8=Q+ Bxc8 $11) 22. cxb6 Bxd6 23. bxc7 Bxc7 $36 24. c5 $5 ({Much better was} 24. Nd4 $1 g5 25. g3 Bxe5 26. fxe5 Bxc4 27. b3 Bd5 $15 {and white has good chanses to hold the endgame.}) 24... g5 25. Nc6 gxf4 26. a4 (26. Nxa7 $1 Be5 27. Kf2 Bxb2 28. c6 Ke7 29. Kf3 Kd6 $15) 26... Bc4 $1 27. Nd2 Bd5 28. Nxa7 Ba5 $15 {This ending is a classic example of "what the pair of bishops is capable to do".} 29. Nb1 Bb4 30. Nb5 Bxc5+ 31. Kf1 f3 32. gxf3 Bxf3 33. Nd2 Bd5 34. Ke2 Ke7 $17 35. Kd3 f5 36. Nc3 Bb7 37. Kc4 Be3 38. Kd3 Bg1 39. b4 Bxh2 40. b5 h5 41. a5 h4 42. Ke2 (42. a6 Bg2 43. Nc4 h3 44. b6 Bb8 $19) 42... h3 43. a6 Bg2 44. Kf2 Bd6 45. Nf3 (45. Na4 Ba8 46. Nf3 h2 47. Nxh2 Bxh2 48. b6 Bc6 $19) 45... Bc5+ 46. Kg3 f4+ 47. Kg4 Bg1 48. b6 Bxf3+ 49. Kxf3 h2 50. Kg2 f3+ 0-1

