1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. a3 Bb7 5. Nc3 d5 6. Qc2 c5 7. cxd5 exd5 8. e4 $1 {Kramnik very correctly opens up the center with a bang, since black is ill prepared for the early opening of the files with 6...c5.} (8. Bf4 Bd6 9. Bxd6 Qxd6 10. e3 O-O 11. Be2 Nbd7 12. dxc5 bxc5 13. O-O Rac8 14. Rfd1 Qe7 15. Rd2 Rfd8 16. Rad1 Nb6 {½-½ Umanskaya,I-Rakitskaja,M/St Petersburg 2003/ (43)}) 8... cxd4 (8... dxe4 9. Bb5+ Bc6 10. Ne5 (10. Qa4 Bxb5 11. Nxb5 Nbd7 12. Ne5 a6 13. Qb3 Nxe5 14. dxe5 axb5 15. exf6 Qd3 16. Qc3 O-O-O 17. Bg5 Rd5 18. Bh4 g5 19. Bg3 Bd6 {½-½ Farago,I-Frick,C/Germany 1997/ (31)}) 10... Bxb5 11. Qb3 Qe7 12. Qxb5+ Nbd7 13. Qc6 Qd8 14. Nxd7 Nxd7 15. O-O Be7 16. dxc5 Rc8 17. Qa4 Rxc5 18. Rd1 Qc8 19. Be3 Ra5 20. Qd4 Nf6 $11 {0-1 Ryskin,A-Aseev,K/Sochi 1993/ (34)}) 9. Bb5+ Nbd7 (9... Bc6 10. Nxd5 Bxb5 11. Nc7+ Ke7 12. Nxb5 $18) 10. e5 $5 {Taking a risky path in a fight for the whole pointy, other would be tempted to be satisfied with more conservative 10.xd4.} (10. Nxd4 dxe4 (10... Nxe4 11. Nc6 Bxc6 12. Bxc6 Rc8 13. Nxe4 dxe4 14. Qxe4+ Qe7 15. Be3 $14) 11. Nc6 Bxc6 12. Bxc6 Rc8 13. Nxe4 Be7 14. Nxf6+ Bxf6 15. Qe2+ Qe7 16. Bxd7+ Kxd7 17. Be3 Rhd8 18. O-O $14) 10... dxc3 11. exf6 Qc7 (11... Qxf6 $5 12. O-O (12. Bg5 Qd6 13. O-O f6 14. Rfe1+ Kd8 15. Be3 $13) 12... h6 (12... cxb2 13. Bxb2 Qd6 14. Rfe1+ Kd8 15. Ng5 Qf4 16. Qc1 $18) 13. Re1+ (13. bxc3 Bd6 14. Qa4 O-O-O 15. Be3 Ne5 $11) 13... Kd8 14. bxc3 Bd6 $13) 12. Qe2+ Kd8 13. fxg7 (13. Bxd7 Kxd7 14. Ne5+ Kd8 15. Bg5 g6 16. Bf4 Bd6 17. Nxf7+ Qxf7 18. Bxd6 cxb2 19. Be7+ Kd7 20. Qxb2 Qe6+ $11) 13... Bxg7 14. O-O Re8 (14... a6 15. Bxd7 Kxd7 16. bxc3 Qxc3 17. Rb1 $40) (14... cxb2 15. Bxb2 Re8 16. Qd2 Bxb2 17. Qxb2 Qf4 18. Rfe1 Rg8 19. Qe2 $40) 15. Bg5+ $1 f6 16. Be3 {[%mdl 128] For all her suffering black has only won a pawn and the king remained in the center.} a6 (16... cxb2 17. Qxb2 Re7 18. Rfe1 Nc5 19. Bd4 $36) 17. Bxd7 (17. Bd3 Ne5 $1 18. Nxe5 fxe5 $11) 17... Kxd7 (17... Qxd7 $2 18. Bxb6+ Kc8 19. Qc2 Qc6 20. Bd4 $18) 18. Nd4 (18. bxc3 Re4 (18... Qxc3 19. Rfc1 Qa5 20. Nd4 Re4 21. Qh5 $18) 19. Nd2 $1 (19. Nd4) 19... Rh4 20. g3 Ra4 21. Qh5 $16) 18... Re4 (18... cxb2 19. Qg4+ $5 (19. Qxb2 f5 20. Rac1 Qd6 21. Qc2 Bxd4 22. Bxd4 Re4 $11) 19... Kd8 20. Rab1 Bc8 21. Qh5 $14) 19. bxc3 Qe5 (19... Rae8 20. Qh5 Kd8 21. Rfb1 $1 $14) 20. Rfb1 $1 b5 (20... Qc7 21. Nf5 Bf8 22. Qh5 $18) 21. a4 {Now the defender can claim no compensation for the horrendous suffering, white must be winning.} Bh6 (21... Bc6 $2 22. axb5 axb5 23. Nxc6 $18) 22. axb5 a5 (22... Bxe3 23. fxe3 Rxe3 24. Qg4+ f5 25. Nxf5 Re4 26. Qh5 $18) 23. Qf3 (23. Re1 $16) 23... Bxe3 24. fxe3 Rg8 (24... Rxe3 25. Qg4+ Kd8 26. Qg8+ Qe8 27. Qxh7 $18) 25. Qh3+ Reg4 (25... Ke8 26. Qxh7 Qg5 27. Qh3 Rxe3 28. Re1 $18) 26. Rxa5 Kd6 (26... Ke8 27. Rb2 $18) 27. Ra2 Bc8 (27... Qe4 28. Rf1 Bc8 29. Qf3 $18) 28. Qf3 Rh4 (28... Re4 29. Rf2 Rxe3 30. Qxf6+ Qxf6 31. Rxf6+ Ke5 32. Rh6 Rxc3 33. Nc6+ Ke4 34. Rxh7 $18) 29. g3 Re4 30. b6 Rxe3 31. b7 $1 {Nice tactical shot, that aims to shorten the burden of poor black king.} Re1+ (31... Rxf3 32. b8=Q+ Ke7 33. Ra7+ Bd7 34. Rxd7+ Kxd7 35. Rb7+ $18) 32. Rxe1 Qxe1+ 33. Kg2 Bxb7 34. Qxf6+ Kc5 (34... Kd7 35. Qf7+ $18) 35. Re2 (35. Nb3+ Kb5 36. Ra5+ Kc4 37. Qd4+ Kxb3 38. Qb4+ Kc2 39. Ra2+ Kc1 40. Qb2+ Kd1 41. Qc2#) 35... Qb1 (35... Qxc3 36. Rc2 (36. Ne6+ Kc4 37. Qe7 $18) 36... Qxc2+ 37. Nxc2 $18) 36. Ne6+ Kb5 37. Qf7 Ka5 38. Qc7+ (38. Qc7+ Ka6 39. Nc5+ Ka7 40. Nxb7 $18) 1-0

