1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 d5 6. Bd3 Be7 7. O-O Nc6 8. c4 Nb4 9. Be2 O-O 10. a3 Nc6 11. cxd5 Qxd5 12. Nc3 Nxc3 13. bxc3 Qd6 $146 14. Rb1 b6 15. Re1 Be6 (15... Bf5 16. Rb5 Qg6 17. Rxf5 $1 Qxf5 18. Bd3 Qa5 (18... Qd7 19. Bb5 $18) (18... Qf6 19. Be4 $1 $16 {[%cal Gc1g5]} h6 20. Bxc6 Qxc6 21. Rxe7 Qxc3 22. Bf4 $16) 19. Ne5 $1 Nxe5 20. Rxe5 Qxc3 21. Rxe7 Rae8 22. Re3 $16) (15... Re8 16. Bd3 Be6 {-see game}) 16. Bd3 Rae8 17. Rb5 $1 {[%cal Gb5h5]} Na5 (17... a6 18. Rb1 a5 19. Rb5 $36) 18. Rbe5 Nc6 19. R5e2 $16 {[%mdl 32] White's army has taken a commanding position and is ready to strike while Black's s look pretty awkward and his light pieces are unable to stretch a helping hand to their } Bd7 (19... h6 20. Bb1 Bd5 21. Qc2 f5 22. Ba2 $16) 20. d5 Na5 21. Ne5 Bf6 (21... Bc8 22. Qc2 Qxd5 23. Bxh7+ Kh8 24. c4 Qc5 25. Bb2 $40 {[%csl Rh8]}) 22. Bf4 $1 Bxe5 23. Bxe5 Qxa3 24. Re3 $1 {The renown 2-s sac is on the cards!} (24. Qd2 h6 25. Bxc7 Rxe2 26. Rxe2 Nb3 27. Qb2 Qxb2 28. Rxb2 Nc5 $14) 24... Qc5 $4 {[%mdl 8192] Karpov overlooks the threat, but it's to be said that Black is already deep in trouble} (24... h6 25. Bxc7 (25. c4 Qb4 26. Bc3 Qd6 27. Rxe8 Rxe8 28. Rxe8+ Bxe8 29. Qg4 f6 30. Qe4 Kf8 31. c5 Qe7 $13) 25... Rxe3 26. Rxe3 Qc5 27. d6 Nc4 28. Re7 $16) 25. Bxh7+ $1 Kxh7 26. Qh5+ (26. Qh5+ Kg8 27. Bxg7 Kxg7 (27... f5 28. Qg6 $18) 28. Rg3+ Kf6 29. Qg5#) 1-0

