1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be3 Ng4 7. Bg5 h6 8. Bh4 g5 9. Bg3 Bg7 10. Be2 h5 11. Bxg4 Bxg4 12. f3 Bd7 13. Bf2 Nc6 14. O-O (14. Qd2 Ne5 15. O-O e6 16. b3 Ng6 17. Rad1 g4 18. f4 h4 19. Nde2 h3 20. g3 Rc8 21. e5 d5 22. Nd4 O-O 23. Qd3 f5 24. Nce2 Rf7 25. Rc1 Bf8 26. c3 Ne7 27. Rfd1 Nc6 28. c4 dxc4 {Anand,V-Kasparov,G/Geneva Credit Suisse 1996/EXP 54/[King]/0-1 (55)}) 14... e6 15. Nce2 (15. Nxc6 {is the most popular alternative.} Bxc6 16. Bd4 Be5 17. Qd2 Qf6 18. Bxe5 dxe5 19. a4 O-O 20. b3 Rfd8 21. Qe3 Qf4 22. Qxf4 gxf4 23. Rfd1 h4 24. Rxd8+ Rxd8 $15 {0-1 Short,N-Topalov,V/Novgorod 1997 (45)}) 15... Ne5 16. Qd2 (16. b3 g4 17. f4 h4 $1 18. Be3 h3 19. g3 Nc6 20. Qd3 O-O 21. Rad1 f5 22. c4 Qa5 23. Nc3 Rae8 24. Rfe1 e5 25. Nxc6 Bxc6 26. b4 Qa3 27. b5 exf4 28. Bxf4 axb5 29. cxb5 Qc5+ 30. Be3 Qxc3 31. bxc6 Qxc6 32. Qxd6 Qxe4 33. Qd5+ Qxd5 34. Rxd5 Bc3 35. Re2 Re4 36. Kf2 Rfe8 37. Rd3 Bf6 38. Red2 Rxe3 {0-1 Shirov,A-Kasparov,G/Linares14th 1997/CBM 57/[Knaak]}) 16... b5 $6 17. b3 Ng6 ({After} 17... g4 18. f4 h4 19. fxe5 dxe5 20. Rad1 {White retains an advantage.}) 18. Rad1 Rc8 (18... Be5 $5 {was worth of considering here.}) 19. c3 Be5 20. Nc2 (20. Be3 $5 {, attacking the g5-pawn, seems a promising alternative to the text move.}) 20... Nf4 21. Nxf4 gxf4 (21... Bxf4 22. Be3 {yields White clearly better chances.}) (21... Bxc3 $2 {is bad in view of} 22. Qxd6) 22. Bd4 {[%csl Re5][%cal Gc2b4,Gb4d3,Gd3e5] Planning the knight transfer to d3 via b4.} ({Still, immediate} 22. Nb4 {was a plausible alternative:} Qf6 (22... Bxc3 23. Qxd6 {is not recommendable for Black.}) (22... Rxc3 23. Bd4 $36 (23. Nd3 $5 $36)) (22... Rg8 23. Nd3 (23. Nxa6 $5 Rc6 $140 24. Nb4 Bxc3 $4 25. Nxc6 $18) 23... Qg5 24. Bd4 $14 {25.e5 de5 26.e5}) 23. Nxa6 Rxc3 24. Nc5 $36) 22... a5 23. Ne1 (23. Qf2 $5 {, intending to double the rooks along the d-file by playing d3, fd1 followed by d2, deserved here a serious attention.}) 23... Qf6 24. Bxe5 Qxe5 25. Nd3 Qxc3 26. Qxf4 Qd4+ 27. Nf2 (27. Kh1 Rc2 $5 {also does not promise White any adavantage.}) 27... Qe5 28. Qd2 Ke7 29. Qxa5 Rc2 30. Rd2 ({A dubious} 30. Qb4 Rxa2 31. Nd3 {(31... g732.f2, intending e4-e5), is strongly met by} Rg8 $1 {, and White must play} 32. Rf2 (32. g3 $4 {would be a terrible mistake in view of} Rxg3+ 33. Kh1 Rg1+ $19)) 30... Ra8 $1 {This natural move equalizes the game. Rook's control over the second rank provides Black a full compensation for a sacrificed pawn.} 31. Qxa8 Rxd2 32. b4 Qd4 33. Qg8 e5 34. Qg5+ Ke8 35. Qg8+ Ke7 36. Qg5+ 1/2-1/2

