1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Nbd7 6. Nf3 h6 7. Nxf6+ Nxf6 8. Bd2 c5 9. c3 $6 {It's hard to call this logical move a dubious one,but it's not the move,which is dubious,but the idea behind this move.White simply gives up the idea to fight for opening avantage and chooses the variation,which almost by force leads to draw.} (9. Bd3 a6 10. Qe2 b5 11. dxc5 Bxc5 12. O-O-O Qc7 13. Bc3 Bb7 14. Be5 Qb6 15. Bxf6 gxf6 16. Be4 $14 {Bologan,V-Komarov,D/Reggio9697}) (9. dxc5 Bxc5 10. Bd3 O-O 11. Qe2 e5 (11... Qd5 12. c4 Qc6 13. Bc3 e5 14. Nxe5 Qxg2 15. O-O-O Re8 $13 {Khalifman,A-Dreev,A/Yalta rapid 1995}) 12. O-O-O Re8 13. Bb5 Bd7 14. Bxd7 Qxd7 15. Be3 Bxe3+ 16. Qxe3 Qa4 $11 {Bologan,V-Dokhoian,Y/BL9394}) 9... cxd4 10. cxd4 (10. Nxd4 Bc5 11. Bb5+ (11. Be3 O-O 12. Nc6 (12. Nxe6 $6 Qxd1+ 13. Rxd1 Bxe3 14. Nxf8 Bb6 $15) 12... Qxd1+ 13. Rxd1 Ba3 $1 14. bxa3 bxc6 $11) 11... Bd7 12. Qa4 $6 Bxd4 13. cxd4 O-O $15) 10... Be7 (10... Qd5 $5) 11. Bd3 Bd7 12. Ne5 Bc6 ({Too dangerous is} 12... Rc8 $6 13. Qf3 Bc6 $6 14. Nxc6 $1 (14. Qg3 $2 Kf8 (14... Qxd4 15. Bc3 Qd5 $5 (15... Bb4 $5 16. O-O Bxc3 17. bxc3 Qxc3 18. Qxg7 Qxe5 19. Qxh8+ Kd7 20. Qxh6 $1 (20. Qg7 $2 Ke7 $1 (20... Rg8 21. Qxf7+ Kc8 22. g3 Qd5 23. f3 $18) 21. Rfe1 Qd5 22. Qg3 $1 Rg8 23. Be4 $1 Qa5 $1 $19) 20... Ng4 21. Qh4 Rh8 22. Qg3 Rxh2 $1 23. Qxg4 $8 Rxg2+ 24. Qxg2 Bxg2 25. Kxg2 $14) 16. Qxg7 Rf8 17. Nxc6 (17. O-O-O $2 Qxg2 18. Qxh6 Ne4 $1 $17) 17... Rxc6 18. Bxf6 Qxd3 $15)) 14... bxc6 15. Ba6 $1 Rc7 16. Ba5 $18) 13. Nxc6 bxc6 14. Bc3 (14. Qa4 O-O 15. Rc1 $6 (15. Qxc6 $2 Qxd4 16. Qc3 Qd5 $1 $15) 15... c5 $1 $15) 14... Nd5 15. Qa4 O-O 16. O-O (16. Qxc6 Rc8 17. Qa6 Nxc3 18. bxc3 Rxc3 $17 {[%csl Rd4]}) 16... c5 $5 $11 {Black has reached the equality with very simple and natural moves.Now both sides start to eliminate pieces from the board and the game very quickly ends up a draw.} (16... Nxc3 17. bxc3 c5) 17. Be4 Nxc3 18. bxc3 Rc8 19. Qxa7 cxd4 20. cxd4 (20. Qxd4 Bf6 21. Qxd8 Rfxd8 22. Rfd1 Rxd1+ 23. Rxd1 Rxc3 $11) 20... Bf6 21. Rad1 Rc4 {[%csl Rd4]} 22. Qa6 Rxd4 23. Rxd4 Qxd4 24. Qd3 Qxd3 25. Bxd3 Ra8 26. Bc4 Kf8 27. Rd1 Ke7 28. Kf1 Be5 29. g3 g5 30. h3 Ra7 31. Ke2 Kf6 32. Rd3 Ke7 33. Ke3 Bd6 34. Ke2 1/2-1/2

