1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. Bd3 {In some cases when Black castles  a g4-g5 push can be forceful with a  on h4. Otherwise it is a loss of a tempo, in the  the h5  blocks g7 and h6.} (8. h5 {is still the main line.}) 8... Bxd3 9. Qxd3 e6 10. Bf4 Ngf6 11. O-O-O Be7 12. Kb1 O-O 13. Ng5 $6 {Unfortunately Black is not forced to take the intruder .} (13. Qe2 Qa5 14. Ne5 Rad8 15. Rd3 {This is a typical manoeuvre in this type of position.} Nd5 (15... Nxe5 $6 {This exchange makes White's  more dangerous. Besides g4-g5 White can also make profit from the h5 square by h5!} 16. dxe5 Nd5 17. Bd2 Qb5 (17... Qb6 $2 18. Nh5 $1 Kh7 19. Nxg7 $1 {destroying Black's .} Kxg7 20. Rg3+ Kh7 21. Qh5 $18) (17... Qa4 18. Ne4 $14 (18. Nh5 Nb4 (18... Kh8 19. Nxg7 $1) 19. Bxb4 Qxb4 20. Rg3 g6 $11)) 18. Qg4 $1 $14 {This is the precise move order.} (18. Ne4 Nb4 $1 (18... Nb6 $2 {founders on tactics again:} 19. Nf6+ $1 Bxf6 (19... gxf6 $2 20. Bxh6 $18) (19... Kh8 20. Bxh6 $1 $18) 20. exf6 Rxd3 21. cxd3 Na4 22. b3 Rd8 23. Rh3 $16) 19. Bxb4 Bxb4 20. Nf6+ {now doesn't lead anywhere after} gxf6 21. Qg4+ Kh7 22. exf6 Rg8 23. Qe4+ Qf5 $15) (18. Nh5 Ba3 $1 19. b3 Ne7 $13) 18... Kh8 19. Nh5 (19. c4 Qa6 20. Bg5 $5 {is again another attacking motif thanks to the  on h4.}) 19... Rg8 20. c4 (20. Bg5 $5) 20... Qa6 21. Rd1 $14 (21. Rc1 $2 {Overlooking in a promising position the following tactical blow.} Ne3 $1 22. Bxe3 $1 {sacrificing the exchange was the lesser evil.} (22. Qe4 $143 Rxd3 (22... Nf5 23. Bc3 Rxd3 {- 22...xd3}) 23. Qxd3 Nf5 24. Bc3 Rd8 25. Qe4 b5 $132 {McShane-Johannessen, Malmo 2003 CBM 97}) 22... Rxd3 23. Qf4 $1 (23. Bxh6 gxh6 24. Qf4 Rg7 $15) 23... Rf8 {and now White can make a draw in two different ways:} (23... Rxe3 $2 24. fxe3 Rf8 25. Qg4 g6 (25... Rg8 26. Rf1 $16) 26. Nf6 $16) 24. Qg3 (24. Nxg7 Kxg7 25. Qxh6+ Kg8 26. Bg5 Bxg5 27. Qxg5+ $11) 24... Rg8 $11)) (15... Qa4 $5) 16. Bd2 Qa4 $1 {is a better place for the .} (16... Qb6 17. Nh5 N5f6 (17... N7f6 18. c4 Nb4 19. Rb3 Nxh5 20. Qxh5 a5 21. c5 Qc7 22. Bxh6 $16 {destroying Black's  shelter.}) (17... Nxe5 18. dxe5 {- 15...xe5}) 18. Rg3 Nxh5 19. Qxh5 Bf6 20. Ng4 $16) 17. Ne4 (17. Nh5 Nxe5 18. dxe5 {- 15...xe5}) 17... N7f6 $142 (17... Nxe5 18. dxe5 $14) 18. Nxf6+ Nxf6 $13) (13. Ne4 Qa5 14. Nxf6+ Nxf6 15. Ne5 Rad8 16. Qg3 Kh8 17. Qb3 {This manoeuvre fails to impress, the  cannot be better for White.} Qb6 18. Rd3 Nd5 19. Bc1 Bf6 20. Rhd1 Qxb3 21. axb3 Kg8 $11 {Hracek-Gyimesi, Medulin 2002}) (13. Ne5 {- Miroshnichenko-Dreev, Keres mem rapid 2003 CBM 93}) 13... Qa5 $1 (13... a5 $6 {is the old, slow plan.} 14. Nh5 $1 $36 c5 (14... hxg5 $4 {opens the h  for White, which has lethal consequences.} 15. Nxf6+ Nxf6 16. hxg5 $18) 15. dxc5 Bxc5 16. Ne4 Nxh5 17. Qxd7 Nxf4 18. Nxc5 Qb6 $13) 14. Bd2 (14. Nh5 $2 hxg5 15. Nxf6+ gxf6 16. hxg5 Qf5 17. Qe2 fxg5 18. Qh5 Bf6 $17) (14. N5e4 Rfd8 $13) 14... Qd5 15. c4 $2 { White pushes it too hard.} (15. N5e4 {was still nothing special.} Rfd8 16. Qe2 (16. c4 $6 Ne5 $1) 16... Nb6 17. Bf4 Qc4 $13) 15... Ne5 $1 16. Qc2 $2 (16. Qa3 Nxc4 17. Qxe7 Nxd2+ 18. Rxd2 hxg5 19. hxg5 Qxg5 $17) (16. Qh7+ Nxh7 17. cxd5 Ng4 $1 18. Nxh7 Kxh7 $17) 16... Nxc4 $19 {Now White is simply lost..., but this was a rapid game.} 17. Bc1 Rfe8 18. f4 Nd6 19. Nf3 Nf5 20. Ne2 {White has to avoid the exchanges.} Nd6 21. Ne5 Qxg2 22. Ka1 Nf5 23. Rhg1 Qe4 24. Qd2 Rad8 25. Ng3 Nxg3 26. Rxg3 c5 (26... Bc5 $1 27. Rdg1 Nh5 $19 {was as good as winning.}) 27. f5 $5 Nh5 28. fxe6 fxe6 (28... f6 $5) 29. Rg4 Qf5 30. Qe2 {White has created some practical counterchances on the g .} Rf8 (30... cxd4 $142 31. Bxh6 (31. Rgxd4 $2 Rxd4 32. Rxd4 Bf6 $19) 31... Bf6 $17 {was still very strong.}) 31. Ng6 Rf7 32. Nxe7+ Rxe7 33. Rf1 {White's pieces become more and more active.} Qd5 (33... Qh7 $2 34. Qe5 Qd3 35. Rgg1 $16) 34. Bxh6 {Now White has already reasonable counterchances.} Rf8 35. Rfg1 (35. dxc5 Rxf1+ 36. Qxf1 Rd7 $13) 35... Qf3 $1 (35... cxd4 36. Rg5 Qf3 37. Qxf3 Rxf3 38. Rxh5 e5 39. Kb1 e4 40. Rhg5 Rff7 41. Rd5 $14) 36. Qc4 cxd4 (36... Qd5 37. Qe2 Qf3 $11 {is only a repetition of moves.}) 37. Qxd4 e5 38. Qc4+ Kh8 39. Bc1 Rf6 40. a3 Rc6 41. Qb4 Rec7 42. Bg5 Qf5 43. Be3 Qf3 1/2-1/2

