1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. Nce2 c5 6. c3 cxd4 7. cxd4 f6 8. f4 fxe5 9. fxe5 (9. dxe5 Nc6 10. Nf3 Bb4+ 11. Nc3 (11. Bd2 Nc5 12. Bxb4 Nxb4 13. Nc3 (13. Ned4 Qa5 $36) 13... O-O 14. a3 (14. g3 d4 $36) 14... Nc6 15. g3 Qb6 16. b4 Nxb4 17. axb4 (17. Rb1 Ncd3+ 18. Bxd3 Qe3+ $19) 17... Qxb4 18. Rc1 Nb3 $17) 11... Nc5 12. Be3 Qa5 13. Qc2 O-O 14. Rc1 $2 (14. a3 Ne4 (14... d4 15. Nxd4 Nxd4 16. Bxd4 Rxf4 17. O-O-O Bxa3 18. g3 $1 $16 (18. bxa3 Qxa3+ 19. Qb2 Nb3+ $19)) 15. Rc1 Bxc3+ 16. bxc3 $13) 14... d4 $1 $17 {Shirov,A-Ivanchuk,V/Tilburg 1993}) 9... Bb4+ (9... Qh4+ 10. Ng3 Bb4+ 11. Kf2 O-O+ 12. Nf3 Nc6 13. Be3 $14) 10. Kf2 (10. Bd2 $2 Qh4+ $17) 10... O-O+ 11. Nf3 Nc6 12. a3 (12. Be3 $13) 12... Ndxe5 $6 {This sacrifice,wich is typical for many variations in french defense now is not so strong that's why black should prefer simple} (12... Ba5 13. Nf4 (13. h4 Qe7 14. Kg3 (14. g4 Ndxe5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Bg2 Nxg4+ $13) 14... Bc7 15. Kh3 Qf7 16. Nf4 Nf6 17. Bd3 Ne4 18. Rf1 $14) 13... Qe7 14. h4 $6 Bb6 $1 15. Kg3 (15. Be3 Ndxe5 $1 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. dxe5 Rxf4+ $19) 15... g5 16. hxg5 Nxd4 $1 17. Nxd4 Qxg5+ $40 {in all the cases with complicated struggle.}) 13. axb4 Qh4+ 14. Kg1 $6 {For some reason white decides to give up a pawn on f3,which is very important one.Better was} (14. Ng3 $5 Nxd4 15. Be2 Nexf3 16. gxf3 e5 17. Be3 $16) 14... Nxf3+ 15. gxf3 Rxf3 16. Ng3 Nxd4 17. Bg2 Rf7 $6 {Missing a chanse to get strong counterplay after} (17... Ne2+ $1 18. Qxe2 Qd4+ 19. Be3 Qxe3+ (19... Rxe3 20. Qf2 Rd3 $13) 20. Qxe3 Rxe3 21. Kf2 Rb3 $132) 18. Be3 $14 {Despite of material balance white has muh better chanse,mainly because of paralised queenside of black.} Nf5 $6 (18... Nc6 19. b5 Ne5 20. Bd4 Nc4 21. b3 Nd6 (21... Rf4 22. Ne2 $18) 22. b6 a6 23. Be5 $14) 19. Nxf5 Rxf5 20. b5 $1 {[%cal Ga1a4,Ga4g4]} Bd7 21. b6 a6 22. Qd4 Qh5 (22... Qxd4 23. Bxd4 Raf8 24. Re1 Rf4 25. Be3 R4f5 26. h4 Bc6 27. Bh3 R5f6 28. Bg5 $16) 23. h3 $1 Bc6 24. Kh2 e5 25. Qg4 Rd8 ({Deserved attention} 25... Qf7 26. Rhf1 Rf8 27. Rxf5 Qxf5 28. Qxf5 Rxf5 29. Ra5 $1 e4 30. Rc5 Rf6 31. Bd4 Re6 32. Kg1 $14 {and it's not so easy for white to breakthrough.}) 26. Qxh5 Rxh5 27. Rhf1 g6 $6 (27... e4 $5) 28. Bf3 $1 {Now the bishop makes hs way to e6 with decisive effect.} Rf5 29. Bg4 $1 Rxf1 30. Rxf1 Kg7 31. Be6 $1 $18 Be8 (31... Rf8 32. Bh6+ Kxh6 33. Rxf8 $18) 32. Bc5 1-0

