1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 {The Centre Counter is a rare guest in the modern tounament practice.} g6 4. c3 Nf6 5. Qe2 {White wants to avoid the main lines after} a6 (5... Bg7) 6. Ba4 (6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. h3 Bg7 8. d4 Nd7 9. O-O O-O 10. Bg5 Re8 11. e5 f6 12. Be3 cxd4 $17 13. Bxd4 c5 14. exf6 exf6 15. Qc4+ $17 Kh8 $5 16. Bxc5 $1 b5 17. Qd4 Bb7 18. Nbd2 $1 f5 $2 {gives away the important g .} 19. Qd6 $1 Nxc5 20. Qxc5 Rc8 21. Qb4 Rc7 22. Rfe1 Rce7 23. Rxe7 $18 Rxe7 24. a4 bxa4 25. Qxa4 {Hunting for pawns by} h6 {is again unhealthy} 26. Nd4 Qb6 27. Nc4 $44 {She had to go for the slightly better  after} Qf6 28. Qd1 Kh7 29. Qd2 Bd5 30. Ne3 Bb7 $14) 6... b5 7. Bc2 Bb7 8. O-O (8. e5 Nd5 9. d4 cxd4 10. cxd4 $1 (10. Be4 d3 11. Qxd3 Nc7 $1)) 8... d6 $6 (8... Bg7 9. e5 Nd5 10. d4 cxd4 11. cxd4) 9. d4 cxd4 10. cxd4 $5 $146 Nb4 $5 11. Bb3 Bxe4 (11... Nxe4 $11 12. a3) (11... d5 12. e5 Ne4 13. Nbd2 (13. a4) 13... Bg7 14. a3 Nxd2 15. Bxd2 Nc6 16. Rac1) 12. Bxf7+ Kxf7 13. Ng5+ Kg8 14. Nxe4 $5 Qd7 (14... Nbd5 15. Nbc3) 15. Nxf6+ exf6 16. Qf3 $6 Re8 (16... Rc8 17. Nc3 Nc2 $1 18. Nd5 Bg7 19. Nb6) 17. Bd2 Nc6 $1 (17... Nc2 18. Qb3+) 18. Nc3 Nxd4 (18... Bg7 19. Rfe1 Kf7 20. Qd5+ Re6 21. Rxe6) (18... Kg7 19. Nd5 Be7 20. Rac1) 19. Qd5+ Ne6 $1 20. Ne4 Qf7 (20... Kf7 21. Nxf6 Kxf6 22. Bc3+) 21. Rfe1 Be7 22. Bc3 (22. Nxd6 Bxd6 23. Qxd6 Rd8 24. Qxa6 Rxd2 25. Rxe6 Kg7 26. Rae1 $5) 22... Ng7 $15 (22... Kg7 23. Nxd6 Bxd6 24. Qxd6) 23. Qc6 Rd8 24. Ba5 Qe8 (24... Rf8 25. Nxd6 Bxd6 26. Qxd6) 25. Nxf6+ Bxf6 {Now already White has to play carefully the slightly worse .} 26. Rxe8+ Rxe8 27. Qxd6 Kf7 28. Qxa6 Bxb2 29. Rb1 1/2-1/2

