1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Nf3 c5 8. Rb1 O-O 9. Be2 Nc6 10. d5 Ne5 11. Nxe5 Bxe5 12. Qd2 e6 13. f4 Bc7 14. O-O exd5 15. exd5 Ba5 16. d6 Rb8 (16... b6) 17. Ba3 (17. Rb5 Bd7 18. Rxa5 Qxa5 19. f5 c4 20. f6 Qc5+ 21. Kh1 Kh8 22. Qh6 Rg8 23. Bg5 Qe5 24. Bxc4 Rbf8 25. Qh4 Qxd6 26. Rf4 Qd1+ 27. Rf1 Qd6 28. Bf4 Qb6 {0-1 Nikolenko,O-Voitsekhovsky,S/Minsk/1998/ (50)} 29. Bh6 Be6 30. Bxf8 Rxf8 31. a4 Bxc4 32. Qxc4 h5 33. h3 Kh7 34. Rf4 Qe6) (17. g4 Bd7 (17... c4) 18. f5 gxf5 19. Bd3 Kh8 20. Bxf5 Rg8 21. Bxd7 Qxd7 22. h3 f5 23. Bb2 c4 {Shirov,A-Topalov,V/Sarajevo/1999/ 1-0 (76)} 24. Qd4+ Rg7 25. Bc1 b5 26. Qf6 $5 Bb6+ 27. Kh2 Bc5 28. Bf4 Re8 29. Rbe1 fxg4 30. Rxe8+ Qxe8 31. Be5) 17... Bf5 18. Rbd1 (18. Rbc1 Rc8 19. g4 $1 $15 Bd7 $6 20. Bf3 b5 21. f5 Qh4 22. Rce1 Qf6 23. Bb2 c4 24. fxg6 hxg6 25. Re7 Bb6+ 26. Kg2 Be6 27. Ba3 $16 Rcd8 28. d7 Bc7 29. Bc6 Qh4 30. Kh1 $14 Qh3 31. Rf6 Qh4 32. g5 $13) 18... Rc8 {Black must get some counterplay on the kingside, since white's two bishops and domination on queenside make his position vulnerable.} (18... b6 19. h3 Qf6 20. Bb2 $1 Rbd8 21. Bb5 Bd7 22. c4 Qf5 23. Bxd7 Rxd7 24. Qe2 $17 Qe6 $5 25. Qxe6 fxe6 26. Be5) 19. g4 (19. Bf3 Qf6 $40 20. d7 (20. Bb2 c4 21. Rfe1 Bd3 22. Re5 $15 Qxd6 23. Bxb7 Rce8 24. Kh1 $15 Rxe5 $5 25. fxe5 Qxe5 26. Re1 Qf6) 20... Rcd8 21. Bxc5 Rxd7 $17 22. Qe3 Rc8 23. Rxd7 Bxd7 24. Bd4 Qd6 (24... Bb6 25. Bxb6) 25. Re1 Rxc3 $15 26. Qe8+) 19... Bd7 (19... Be4 20. d7 $17 Rc7 21. Bf3 $17) 20. f5 Qh4 21. Bf3 gxf5 (21... Rfe8 22. Kh1 $1 Re5 $1 (22... b5 23. fxg6 hxg6 24. Bd5) 23. fxg6 hxg6 24. Qf4 Qg5 (24... Bxc3 25. Bg2 $40 Rf8 26. Rd3 g5 $17 27. Qf6 Bd4 28. Bxc5 (28. Rxd4 Re6 29. Qe7 $11) 28... Rxc5 29. Qxd4) (24... Rf5 $2 25. Qe3 $1 $16 Rxf3 $5 26. Qxf3 Bc6 27. Rd5 Rf8 28. c4) 25. Bxb7 (25. Bc1 Qxf4 26. Bxf4 Ree8 27. Bxb7 $11 Re2 28. Rfe1 Rce8) (25. Qg3) 25... Qxf4 $19 26. Rxf4 Rb8 27. Bd5 Bxc3 $19 (27... Rxd5 28. Rxd5 Bc6 29. c4) 28. Bxf7+ Kg7 29. Bc4 Rf8 30. Rxf8 Kxf8 31. h3 Ke8 $1 32. Kh2 Bc6 33. Bc1 (33. Bd3 g5 34. Bc1 $1 Rd5 35. Bg6+ Kd7 36. Rxd5 $19 Bxd5 37. Bxg5 Be5+ 38. Kg1 Bxa2) (33. Bc1 Kd7 34. Rf1 (34. Bd2 $13 Bxd2 35. Rxd2 Re4) 34... Kxd6 35. Bf4 Ke7 36. Bxe5 Bxe5+ 37. Kg1 Bd4+)) (21... b5) 22. gxf5 Rfe8 23. Kh1 Re5 24. Qf4 Qg5 25. Bxb7 $2 {Svidler is making a move, that equals positional bancrupcy. Black seems to be having a good game, but after this move all white pawns on the queenside are of lesser quality.} Qxf4 26. Rxf4 Rb8 27. Bd5 Bxc3 28. Bxf7+ Kg7 $1 29. Bg6 hxg6 $1 30. h3 Kf8 $1 {[%mdl 128] Polgar plays her cards very skilfully, white has problems to hold his endangered kingside.} 31. Kh2 Ke8 32. Bc1 Bc6 0-1

