1. e4 {Golod,V} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 Nbd7 8. Qf3 Qc7 9. O-O-O {White's plan is: c2,e4(control over point e4).Besides,white has two principales moves: Golod,V: 'White's plan is: c2, e4 (control over the e4-square). Besides this, White has two main moves:'} b5 {c5(×d4) and so on.} 10. Bd3 {[%csl Re4][%cal Ge2c3]} b4 $5 $146 (10... Bb7) (10... Bb7 {Golod,V: '-transfer to 13.d1'} 11. Rhe1 O-O-O 12. f5 {[%csl Yd1,Yd2] e2,0-0 with equal game. Golod,V: 'e2,0-0 with a level game.'} e5 $5 13. Nb3 Be7 14. a4) 11. Nd5 $140 exd5 {Just so!} (11... Qb7 12. Rhe1 $15 (12. Nxf6+ Nxf6 {-transfer to 13.d1} {Another alternative is:} 13. Bxf6 gxf6) {Badly right away: Golod,V: 'Playing'} 12... exd5 {because of: Golod,V: 'right away is bad, because of:'} 13. exd5+ (13. Nc6 $15) 13... Kd8 14. Nc6+ {[%csl Rd4]} {Can be recommended: Golod,V: 'What can be recommended is:'} Kc7 15. Re4) 12. exd5 $6 {[%mdl 16384]} Bb7 {This move better than: Golod,V: 'This move is better than:'} (12... Be7 13. Rhe1 $36 (13. Nf5 Kf8 14. Rhe1 Bd8 15. Qg3 Rg8) {Probably better is:} 13... Kf8 14. Nc6) 13. Rhe1+ Kd8 14. Nc6+ $6 {[%mdl 16384] Again strategical blunder. Much better is: Golod,V: 'Again, a strategical blunder. Much better is:'} (14. Bf5 Be7 15. Be6) (14. Qe2 Kc8 $11 (14... Qc5) 15. Qe8+ Qd8 16. Bxf6 Nxf6 $13 17. Bf5+ $4 Kc7 {Also dubious: Golod,V: 'Also dubious is:'} 18. Qxf7+ {in view of:} Kb6 19. a4) 14... Bxc6 $15 15. dxc6 Nb8 $5 {[%cal Yc6a4] 16...d4} (15... Nc5 16. Bxf6+ $15 gxf6 $143 17. Bc4 Ra7 18. Qd5 {20...ab8(קb2) and 21...d4} {Very weakly:} Ne6 {because of: Golod,V: 'is very weak, because of:'} (18... Qb6 19. Qf5 Be7 {[%csl Ra3,Rc3]} 20. Bd5 a5 21. Qg4 a4 22. Qg7) 19. f5 Ng7 20. Re4 Qb6 21. Bb3 $19 {After:} Rc7 $6 22. Ba4 {[%csl Rb2,Yd2,Re3][%cal Gg4e3,Yd2b2,Yd2e3] black has a strong initiative. Golod,V: 'Black has a strong initiative.'} {Dubious: Golod,V: 'Dubious is:'} Kc8 $2 {because of:} 23. Qd2 a5 24. Qe2 {[%csl Rb6,Rd4]}) 16. Bxf6+ $6 {[%mdl 16384] ×e4;g4} gxf6 $1 {[%csl Re3]} 17. Be4 h5 {With the idea:18...xf2 19.xf2 g4 and 20...d4} 18. Bd5 Ra7 $5 19. Qe4 $140 Bg7 $1 20. Qxb4 a5 {[%csl Rc3,Re3]} 21. Qc4 $2 f5 $17 22. Re3 Na6 $1 {[%csl Rf4]} 23. Bf3 Kc8 {[%csl Rg2]} 24. Rde1 Rd8 25. Qd5 Nc5 26. Qxf5+ Kb8 $19 {[%csl Rg3,Rh7][%cal Yc7f7]} 27. Qd5 (27. Qxh5 d5) 27... Qb6 28. c3 {[%csl Rg7]} Ne6 (28... Na4 $19 29. R1e2 $2) (28... Rc7 $19 {[%csl Rb2,Rg2]} {More stubborn resistance after: Golod,V: 'More stubborn resistance is put up after:'} 29. Bxh5 {It is necessary:} Rxc6 30. Bxf7) 29. g3 h4 30. Kb1 (30. Kc2) 30... hxg3 {[%csl Rg7,Yg8][%cal Yg8g7] The rest it is of no importance. Golod,V: 'The rest is of no importance.'} 31. hxg3 Rc7 32. Kc2 Ka7 33. f5 Ng5 {Whole this game despite the white's mistakes Judit Polgar conducted very strong. Golod,V: 'White's mistakes notwithstanding, Judit Polgar conducted the whole of this game very strongly.'} (33... Nc5 34. Re7 $1) 34. Bg2 {is refuted by:} Rb8 $1 35. b3 Be5 36. Qd2 f6 37. Rd3 Qc5 38. Rd5 Qa3 39. Kb1 Rb6 40. c4 (40. Qe3) 40... Ra6 (40... Rb4 41. Re3 Nf7 {[%csl Rf4]}) (40... Ka6 41. Bf1 Rxb3+ 42. axb3 $19 {and} Qxb3+ 43. Kc1 {[%csl Rd3,Ge3,Rg2]} Bc3 $140) 41. Rb5 (41. Rexe5 $140 dxe5 (41... fxe5 42. Qe3+ Ka8 $19 ({Slightly better is:} 42... Rb6 {Loses right away:} 43. Rb5) {Also win: Golod,V: 'Also winning is:'} 43. Qxg5) 42. Rd7) 41... a4 {[%csl Ra4]} 42. Re3 (42. Rexe5 fxe5 ({Also loses: Golod,V: 'Nother losing move is:'} 42... dxe5 43. Qd8 $1) 43. Qe3+ $1 Ka8 44. Qxg5 {[%csl Rb2,Re2] and mate in 5 moves.}) 42... axb3 $19 {[%csl Rc1,Rd3,Rh7][%cal Ge2e1]} 43. Rexb3 Qa4 44. Qe3+ 0-1

