1. c4 e6 2. g3 d5 3. Bg2 Nf6 (3... dxc4) 4. Nf3 dxc4 5. Qa4+ Nbd7 6. Qxc4 c5 7. Qb3 Rb8 8. d3 Bd6 9. a4 (9. Nc3 a6 10. Ng5 b5 11. O-O Qb6 12. Nce4 Nxe4 13. Nxe4 O-O) 9... b6 10. Na3 a6 11. Nc4 (11. O-O Bb7 $19 12. Nc4 Bc7 13. Bd2 O-O 14. Qc2 (14. Rfc1 Qe7 15. Qa3 (15. Qd1 Rfe8 (15... Rfc8) 16. Qe1 Nd5 17. e4 Nb4 18. Bxb4 cxb4) 15... b5 $11 16. axb5 (16. Ba5 Bxa5 17. Nxa5 Bd5 18. axb5 axb5 19. e4 Ba8 20. Qc3 Rfc8 {½-½ Adams,M-King,D/England/1998/ (27)}) 16... axb5 17. Ne3 Nd5 18. d4 Bd6 19. Qd3 $13 c4 20. Qc2 N7f6 21. Nd1 Rfc8 22. e4 Nb4 23. Bxb4 Bxb4 24. e5 Nd5 25. h4 h6) 14... Qe7 15. e4 (15. b4 cxb4 16. Rab1 $16 Nd5 17. e4 $17 Nc3 18. Bxc3 $11 bxc3 19. Qxc3 Rfc8 $11 20. Rfe1 $5 Ba8 21. Qb3 Nc5 22. Qa3 Qd7 23. Nb2 Bd6 $11 24. Qa2 b5 25. axb5 axb5 26. Rbd1 Na4) 15... Rfc8 (15... h6 16. Rfe1 $19 Rfd8 17. Rab1 $1 b5 18. axb5 axb5 19. Na5 Ba8 20. b4 $15 Bb6 21. h3 Rdc8 22. Qa2 $19 cxb4 23. Bxb4 Qd8 24. Nb3 Qc7 25. Nfd4 $14 Ne5) 16. Qb1 $17 b5 17. axb5 $15 axb5 18. Na5 $1 {xb4} Ba8 19. Re1 Bb6 $15 20. b4 c4 21. d4 c3 $17 22. Bf4 Bxe4 $17 23. Rxe4 $2 c2) 11... Bc7 12. Ng5 (12. Bd2 O-O 13. O-O Bb7 14. Rfc1 Qe7) 12... h6 (12... O-O $19 13. Bd2) 13. Ne4 Nxe4 14. Bxe4 O-O $1 15. O-O Nf6 16. Bg2 {Black's set up on the queenside is not nice, but it certainly slows down white's build up with his pawn majority.} Qd7 $5 (16... Bb7 17. Bxb7 Rxb7 $17 18. Na5 Rb8 (18... Ra7 19. Nc6) 19. Nc6) 17. Rd1 Rd8 (17... Bb7 $3 $16 18. Bxb7 $5 Rxb7) 18. Bd2 Bb7 19. Bxb7 Rxb7 $1 20. Bc3 Nd5 21. Be1 (21. e4 Nxc3 22. bxc3) 21... b5 22. axb5 axb5 23. Nd2 Bb6 24. Ne4 Rc8 (24... Ra7 25. Rxa7 $19 Bxa7 $2 26. Ra1) 25. Qc2 Ra7 $5 {The pawn sacrifice is very profound and depends on the activity of all black pieces.} (25... f5 26. Nc3) 26. Rxa7 Bxa7 $1 (26... Qxa7 27. Nd6) 27. b3 Bb6 28. Rc1 Rc7 29. Qb2 f6 $1 (29... f5) 30. Rc2 f5 31. Nc3 Nb4 (31... Nxc3 32. Bxc3) 32. Rc1 Ra7 33. Bd2 e5 {The result of the whole operation is rather gloomy for white. He can claim only one asset in pawn d5, but black controls the whole board and can roll over his enemy with pawns.} 34. Ra1 Rxa1+ 35. Qxa1 e4 (35... Qc6 $19 36. Nd1 Bc7 37. Bxb4 cxb4 $19 38. Ne3) 36. Qa8+ Kh7 $1 37. Qb8 exd3 (37... Ba7 $19 38. Qxb5) 38. Qxb6 (38. exd3 Nxd3 (38... Qc6) 39. Qxb6 Qd4 $19 40. Be3 $1 (40. Nd1 Qa1 $1) 40... Qxc3 41. Qxb5) 38... dxe2 39. Qxc5 (39. Be1 Qd1 40. Nxd1 exd1=Q) 39... Qxd2 40. Qxf5+ Kh8 41. Nxe2 (41. Qf8+ Kh7 $1 42. Qf5+) 41... Nd3 {The pawn mass e3-f4-g4 is much more dangerous than the lonely hero on d7.} (41... Qxe2 42. Qf8+ Kh7 43. Qxb4) 42. Qf8+ (42. Qf8+ Kh7 43. Qf5+) (42. Qf3 Qd1+ 43. Kg2 Ne1+) 0-1

