3 $14 Be4 $5 23. Rf1 Re6) 20... Qxd5 21. Nf1 Qb5 (21... Re4 22. Nxe3 Qe6 $14 {[%cal Ge2e3,Gc3e2,Ge2f4]} 23. Nf1 Nc4 24. b3 Nd6 25. Ng3) (21... Qe4 22. Qa4 Nc6 $14 {white has got better chanse in Leko,P-Morozevich,A/Frankfurt-West Masters 1999} (22... e2 23. Qxa5) 23. Rxe3 Qxf4 24. Rf3) 22. Nxe3 (22. Qe2 $5 Re4 (22... Nc4 23. b3 Nd6 24. Qxb5 Nxb5 25. Rac1 (25. Rxe3 Rxe3 26. Nxe3 Nxc3) (25. Nxe3 Nxc3 26. Rac1 Nxa2 27. Rxc7 Nb4 $13) 25... e2 26. Ng3 $13 Re3 27. Nxe2 Rae8 28. Kf2) (22... Qxe2 23. Rxe2 Re4 24. Rxe3) 23. Qxb5 $5 {[%csl Ra3,Rb3]} axb5 24. Rxe3 Rxf4 (24... Nb3 25. Rxe4 fxe4 26. Rb1 Rxa2 27. Kf2 $14) 25. Nd2 $13) 22... Re4 (22... Qxb2 23. Nxf5 Rxe1+ (23... Qxc3 24. Rxe8+ Rxe8 25. Rc1 Qb4 26. Qg4 $19) 24. Qxe1) 23. Qd2 (23. Qe2 Qxe2 24. Rxe2 $6 Rae8 25. Rae1 g5) 23... Rae8 24. b3 (24. b4 $19 Nc4 (24... Nc6 25. a4 $19) 25. Nxc4 $1 Qxc4 26. Kf2) 24... b6 25. c4 (25. Nf1 Re2 26. a4) 25... Qd7 26. Nc2 (26. Nd5 Nc6 $1) 26... Nb7 $36 {I don't see where white made mistake,but now her position is pretty bad!} 27. Rxe4 (27. d5 $19 {[%csl Gg4][%cal Gg8g4]}) 27... Rxe4 28. Re1 $6 (28. d5 b5) 28... Nd6 29. Rxe4 (29. d5 b5 30. Rxe4 Nxe4 31. Qd4) (29. Nb4) 29... Nxe4 $1 $17 {[%csl Ra4] The knight on a4 is out of play,while black develops the inititive on the kingside.} 30. Qe3 b5 31. Nb4 a5 32. Nd5 (32. Nd3 bxc4 {[%cal Gg8g3]} 33. Ne5 Qb5 34. Nxc4) 32... b4 33. Kh2 Qd8 34. Qd3 (34. Qd3 $1 $19 {After this simple and very strong move at the sme time white is helpless.} Qd6 35. g3 g6 36. Kg2 Kf7 37. Kf3 c6 38. Ne3 $1) 0-1

