1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 e6 3. e4 c5 4. e5 Ng8 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. d4 cxd4 7. Nxd4 Nxe5 8. Ndb5 a6 9. Nd6+ {Rare, double-edged move. Usual continuation is something like} Bxd6 10. Qxd6 f6 {deserves attention} (10... Nc6 $8) (10... Ng6 11. Be3 Qe7 (11... Nf6 12. O-O-O Qe7 13. Qc7 (13. Bc5 Qxd6 14. Bxd6 b5 15. cxb5 axb5 16. Nxb5) (13. Qb6) 13... d5 14. Qxe7+ Nxe7 15. Bc5 dxc4 16. Bxc4 b5 17. Bb3 Bb7) (11... N8e7 12. Bd3 Nc6 (12... Nh4 13. Bb6 Nhf5 14. Ne4) (12... O-O 13. Bb6 Qe8 14. O-O f5 15. Rfe1 e5 16. Nd5 (16. c5 Rf6 17. Bc4+ Kh8 18. Qd2 e4 19. Bc7) 16... Nxd5 17. cxd5 Rf6 18. Qc7 d6 19. g3 Qf8) 13. O-O-O Qe7 14. Ne4 O-O 15. Qg3 (15. Qxe7 Ngxe7 16. Nd6 b5 17. c5 f5 18. Rhe1 (18. Bc2) 18... Rb8 19. Be2) 15... d5 (15... f5 16. Bc5 Qd8 17. Nc3) 16. Bc5 Qh4 (16... Qd8 17. Nc3 Nge7 18. Rhe1 Re8 19. Be4 Qa5 20. Bxe7 Nxe7 21. cxd5) 17. Ng5 (17. Qxh4 Nxh4 18. Ng5 h6 19. Bh7+) 17... Re8 18. Qxh4 Nxh4 19. Bxh7+) 12. Qb6 (12. Ne4 Nf6 (12... f5 13. Qxe7+ N8xe7 14. Nd6+ Kf8) 13. Qxe7+ Nxe7 14. Nd6+ Kf8 15. c5 Ne8 16. Nc4 Nd5 17. Bd4) 12... Qd8 (12... d6 13. Ne4 Qd7 14. Nxd6+ Kf8 15. Bc5 N8e7 16. O-O-O f6 17. Ne4 Qc6 $132 {½-½ Velimirovic,D-Drasko,M/YUG t-ch 1996 (71) just one thing is interesting for me: did Judit know about this game?} {White could play also} 18. Qxc6) (12... f5 13. O-O-O Kf7 14. Qa5 {1-0 Ginzburg,M-Robledo,N/Buenos Aires FMDA tt 1992 (24) with big complications, but Judit never worried too much about pawns.} (14. c5 Nf6 15. h4 Ne5 16. Be2 Nc6 17. Rd6) 14... d6 15. Nb5 axb5 {for example} 16. Qxa8 Nf6 17. Qa3 (17. cxb5 f4 18. Bb6 e5 19. Bc4+ d5 20. Bxd5+ Nxd5 21. Rxd5 {0-1 Bragin,A-Rychagov,A/RUS t-ch Orel 1997 (24)}) 17... Rd8 18. Bb6 Rd7 19. cxb5) (12... Nf6 13. Bc5 (13. c5) 13... Qd8 14. Qd6 (14. Qxd8+ Kxd8 15. O-O-O d5 16. cxd5) 14... Qa5 (14... Nh4 15. Bd3 Nxg2+ 16. Kf1 Nh4 17. Rd1) 15. O-O-O b6 16. Bxb6 Qe5 17. Qxe5 Nxe5 18. Bd4 Ng6 19. Bxf6 gxf6 20. Ne4 Ke7 21. Nd6) 13. Qb4 (13. O-O-O) (13. Na4) 13... N8e7 14. Bd3 $1 $132 (14. Ne4 Nf5 15. Bb6 $1 Qh4 16. c5 $18 d5 17. cxd6 Ne5 18. g3 Qh6 19. f4 $5 Nd7 20. Bg2 $1 O-O 21. Rc1 $18) ({Velimirovic played} 14. Bb6 Nc6 15. Qc5 Qf6 16. Rd1) 14... O-O 15. Rd1 $16 Ne5 16. Be2 {[%csl Rf6,Rg7,Rg8]} N5c6 17. Qb3 $1 Nf5 18. Bb6 Qf6) 11. Be3 Nf7 (11... Qe7 12. Qb6 Nc6 13. O-O-O (13. Ne4 $13 {everithing is more complicated in the case of} d5 14. Bc5 $1) 13... Qb4 14. Qc7 (14. Qxb4 Nxb4 15. Bc5 Nc6 16. Ne4) 14... Qa5 (14... Nge7 15. Ne4 $143 $2 d5 16. a3 Qb3 17. Nd6+ Kf8 18. Bd3) 15. Bb6 $18) 12. Qb4 {[%cal Gg2g4,Rg1g7,Rd2h6][%mdl 512]} Ne7 13. Bb6 (13. O-O-O {with unclearconsequences.} Nc6 14. Qb3 $19 (14. Qa3 d6 {White has dangerous attack after} 15. Nb5 $6) {It,s funny what white will do after} 14... Qe7 $1 15. g3 Qb4 (15... b5) 16. Qxb4 Nxb4 17. a3 Nc6 18. Bb6 O-O $40 (18... d6 19. f4 Ke7 20. Bg2) 19. c5 f5 20. f4) (13. Rd1 $1) 13... Nc6 14. Qc5 Qe7 15. Qe3 d6 $1 {[%csl Gb3][%cal Ga5b3]} (15... Nd6 16. Bd3 $18 Ne5 17. b3 Nxd3+ 18. Qxd3 Nf5 19. O-O $1 $18 O-O $142 20. Rfe1) 16. O-O-O (16. Be2 O-O 17. O-O f5 18. f4 Bd7 19. Rad1) 16... O-O 17. Be2 f5 {Judit sucrificed ( lost?) two pawns and only her chance for survival is just to give checkmate to oppenent. With real astonishment I found, that this crazy position came to life not in the first time , ant instead of Polgars,} 18. f4 {[%mdl 128]} Bd7 19. Rhe1 Rac8 20. Bf3 {[%cal Rf3g5]} Rfe8 21. Kb1 Qf8 {Black organized tough defence, but Judit found way to increase preasure on the black king} 22. g3 $1 {[%cal Gc2g2]} Ncd8 $6 {Knight moves too far.} 23. b3 Bc6 24. Bh5 e5 $2 {Decisive mistake, it was obligatory to sucrifice exchange} 25. Nd5 $1 $18 Ne6 26. Bxf7+ Qxf7 27. fxe5 dxe5 (27... Nf8) 28. Qxe5 f4 29. gxf4 Nxf4 30. Qxf4 Bxd5 31. Rxe8+ Rxe8 32. Qxf7+ Bxf7 33. Rd7 Bg6+ 34. Kc1 Be4 35. Bd4 $18 g5 36. Rg7+ Kf8 37. Rxg5 $18 Kf7 38. Rg7+ Ke6 39. Kd2 Re7 40. Rg5 Kd7 41. Kc3 Bb1 42. a4 Rf7 $1 43. Kb2 Bg6 44. a5 $8 Rf5 45. Rxf5 Bxf5 1-0

