1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 O-O 8. Bd3 f5 9. Qh3 (9. exf6 Rxf6 10. Bg5 Rf7 11. Qh5 g6 12. Qd1 Qa5 13. Bd2 Nbc6 14. Nf3 c4 15. Be2 Nf5) 9... Qa5 10. Bd2 Nbc6 (10... Qa4 11. dxc5 Nd7 12. Nf3 Nxc5 13. O-O b6 14. Be3 Ng6 15. Rfd1 Ne4 16. Bd4 Ba6 17. Nd2 Rac8 18. Bxe4 dxe4 19. Qe3 Ne7) 11. Nf3 Qa4 12. Rg1 (12. Kd1 Bd7 13. g4 cxd4 14. Rg1) 12... c4 13. Be2 Qxc2 $6 {Spassy tries something new. The standard approach is to strengthen e5 by f8. Perhaps he wanted to surprise his theoretically well prepared opponent.} 14. Rc1 Qb2 15. g4 Na5 {A good post for the  - if it is allowed to stay.} 16. Bd1 $1 Nb3 17. Rc2 Qxa3 18. Bh6 (18. Ng5 h6 19. Nf3 Nxd2 20. Kxd2 fxg4 21. Rxg4 Nf5 22. Nh4 Bd7 23. Nxf5 exf5 24. Rg1 Kh7 25. Qg2 Qe7 26. Qxd5 b5) 18... Ng6 (18... Na1 $16 19. Rd2 $2 (19. gxf5 Nxc2+ 20. Bxc2 Qxc3+ 21. Kd1 Nxf5 22. Bxf5 Rxf5 23. Rxg7+ Kf8 24. Rxh7+ Ke8 25. Be3) 19... Qxc3 20. Bxg7 Kxg7 21. gxf5+ Kh8 (21... Ng6) 22. Qh6 Rf7 23. Ng5) (18... f4 19. Ng5 Rf7 (19... gxh6 20. Qxh6 Rf7 21. Qh5 (21. Nxf7 Kxf7 22. Qxh7+ Ke8 23. g5 Na1) 21... Ng6 22. Nxf7) (19... Nxd4 20. Bxg7 Nxc2+ 21. Kd2) 20. Qh5 (20. Nxf7 Nxd4 21. Rd2 Nb3) 20... Ng6 (20... g6 21. Qh4) 21. Nxf7 Na1 (21... Kxf7 22. Bxf4) 22. Rd2 Kxf7 23. Bxf4 Kg8) 19. gxf5 Rxf5 (19... exf5 20. Rxg6 hxg6 21. Bf4 $40 Na1 22. Rc1 (22. Ng5 Nxc2+ $40 23. Bxc2 Re8 24. Qh7+ Kf8 25. Qh8+ Ke7 $18 26. Qxg7+ Kd8) 22... Kf7 23. Qh7) 20. Be3 Bd7 21. Ng5 {[%mdl 128] The attack begins. Quite logical given the weaknesses surrounding the black .} Nf8 22. f4 Na1 (22... Qa1) 23. Rcg2 Qxc3+ 24. Kf2 g6 (24... Rxg5 25. Rxg5 (25. fxg5 $18 Nc2) 25... g6) 25. Nxh7 $5 {Clearing the way for the attackers and very much in the style of Judit Polgar. But the alternative looks quite good too.} Rxf4+ (25... Nxh7 26. Rxg6+ Kh8 27. Qh6 Rf7 (27... Rxf4+ 28. Bxf4 $18 Qxd4+ 29. Be3 $1 $132 Qxe5 30. Qxh7+) 28. Rg7 Rxf4+ 29. Qxf4) 26. Bf3 Qc2+ (26... Nxh7 27. Rxg6+ Kh8 28. Bxf4 Qxd4+ $1 {A nice touch to finish the game.} 29. Be3 Qb2+ 30. Be2 Rf8+ 31. Kg2 Qxe2+ 32. Kh1 Qxe3 33. Qxe3 d4 34. Qxd4 Bc6+ 35. R6g2) 27. Kg3 Rxf3+ (27... Rf5 28. Rxc2 (28. Nf6+) 28... Nxc2 29. Qh6) 28. Kxf3 Qe4+ 29. Kf2 (29. Kf2 Qc2+ (29... Qf5+ 30. Qxf5 exf5 31. Nxf8 Kxf8 32. Rxg6) 30. Kg3 Nxh7 31. Rxc2 Nxc2) 1-0

