1. c4 {Schussler} g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. e4 e5 5. dxe5 dxe5 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 7. f4 Nd7 8. Nf3 c6 9. Be2 (9. fxe5 Nxe5 10. Bf4 Nxf3+ (10... f6 11. O-O-O+ (11. Be2 Nh6 12. Rd1+ Ke8 13. O-O Nhf7 14. Na4 {And Black was ok in Nunn-Karpov, Rotterdam 1989.} Ke7 15. Bg3 (15. Nc5 b6 $14 {Anand,V-Speelman,J/Thessaloniki ol/1988/ -> TD 1988/6} 16. Nd3) 15... b6 16. c5 b5 17. Nc3 Be6 18. Nd4) 11... Ke8 12. Be2 $14 (12. Kb1) 12... Bh6 13. Bxh6 Nxh6 {15...b4!?} 14. Nxe5 fxe5 15. b4 Ke7 16. c5 $14 Be6 $5 17. a3 {Schussler} Rad8) 11. gxf3 Be6 (11... Ke7 12. c5 $1 Be6 13. Bd6+ Ke8 14. O-O-O $14 Nf6 15. Kc2 $14 Nd7 16. f4 f5 {15...c5? 16.d5!} 17. Bd3) 12. O-O-O+ Ke8 13. Kc2 $14 Nf6 $2 14. b3) (9. Be3 exf4 10. Bxf4 Nh6 11. h3 f6 12. O-O-O Nf7 13. h4 Bh6 14. Bxh6 Nxh6 15. e5 fxe5 16. h5 Nf7 17. hxg6 hxg6 18. Rxh8+ Nxh8 19. Nxe5) (9. g3 Ngf6 10. Bh3 Re8 11. O-O h6 12. fxe5 Nxe5 13. Bxc8 Rxc8 14. Nxe5 Rxe5 15. Be3 Re6 16. Rf3 Ke8 17. Raf1 Rc7 18. Bd4) 9... f6 (9... Ke8 $18 10. O-O Ne7 {Black has difficulties finding a move} 11. Bd2 exf4 12. Bxf4 Nc5 13. Rac1 (13. Be3 $2 Ne6 14. Rad1) 13... Bg4 $10 14. b4 $2 Bxf3 15. gxf3 $2 Ne6 $1 { 25.eb1} 16. Be3 g5 $6 17. Rfd1 { 24...b7} Ng6 $1 18. Na4 b6 $1) 10. O-O (10. fxe5 Nxe5 11. Nxe5 fxe5 $2 12. Bg5+ $18 Ke8 $2 13. O-O-O Bf6 14. h4 Be7 15. Rd2 { 26.xc8} Be6 16. Rhd1 Nf6 17. c5 Rf8) 10... Nh6 {10...b6} (10... Ke8 11. Rb1 Nh6 12. fxe5 Nxe5 13. Nxe5 fxe5 14. b4 Rf8 {with the black pawn at the second rank the win is much more difficult for white than in the game, if it is possible at all.} 15. Rd1 Nf7 16. b5 {not better} Nd8 17. bxc6 bxc6 18. Be3) 11. fxe5 Nxe5 12. Nxe5 fxe5 13. Be3 (13. Bg5+ Ke8 14. Rad1 Nf7 15. Be3 Bf8 $2 {looses immediatly, but the black position is lost anyway.} 16. c5 Be7 (16... Bh6) 17. Nb5 {Black is in total Zugzwang} cxb5 18. Bxb5+ Kf8 19. Bh6+) (13. b4 Be6 $18 14. b5 Nf7 15. Bg4 Bxg4 16. Rxf7 Bf8 17. Bg5+ Kc8 $18 18. Be7 Bh6 { a2-a7, f2-f4} 19. Bd6 Be3+ 20. Kh1 Bb6 $1 $18 21. c5 Ba5 $1 $18 22. Bxe5 $2) 13... Ke8 14. Rad1 {N; the theory recommends 14.a3} (14. h3 Nf7 15. b4 {to stop 35...d3} Nd8 {If black would take a passive set-up with g7,f8,h6, than I put both my rooks on the 7th rank ( b7,d7 ), push my pawns g4,f4, put my king on g3 - than h4,g5 is the winning plan.} 16. b5 Ne6 17. bxc6 bxc6 18. Rab1 Rf8 19. Rfc1 Nd4) 14... Rf8 15. Rfe1 Nf7 {15...f4 is interesting} 16. b4 Bh6 17. Bf2 Bg5 18. b5 Be7 $6 19. c5 Ng5 20. Be3 Ne6 21. bxc6 $1 bxc6 22. Nd5 cxd5 23. exd5 $1 Bxc5 $8 24. Bb5+ $1 Ke7 25. dxe6 Bxe3+ 26. Rxe3 Bxe6 27. Rxe5 Kf6 28. Re2 Rab8 29. a4 Rb6 30. h3 h5 31. Bd7 $1 Rd8 32. a5 Ra6 33. Rf1+ Bf5 1-0

