1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Nf3 e6 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bh4 dxc4 7. e4 g5 8. Bg3 b5 9. Be2 Bb7 10. O-O Nbd7 11. Ne5 Bg7 12. Nxd7 Nxd7 {Provoking a concession.} 13. Bd6 {White does not have a better option.} a6 14. Bh5 {From now on, and until the end of game the play is quite forced!} (14. Re1) 14... Bf8 $1 {This is tactically justified. Radjabov exploits the weakness of the diagonal a7-g1.} 15. Bxf8 Rxf8 16. d5 (16. e5 Qb6 17. b3 (17. Ne4 O-O-O 18. Nd6+ Kb8 19. Nxf7 Rxf7 20. Bxf7 Nxe5 21. Qh5 Rxd4 22. Bxe6 c5) 17... O-O-O 18. bxc4 Nxe5 19. c5 Qa5 20. Ne4 Qb4 (20... Nc4 21. Be2 f5 22. Bxc4 fxe4 23. Bxe6+ Kb8 24. Re1 Qc3 25. Rxe4 Qb2 26. f3 Rf4 27. Qc1 Qxc1+ 28. Rxc1 Rxd4 29. Rxf4 gxf4 30. g4 fxg3) 21. Nd6+ Rxd6 22. cxd6 Nd7 23. a4 Qxd6) 16... cxd5 (16... Qe7 17. b3 cxb3 18. Qxb3 Ne5 19. Rac1 c5 20. dxe6 O-O-O 21. exf7 Rd3 (21... Nd3) 22. Be2 Qxf7 23. Bxd3 Nxd3) 17. exd5 Nf6 18. dxe6 $1 (18. Re1 Ke7 (18... Bxd5 19. Nxd5 Qxd5 20. Qxd5 Nxd5 21. Rxe6+ Kd7 22. Rxh6 Rh8 23. Rxh8 Rxh8 24. Bxf7 Nf4 25. g3 Nh3+ 26. Kg2 Nxf2) 19. Bf3 b4 20. Ne2 (20. d6+ Qxd6 21. Qxd6+ Kxd6 22. Bxb7 bxc3 23. Bxa8 cxb2 24. Rad1+ Nd5) 20... Bxd5 21. Nd4 Rg8) 18... Qxd1 19. Bxf7+ Ke7 20. Raxd1 Rfd8 21. Ne2 Be4 22. f4 b4 23. fxg5 (23. Ng3 Bd3 (23... Bh7 24. f5) (23... Bc2 24. Rc1) 24. fxg5 hxg5 25. Rf5) 23... hxg5 {This game is short but rich in content and important for theory.} 24. Ng3 $2 Rxd1 $1 25. Rxd1 Bh7 26. Nh5 (26. Ne2) 26... c3 27. Nxf6 Kxf6 28. bxc3 bxc3 {[%cal Gf1f7]} 29. Rc1 $8 c2 30. Kf2 Rd8 $18 31. Ke2 Rd4 32. h3 Be4 33. Bh5 Kxe6 {Black is slightly better thanks to pair of strong bishops.} 34. g3 $4 Ke5 35. h4 gxh4 $18 {The point is that White can't take on c6 in view of} 36. gxh4 $2 Rd5 (36... Rd6 37. Ke3 (37. Bf3 Bh7) 37... Rd3+ 38. Ke2 Kd4) 37. Bf3 $2 Rd1 $19 38. Bxe4 Rxc1 39. Kd2 Rg1 (39... Ra1 40. Bxc2 Rxa2 $16 41. h5 $1 Ra3 42. h6 Rh3 43. h7 Kd4 44. Bf5 Rh2+ 45. Kc1 Kc3 46. Kb1 $18 Kb4 $2 (46... Kb3 47. Be6+ Ka3 48. Bg8) 47. Bg6 {loses an exchange.} Ka3 48. Bf5 (48. Be4) 48... Rh1+ 49. Kc2 Ka2 50. Be4 Rh2+ 51. Kc1 a5 52. Bf5 a4 53. Be4 $132 {0-1 Popovic,P (2540)-Kurajica,B (2535)/Sarajevo 1985/MCD (37)} a3 $2 {is bad in view of} 54. Bf5 Ka1 55. Be4 a2 56. Bf5 Rh4 57. Be4) 40. Bxc2 Kd4 {and Black is at least not worse.} 41. Bd3 a5 (41... Ra1 42. h5) 42. a4 Rh1 43. Bb5 Rh2+ 44. Kd1 Ke3 45. Kc1 Rxh4 46. Kc2 Rh7 47. Ba6 $11 {1-0 Govedarica,R (2395)-Grujic,Z (2275)/Vrbas 1994/EXT 2002 (34)} Rc7+ 48. Kd1 Rc6 49. Bb5 Rc3 50. Ba6 Ra3 51. Bb5 Ra2 52. Kc1 Kd4 53. Kd1 Kc3 54. Ke1 Rd2 55. Ba6 Rd4 56. Bb5 Kc2 57. Ke2 Re4+ 58. Kf3 $14 {0-1 Peters,J (2454)-Khachiyan,M (2473)/Costa Mesa 2003/CBM 095 ext (49)} Re7 59. Kf2 Kc3 60. Kf3 $17 {½-½ Kveinys,A (2545)-Binham,T (2330)/Kuopio 1992/EXT 2000 (41)} Kd4 61. Ba6 Re3+ 62. Kf2 Ke4 63. Bb5 Kf4 64. Ba6 Re4 65. Bb5 Re6 $11 {1-0 Rytshagov,M (2495)-Boey,J (2285)/Antwerp 1996/EXT 1999 (31)} 66. Bc4 Re4 67. Bb5 Rd4 68. Ke2 Rd6 69. Bd3 Rh6 70. Bb5 Ke4 71. Bd3+ $15 {1-0 Becerra Rivero,J (2445)-Alonso Garcia,R (2380)/Cuba 1993/CBM 035 ext (53)} Kd4 72. Bb5 Rh2+ 73. Kf3 Ra2 74. Bd7 Ra3+ 75. Kf2 $15 {0-1 Renet,O (2515)-Tseitlin,M (2445)/Palma de Mallorca 1989/TD (29)} Kd3 76. Kf3 Kd2+ 77. Kf4 $2 Re3 $132 {½-½ Mantovani,R (2370)-Godena,M (2425)/Chianciano 1989/EXT 2000 (18)} 78. Bb5 Re7 79. Kf3 $14 Kc3 $2 80. Ba6 Kd4 81. Bb5 Re6 82. Kf2 Re5 83. Kf3 Kc5 84. Kf2 Kb6 85. Bd3 Kc5 86. Bb5 Kb4 $2 87. Kf3 Kb3 88. Kf4 Re1 89. Kf3 Ra1 90. Ke2 $18 {1-0 Speckner,R (2290)-Bredl,H (2275)/Bayern 1995/EXT 1999 (34)} Rxa4 91. Bxa4+ Kxa4 92. Kd2 Kb3 93. Kc1 1/2-1/2

