1. d4 {Petrov,Marian} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. e3 Bb7 5. Bd3 d5 6. O-O Nbd7 7. b3 Bd6 8. Bb2 O-O 9. Nc3 a6 10. Rc1 {Petrov,Marian: 'This looks a bit slow, but at least it is protecting the position of the knight.'} Qe7 11. Na4 dxc4 {Petrov,Marian: '?!'} 12. bxc4 Ba3 13. Bxa3 Qxa3 14. Nc3 {Petrov,Marian: '?'} Qd6 {Petrov,Marian: '?'} (14... Rfe8 15. e4 e5 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. dxe5 Rxe5 18. f4 Ree8 19. e5 $10 {Beshukov,S-Ruban,V Sochi 1990 0-1 40} Nd7 $5 20. Nd5 (20. Bxh7+ Kxh7 21. Qxd7 Qc5+)) 15. e4 ({A more precise way is} 15. Ng5 {Petrov,Marian} c5 16. Nge4 Bxe4 $5 17. Bxe4 $140 {Petrov,Marian} Rad8 $1 18. Bf3 cxd4 $17 19. exd4 e5) 15... e5 16. Nd5 $1 (16. d5 Nc5 17. Re1 $11) 16... exd4 17. Nxd4 {Petrov,Marian: 'Now the black monarch is in big trouble.'} Nc5 (17... g6 18. Nb3) 18. Re1 {Petrov,Marian: '+-'} Rfe8 19. Nf5 $1 {x a7} Qd8 20. Qf3 c6 (20... Nxd3 21. Qxd3 c6 22. Nxf6+ Qxf6 23. Nd6 $40 Re7 24. e5) 21. Nxf6+ $1 $16 Qxf6 22. Bc2 Qe5 (22... Re5 23. Qg3 Bc8 24. f4 Rxf5 $18 (24... Re8 25. e5) 25. exf5 Bxf5 $18 26. Qe3) (22... Bc8 23. e5 Rxe5 $40 {Black has achieved a nice position but his good opening plan must be finished with} 24. Rxe5 {Petrov,Marian} Qxe5 25. Qxc6 {which actually is the point of this setup} Bb7 26. Qxb6 Be4 27. Bxe4 Nxe4 $11 28. Rd1 {Petrov,Marian}) (22... Rad8 23. Qg3 $16 Ne6 {Petrov,Marian looks risky but is maybe the best move} (23... h6 {Black is winning.} 24. h4 Qg6 25. Qc7 $13) 24. c5 bxc5 25. e5 Qg5 26. Qxg5 Nxg5 {surely a human can not spot this line, but after} 27. Nd6 $2 Re7 28. Rb1) 23. Rcd1 (23. Qe3 Bc8 (23... Rad8 24. Rb1 Qc7 (24... b5 25. f4) 25. e5 f6 26. f4 fxe5 27. fxe5 Bc8 28. Nd6) 24. Nd4 Qc7 25. Nb3 Nxb3 26. axb3) 23... Rad8 24. Rxd8 Rxd8 25. Rd1 Rxd1+ 26. Qxd1 Qc7 (26... h6 27. Qd8+ Kh7 28. Ne7) 27. e5 $1 $18 1-0

