{Moskalenko,Viktor: 'A wonderful game which shows how Black can blow his opponent away in a seemingly solid position. '} 1. d4 {Moskalenko,Viktor} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. g3 O-O 5. Bg2 d6 6. O-O Nc6 7. Nc3 a6 8. Bf4 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'This pseudo-active bishop placement is quite wrong in many sub-Winawer lines.'} h6 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '!' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'Once again using Black's most important motif in the Winawer system.'} (8... Bf5 9. Qd2 (9. d5 Na5 10. Nd2 (10. b3 c5 11. Rc1 b5) 10... c5 11. e4 Bd7 12. Re1 Ng4 13. Qc2 b5 14. cxb5 axb5 15. Ne2 b4 16. Nf3 Bb5) 9... Ne4 10. Nxe4 Bxe4 11. d5 e5 12. dxe6 fxe6 13. Qe3 Bf5 14. Nh4) (8... Nd7 9. Qd2 e5 10. dxe5 dxe5 11. Bh6 Nb6 12. Bxg7 Kxg7 13. b3 Qxd2 (13... f5 14. Qb2 Be6 15. Nd5 Nd7 16. Rfd1) 14. Nxd2) (8... Bg4) (8... Bd7) (8... Rb8) 9. e4 (9. Qd2 g5 10. Be3 Ng4) (9. Qc1 Kh7 10. d5 Na5 11. Nd2 c5) (9. d5 Na5 10. Qd3 c5 (10... e5 11. Bd2 c5 (11... b5 12. cxb5 axb5 13. Qxb5) 12. e4) 11. dxc6 Nxc6 (11... bxc6 12. Rfd1 (12. b4 e5 13. Bxe5 dxe5 14. Qxd8 Rxd8 15. bxa5 e4 16. Ne5 Re8 17. Nxc6 Bd7) 12... c5) 12. Rad1 Qa5 13. h3 Bd7) (9. h3 g5 (9... e6 10. Qd2 (10. Rc1 Nh5 11. Be3 Ne7 12. g4 Nf6 13. Qd2 Kh7 14. Bf4 Nd7 15. e4 Nc6 16. Be3 e5 17. dxe5 Ncxe5) 10... Kh7 11. Rfd1) (9... Bd7) 10. Bd2 (10. Be3 g4 11. hxg4 Nxg4 12. Bc1 (12. Qd2 Nxe3 13. Qxe3 e5) 12... e5 13. d5 Ne7) 10... g4 11. hxg4 Nxg4 12. d5 Nce5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. b3 c5 15. dxc6 bxc6 16. Qc1 Kh7 17. Qc2+ f5 18. Rad1 Qe8) 9... Bg4 10. d5 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'Trying to open up the game.'} (10. h3 Bxf3 11. Bxf3 e5 $5 12. dxe5 dxe5 13. Be3 Nd4) (10. Qd2 Nd7 11. d5 (11. Bxh6 Bxh6 12. Qxh6 Bxf3 13. Bxf3 Nxd4) 11... Bxf3 12. Bxf3 (12. dxc6 Bxg2 13. Kxg2 bxc6 14. Bxh6 Qb8 15. b3 Qb4) 12... Nde5 13. Be2 Nd4 14. Kg2 Nxe2 15. Qxe2 Qd7) 10... Na5 (10... Ne5 $5 {Moskalenko,Viktor} {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'It was the same story with'} 11. Bxe5 dxe5 12. c5 $5 {Moskalenko,Viktor}) 11. b3 b5 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '!?'} ({Moskalenko,Viktor: 'After'} 11... c5 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '?!' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'White lost almost all the games.'}) 12. cxb5 $6 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'White does not worry too much about the pawns.'} axb5 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '!' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'And Black won in 31 moves.'} 13. Nxb5 Nxe4 $1 14. Rc1 g5 (14... Qd7 $15 15. Qe2 (15. Nxc7 Ra7 $11 {Corrales Jimenez,F (2599)-Barria Zuniga,D (2419) Parla 2010})) 15. Be3 Qd7 16. Nbd4 (16. Nxc7 Rac8 {Moskalenko,Viktor: '' Moskalenko,Viktor: 'and ...d7'} 17. Bb6 Nc3 18. Qe1 Bxf3 (18... Nxb3 19. Rxc3) 19. Bxf3 Nxb3 20. axb3 $13 Rxc7 $5 {Moskalenko,Viktor} 21. Bxc7 Qxc7 $1 22. Be2) 16... Nf6 17. b4 Nxd5 18. bxa5 Rxa5 (18... Nxe3 $19 19. fxe3 {Moskalenko,Viktor: ''} Rxa5) 19. Qd2 Ra6 20. Nc2 Nxe3 (20... c6) 21. Nxe3 $6 Be6 22. Nd4 Rxa2 23. Qd3 Bxd4 24. Qxd4 c5 25. Qd3 Ra4 26. Bd5 Rd4 27. Bxe6 Qxe6 28. Qc2 f5 29. Rfe1 Re4 30. Ng2 Ra8 31. Rxe4 Qxe4 {Moskalenko,Viktor: 'Later, in 1997 in a game between the same players, White opted for 8.d2!? - see line in Game2.'} (31... fxe4 $17) 32. Qb3+ e6 33. Re1 $19 Qd5 34. Qxd5 (34. Qb5) 34... exd5 35. Ne3 Re8 $17 36. Rd1 d4 37. Nxf5 Re6 $1 38. g4 Kf7 39. Kg2 Kg6 40. Kf3 h5 $17 41. h3 Kf6 $1 42. Rc1 hxg4+ 43. hxg4 Ke5 $19 44. Re1+ (44. Rh1 Kd5 $17 45. Rh5 $2 Kc4 $1 46. Rxg5 d5) 44... Kf6 45. Rd1 Ke5 { f6} 46. Re1+ Kf6 0-1

