1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 {Judith Polgar avoids the Petroff Defence as she needed to win this game to level the score.} e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 {This move is directed to prevent the advance d7-d5.} Be7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. O-O Nbd7 7. Nc3 (7. Qc2) 7... dxc4 8. e4 c5 9. Qe2 (9. d5 exd5 $19 10. e5 Ng4 11. Qxd5 Nb6 12. Qe4 Qd3 13. h3 Qxe4 14. Nxe4) (9. Bf4 $1 cxd4 10. Qxd4 Nc5 11. Qxc4 {with fine compensation for an exchange.} Qd3) 9... a6 {Boris is going for an immediate queenside expansion.} 10. Be3 (10. d5 $1 exd5 $1 11. exd5 $11 {Another spectacular line by an engine!} b5 $2 12. Nh4) 10... Ng4 11. Qxc4 (11. a4 Nxe3 12. fxe3 cxd4 13. exd4 Qc7 $40 {[%csl Rf6][%cal Ga1f1]} 14. e5 {would allow Black to sacrifice an exchange:} Rb8 15. Ne4 b5 16. axb5 axb5 17. Nfg5 Qb6 $13 18. Qh5 Qxd4+ 19. Kh1 Bxg5 20. Nxg5 h6 21. Nxf7 Qd3 22. Rad1 Qc2 23. Qg4 $1 Rxf7 24. Qxe6 Nxe5 25. Qxe5 Bb7 26. Qxb8+ Kh7 27. Bxb7 Qe2 28. Bg2) 11... Nxe3 12. fxe3 b5 13. Qd3 b4 14. Ne2 a5 15. b3 Ba6 16. Qd2 {The situation in the match urges Judith to play aggressively without really concerning about the risk.} Rc8 17. Rac1 c4 18. bxc4 Bxc4 19. d5 $1 {The only way to continue the initiative.} Bf6 20. Rf2 e5 $2 {Boris Gelfand played superbly in Khanty-Mansiysk, but in the current game he lost control over the position.} 21. Bh3 $2 {This is tempting, but the simple 21.xf7 could yield White already a crushing attack.} Bb5 22. Rxc8 Qxc8 23. g4 h6 24. Ng3 Qc5 25. Nf5 Rc8 26. Kg2 Kh7 $2 {Too greedy. Boris had to bring his queenside pieces into action as soon as possible.} 27. d6 $1 g6 28. g5 hxg5 29. Ne7 {Most of black's pieces got stuck on the queenside and can't help his king.} Rd8 30. Nxg5+ Bxg5 31. Rxf7+ Kh6 32. Qd1 $1 {[%csl Rf6] There is no defense against 33.f6+ or 33.f6.} Nf6 33. d7 Qc4 34. Ng8+ Nxg8 35. Rf3 Nf6 36. Qd6 Qe2+ 37. Rf2 Qxf2+ 38. Kxf2 Nxe4+ 39. Kg2 $18 Nxd6 40. Be6 $40 {[%cal Gf1g1]} 1-0

[Event "FIDE World Cup"]
[Site "Khanty Mansiysk"]
[Date "2011.09.07"]
[Round "4.2"]
[White "Dominguez Perez, Leinier"]
[Black "Polgar, Judit"]
[Result "0-1"]
[ECO "B08"]
[WhiteElo "2719"]
[BlackElo "2699"]
[Annotator "Polgar,Judit"]
[PlyCount "84"]
[EventDate "2011.08.28"]
[EventType "k.o."]
[EventRounds "7"]
[EventCountry "RUS"]
[SourceTitle "CBM 145"]
