1. d4 g6 (1... d6 2. Nf3 Bg4) 2. c4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 e5 (4... Nf6 5. e4 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. d5 a5 (7... Na6 8. Nd2) (7... Nh5 8. g3) 8. Bg5 h6 9. Bh4 Na6) 5. e4 Nd7 6. Be2 Ngf6 7. d5 (7. O-O) 7... O-O 8. Bg5 (8. O-O) (8. h3 $6 Nc5 $36 {0-1 Rogic,D (2581)-Brkic,A (2588)/Stari Mikanovci CRO 2011/The Week in Chess 862 (35)} 9. Qc2 $11 {After the queen exchange} a5 10. g4) (8. Be3 Ng4 {White has no more reasons to hope to get an advantage.} (8... Nc5 9. Nd2 a5 10. a3 Ne8 11. O-O f5 12. f3 f4 $11 {Smeets,J-Aronian,L/Nice 2010. The powerful position in the centre compensates for the weakness of the black squares.} 13. Bf2 h5 14. b4 $13 axb4 15. axb4 Rxa1 16. Qxa1 Na6 17. Rb1 $13 {Smeets,J-Karjakin,S/Nice 2010} g5 18. c5) 9. Bg5 f6 10. Bh4 h5 11. Nd2) 8... h6 9. Bh4 Qe8 (9... g5 $13 10. Bg3 $6 {is doubtful} Nh5 $15 11. h4 (11. Nd2 Nf4) 11... g4 (11... Nxg3 12. fxg3 g4 13. Nh2 $13 {1/2 Vedmediuc,S (2465)-Brkic,A (2605)/Porto Carras GRE 2011/[Microsoft] (38)} {Or} h5 14. O-O) 12. Nh2 (12. Nd2 f5) 12... Nxg3 13. fxg3 h5 {The bishop development on f4 doesn't make problems for Black.} 14. O-O f5 15. exf5 (15. Rxf5)) 10. Nd2 c5 (10... a6) 11. g4 a6 12. Bg3 Nh7 13. Qc2 {The most ambitious move.} (13. h4 f5 14. gxf5 $17 {Wieczorek,O-Banusz,T/Krakow POL 2011} {Perhaps it's more secure to play without the kingside being weakened by the move g6-g5.} gxf5 $5 15. Rg1 Ndf6 (15... f4 16. Bh2)) 13... Ndf6 14. h3 $13 Bd7 15. a4 (15. Nf1 b5 16. Ne3) 15... Qd8 16. a5 $1 {This is the only way White can create problems to the opponent.} Ne8 17. Kd1 (17. Kf1 $11 f5 $2 {was followed by the energetic} 18. exf5 $1 $17 {0-1 Kislik,E (2320)-Banusz,T (2552)/Szombathely HUN 2011/The Week in Chess 891 (54)} gxf5 $2 19. Kg2 $1 f4 20. Bh2) 17... Rb8 18. Kc1 $1 b5 19. axb6 Rxb6 20. Kb1 f5 $6 {A natural but inaccurate move.} 21. f3 $36 {White has got more than enough compensation for the pawn.} Qg5 22. Nd1 h5 23. h4 Qe7 24. gxh5 gxh5 25. exf5 (25. Rg1 $1) 25... Bxf5 26. Ne4 Nef6 27. Bd3 Nxe4 28. Bxe4 Bxe4 29. fxe4 (29. Qxe4 {White should play with care.}) 29... Rf3 30. Rg1 (30. Qg2) 30... Nf6 31. Be1 Ng4 32. Qe2 Qf7 33. Bd2 Kh7 34. Ba5 Rb8 35. Bd2 (35. Bc7) 35... Nf2 36. Nxf2 (36. Rxa6) (36. Rf1) 36... Rxf2 37. Qe3 Qf4 38. Qxf4 (38. Kc1) 38... exf4 39. Rxg7+ Kxg7 40. Bc3+ Kg8 41. Rxa6 Rd8 42. Bf6 Rd7 43. Kc1 f3 44. Kd1 Re2 {led to an unclear game:} 45. Ra3 Rxe4 46. Rxf3 Rxc4 47. Ke2 Rf7 $13 48. Ke3 {was in vain:} Kh7 1-0

