1. d4 {Chekhov,V Chekhov,V: 'Marin'} d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Nf3 a6 5. c5 Nbd7 6. Bf4 Nh5 7. Bd2 Nhf6 8. Rc1 g6 9. h3 Bg7 10. Bf4 O-O 11. e3 b6 12. cxb6 Qxb6 13. Bd3 (13. Qc2 c5 $15 {[%csl Gc1,Gd5] Marin}) (13. Qd2 {(Chekhov,V) Marin} Ne4 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15. Ne5 Nxe5 {This is another moment when h2-h3 favours Black, as White cannot answer h3. Compare with the similar position arising in line A2).} 16. Bxe5 Bxe5 17. dxe5 Be6 18. b3 a5) (13. Na4 Qa5+ 14. Nd2 e5 (14... Ne4 15. a3 Nxd2 16. b4 Qd8 17. Qxd2 $132 {Chekhov,V: '(This is an even better version for Black of the line mentioned above - Marin)'}) 15. Bxe5 Nxe5 16. dxe5 Ne4 $19 {Eingorn,V (2470)-Petrosian,A (2435) Tallinn 1980 (½-½, 29)} 17. a3 Bxe5 18. b4 Qc7) 13... c5 (13... Qxb2 14. O-O $2 Qa3 (14... a5 $146 15. Rb1 {[%cal Ge8d7,Ga8g8] Chekhov,V} Qxc3 16. Rb3) 15. Na4 Bb7 16. Rc3 Qb4 $16 17. Qc2 Qa5 18. Rb1 Ra7 19. Nc5 Nxc5 20. Rxc5 Qd8 21. Ne5) 14. Qe2 $6 (14. Qd2 cxd4 $17 {Marin} 15. exd4 Bb7 16. O-O Ne4 17. Qe3 Ndf6 $17 18. Na4 $2) 14... Bb7 $1 15. O-O Rfc8 (15... Ne4) 16. a3 (16. Rfd1) 16... cxd4 (16... c4 17. Bb1 Bc6) 17. exd4 Nh5 18. Be3 (18. Bh2 Bh6) 18... Qd6 19. Qd2 (19. Bb1) 19... Ndf6 (19... Nb6) 20. Ne5 Ne4 (20... Nd7 {Chekhov,V}) 21. Nxe4 dxe4 22. Nc4 Qd8 23. Be2 Nf6 24. Na5 Qd7 (24... Bd5 $5) 25. Nb3 e6 26. Nc5 $6 Qe7 $1 27. b4 Nd5 (27... Rd8 $5 28. Rfd1 $5 e5 29. Bc4 exd4 30. Bxd4 $44 {Chekhov,V: '(!? Marin)'}) 28. Bg5 f6 29. Bh4 g5 30. Bg3 Rd8 31. Bc4 (31. Nxe4 Nf4 32. Bxf4 gxf4 33. Qxf4 $19 Rxd4 34. Rc7 $19 Rxe4 35. Rxe7 $19 Rxf4 36. Rxb7 $19) 31... h6 (31... f5 32. Nxb7 Qxb7 33. Qxg5 $19 h6) 32. h4 Kh8 33. hxg5 hxg5 34. Qe2 Bc8 35. Nxe4 Kg8 36. Qh5 Ra7 $19 37. Rfe1 Nf4 38. Bxf4 gxf4 39. Nc5 Rd6 40. Qf5 0-1

