1. e4 {Huzman} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be3 e5 7. Nb3 Be6 8. f3 Nbd7 9. Qd2 b5 10. g4 Nb6 11. g5 Nfd7 12. Nd5 Rc8 {about 3 monthes ago gelfand was very successfull with this line with the black pieces beating Shirov with only 27 moves} (12... Bxd5 13. exd5 Rc8 (13... Qc7 14. h4 Rc8 15. Rh2 Be7 16. O-O-O Nc4 17. Bxc4 bxc4 18. Na5 c3 19. Qxc3 Qxc3 20. bxc3 Bd8 21. Nc6 $16 {Grabarczyk,B-Kuczynski,R POL-ch 1996}) 14. Na5 (14. O-O-O {transposes to the game}) 14... Qc7 (14... Nxd5 15. Nb7 Nxe3 16. Nxd8 Nxc2+ 17. Kd1 Nxa1 18. Nb7 Nc2 {Gelfand}) 15. Bxb6 $6 (15. c4 $1 Nxc4 16. Nxc4 bxc4 17. Rc1 $16 {Gelfand}) 15... Nxb6 16. Bh3 Ra8 17. Nc6 g6 18. f4 h6 $13 {Shirov,A-Gelfand,B Madrid 1996}) (12... Nxd5 13. exd5 Bf5 14. Bd3 Bxd3 15. Qxd3 Be7 16. Rg1 {Jirovsky-Vacek 1994}) 13. O-O-O (13. Na5 {there is a big difference playing a5 when black still has his bishop} Nxd5 14. exd5 Bxd5 {now white does not have b7} 15. Qxd5 Qxa5+ 16. c3 Be7 17. a4 O-O 18. Bd3 Qd8 19. h4 Nc5 20. Bf5 Nxa4 21. Bxc8 Qxc8 {with a very good position for black Diaz,Joa-Herrera,I Capablanca mem-B 1996}) (13. Nxb6 {Huzman} Nxb6 14. Qa5 Nc4 15. Qxd8+ Kxd8 16. Bxc4 Bxc4 (16... bxc4 17. Na5 $13) 17. O-O-O $10) 13... Bxd5 14. exd5 Nc4 15. Qf2 Be7 (15... Nxe3 16. Qxe3 Be7 17. Rg1 (17. h4 $5) 17... Qb6 18. Qxb6 Nxb6 19. Bd3 Nc4 20. Rde1 Bd8 $1 {with a nice position for black Arams,J-Balzar,A Dortmund op 1988}) 16. h4 h6 (16... Nxe3 $1 {Huzman} 17. Qxe3 h6 18. g6 Bxh4 (18... f5 19. Qe1 (19. Bh3 O-O 20. Qd3 Bxh4 21. Bxf5 $140 Qg5+ 22. Kb1 Qxf5 (22... Rxf5 23. Rxh4 Rcf8 $17) 23. Rxh4 Qxf3 $19) 19... O-O 20. Na5 $132) 19. gxf7+ Kxf7 20. Kb1 Bg5 $15) (16... Ndb6 17. Na5 $1 Nxe3 18. Qxe3 Nxd5 19. Rxd5 Qxa5 20. Kb1 $44) 17. gxh6 gxh6 (17... g6 {Huzman} 18. Bxc4 (18. f4 Bxh4 19. Qe2 Bg3 $17) 18... bxc4 19. Nd2 c3 (19... Qa5 20. Ne4 Qxa2 21. Nc3 Qa5 (21... Qa1+ $2 22. Kd2 Qxb2 23. Rb1 Qa3 24. Ra1 Qb4 25. Rhb1 $18) 22. f4 $13) 20. Ne4 cxb2+ 21. Kb1 $36) 18. Kb1 (18. Bxc4 $1 {Huzman} bxc4 19. Nd2 c3 20. Ne4 (20. Nb3 cxb2+ 21. Kb1 a5 $15) 20... cxb2+ 21. Kb1 f5 $6 22. Qg2 $40) (18. f4 {Huzman} Bxh4 19. Qe2 Bf6 $13 (19... Bg3 $5)) 18... Bxh4 19. Qe2 (19. Rxh4 $2 Nxe3) 19... Nxe3 (19... Bg5 {Huzman} 20. Bxg5 Qxg5 21. Bh3 $1 $132 (21. Nd4 $4 Ne3)) 20. Qxe3 Bg5 21. Qe1 O-O 22. Bd3 f5 (22... Nc5 {Huzman} 23. Bf5 Rc7 24. Qa5 $1 $132) 23. Qg1 (23. Nd4 {Huzman} exd4 24. Qe6+ Kg7 $19) (23. f4 {Huzman} Bxf4 24. Nd4 exd4 25. Qe6+ Rf7 26. Rdg1+ Kf8 27. Rxh6 Bxh6 28. Qxh6+ Ke7 29. Qe6+ Kf8 $10) 23... Kh7 24. Rh5 $1 Nc5 25. f4 $3 {a very strong move forcing black to clear his control over the d4 square which means white knight is coming!} (25. Nxc5 {Huzman} Rxc5 26. Qg3 Rc7 27. Rdh1 Rg7 28. Qh3 Qf6) 25... exf4 (25... Nxd3 26. fxg5 Nf4 27. Rxh6+ Kg7 28. Qh2 {winning}) (25... Bxf4 26. Bxf5+ Rxf5 27. Rxf5 Qd7 28. Qg4 $1 {with h5 on the next move}) 26. Nd4 Kg6 27. Qh2 Qf6 $6 (27... Rc7 28. Rg1 $1 Rh7 29. Nf3 $1 Rhh8 30. Qh4 {winning}) (27... Nxd3 $8 {this seems black best chance since Gelfands move gives very little hope} 28. Ne6 (28. cxd3 {Huzman} Qf6 29. Ne6 $18) 28... Qf6 (28... Qe8) (28... Ne5 $1 29. Nxd8 Rcxd8 $132) 29. cxd3 $1 Rh8 30. Rh1 Kf7 {is not xg5 followed by h6} 31. Nxg5+ hxg5 32. Rh7+ $3 {the correct move since,the very natural move xh8 is not good at all} (32. Rxh8 Rxh8 33. Qxh8 Qxh8 34. Rxh8 f3 {and the pawns are quick!}) 32... Rxh7 33. Qxh7+ Kf8 34. Rh6 Qe5 (34... Qf7 35. Qh8+) 35. Re6 {and white is winning}) 28. Bxf5+ Qxf5 (28... Kf7 29. Bxc8 Rxc8 30. Qh3 {with f5}) 29. Nxf5 Rxf5 30. Rh1 Rh8 31. Rxg5+ $1 Rxg5 (31... Kxg5 32. Qh4+ Kg6 33. Qg4+ Kf6 (33... Rg5 34. Qxf4 {is the game}) 34. Rg1 Rg5 35. Qxf4+ Ke7 36. Re1+ $18) 32. Qxf4 Rd8 33. a3 $2 {33.b4 is winning immediately} (33. b4) 33... Kg7 34. Rf1 Kh7 35. b4 Na4 36. Qe4+ Kh8 37. Qe7 Rdg8 38. Qxd6 Kh7 39. Qe7+ R8g7 40. Qe4+ Kg8 41. Qe8+ Kh7 42. d6 1-0

