1. e4 c5 2. c3 d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Be2 cxd4 7. cxd4 e6 8. O-O Be7 9. Nc3 Qd6 (9... Qd8) 10. Nb5 Qd8 11. Bf4 (11. Ne5 $5 O-O (11... Bd7 12. Be3 O-O 13. Rc1 Nd5 14. Nxd7 Qxd7 15. Nc3 Rfd8 $10 {Danek-Roeder/Vienna op/1991/}) 12. Nxc6 bxc6 13. Nc3 Nd5 14. Na4 Bf6 15. Bf3 Rb8 16. b3 Ba6 17. Re1 Bb5 18. Nc5 Nc3 19. Qc2 Bxd4 20. Bb2 Bxc5 21. Qxc3 Qf6 22. Qxf6 gxf6 23. Bxf6 $14 {Braga-Schlosser/Mitropa Cup/1993/}) 11... Nd5 (11... O-O $2 12. Bc7 $1 Qd7 13. Ne5 Nxe5 14. dxe5 Nd5 15. Bd6 $16 {×d6}) 12. Bg3 a6 (12... b6 $2 13. Bc4 $1) (12... O-O 13. Bc4 {Sveshnikov,E-Tiviakov,S/Podolsk/1992/0.5/13/} a6 (13... Qb6 14. Qe2 a6 15. Nc3 Qa5 {Godena,M-Tiviakov,S/Forli op/1992/0.5/57/}) 14. Bxd5 exd5 (14... axb5 15. Be4 $1 (15. Bb3 Bf6 16. Be5 Bd7 17. Qe2 Na5 18. Bc2 Bc6 $10 {Schulz-Gheorghiu,F/Altensteig/1987/}) 15... Ra6 $6 16. Qe2 f5 17. Bd3 Ra5 18. Rfd1 Nb4 $13 {Sveshnikov,E-Kortschnoj,V/Biel/1993/}) 15. Nc7 Ra7 {Looks nice for White} 16. Qb3 Bd6 17. Bxd6 Qxd6 18. Qb6 $1 $14 {Lautier,J-Polgar,J/Linares/1994/1-0/; Fomin,T-Shulman,Y/St.Petersburg op/1994/½-½/} Ra8) 13. Nc3 O-O (13... Nxc3 14. bxc3 b5 {Sveshnikov}) 14. Rc1 (14. Qb3 b6 $6 15. Nxd5 exd5 16. Rac1 {Sveshnikov,E-Micic,C/Chelianinsk/1989/1-0/46/}) (14. Ne5 $6 Nxc3 15. bxc3 Nxe5 16. Bxe5 Bd6 17. Bxd6 $15 {Harley,AD-Mortavazi,A/London Simpson/½-½/1994/}) 14... Nf6 (14... Bd7) (14... Nxc3 $5) 15. h3 {Preventing 15...h5, but Tiviakov didn t intend to play this move.} b6 (15... Qb6 $6 16. Na4) (15... Nb4 16. Ne5 Nbd5) (15... b5 $5 16. Nxb5 axb5 17. Rxc6 Rxa2 $10) 16. a3 (16. Qd2 {17.fd1}) 16... Bb7 17. Bd3 (17. Bc4 $5 b5 18. Ba2 b4 19. axb4 Nxb4 20. Bb1 {Now White can t continue with d3.}) 17... Rc8 18. Bb1 b5 $5 19. Qd3 $6 (19. Re1 Na5 20. Ne5 (20. Qe2 Nc4 21. Rcd1 Nxa3 $1)) 19... Na5 $5 20. Ne5 Nc4 {Black has a good game} 21. Rc2 Nd6 $6 {Provoking f2-f3} (21... g6 {f6-d5}) 22. f3 {Preventing 22...de4} (22. Re2 Nf5 $1) 22... g6 (22... Nf5 23. Bf2 Nh5 24. Ne2 $10) 23. Bf2 Re8 24. Ba2 (24. Re2 {25.e4}) 24... Bf8 25. Re2 Bg7 26. Rfe1 (26. Ne4 $2 Nfxe4 27. fxe4 Bxe5 28. dxe5 Nxe4 $17) 26... Nd5 (26... Nh5 $5 27. Qd2 Nc4 28. Nxc4 bxc4 29. Bb1 $13) 27. Nxd5 exd5 {Now Black has a horrible bad bishop on b7, and White a very good one on a2.} (27... Bxd5 $1 28. Bxd5 exd5 $10) 28. Qd1 {e5-d3-c5} a5 (28... Rc7 $5 {c7-e7}) (28... Nc4 $2 29. Nxf7 $1 $18) 29. h4 Qc7 30. h5 {One Idea is to open the h-line with 31.h5xg6 and to start an attack in zhe h-line with g2 and doubling in the h-line. Additional the a2 can go to b1 with the theat to sacrifice somthing on g6.} Nc4 $2 31. h6 $1 Bxh6 (31... Bf8 $142 32. Ng4 Rxe2 33. Qxe2 $16 {White has an advantage on the black squares.}) (31... Bxe5 32. dxe5 $18) (31... Bh8 $2 32. Nxc4 Rxe2 33. Qxe2 bxc4 34. Qe8+ Rxe8 35. Rxe8#) 32. Ng4 Rxe2 33. Nxh6+ Kg7 34. Rxe2 $1 (34. Nf5+ $5) (34. Qxe2 Kxh6 35. Bh4 Kg7 $13) 34... Kxh6 35. Qe1 $1 {The key move: e7 and g3} Kg7 (35... Qd6 36. Re7 Rc7 37. Rxc7 Qxc7 38. Qc1+ Kg7 39. b3 $18) 36. Re7 Qb6 (36... Qc6 37. Bxc4 dxc4 38. Qe5+ Kg8 39. Be3 Qd5 (39... f6 40. Qh2 $1 h5 41. Qg3 $18) 40. Qf6) 37. Bxc4 bxc4 38. Qe5+ Kg8 39. Be3 $18 {h6} f6 40. Qf4 {h6} Kf8 (40... g5 41. Qh2 $18) 41. Rxh7 Ke8 42. Qh6 1-0

