1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Be2 O-O 6. Nf3 e5 7. d5 a5 8. Bg5 {Shirov has never before played this line, which is a favoured line by Kramnik and Illescas.} h6 9. Bh4 Na6 10. O-O Qe8 11. Nd2 Nh7 12. a3 Bd7 13. Kh1 (13. b3 {The older line} f5 14. exf5 gxf5 15. Bh5 Qc8 16. Be7 Re8 17. Bxe8 Qxe8 18. Bh4 e4 $15 {Yusupov,A-Kasparov,G/Barcelona WCup/1989/1-0/}) 13... h5 14. f3 Bh6 15. b3 Qb8 $146 {a7} (15... Be3 16. Qc2 c6 (16... Qb8) 17. Bf2 $1 Bxf2 18. Rxf2 $14 {Illescas Cordoba,M-Gelfand,B/Linares/1994/1-0/}) 16. Qc2 (16. Bf2) 16... Be3 17. Bf2 Qa7 18. Bxe3 Qxe3 19. f4 $6 {Too agressiv} (19. Rae1 Qg5 20. Qb2 {b3-b4} Nc5 21. b4 axb4 22. axb4 Na4 23. Nxa4 Rxa4 24. c5) 19... exf4 20. Rae1 Qc5 {Because the white  is worse on b2 or c1 than on c2.} 21. Qc1 (21. Qb2 Qd4 22. Rxf4 Rae8 {g7, the pawn structure is better for Black.}) 21... Qd4 22. Rxf4 Rae8 (22... f5 $2 23. Nf3 Qg7 24. exf5 {d4}) 23. Rff1 (23. Ref1 Qg7 {e7,fe8} (23... g5 $5 24. R4f2 g4 {g7,g5})) 23... Qg7 24. Qc2 h4 $6 {Very agressiv. The idea is to play h4-h3 first before playing f7-f5.} (24... Re7 $142 {fe8, h6, g5 It s better to prepare the push h5-h4.}) 25. Nf3 h3 $2 (25... Qh6 $142 {e7. The situation has improved for White, who can play d3 and f2.}) 26. gxh3 $1 {Black misses, that opening the g-file does not expose the White king, but might well expose the Black king.} Bxh3 (26... f5 $2 27. Rg1 $1) 27. Rg1 Qh6 (27... f5 28. exf5 (28. Nh4 $142 $1) 28... Bxf5 29. Bd3 Bxd3 30. Qxd3 Rxe1 31. Nxe1 $14) 28. Rg3 Kg7 (28... Kh8 29. Reg1 Rg8 {g7 looks too passive.}) 29. Qb2 $6 {Weakens the e-pawn. The Diagonal a1-g7 is not so dangerous.} (29. Nd1 $142 Nc5 $2 30. Nf2) 29... Nf6 30. b4 axb4 31. axb4 Bg4 (31... Rh8 32. Reg1 {3-d4-f5}) 32. Nd1 $6 (32. Nd4 $5 Bc8) (32. Reg1 Rh8 $15) 32... Bxf3+ (32... Rxe4 33. Nf2 Bxf3+ 34. Rxf3 Rf4 35. Rf1 $1 $40 {36.xf4 xf4 37.g4 +-} (35. Ng4 $2 Rxg4 36. Rxf6 Qxh2+ $1 {Shirov} 37. Kxh2 Rh8#)) 33. Bxf3 Rh8 34. Ne3 Kf8 $1 $15 {Unpinning the f6.} 35. Ng4 $6 (35. Qxf6 $4 Qxh2#) (35. Rf1 $5 Nxe4 36. Bxe4 Rxe4 37. Ng4 $132) 35... Nxg4 $17 36. Bxg4 Qg7 37. Qf2 $2 (37. Qxg7+ $2 Kxg7 38. Rb3 Rh4 39. Bf3 f5 $19) (37. Qd2 $5 Qe5 {/}) 37... Nxb4 38. Rb1 $2 (38. Rf3 Rh7 39. Rf1 Kg8 40. Bd7 Re7 41. Be6 Na6 $19) 38... Na6 39. Rxb7 Nc5 40. Rxc7 Nxe4 0-1

