1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be3 Ng4 7. Bg5 h6 8. Bh4 g5 9. Bg3 Bg7 10. h3 Nf6 11. Qe2 $5 {Ponomariov is comming with the whole new concept of treating this famous position. The queen sits more naturally on e2 than on f3.} Nc6 12. Nxc6 bxc6 13. e5 dxe5 14. Bxe5 O-O 15. h4 (15. g3 Be6 16. Bg2 Qb6 17. O-O-O Rad8 18. f4 $14) 15... g4 $1 16. g3 Qb6 17. O-O-O Be6 18. Bg2 Rfd8 19. Rhe1 (19. f3 Qa5 20. Rxd8+ Rxd8 21. fxg4 Bxg4 22. Qe3 Be6 $15) 19... h5 20. b3 (20. f3 $1 Qa5 21. Rxd8+ Rxd8 22. fxg4 Bxg4 23. Qe3 $14) 20... Rac8 21. Na4 Rxd1+ 22. Rxd1 Qb5 23. Bf1 $2 {[%mdl 64] White misses small combination of his lady opponent in the very moment, when he had the chance to get serious advantage.} (23. Qxb5 cxb5 (23... axb5 24. Nb6 Rf8 25. Bxc6 $18) 24. Bb7 Rf8 25. Nc5 Bc8 26. Bxa6 $16) 23... Bc4 $1 24. Qxc4 (24. Qe1 Bxf1 25. Bxf6 Bxf6 26. Qxf1 e6 $15) 24... Qxe5 25. c3 (25. Qxa6 Qa1+ 26. Kd2 Rd8+ 27. Bd3 Ne4+ 28. Ke1 Qe5 $17) 25... Qf5 26. Qc5 (26. Qxa6 Bh6+ 27. f4 gxf3+ 28. Kb2 Rc7 29. Qd3 Qxd3 30. Rxd3 f2 $15) 26... Qf3 27. Bd3 Bh6+ 28. Kc2 Ne4 29. Qe5 $2 {The centralization of the strongest piece is not necessarily always the best move, much more promising was 29.xh5!} (29. Qxh5 $1 Qxf2+ (29... Nxf2 30. Nb2 Nxd1 31. Qxh6 Ne3+ 32. Kc1 Nf5 33. Qg5+ Ng7 34. Qh6 $11) 30. Kb1 Qf3 31. Bc2 Bg7 32. Rd3 Qe2 33. Qa5 Rf8 34. Kb2 $13) 29... Nxf2 (29... Qxf2+ $5 30. Kb1 Qf3 31. Bc2 Nxg3 32. Qxe7 Rf8 $17) 30. Be2 Qg2 (30... Nxd1 31. Bxf3 Ne3+ 32. Kb2 gxf3 33. Qxh5 f2 34. Qxh6 f1=Q (34... Nd1+ 35. Kc2 f1=Q 36. Qg5+ Kf8 37. Qh6+ Ke8 38. Qh8+ Kd7 39. Nb6+ $16) 35. Qxe3 Qg2+ 36. Ka3 $11) 31. Re1 (31. Bf1 Qh2 32. Re1 Nh1+ 33. Kb1 Nxg3 $17) 31... Rd8 32. Qxe7 (32. Bf1 Rd2+ 33. Kb1 Qd5 34. Qxd5 cxd5 35. Bxa6 Ne4 $19) 32... Rd2+ 33. Kb1 Qd5 34. Ka1 (34. Nb2 Rxb2+ 35. Kxb2 Qd2+ 36. Ka3 Bf8 $19) (34. Bc4 Rd1+ 35. Kb2 Bc1+ 36. Kc2 Qd2+ 37. Kb1 Ba3+ 38. Rxd1 Qxd1#) 34... Ne4 {The FIDE world champion is in real trouble, as black pieces are clearly dominating the board.} 35. Qe8+ Kg7 36. Nb2 (36. Bxg4 hxg4 37. Qxe4 Rd1+ 38. Kb2 Bc1+ 39. Kc2 (39. Ka1 Be3+ 40. Kb2 Rd2+ 41. Ka3 Qxe4 $19) 39... Qd2+ 40. Kb1 Ba3+ 41. Rxd1 Qxd1#) 36... Rxb2 (36... Nd6 37. Bc4 Nxe8 38. Bxd5 cxd5 39. Rxe8 Rg2 40. Na4 Rxg3 $19) 37. Kxb2 (37. Bc4 $1 Rxa2+ 38. Kxa2 Qa5+ (38... Nxc3+ 39. Kb2 Qd2+ 40. Ka3 Nb5+ 41. Bxb5 axb5 42. Qe2 Qd6+ 43. Ka2 Qxg3 $17) 39. Kb2 (39. Kb1 Nxc3+ 40. Kc2 Qa2+ 41. Kxc3 Qd2#) 39... Qxc3+ 40. Ka2 Qa5+ 41. Kb2 Qd2+ 42. Ka3 Nd6 43. Qe2 Nxc4+ 44. bxc4 Qc3+ 45. Ka2 Kg8 $17) 37... Qd2+ 38. Ka3 Nf6 $1 (38... Nf6 $1 39. Rd1 Qxd1 40. Bxd1 Nxe8 $19) 0-1

