1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. Be3 Ng4 8. Bg5 f6 9. Bh4 g5 10. Bg3 Nh6 11. h3 Nc6 12. dxe5 fxe5 $6 $14 ({Good reputation has another recapture:} 12... dxe5 13. O-O (13. Qd5+ Kh8 14. Qxd8 Nxd8 15. O-O c6 16. Rfd1 Ne6 17. Bf1 Re8 18. Nd2 Nd4 19. Nb3 Nf7 20. Rac1 Nxb3 21. axb3 Bf8 22. f3 Bc5+ 23. Bf2 Bxf2+ 24. Kxf2 Be6 $11 {½-½ Nogueiras,J-Pecorelli Garcia,H/Santa Clara 1996/EXT 99 (42)}) (13. Qxd8 Nxd8 14. Nd5 Rf7 15. O-O-O Nc6 16. h4 g4 17. Ng5 fxg5 18. hxg5 Nf5 19. exf5 Bxf5 20. Rh4 Nd4 21. Bxg4 Bxg4 22. Rxg4 Ne2+ 23. Kc2 Nxg3 $132 {1-0 Timoscenko,G-Nedev,T/Bled 2002/EXT 2003 (51)}) 13... Be6 (13... Qe8 $6 14. Nd5 Qf7 15. b4 Rd8 16. b5 Nb4 17. Qb3 Nxd5 18. cxd5 Bf8 19. Rac1 Bd6 20. Qe3 Qg7 21. Rc3 b6 22. a4 $16 {1-0 Tisdall,J-Gurcan,S/Moscow 1994/CBM 44 ext (41)}) 14. Qc1 {-see commented game 0-1 Yermolinsky,A-Fedorowicz,J/Los Angeles 1991/CBM 25[Ftacnik,L] (40)}) 13. Qd2 ({Played before this game} 13. c5 $1 {Brought an advantage to White:} dxc5 (13... Nf7 $5 14. cxd6 Qxd6 15. Qxd6 Nxd6 (15... cxd6 16. Nd5 $14) 16. Nxg5 Nd4 17. Rc1 $16) 14. Qxd8 Rxd8 15. Bc4+ Kh8 16. Nxg5 $16 {1-0 Solozhenkin,E-Aleksandrov,L/Leningrad 1990/CBM 18 ext (29)}) 13... Nf7 14. Nh2 Nd4 15. Bg4 Nh8 16. Nf1 $6 $132 {Too passive.} ({Strong was} 16. Nb5 $1 Ne6 17. Nf3 Nf4 18. Bxf4 gxf4 19. c5 $14 {1-0 Ehlvest,J-Van Wely,L/Reykjavik 1994/CBM 39 ext (45)}) (16. Ne2 Ng6 17. Nxd4 exd4 18. Nf3 Nf4 19. Bxc8 Rxc8 20. Nxd4 Nxg2+ (20... Qf6 21. Nf5 Rce8 22. O-O Rxe4 $11 {½-½ Mozetic,D-Vukic,M/Novi Sad 1995/CBM 49 (24)}) 21. Kf1 Qe7 $17) 16... Ng6 17. Ne3 Nf4 18. f3 c6 19. Bxc8 (19. h4 $6 Bxg4 20. Nxg4 Nfe6 $15) 19... Rxc8 20. h4 b5 $1 21. cxb5 cxb5 22. Bxf4 $6 $15 {White decided to get rid of strong f4, however better was to continue to suffer...} (22. Nc2 {[%cal Gc2d4]} Nxc2+ 23. Qxc2 g4 24. Qd2 gxf3 (24... Qa5 25. Bxf4 exf4 26. Nd5 Qxd2+ 27. Kxd2 $14) 25. gxf3 Nh5 26. Bf2 Rxf3 27. Qe2 Qf8 28. Rd1 $132) 22... exf4 {[%cal Gg7c3] White king sticks in the centre. Castle will be too dangerous...} (22... gxf4 $6 23. Nc2 $132) 23. Ned5 a5 (23... g4 $15) 24. Rc1 g4 25. fxg4 $4 $19 {Allows Black to open f-line and develop dangerous Attack against white .} ({The only possibility of resistance was} 25. Qd3 Rc5 $15 {[%csl Re1]}) 25... f3 {[%csl Re1]} 26. Kd1 ({Loses other continuations:} 26. g3 b4 $1 (26... f2+ 27. Kf1 b4 28. Ne2 Rxc1+ 29. Qxc1 Nxe2 30. Kxe2 Qd7 31. Nf4 Qxg4+ 32. Kxf2 Be5 (32... Qe6 {[%csl Ra2,Re4]} 33. Re1 Qxa2 34. Re2 $15) 33. Qd1 $8 Qg7 34. Qd2 Bxb2 35. Kg2 Be5 $15) 27. Nd1 f2+ 28. Kf1 Qe8 {[%csl Re4,Rf1][%cal Ge8b5,Gb5f1,Ge8e4]} 29. Nf4 Qxe4 30. Nxf2 Qf3 {[%csl Rg3]} 31. Rh3 b3 32. Rxc8 Rxc8 33. axb3 Rc2 34. Qe1 Rxb2 $19 {[%csl Rf1,Rh3]}) (26. Kf2 $4 $19 b4 27. Nd1 Qe8 28. Re1 fxg2+ 29. Kxg2 Rxc1 30. Qxc1 Qf7 $19) 26... b4 27. Na4 Rxc1+ 28. Kxc1 Ne2+ 29. Kb1 fxg2 0-1

