1. d4 {Hecht} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Ba6 5. b3 Bb4+ (5... Bb7 6. Bg2 Bb4+ 7. Bd2 a5 8. O-O O-O 9. Qc2 d6 10. Nc3 Nbd7 11. Rfe1 {[%cal Ge2e4]} (11. Ne1 {Probably a harmeless move.} Qc8 12. Rc1 Re8 13. Nb5 Bxg2 14. Nxg2 Qb8 15. a3 Bxd2 16. Qxd2 c6 17. Nc3 d5 $11 {½-½ Kortschnoj,V-Adams,M/Wijk aan Zee 2000/CBM 75 (22)}) (11. Rad1 Bxc3 12. Bxc3 Be4 13. Qc1 a4 14. Bh3 b5 15. Nd2 axb3 16. axb3 bxc4 17. bxc4 Ra2 18. f3 $6 (18. Nxe4 Nxe4 19. Bg2 $11) 18... Bc2 $15 {0-1 Morovic Fernandez,I-Adams,M/Istanbul TUR 2000/The Week in Chess 313 (35)}) 11... Bxc3 12. Bxc3 Be4 13. Qb2 a4 14. Bf1 {[%cal Gf3d2,Ge2e4]} c5 15. Nd2 Bb7 16. b4 a3 17. Qb3 cxd4 18. Bxd4 e5 19. Be3 Qc7 20. Rac1 Qc6 21. f3 Qa4 22. Qb1 d5 $15 {0-1 Topalov,V-Adams,M/Frankfurt GER 2000/The Week in Chess 294 (65)}) 6. Bd2 Be7 7. Bg2 (7. Nc3 Bb7 8. Bg2 O-O 9. O-O Na6 10. Re1 d5 11. cxd5 exd5 12. Ne5 c5 13. Be3 Nc7 14. dxc5 bxc5 15. Na4 Ne6 16. Rc1 Rc8 17. Nd3 Qa5 18. Naxc5 Bxc5 19. Bxc5 Nxc5 20. Rxc5 Rxc5 21. b4 Qxa2 22. bxc5 $16 {1-0 Anand,V-Gelfand,B/Shenyang CHN 2000/The Week in Chess 305 (41)}) 7... c6 (7... Bb7 8. Nc3 d5 9. cxd5 exd5 10. O-O O-O 11. Nh4 g6 12. Bg5 Ne4 13. Bxe7 Qxe7 14. Rc1 Na6 15. Qd3 c5 16. Nf3 Rad8 {½-½ Korchnoi,V-Kramnik,V/Wijk aan Zee NED 2000/The Week in Chess 273 (43) Looks like black has no problems.}) 8. Bc3 d5 9. Ne5 Nfd7 10. Nxd7 Nxd7 11. Nd2 O-O 12. O-O Rb8 {[%cal Gb6b5]} (12... f5 13. Rc1 Rc8 14. Bb2 Bb7 15. e3 Nf6 {1-0 Van Wely,L-Lautier,J/Wijk aan Zee 1997/CBM 57 (37) Not everybody enjoys of playing Stonewall structure,but this one seems to be a very interesting one.Although the position looks almost equal,white still has a slightly better chances.}) (12... Rc8 13. e4 b5 14. Re1 dxc4 15. bxc4 Nb6 (15... bxc4 $5 16. Qa4 Bb5 17. Qc2 Re8 18. a4 Ba6 19. Rad1 Bf8 20. Nf1 Rb8 21. Ne3 Bb4 22. d5 exd5 23. exd5 c5 {0-1 Sturua,Z-Shariyazdanov,A/Biel SUI 2000/The Week in Chess 300 (82) White didn't succede to prove the compensation for sacrafised pawn.}) 16. c5 Na4 17. Qc2 $14 {[%csl Ra6] 1-0 Hertneck,G-Wahls,M/Passau GER 2000/The Week in Chess 276 (29)}) 13. a4 $6 {Not a best move.First it looks like it preventing b5,but from the other side now pushing e4 will bring white nothing .} (13. Re1 b5 14. e4 bxc4 15. bxc4 dxc4 16. Qa4 Bb5 17. Qc2 {[%cal Ga2a4]} Ba3 18. Nb1 Bd6 (18... Be7 19. Nd2 Ba3 20. Nb1 Be7 21. Nd2 {½-½ Danielsen,H-Sax,G/Valby 1994/EXT 98 (21)}) 19. a4 Ba6 20. Nd2 Qc7 {½-½ Balogh,T-Butnorius,A/Batumi GEO 1999 (22) Black defenetly has no problems.} (20... Bb4 $5)) 13... Nf6 {[%cal Gc6c5]} 14. e4 c5 15. e5 (15. exd5 exd5 $15) 15... Nd7 16. Re1 cxd4 {Simple and good.Black exchanges few pieces in the center and leaves white with the weakness on c4.} 17. Bxd4 dxc4 18. Nxc4 Bxc4 19. bxc4 Nc5 20. Bxc5 {White uses an apportunity and transfers the game into the ending with opposite colour bishops.Unfortunatly it is not getting easier.} Bxc5 {[%csl Ra4,Rc4,Gc5,Rg2][%cal Gc5f2]} 21. Qc2 (21. Qxd8 Rfxd8 {[%cal Gd8d2,Gd2f2]} 22. Rad1 Bb4 23. Rf1 Bc3 24. f4 Bd4+ 25. Kh1 Rbc8 $15 {With good chances for a winning.}) 21... Qc7 $15 {[%csl Ra4,Rc4,Re5]} 22. Rad1 Rbd8 (22... f6 23. Be4 h6 (23... f5 24. Bf3 f4 25. g4 $13) 24. exf6 Rxf6 25. Re2 Rbf8 26. Rdd2 {[%cal Gg1g2,Gf2f3] And white is holding the position.}) 23. Qb2 Rxd1 24. Rxd1 Rd8 {[%csl Ra4,Rc4,Re5,Rf2] The simplest choise.Instead of calculating positions with the rooks in the game,black prefers to play  and  against  and .. But there is too big difference between the bishops and existence of 4 pawn weaknesses is not making white's life any easier.} 25. Bf3 g6 26. Rxd8+ {Because of the weaknesses white can't even fight for d-file.} Qxd8 27. Kg2 {Hecht: ' Aktiver schwarzer Läufer bei besserer Bauernstruktur.'} Qd3 {It is very difficult to defend white position.Black will attack the white  with at least one piece more,because white bishop can't really stop the black one.} 28. Qe2 (28. Be2 Qe4+ 29. Kg1 Bd4 $19) 28... Qd7 {[%cal Gd7a4] Very nice idea.Black forces white to put the  on c2,afterwards the black  will take very important for attack place:D4!} 29. Qc2 Kf8 30. Bd1 (30. Be4 $142 {Hecht oder La8}) 30... Qd4 31. Qe2 h5 {[%cal Gh5h4]} 32. h4 Kg8 33. Bc2 Qc3 {Black gains more space and some good squares for pieces.} 34. Bd3 Kg7 35. Bc2 Bd4 {Black position is already winning.} 36. f4 {[%csl Rg2]} Bc5 {[%cal Gc3d4,Gd4g1]} 37. Bd3 {'?' Hecht.} (37. Be4 $1 {Hecht} Qa1 38. Bc6 $15) 37... Qa1 {[%cal Ga1g1]} 38. Bc2 Qg1+ 39. Kf3 (39. Kh3 {Hecht} Qh1+ 40. Qh2 Qf1+ 41. Qg2 Qxc4 $17) 39... a5 $22 40. Bb3 Qh1+ 41. Qg2 Qe1 {[%cal Ge1e3,Ge1c3]} 0-1

