3. Rg1 Nef5 24. Qh3 Qc5 $40 {Dearnley,A (2337)-Mason,I (2205)/email/2011/}) 19. Rd1 (19. Nd6+ Rxd6 $1 20. exd6 Qxd6 $44) 19... Kb8 ({It looks that Psakhis,L: 'It looks as if'} 19... Bxe4 20. Qxe4 Nc6 21. a4 {[%cal Gc1a3]} Ng6 {[%cal Gg8h8] leads to nice position for Black}) 20. Rb4 Bxe4 21. Qxe4 Nc6 22. Rb1 Ka8 ({Again} 22... Ng6 {[%cal Gg8h8] was not a bad idea, for example} 23. Ba6 b6 24. Be2 Rh8 25. Bf3 Nge7 $13) 23. a4 a6 (23... Ng6 $1) 24. Ba3 {[%cal Ga3d6,Ga3c5]} Rd5 $4 {[%mdl 8192] It was a last chance to play Psakhis,L: 'This was a last chance to play'} (24... Ng6 $142 $5 {with the idea to organize couterplay on the h line and i am not sure, that White can get any advantage, for example Psakhis,L: 'with the idea to organise counterplay on the h-file and i am not sure that White can get any advantage, for example'} 25. Bc5 (25. Rb3 Rh8 26. Kg1 f5 $1 $132) 25... Rd5 26. Bd6 Rxd6 27. exd6 Qxd6 28. Rb6 $140 Nxf4 29. Bxa6 Nd5 $1 30. Bxb7+ Ka7 $17) 25. Qh7 $1 $18 {Now game is over, Judit doesn't lose her chance to win key pawn and , soon , game. Psakhis,L: 'Now the game is over; Judit doesn't miss her chance to win a key pawn and, soon, the game.'} Qd8 $8 26. Qxf7 Rd7 27. Qf6 Qa5 28. Qxe6 Rgg7 29. Bd3 1-0

