1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 {Enough with Petrosian System!} Ba6 5. b3 Bb4+ 6. Bd2 Be7 7. Bg2 c6 {Judit likes this system,it does not offer black much however it is a tough nut to crack.} 8. Bc3 d5 9. Nbd2 {I prefer this} ({to} 9. Ne5 Nfd7 10. Nxd7 Nxd7 11. Nd2 O-O 12. O-O) 9... Nbd7 10. O-O O-O 11. Re1 c5 12. e4 dxe4 (12... Nxe4 13. Nxe4 dxe4 {looks more accurate if you want to exchange on e4 everything.}) 13. Nxe4 (13. Ng5 cxd4 14. Bxd4 Bb7 15. Ndxe4 Nxe4 {transposes to the text.}) 13... Bb7 14. Nfg5 cxd4 (14... Qc7 {was played by GM Lautier against me in Ohrid 2001.}) 15. Bxd4 ({I was calculating the following line during the game.} 15. Nxf6+ Nxf6 16. Bxb7 Rb8 17. Qxd4 Qxd4 18. Bxd4 Rxb7 $11) 15... Nxe4 16. Bxe4 $5 {I wanted to place my queen on f3 that was why I went for this exchange.} (16. Nxe4 Qc7 17. Nc3 {has even Karpov's trademark on.} Bxg2 18. Kxg2 Qc6+ 19. Qf3 Qxf3+ 20. Kxf3 Rfd8 $11) 16... Bxe4 17. Nxe4 Nc5 18. Bc3 $1 $146 {Showing good fighting ability but nothing more.} (18. Nxc5 bxc5 19. Bc3 a5 $132) 18... Nxe4 {Draw offer.} 19. Rxe4 $14 Bf6 (19... Qxd1+ 20. Rxd1 Rfd8 21. Ree1 $1 $14 {and white is slightly better.} (21. Red4 Rxd4 22. Rxd4 Bf6 23. Rd3 Bxc3 24. Rxc3 Kf8 $11)) 20. Qxd8 $6 {I have forgotten my prepared move against 19...f6.} (20. Qf3 $1 {Grischuk} Bxc3 21. Qxc3 Qe7 22. Rd4 Rfd8 23. Rad1 $14 {and once GM Adorjan was aiming for such an ending against GM Sax..}) 20... Rfxd8 21. Bxf6 gxf6 22. Rg4+ {Here I have decided to force a draw because after white has lost the d line black objectively could not be better.} (22. Re2 $1 Rd4 $1 23. Rc1 Rad8 24. f4 f5 25. Kf2 Kg7 26. c5 bxc5 27. Rxc5 R8d7 $11) (22. c5 bxc5 23. Rc4 Rac8 (23... Rd2 24. Rxc5 a5 $11) 24. Rac1 Rd2 25. Ra4 Rc7 26. Rcc4 Rdd7 27. Ra5 Rd5 28. Rca4 $11) 22... Kf8 23. Rh4 Kg7 24. Rg4+ Kf8 25. Rh4 1/2-1/2

