1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Nxd7 5. O-O Ngf6 6. Qe2 e6 7. b3 Be7 8. Bb2 O-O 9. c4 a6 (9... Re8 10. d4 cxd4 11. Nxd4 a6 12. Nc3 Qc7 13. f4 (13. Rac1 Rad8 14. Kh1 Qc5 15. Rfd1 Bf8 16. Nc2 Qc7 17. Ne3 Qb8 18. Ng4 Nxg4 19. Qxg4 b5 20. Qe2 b4 {½-½ Svetushkin,D-Ristic,N/EUCup Krunica 1997/CBM 62 (88)}) 13... Qc5 14. Na4 Qh5 15. Qxh5 Nxh5 16. f5 Bf6 17. fxe6 fxe6 18. Rad1 Nc5 19. g4 Nxa4 20. bxa4 Bxd4+ 21. Bxd4 e5 22. gxh5 exd4 23. Rxd4 $14 {1-0 Tal,M-Miles,A/Riga (izt) (54)}) 10. d4 cxd4 11. Nxd4 Rc8 12. Nc3 Qc7 13. Rad1 Rfe8 14. Kh1 Bf8 15. f4 Qa5 16. Nf3 $146 (16. Rd3 g6 17. Nf3 Nh5 18. g3 b5 19. cxb5 axb5 20. e5 d5 21. Nd4 b4 22. Na4 Qa6 23. g4 Ng7 24. Nf3 Rc7 {0-1 Fette,M-Gallagher,J/Krumbach op 1991 (36)}) 16... Red8 17. e5 dxe5 18. fxe5 Ng4 19. Ng5 Ndxe5 ({It was to dangerous to play} 19... Ngxe5 20. Qe4 (20. Qh5 Nf6 21. Rxd8 Nxh5 22. Rxc8 Nf6 23. Rd1 $13) 20... g6 21. Nxf7 $1 Nxf7 22. Qxe6 Nde5 23. Nd5 Rc6 $8 24. Ne7+ Bxe7 25. Qxe7 $16 {[%csl Gb2,Ge7,Gf1,Rg8] but saving herself from one threat, Black is under a new one.}) 20. Nd5 (20. Nxf7 $1 Rxd1 (20... Nxf7 21. Rxd8 Nxd8 22. Qxg4 $16 {[%csl Gb2,Gf1,Gg4]}) 21. Nxd1 $5 Nxf7 (21... Nxh2 22. Nxe5 (22. Kxh2 Nxf7 23. Qxe6 Qh5+ $1) 22... Nxf1 23. Qxf1 $16) 22. Qxg4 Re8 $14) 20... exd5 ({Possibly Judit could play superbrave} 20... Qxa2 $5 {for example:} 21. Qc2 Ng6 22. Ra1 $140 Qxa1 23. Bxa1 Rxd5 $13) 21. Bxe5 Nxe5 (21... dxc4 $2 22. Qxg4 Rxd1 23. Qxd1 Qxe5 24. Qh5 $18) 22. Qxe5 Rc7 $5 23. cxd5 $6 ({Black experiences much more difficulties after} 23. Qf4 $5 {[%cal Gd1d8,Gf1f7] for example} Bd6 $140 24. Qf5 g6 25. Qh3 h5 26. Rxd5 $18) 23... Re7 (23... Qb6 $5 {bringing queen to the king side.}) 24. Qf5 $6 {Facing stubborn defense, Fressinet loses his rate of attack.} (24. Qf4 $140 $1 Rdd7 $140 25. d6 Re8 26. Nxf7 $18) 24... g6 25. Qh3 ({Worth considering} 25. Qf6 $5 Rdd7 26. d6 Re8 27. Nxf7 Bg7 28. Qf4 $14 {although, the lion's share of advantage had been already missed.}) 25... f5 $8 (25... h6 26. d6 Rxd6 27. Rxd6 Qxg5 28. Rd8 $16) 26. d6 Red7 27. g4 (27. Qd3 Re8 28. Qc4+ Kh8 $13) 27... f4 $5 28. Ne6 (28. Ne4 Kh8) 28... Re8 29. g5 $5 {It looks like White has managed to cause serious threats, but it is just an illusory thing.} ({The following does not give anything to White} 29. Nxf8 Rxf8 30. g5 Qf5) 29... Rxd6 $1 (29... Bxd6 30. Nxf4 {[%cal Gh3d7]} Rdd8 31. Ne6 Rd7 32. Nf8 $1 Rde7 33. Rxd6 Rxf8 34. Rxf8+ Kxf8 35. Rf6+ Rf7 $8 36. Rxf7+ Kxf7 37. Qxh7+ $16) (29... Qb5 $5) 30. Nxf8 Rxd1 31. Qxh7+ Kxf8 32. Qh8+ Kf7 (32... Ke7 $2 33. Qg7+ Kd8 34. Rxd1+ Kc8 35. Qd7+ $18) 33. Qf6+ Kg8 34. Qxg6+ Kf8 35. Qh6+ Kg8 36. Qg6+ (36. Rxd1 Re1+ 37. Rxe1 Qxe1+ 38. Kg2 Qe2+ 39. Kh3 f3) 36... Kf8 37. Rxd1 Re1+ 38. Rxe1 Qxe1+ 39. Kg2 Qe2+ 40. Kh3 f3 41. Qf5+ Ke7 42. Qf6+ Kd7 43. Qf7+ Kd6 44. Qf4+ Kc6 45. Qc4+ Kb6 46. Qd4+ Kc6 {White queen and Black king had strange and very long dance together!} 1/2-1/2

