1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f3 Qb6 7. Nb3 e6 8. g4 Nc6 9. g5 {Acs has decided not to pursue the bishop to e3 right away. Black queen can not sit on b6 forever, since otherwise Polgar would not be able to develop the queenside.} Nd7 10. h4 Qc7 (10... Be7 11. h5) 11. Be3 b5 12. h5 Bb7 (12... b4 13. Ne2 Bb7 14. Nf4 Be7 15. Rg1 $13) 13. Rh3 Nb6 (13... g6 $2 14. hxg6 fxg6 15. Nd4 $16) 14. Qd2 (14. g6 b4 15. gxf7+ Kxf7 16. Nb1 d5 $13) 14... Ne5 (14... b4 15. Nd1 (15. Qf2 bxc3 16. Bxb6 Qe7 17. Be3 cxb2 18. Rb1 d5 $132) 15... Rd8 16. Qf2 Nc8 $13) 15. Qf2 Nec4 (15... Nbc4 16. Bd4 b4 17. Nd1 d5 18. h6 $14) 16. Bd4 b4 (16... e5 17. Bxb6 Nxb6 18. O-O-O b4 19. Nd5 Nxd5 20. exd5 Rc8 21. Rg3 $11) 17. Nd1 d5 {Black is keeping low profile on the kingside, all her energy goes into activity in the center and the queenside.} (17... e5 $5 18. Bxb6 Nxb6 19. Ne3 d5 20. exd5 Nxd5 21. Nxd5 Bxd5 22. f4 exf4 23. O-O-O Be6 24. Rhd3 $13) 18. e5 (18. h6 e5 19. hxg7 Bxg7 20. Bc5 dxe4 21. fxe4 Bxe4 $13) 18... Nd7 19. f4 Be7 20. Ne3 (20. g6 fxg6 21. hxg6 h6 22. Ne3 O-O 23. Qh2 Ndb6 24. O-O-O Nxe3 25. Bxe3 Nc4 $11) 20... a5 21. Nd2 (21. h6 g6 22. O-O-O O-O $11) 21... Nxd2 22. Qxd2 Nc5 23. g6 (23. h6 g6 24. Bb5+ Bc6 25. Bxc5 Bxc5 26. Nxd5 exd5 27. Qxd5 Bf2+ 28. Kf1 Ra6 29. Qd3 Rb6 30. Bxc6+ Rxc6 31. Kxf2 Rxc2+ $11) (23. Bb5+ Bc6 $11) 23... hxg6 24. hxg6 Rxh3 25. Bxh3 (25. gxf7+ Kxf7 26. Bxh3 Ne4 27. Qg2 Bh4+ 28. Kd1 Bg3 29. f5 Bxe5 30. fxe6+ Kg8 $17) 25... Bh4+ 26. Kf1 $2 {The classical problem with schematic thinking, Acs subconciously drifts the king to his flank. Somewhat paradoxically the right approach was to move in the opposite direction to d1 with equal chances.} (26. Kd1 $1 Ne4 (26... f5 27. Bxf5 exf5 28. Nxf5 Ne4 29. Qh2 Qc4 30. Nxg7+ Kd7 31. Qh3+ Kc6 32. Ne6 Ba6 $11) 27. Qg2 Bg3 28. Qf3 Rc8 29. Bf1 f5 30. Bd3 $11) 26... Ne4 27. Qd1 (27. Qg2 Bg3 28. gxf7+ Qxf7 29. f5 Ba6+ 30. Kg1 Bf2+ 31. Kh2 exf5 $19) 27... Bf2 $1 28. Qg4 (28. gxf7+ Qxf7 29. Qg4 Bc8 30. Ke2 g5 (30... Bg3 31. f5 Ba6+ 32. Kf3 $13) 31. fxg5 Bg3 $17) 28... Bxe3 29. Bxe3 d4 30. gxf7+ (30. Bg1 Qxc2 31. gxf7+ Kf8 32. Rd1 Nd2+ 33. Rxd2 (33. Kf2 Nf3+ 34. Kg3 Qxd1 $19) 33... Qxd2 34. Bf2 Rc8 $19) 30... Kf8 $1 {The key move of the tactical shoot out, black will be tempo ahead in the attack.} 31. Qh4 (31. Bxd4 $2 Qc4+ 32. Ke1 Qxd4 $19) 31... Qc4+ 32. Kg1 dxe3 33. Bg4 (33. Qh8+ Kxf7 34. Qh5+ Kg8 35. Re1 Bd5 36. Rxe3 Qxc2 $19) 33... e2 0-1

