1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. c4 b6 4. a3 Bb7 5. Nc3 d5 6. cxd5 Nxd5 7. Qc2 Nxc3 8. Qxc3 h6 9. e3 Nd7 10. b4 Be7 11. Bb2 O-O 12. Rd1 a5 {Polgar is looking for the compensation, that would balance the dangerous battery along the a1-h8 diagonal.} 13. b5 (13. bxa5 Rxa5 14. Rc1 c5 $15) (13. Be2 axb4 14. axb4 Nf6 15. b5 Nd5 16. Qc4 Bb4+ 17. Kf1 Bd6 $15) 13... Rc8 14. Qb3 (14. Be2 c6 15. bxc6 Bxc6 16. Qd3 $11) 14... c6 15. bxc6 Bxc6 16. Bb5 $2 (16. Be2 Bd5 17. Qb5 $11) 16... Bb4+ (16... Bd5 17. Qd3 Nf6 18. O-O Be4 19. Qe2 Rc2 20. Rd2 Bxf3 21. gxf3 Rxd2 22. Qxd2 Qd5 23. Qe2 Qh5 24. a4 $11) 17. axb4 Bxb5 18. bxa5 $6 {Karpov was surely not very happy about the last few moves, but this simple capture will only make matters worse.} (18. d5 $5 a4 (18... Bc4 19. Qc3 f6 20. dxe6 Bxe6 21. Qa3 $11) 19. Qa3 e5 $1 $17 (19... exd5 20. Rxd5 Bc6 21. Rd2 Qe8 $11)) 18... Bc4 19. Qa3 (19. Qc3 $2 Be2 $1 $17) 19... bxa5 20. Qd6 (20. Bc3 Ra8 21. e4 Qf6 22. Nd2 Bb5 $15) (20. Ra1 Qf6 21. Nd2 (21. Qxa5 Nc5 $3 22. dxc5 (22. Ne5 Nb3 23. Qa4 Nxa1 24. Nxc4 Ra8 25. Qd1 Rfc8 26. Nb6 Rc2 $19) 22... Qxb2 23. Nd2 Rxc5 24. Qa3 Qxa3 25. Rxa3 Bd3 26. Ra1 Rc2 $17) 21... Qg6 22. Rg1 Qh5 $15) 20... Bb5 21. d5 (21. Rd2 Qf6 22. Rg1 Rfd8 $17) 21... Rc2 {[%mdl 128] Black already faced difficult choice between the two very attractive options both promising huge advantage.} (21... Nc5 $5 22. Qg3 (22. Qxd8 Rfxd8 23. dxe6 Nd3+ 24. Rxd3 Bxd3 25. exf7+ Kxf7 $19) 22... f6 23. Qg6 (23. Ba3 Nd3+ 24. Rxd3 Bxd3 25. Nd4 Qxd5 26. Bxf8 Kxf8 $19) (23. Nd4 Qxd5 24. Nxb5 Nd3+ 25. Rxd3 Qxd3 26. Nd4 Rb8 $19) 23... a4 24. Bc3 Bc4 25. Bb4 exd5 26. Bxc5 Rxc5 $19) 22. Rd2 (22. dxe6 Re2+ 23. Kf1 Rd2+ $19) (22. Ba3) 22... Qc8 23. Qa3 (23. dxe6 Rxb2 $1 24. Rxb2 (24. exd7 $2 Qc1+ 25. Rd1 Re2+ $19) 24... Qc1+ 25. Qd1 Qxb2 26. exd7 Rd8 27. Nd4 Rxd7 28. Qb3 Qc1+ 29. Qd1 Qc4 $17) 23... Rxd2 24. Kxd2 (24. Nxd2 Nc5 25. Bc3 exd5 26. Qxa5 Nd3+ 27. Kf1 Qc6 $19) 24... Nb6 $1 25. Qc3 (25. Ne5 Nc4+ 26. Nxc4 Qxc4 27. Qc3 Qxd5+ 28. Kc1 Qxg2 $19) 25... Nc4+ 26. Kc2 (26. Ke1 Nxb2 27. Qxb2 exd5 28. Nd4 Bc4 29. f3 Qb8 $19) 26... e5 27. Kb1 Qg4 $1 {Karpov's king on b1 is a great target for the black pieces, on top of it white has problems to finish his development.} 28. Rc1 (28. Rg1 Qe4+ 29. Ka1 (29. Qc2 Na3+ 30. Bxa3 Bd3 $19) 29... Rd8 30. Nd2 (30. Nxe5 Nxe5 31. Qxe5 Qa4+ 32. Kb1 Bd3+ $19) 30... Nxd2 31. Qxd2 Qa4+ 32. Kb1 Bc4 33. Qc2 Qb5 $19) (28. Nxe5 Nxe5 29. Qxe5 Bd3+ 30. Kc1 Rc8+ 31. Bc3 f6 32. Qe6+ Qxe6 33. dxe6 Rxc3+ 34. Kd2 Ra3 $19) 28... Rb8 29. Rc2 (29. Nxe5 Nxe5 30. Qxe5 Bd3+ $19) (29. Ka1 Ba6 30. Ba3 Qd7 31. Nxe5 Qa4 32. Nxc4 Rb3 $19) 29... f6 30. d6 (30. Ne1 Qd1+ 31. Ka2 Qxd5 $19) 30... Qxg2 31. Nd2 (31. Ne1 Qd5 32. Qd3 Qxd3 33. Nxd3 Nxe3 34. Rd2 Nc4 35. Rc2 Na3+ 36. Bxa3 Bxd3+ $19) 31... Qh1+ 32. Ka2 Nxd6 33. Qc5 (33. Rc1 Qd5+ 34. Ka1 Be2 $19) 33... Rc8 $1 {The fine final move completed the strategical triumph for black, white is losing material.} (33... Rc8 $1 34. Rc1 (34. Qxd6 Rxc2 35. Qb8+ Kh7 36. Qxb5 Rxd2 $19) 34... Rxc5 35. Rxh1 Rc2 $19) 0-1

