1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 Nbd7 4. Be3 e5 5. f3 c6 6. Qd2 Be7 7. O-O-O O-O 8. g4 b5 (8... Qa5 9. Kb1 Rd8 $4 10. h4 $2 (10. Nd5 $18) 10... b5 11. h5 Nf8 12. Nd5 {1-0 Petursson,P-Wittal,W/Bayern 1999/EXT 2000 (12)}) 9. Kb1 (9. g5 Nh5 10. Nce2 Nb6 11. Ng3 Nf4 12. h4 f6 13. Qh2 Be6 14. Bxf4 exf4 15. Nh5 $14 {Atlas,R-Neverovsky,G/Roslavl 1989/EXT 98 (46)}) (9. h4 Qa5 10. Kb1 b4 11. Nce2 Nb6 12. Nc1 exd4 13. Bxd4 c5 14. Bxf6 $2 (14. Nb3 Qa4 15. e5 dxe5 16. Bxc5 Bxc5 17. Nxc5 Qc6 18. Qd6 $13 {Savushkina,N-Skripova,T/St Petersburg 2000/CBM 75 ext (47)}) 14... Bxf6 15. Qxd6 Be6 16. Qf4 Bxb2 $1 $19 {Goh,W-Akopian,V/Paris 1995/EXT 99 (21)}) (9. Nce2 $6 Nb6 10. dxe5 $6 Nc4 $1 11. Qc3 Nxe3 12. Qxe3 Nxg4 $1 13. fxg4 Bg5 14. Nf4 Qb6 15. Qf3 dxe5 $15 {Meszaros,G-Shvidler,E/Kecskemet 1993/EXT 99 (60)}) 9... Nb6 10. Qe1 $1 {[%cal Gd1d8] Very strong move preventing black from playing d5.} (10. dxe5 $6 dxe5 11. Qf2 Qc7 12. g5 Nh5 13. Nce2 Be6 14. Ng3 Nf4 15. h4 Rfd8 $17 {Genocchio,D-Caposciutti,M/Montecatini Terme 1998/EXT 99 (20)}) 10... b4 11. Nce2 Nc4 12. Bc1 d5 $6 {Extremly risky continuation:black sacrifices his central pawn hoping to get an initiative instead,but with calm and accurate play white manages to deprive black attacking chanses and finally to win the game.} (12... a5 $2 13. Ng3 $18) (12... Qa5 13. g5 Nd7 14. f4 Ndb6 15. f5 $14) 13. b3 Na3+ 14. Bxa3 bxa3 15. dxe5 Nd7 16. f4 (16. exd5 cxd5 (16... Nxe5 $6 17. dxc6 Qc7 18. Nc3 $16) 17. Nd4 Qc7 18. f4 Nc5 19. h3 Ne4 20. Nge2 $16) 16... Nc5 17. Bg2 $5 (17. exd5 $5) 17... Bxg4 18. exd5 cxd5 19. Bxd5 Rc8 20. h3 $1 ({Not so clear is} 20. Bxf7+ Kxf7 21. Rxd8 Rfxd8 22. h3 Bf5 23. Nf3 Ne6 $44 {and black has good compensation.}) 20... Bf5 21. Nc3 Qa5 22. Nge2 Na6 (22... Rfd8) 23. Be4 Bxe4 24. Nxe4 Qc7 25. c4 $16 Bb4 $2 26. Qg3 $1 Qb7 27. Nf6+ Kh8 28. Rhg1 $1 $18 g6 29. Qh4 h5 30. Qg5 (30. Nxh5 Qe4+ 31. Ka1 g5 32. Qxg5 Qg6 33. Nf6 Qxg5 34. Rxg5 $18) 30... Kg7 31. Rd7 Rc7 32. Qxg6+ 1-0

