1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O Bc5 5. c3 O-O 6. d4 Bb6 7. dxe5 Nxe4 8. Qd5 Nc5 9. Re1 (9. Bg5 {is mainline}) 9... Ne7 10. Qd1 Ne6 {Black has quite a good score in this line. The main reason is that he has a very sound position with few weaknesses. He can usually counter by pushing the d- or f- in the right moment.} (10... h6 11. Bf4 Ne6 12. Bg3 Nf5 13. Na3 Nxg3 14. hxg3 Qe7 15. b4 a6 16. Bd3 Rd8 17. Nc4 Ba7 18. a4 d5 19. exd6 cxd6 20. Ne3 d5 $13 {0-1 Solak,D-Kogan,A/Sabac 1998/CBM 65 (34)}) 11. Na3 Ng6 12. Bc4 Bc5 {A preparation for c6 and d5.} 13. Nc2 c6 14. Ncd4 d5 15. Bd3 (15. exd6 Nxd4 16. Nxd4 Bxd6 17. Qh5 $14) 15... Nef4 16. Bc2 f6 17. e6 $5 {Only chance to play for an advantage, but the  is also a weakness.} (17. exf6 Qxf6 $132) 17... Re8 18. Bf5 Qd6 19. Qc2 Bxd4 {Leko goes for a draw - the trick is to exchange.} (19... Bxe6 $2 20. Bxf4 Nxf4 21. Nxe6 Nxe6 22. Bxh7+ $16 {[%cal Yf3h4,Yh4g6]}) 20. Nxd4 Bxe6 21. Nxe6 $6 (21. Bxf4 $5 {is trickier} Nxf4 22. Nxe6 Nxe6 23. Bxh7+ Kf8 24. Bg6 Re7 25. Qf5 Ng5 (25... Nf4 26. Rxe7 Kxe7 27. Re1+ Kf8 28. Bh7 $16) 26. h4 $14) 21... Nxe6 22. Bxg6 hxg6 23. Qxg6 Re7 24. Bd2 Nf8 25. Qg4 Rae8 26. Rxe7 Rxe7 27. Re1 Rxe1+ 1/2-1/2

