1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. b4 Nh5 10. Re1 f5 11. Ng5 Nf6 12. f3 Ne8 13. Kh1 {Right here this useful move is a slow one and gives black opportunity to get good counterplay.} (13. Qb3 {see Haritakis-Kotronias 1996}) (13. c5 $142 $1 {create serious problems for black ,as you can see from my comments to Khalifman-Peng Xiaomin 2001}) 13... h6 $1 14. Ne6 Bxe6 15. dxe6 Qc8 $1 16. c5 $2 (16. Nd5 Qxe6 17. Nxe7+ Qxe7 18. Qd5+ Qf7 19. Qxb7 Nf6 20. exf5 gxf5 21. Bd2 $13) 16... Qxe6 17. Be3 Rd8 18. Qa4 (18. Qb3 Qxb3 19. axb3 {[%cal Ga1a7]} a6 20. Red1 $15) 18... a6 19. b5 $44 (19. Rad1 $5) 19... axb5 20. Qxb5 c6 21. Qxb7 d5 $13 22. exd5 cxd5 23. Nb5 Kh7 24. a4 d4 25. Bxd4 $1 (25. Bd2) 25... exd4 26. Bd3 Rd7 27. Rxe6 Rxb7 28. c6 Nxc6 29. Rxc6 $14 Nf6 30. a5 Nd5 31. a6 Re7 32. a7 Nb4 33. Rc7 Rxc7 34. Nxc7 Nxd3 35. a8=Q Rxa8 36. Rxa8 Nb2 37. Ne6 d3 38. Nf8+ Bxf8 39. Rd8 Bb4 0-1

