1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Qc7 7. Nf3 Ne7 8. a4 h6 9. dxc5 $5 {This move leads to interesting complications. The alternatives are:} (9. Bb5+ Bd7 10. Bd3 Nbc6 11. O-O cxd4 (11... b6 {- 53/284, 285}) 12. cxd4 Nb4 13. Ba3 Nxd3 14. cxd3 Bc6 $13 {Sherzer,A-Yermolinsky,A/New York 58/(329) 1993}) (9. Bd3 b6 10. O-O Ba6 11. a5 O-O 12. Re1 Qc6 13. h3 Bxd3 14. cxd3 Nd7 15. dxc5 bxc5 16. Nh2 $14 {1-0 Nijboer,F-Romero Holmes,A/Wijk op (03) ;CBM 46 1995}) 9... Nd7 10. Bb5 O-O 11. Bxd7 Bxd7 12. O-O f6 13. Re1 (13. exf6 Rxf6 14. c4 dxc4 (14... Bc6 15. Bb2 Rf7 16. Ne5 Rf4 17. cxd5 Bxd5 18. c4 Bxc4 19. Nxc4 (19. Qd6 Qxd6 20. cxd6 Bxf1 21. dxe7 Be2) 19... Rxc4 20. Qe2 Rxc5 21. Qxe6+ Kh7 22. Rad1 $1 $36) (14... Raf8 15. Bb2 Rf5 16. Nd4 $14) 15. Qd6 Nd5 16. Ne5 $14) 13... Ng6 14. Qd4 Rac8 15. c4 fxe5 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. Rxe5 Qxc5 18. Qxc5 Rxc5 19. cxd5 {After} (19. Ba3 $6 Rxc4 20. Bxf8 Kxf8 {it is Black who can play for a win.}) 19... Rxd5 1/2-1/2

