1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Bb7 12. Nbd2 cxd4 13. cxd4 exd4 14. Nxd4 Re8 15. b4 Nc6 16. Nxc6 Bxc6 17. Bb2 Nd7 18. Bb3 (18. Nb3 Bf6 19. Bxf6 Qxf6 20. Nd4 Ne5 21. Nxc6 Nxc6 22. Qd2 Rac8 23. Bb3 Nd4 $10 {Popovic,P-Romanishin,O/Novy Smokovec/1992/-/27}) 18... Bf6 19. Bxf6 Nxf6 (19... Qxf6 20. Rc1 Rac8 21. Nf1 Ne5 22. Qd2 Qg6 23. Ng3 Bd7 24. Rxc8 Rxc8 25. Rd1 Rc6 $13 {[%cal Ye5c4] ½-½ Qin Kanying-Voiska,M/Jakarta 1993/EXT 97 (51)}) 20. Rc1 Rc8 21. Qf3 Bb7 22. Rxc8 $146 (22. Rcd1 Rc7 23. Re3 Rce7 24. Qg3 Bxe4 25. Nxe4 Nxe4 26. Qf4 Qc7 27. Rd4 $44 {1-0 Lukov,V-Romanishin,O/Tbilisi 1988/TD (58)}) 22... Qxc8 23. Qf4 Qc7 {White has the slightly better -formation, but Black's pressure against e4 seems to balance the play.} 24. f3 Qb6+ 25. Qe3 Qxe3+ 26. Rxe3 d5 $1 $132 27. e5 Nh5 28. Bc2 Rc8 (28... f6 $5 29. e6 Nf4 30. e7 Kf7 {looks quite interesting for Black, but so does the game continuation.}) 29. Bf5 Rc1+ 30. Kf2 g6 31. Nb3 Rc4 32. Bd3 Rxb4 33. g3 {White has lost a  but the black pieces are a bit uncoordinated.} Ng7 34. Re2 Bc8 35. Rc2 Bxh3 36. Rc6 Ra4 37. g4 h5 38. Nc5 Rxa2+ 39. Kg3 hxg4 40. fxg4 Ne6 (40... Ra3 $5 {} 41. Kxh3 Ne6) 41. Nxe6 fxe6 42. Bxg6 Kg7 43. Bh5 $1 {White is setting up an attack against the black .} Bf1 44. Rxe6 {[%csl Rg7]} b4 45. Rg6+ Kh8 46. Rb6 Bb5 47. g5 Ra1 48. g6 Rg1+ 49. Kf4 b3 50. Rb8+ Kg7 51. Rb7+ Kh8 52. Rb8+ Kg7 53. Rb7+ Kh8 54. Rb8+ 1/2-1/2

