1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 d5 6. Bd3 Be7 7. O-O Nc6 8. Re1 Bg4 9. c4 Nf6 10. Nc3 Nxd4 $5 11. cxd5 Bxf3 12. gxf3 c5 13. dxc6 {White avoids any real infighting.} Nxc6 14. Bb5 O-O 15. Qxd8 Bxd8 {Forced, but the bishop will be fine on b6.} 16. Bxc6 ({Or} 16. Be3 Bb6 $11) 16... bxc6 17. Be3 Bb6 $11 18. Rad1 (18. Rac1 Rfe8 19. Na4 Re6 {and Black defends easily.} 20. Nc5 Re5) 18... Rfd8 ({Also possible is} 18... Rfe8 19. Rd6 Rac8) 19. b4 {The most direct. White could also just be calm.} (19. Kg2) (19. a3) 19... Bxe3 20. fxe3 Kf8 21. Kf2 Ke7 22. e4 Rxd1 23. Rxd1 a5 $1 {Karpov exploits the fact that White pushed b4 to eliminate some pawns.} 24. b5 cxb5 25. Nxb5 Rc8 26. Ke3 g6 {This is just equal.} 27. Rd3 Rc2 $5 28. Ra3 Rxh2 29. Rxa5 h5 30. Ra7+ Nd7 31. Nc3 h4 32. Nd5+ Kd6 33. Ra6+ Kc5 34. Ra7 Kd6 35. Ra6+ Kc5 36. Ra7 Ne5 $5 37. Ra5+ Kd6 38. Ra6+ Kc5 39. Ra5+ Kd6 40. Ra6+ Kd7 41. Kf4 Nd3+ 42. Ke3 Ne5 43. Kf4 1/2-1/2

