1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 cxd4 7. Qg4 Ne7 8. bxa5 dxc3 9. Qxg7 Rg8 10. Qxh7 Nbc6 11. Nf3 Qc7 12. Bf4 Bd7 13. Bd3 O-O-O 14. Bg3 Qxa5 15. O-O Rh8 $1 {It is interesting why Judit decided to repeat this line - just two round ago Khalifman won nice game against Galkin - without preparing real improvement.} 16. Qg7 $146 (16. Qxf7 Rdf8 17. Qg7 Rhg8 18. Qh6 Rxf3 19. gxf3 Nd4 20. Qf4 Nef5 21. Kh1 Bb5 22. Rfd1 Bxd3 23. Rxd3 Qc5 24. Qc1 Kb8 $15 {0-1 Galkin,A-Khalifman,A/Hoogeveen Essent 2000/ (37)}) 16... d4 17. Qg4 Nf5 $1 {[%mdl 4] Black manage to keep material balance ( rare achievement in this variation! ) and I think that his position already better.} 18. Rfb1 (18. Bxf5 exf5 19. Qf4 Be6 {[%cal Ga5a4]}) 18... Nxg3 {Eliminating main defender of e5 pawn.} (18... Rdg8 19. Qf4 Nxg3 20. hxg3 $13) 19. Qxg3 {What else?} (19. hxg3 $2 Nxe5 20. Qxd4 Nxf3+ 21. gxf3 Qh5 $17 {lose almost by force}) 19... Qc7 $1 {[%cal Gc7g3]} 20. Kf1 {Trying to escape fronm the dangerous zone.} (20. Qf4 f5) 20... Rhg8 21. Qf4 (21. Qh4 Nxe5) 21... f5 $1 {[%cal Gg8g4]} ({Worth consideration and} 21... f6 $5 22. Qxf6 Rdf8 23. Qh4 Nxe5) 22. h3 Kb8 $5 {Khalifman hasn't reasons to hurry up and find  time to improve position of the king} 23. Re1 (23. Nxd4 $2 Nxd4 24. Qxd4 Bc6 $19) 23... Bc8 {[%cal Gb7b6]} 24. Ng5 Rd5 (24... Qg7 25. h4 Ne7 $5 $17 {[%cal Ge7d5,Ge7g6]}) 25. Nf3 $8 Ne7 (25... Qg7) 26. Rab1 ({Maybe} 26. Nxd4 $5 {was better, at least after posiible continuation} Ng6 27. Qe3 f4 28. Qe4 Rxe5 29. Qf3 Nh4 30. Rxe5 $8 Nxf3 31. Nxf3 $17 {White have chances for successful defence.}) 26... Ng6 27. Qh2 (27. Qg5 Rg7 $1 {[%csl Re5]}) 27... Qh7 {Black's pieses coming to the king's fland one after another.} 28. Rb4 (28. Rb5 $5 Rd7 $5 {[%cal Gd7g7]}) 28... Nh4 $19 29. Nxd4 (29. Nxh4 Qxh4 {[%csl Rf1,Rh2,Gh4] looks terrible for White}) 29... Nxg2 30. Reb1 Qd7 31. Ne2 (31. Bb5 Qd8 32. Nc6+ bxc6 33. Bxc6+ Kc7 34. Bxd5 Qxd5 $19) 31... Rxd3 $1 {Nice end of good game!} 32. cxd3 Qxd3 {[%csl Rf1,Rh2][%cal Rd3f1]} 33. Rc1 c2 {[%cal Gb7b6,Gc8a6]} 34. Rd4 $8 Qf3 35. Nf4 (35. h4 b6) 35... b6 $1 36. Nxg2 Ba6+ 37. Kg1 Bb7 0-1

