1. e4 {Lukacs} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. f4 {Lukacs: 'From time to time this aggressive plan attracts the attacking players, who want to avoid the solid positional main lines.'} (6. h4 {Lukacs is the popular main line.}) 6... e6 7. Nf3 {Lukacs: 'White has an enormous pressure on e5, but after the inevitable c6-c5 sometimes he regrets the weakening of the g1-a7 .'} Bd6 8. Be2 $146 {Lukacs: 'White wants to keep his , although the  on g6 is well-posted.'} (8. Bd3 Ne7 9. O-O Nd7 10. Kh1 (10. Ne5 {Lukacs} Qb6 $6 (10... Qc7 {is the usual plan.}) 11. Nc4 Qc7 12. Bxg6 hxg6 13. Ne4 Nc8 {Now the  is badly placed here.} 14. a4 Be7 15. b3 {in order to activate the  on the a3-f8 .} Nd6 16. Ncxd6+ Bxd6 17. Nxd6+ Qxd6 18. Ba3 Qc7 19. Qd2 $14 {and suddenly the  becomes strong, Socko-Burmakin, Pardubice op 1993.}) (10. Ne4 Bc7 {and it is not easy for White to go ahead.}) 10... Qc7 11. Ne5 Rd8 {Lukacs: 'c6-c5 will come soon.'} 12. Qe2 Bxd3 13. Nxd3 O-O 14. Bd2 c5 15. Ne4 Nf5 $11 {Marshall,F-Capablanca,J/New York 1927} (15... Nf5 16. dxc5 Nxc5 $11 {and it is time to regret f4, Marshall-Capablanca, New York 1927.})) (8. Bc4 Ne7 9. O-O Nd7 10. Ne5 Nf6 11. c3 Qc7 {Lukacs: 'It is not easy for White to continue his march ahead because Black can fully blockade the light squares.'} 12. Qe2 O-O 13. Be3 c5 {Lukacs: 'Soon or later this comes, and White's  becomes shaky.'} 14. dxc5 Bxc5 15. Bxc5 Qxc5+ 16. Kh1 Rad8 $11 {Stoltz,G-Flohr,S/Bled 1931 Lukacs: 'Stoltz-Flohr, Bled 1931'}) 8... Ne7 (8... Nd7 {Lukacs} 9. O-O Qc7 10. Ne5 Ne7 11. c3 (11. h4 $6 {is illogical, when White has already castled .} O-O-O 12. Qe1 (12. h5 $4 {is only a dream, because after} Nxe5 13. fxe5 Bxe5 $19 {White has to wake up.}) 12... f6 13. Nd3 Nf5)) 9. Ne5 $2 {Ein grober Fehler im Sinne des Spiels auf Gewinn (J.Polgar lag mit 0:1 zurück und mußte diese Partie unbedingt gewinnen, um auszugleichen). Schwarz kann nun direkt ins Endspiel übergehen, ein Partiestadium, das Judith bekannterweise nicht liegt.} (9. O-O Nd7 10. Ne5 Nf6 $11 {mit einem ausgeglichenen, aber komplizierten Spiel hätte Judit sicherlich besser geschmeckt.}) 9... Bxe5 {'=!' Lukacs.} (9... O-O {Lukacs} 10. Nxg6 hxg6 (10... Nxg6 11. O-O { f5}) 11. Ne4 {keeping the  can slightly be better for White.}) (9... Nd7 {Lukacs} 10. O-O) 10. fxe5 (10. dxe5 Qxd1+ 11. Bxd1 (11. Kxd1 {Lukacs doesn't look nice.} Na6 $1 12. Bxa6 bxa6 $11) 11... Na6 {'!' Lukacs. Lukacs: ' b4 × c2'} 12. Bd2 O-O-O $11) 10... c5 $1 11. dxc5 (11. c3 $2 cxd4 12. cxd4 Nbc6 {'' Lukacs. Lukacs: 'leaves White with a perfectly blockaded isolated .'} 13. Be3 Nd5 $17) 11... Qxd1+ ({Eine gute Alternative bestand in} 11... Qa5+ 12. c3 Qxc5 13. Qd6 Nd7 $11 ({aber nicht} 13... Qxd6 $2 14. exd6 Nc8 15. Bf4 $16 {0-0-0})) 12. Bxd1 (12. Kxd1 {Lukacs is again not impressive because of} Nd7) 12... Na6 (12... Nd7 $2 {Lukacs allows} 13. b4 $1 Nxe5 14. Bb2 {and White's   majority and his  in the opened position secure her the better chances.}) 13. O-O (13. Be3 Nb4 (13... Nd5 {Lukacs} 14. Bd4 Ndb4 15. Rc1 O-O-O $44) 14. O-O (14. Kd2 $2 Rd8+ 15. Kc1 Rxd1+ $1 16. Rxd1 Nxc2 $15) 14... Nxc2 15. Bxc2 Bxc2 $11) 13... Nxc5 14. Bf3 Nc6 $1 {×e5 Lukacs: ' d4' Khalifmans Strategie ist leicht zu verstehen, er reduziert konsequent den Figurenbestand und läßt keine Komplikationen zu.} ({Dagegen käme} 14... Bxc2 $6 {Weiß sehr gelegen:} 15. Be3 Nd3 (15... Rc8 16. Bxc5 $1 Rxc5 17. Rac1 b6 (17... O-O 18. Ne4 Rc7 19. Nd6 $16) 18. b4 Rc4 19. Be2 $16) 16. Bxb7 Rb8 17. Be4 Rxb2 18. Bxa7 $14 {,}) 15. Bxc6+ {Lukacs: 'The dangerous  has to be eliminated.'} (15. Bf4 Nd4 $11) (15. Re1 {Lukacs is also answered by} Nd4 16. Be3 Nxf3+ 17. gxf3 Rc8 $11) 15... bxc6 16. b3 {'!' Lukacs. Lukacs: 'in order to activate the  on the a3-f8 .'} (16. b4 {Lukacs} Ne4 $11) (16. Rf2 {Lukacs is simply met by} O-O $142 {and Black has excellent drawing chances because of the .} (16... h5 $5 {provokes} 17. h4 O-O-O 18. Be3 Nd7 19. Bxa7 Nxe5 $13 (19... c5 20. b4 cxb4 21. Bd4 {is less clear.}))) 16... Nd7 $1 (16... Bxc2 $2 17. Ba3 (17. Nh5 $1 {Lukacs} g6 (17... O-O $2 {loses to the pin after} 18. Ba3) (17... Bg6 18. Nxg7+ Kf8 19. Bh6 {is not recommended either.}) 18. Nf6+ Kd8 19. Bh6 $1 $18 {with too many threats.}) 17... Nd3 18. Ne4 $36) (16... h5 $5 {Lukacs is interesting to chase the , although on g3 it isn't very impressive either.} 17. Ba3 (17. h4 $2 {is already met by} Bxc2 {because h5 is not possible.}) 17... Nd7 18. c4 (18. Bd6 h4 $1) 18... h4) 17. c4 a5 $1 (17... Nxe5 $2 18. Bb2 f6 (18... Ng4 {Lukacs} 19. Bxg7 Rg8 20. Bd4 e5 21. Bc5 {and Black's pawns are in four islands.}) 19. Bxe5 fxe5 20. Rae1 {'' Lukacs. Lukacs: 'with too many  islands for Black.'} Ke7 21. Rxe5 Rhf8 22. Rxf8 Rxf8 23. Ra5 $16) 18. Ba3 (18. Bb2 a4 (18... Ke7 19. Rfd1 Rhb8 20. Rd6 c5 21. Rad1 Rb7 $11 {a4}) 19. b4 a3 20. Bc3 Nb6 21. Rf4 Rd8 $11) (18. Re1 {Lukacs} a4 19. Ba3 {deserved attention.}) 18... Nxe5 {Führt zu weiteren Vereinfachungen und einer remislichen Stellung. '!' Lukacs.} (18... c5 $5 19. Rfd1 a4 $11) 19. Bb2 f6 20. Bxe5 fxe5 21. Rae1 {Lukacs: 'Now Black has got an important a5 tempo to get rid of his weak pawns.'} ({Die Stellung nach} 21. Rfe1 O-O 22. Rxe5 a4 23. b4 a3 24. Rxe6 Rfb8 $1 25. Rxc6 Rxb4 $11 {b1,×a2 war für Weiß trotz des Mehrbauerns wenig erstrebenswert.}) 21... Rf8 22. Rxe5 Rxf1+ 23. Nxf1 Ke7 $11 24. Nd2 a4 {Lukacs: 'This is the point, now White has also weaknesses in his plans.' Schwarz wird damit seine letzte Bauernschwäche los. Der Rest ist leicht zu verstehen.} 25. Kf2 axb3 26. axb3 Kd6 27. Rg5 (27. Nf3 {Lukacs} c5 $1 $11 {blockading the  on the colour of the .} (27... Ra3 28. c5+ Kd7 29. Re3 $14 {and the black pawns are on the colour of the .}) (27... Ra2+ 28. Kg3 (28. Re2 $2 {is out of question because of} Rxe2+ 29. Kxe2 Kc5 $1) 28... Rb2 29. c5+ Kd7 30. Re3 $14 {with a good  versus bad  .})) 27... c5 28. Ke3 Rb8 29. h4 Rb7 30. Ne4+ (30. h5 {Lukacs} Bc2) 30... Bxe4 {Lukacs: 'The   cannot pose any serious problems for Black to reach the highly desired draw.'} 31. Kxe4 Rxb3 32. Rxg7 h6 (32... Rc3 {Lukacs} 33. Rxh7 Rxc4+ 34. Ke3 Rc3+ $11 (34... Rg4 35. Kf3)) 33. Rg6 Rc3 34. Rxh6 Rg3 (34... Rxc4+ {Lukacs}) 35. h5 Rxg2 36. Rh8 Rg4+ 37. Kd3 Rd4+ 38. Kc3 Rh4 39. h6 Rh3+ 40. Kc2 Ke5 {'!' Lukacs.} 41. h7 Ke4 42. Kd2 1/2-1/2

