{A one possibility vs 0-0-0.} 1. e4 {Anand,Viswanathan Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand Anand Anand Boensch'} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bc4 Qb6 7. Nb3 e6 8. Be3 Qc7 9. Qe2 {Anand,Viswanathan: 'Judit played 9.f4 against Damljanovic in an earlier round' Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand: 'Judit played 9.f4 against Damljanovic in an earlier round'' Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand: 'In einer früheren Runde spielte Judit gegen Damljanovic 9.f4.''} a6 10. Bd3 b5 11. g4 {Anand,Viswanathan: '!?'} h6 12. f4 Be7 13. O-O-O Nb4 14. Kb1 (14. h4 {(Anand,Viswanathan) Boensch} Nxd3+ 15. Rxd3 Bb7 $13) 14... Rb8 15. Rc1 (15. h4 {(Anand,Viswanathan) Boensch} h5 $1) 15... Nd7 16. a3 Nc6 (16... Nxd3 $2 {Anand,Viswanathan} 17. cxd3 Qd8 18. Na2 $16) 17. Na2 {Anand,Viswanathan: 'Otherwise b4 would be very strong' Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand: 'Otherwise b4 would be very strong'' Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand: 'Sonst würde ...b4 zu stark.''} (17. Rhe1 {(Anand,Viswanathan) Boensch} b4 18. Nd5 exd5 19. exd5 Nce5 20. fxe5 Nxe5 21. Bd4 $13) 17... g5 {Anand,Viswanathan: '!'} 18. h4 gxf4 19. Bxf4 Nde5 20. Rcg1 {Anand,Viswanathan: '?!'} (20. Bd2 $1 {(Anand,Viswanathan) Stopping b4 and intending 21.g5 h5 22.hf1 with counterplay Anand: '!?' '!?' '!?' Anand: 'Boensch' Anand,Viswanathan: '!?' Anand: 'Stopping b4 and intending 21.g5 h5 22.hf1 with counterplay' Anand: 'Der Vorstoß ...b4 wird gestoppt und Weiß beabsichtigt 21.g5 h5 22.hf1 mit Gegenspiel.'}) 20... Nxd3 21. Qxd3 (21. cxd3 {Anand,Viswanathan} b4 $1 22. a4 e5 23. Be3 Be6 $17) 21... b4 {Anand,Viswanathan: '!'} 22. axb4 Nxb4 23. Qc3 (23. Nxb4 {Anand,Viswanathan} Rxb4 $17 (23... Rxb4 {Boensch} 24. Rd1 Bb7 25. Bxd6 Qxd6 26. Qxd6 Bxd6 27. Rxd6 Bxe4 28. Rh3 $15)) 23... Qxc3 24. Nxc3 e5 25. Bd2 Be6 26. Nc1 Kd7 {Anand,Viswanathan: '' Anand,Viswanathan: 'White's weaknesses on the kingside and his two bishops give Black a clear edge' Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand: 'White's weaknesses on the kingside and his two bishops give Black a clear edge'' Anand,Viswanathan: 'Anand: 'Das Läuferpaar sowie die weißen Schwächen am Königsflügel räumen Schwarz einen klaren Vorteil ein.''} 27. b3 a5 28. N1a2 {Anand,Viswanathan: '?!'} a4 {Anand,Viswanathan: '!'} 29. Nxa4 Nxc2 30. Kxc2 Bxb3+ 31. Kd3 Bxa2 32. Nc3 Be6 {Anand,Viswanathan: '-+'} 33. g5 hxg5 34. hxg5 Rxh1 35. Rxh1 Rg8 36. Rg1 Kc6 37. Be3 Bd8 38. Ra1 Bc8 39. Nd5 Bb7 40. Nb4+ Kd7 41. Nd5 Ke6 42. Kc4 Bxg5 43. Ra7 Bxd5+ 44. exd5+ Kf6 45. Bb6 (45. Bxg5+ {Anand,Viswanathan} Kxg5 46. Rxf7 Rc8+ 47. Kd3 Rc5 48. Ke4 Rc4+ 49. Ke3 Rd4) 45... Rc8+ 46. Kd3 Rb8 47. Ra6 Kf5 48. Bc7 e4+ 49. Kc4 Rc8 50. Rc6 Bf4 51. Kd4 Re8 0-1

