d.} (20. Nc3 $5 c6 21. Ne4 $14) 20... Bxe6 $2 {Karjaking is a brilliant talent from the Ukraine, but currently playing for Russia. The change of the federation did not come cheap - the conditions for him had an implicit guarantee of the Russian government. The goal is to groom a player with the potential to win the world championship title. In World Cup he had the bad luck of meeting Judit Polgar who was coming back after longish maternity leave at the height of her powers. The strongest woman player in history is not afraid of any opponent. The Russian hope missed the chance to apply an unusual solution. After the less appealing recapture with a pawn chances would have remained balanced. Karjaking is a brilliant talent from the Ukraine, but currently playing for Russia. The change of the federation did not come cheap - the conditions for him had an implicit guarantee of the Russian government. The goal is to groom a player with the potential to win the world championship title. In World Cup he had the bad luck of meeting Judit Polgar who was coming back after longish maternity leave at the height of her powers. The strongest woman player in history is not afraid of any opponent. The Russian hope missed the chance to apply an unusual solution. After the less appealing recapture with a pawn chances would have remained balanced.} (20... fxe6 21. Bxc7 Bb7 22. Nfg5 Rh6 (22... Nd4 23. Bb8 Rf8 $13) 23. Bb8 Rg6 24. f4 a6 $11) 21. Bxc7 f6 (21... Bc8 22. Nc3 Bb7 23. Nd5 Rh5 24. Bb8 Nd4 25. Nxd4 Bxd5 26. Nb5 Bb7 27. Bxa7 Rg5 28. Nc7+ Kf8 29. Nd5 $16) 22. Bb8 a6 (22... Bd8 23. Bxa7 Bc7 24. Nc3 Kf7 25. Nb5 Ra8 26. Nxc7 Rxa7 27. Nxe6 Kxe6 28. a4 $16) 23. Ba7 Bd8 (23... b5 24. cxb5 axb5 25. Bxc5 $16) 24. Nc3 Kf7 (24... Bc7 25. Na4 b5 26. Nxc5 Bc8 27. Rc1 $16) 25. Na4 $1 {Bologan,Viktor: '' '' The position has significantly moved towards understandable problems without original features. Black is losing a pawn and has to look for the most promising form of resistance. The position has significantly moved towards understandable problems without original features. Black is losing a pawn and has to look for the most promising form of resistance.} b5 26. Nxc5 Bc8 (26... bxc4 27. Nxe6 Kxe6 28. bxc4 Be7 29. Kf1 $16) 27. cxb5 axb5 28. a4 $5 (28. Ne4 Be7 29. Nc3 $14) 28... bxa4 (28... b4 29. Nd2 Be7 30. Nc4 Bxc5 31. Bxc5 Be6 32. Na5 Kg6 33. Rd3 Rb8 34. g4 hxg3 35. fxg3 $18) 29. bxa4 Re8 {Knowledge of the course of the game enables us to guess, that somewhat better chances for a real fight were offered by the idea of opening the d-file for counterplay. Knowledge of the course of the game enables us to guess, that somewhat better chances for a real fight were offered by the idea of opening the d-file for counterplay.} (29... Bc7 $5 30. Rb1 Rd8 31. Bb6 Rd5 32. Bxc7 Rxc5 33. Bb6 Rc2 34. Rb4 g5 35. a5 Bb7 36. Nd4 $16) 30. Rb1 $1 g5 (30... Bc7 31. Bb8 Bd8 32. Rb5 Be7 33. Bc7 $16) 31. Bb6 Be7 (31... Bxb6 32. Rxb6 Re2 33. a5 Ra2 34. Ne4 $18) 32. a5 Bxc5 {When the position is sliding the defender should try keep das far away from the abyss as possible. Defence with both bishops would have enabled Polgar to dream about the ideal location for the knight on the c7-square. When the position is sliding the defender should try keep das far away from the abyss as possible. Defence with both bishops would have enabled Polgar to dream about the ideal location for the knight on the c7-square.} (32... Nd6 33. Nd2 Nb7 34. Na6 Bf5 35. Ra1 Rc8 36. Nc7 Bc5 37. Bxc5 Nxc5 38. a6 Rxc7 39. a7 Rxa7 40. Rxa7+ $18) 33. Bxc5 Re6 34. Rb6 (34. Rb8 Ba6 35. Bb4 Rc6 $16) 34... Ng7 {The blockade on the light square is seriously complicating the advance of the a-pawn, but Polgar will easily refocus on the pawn weaknesses of the kingside. The blockade on the light square is seriously complicating the advance of the a-pawn, but Polgar will easily refocus on the pawn weaknesses of the kingside.} (34... Rxb6 35. Bxb6 Ke6 36. Nd2 Nd6 37. f3 Ba6 38. Bd4 f5 39. Nb3 $16) 35. Be3 (35. Nd4 Rxb6 36. axb6 Ne6 37. Nb3 Ke8 38. Bb4 f5 39. Na5 Nd8 40. f3 Kd7 41. Bd2 f4 42. Bc3 $18) 35... Nf5 (35... Rxb6 36. axb6 Nf5 37. Bc5 Ke6 38. Nd2 Kd5 39. Ba3 $16) 36. Rb8 Re8 (36... Nxe3 37. Rxc8 Nd5 38. Rc5 $18) 37. Ra8 Bb7 {The choice of the endgame, in which the defender could stand a chance to save the difficult position is a very complicated task. The battle of the bishop against the knight in the event of an exchange on e3 would not have been pretty for Black. The choice of the endgame, in which the defender could stand a chance to save the difficult position is a very complicated task. The battle of the bishop against the knight in the event of an exchange on e3 would not have been pretty for Black.} (37... Nxe3 38. fxe3 Bf5 39. Rxe8 Kxe8 40. Nd2 Kd7 41. e4 Be6 42. e5 fxe5 43. Ne4 Kc6 44. Nxg5 Bd5 45. Nf3 $18) 38. Ra7 Re7 39. Bc5 Rd7 40. a6 Bc6 41. Rxd7+ Bxd7 42. Nd2 (42. Nd4 Nxd4 43. Bxd4 Ke6 44. a7 Bc6 45. f3 f5 46. Kf2 $16) 42... Ke6 43. Nc4 Bc6 {The last moment when the final part of the game might have developed differently. Unfortunately also the fight of the black knight against the bishop would have been hopelessly lost. The last moment when the final part of the game might have developed differently. Unfortunately also the fight of the black knight against the bishop would have been hopelessly lost.} (43... Kd5 44. Na5 $1 Bc6 45. Nxc6 Kxc6 46. Kf1 Ng7 47. Be7 Nh5 (47... Ne8 48. Bd8 $18) 48. Ke2 $18) 44. Nb6 Nd6 (44... Ng7 45. a7 Kf5 46. a8=Q Bxa8 47. Nxa8 Ne6 48. Bd6 $18) 45. Bxd6 Kxd6 46. a7 Kc7 47. a8=Q Bxa8 48. Nxa8+ Kb7 49. f4 $1 {Bologan,Viktor: '1-0 (49) Polgar,J (2699)-Karjakin,S (2788) Khanty-Mansiysk 2011 CBM 145 [Ftacnik]' The charming finish is reminiscent of the sharp intake of breath you experience at the moment, when everything is beautiful around you. White will win the pawn endgame without any effort, since the black king has to go to the far away a8-square. The charming finish is reminiscent of the sharp intake of breath you experience at the moment, when everything is beautiful around you. White will win the pawn endgame without any effort, since the black king has to go to the far away a8-square.} (49. f4 $1 Kxa8 (49... gxf4 50. Kf2 Kxa8 51. Kf3 Kb7 52. Kxf4 Kc6 53. Kf5 $18) 50. fxg5 fxg5 51. Kf2 Kb7 52. Kf3 Kc6 53. Kg4 $18) 1-0

[Event "WchT 8th"]
[Site "Ningbo"]
[Date "2011.07.23"]
