1. e4 {Polgar,Judit Postny,E Postny} e5 2. Bc4 {Judith Polgar avoids the Petroff Defence as she needed to win this game to level the score.} Nf6 3. d3 c6 4. Qe2 {This move is directed to prevent the advance d7-d5.} ({In case of} 4. Nf3 {Black can play} d5 $11) 4... Be7 ({Actually} 4... d5 $5 {is possible at this point too, but Black has to be ready to sacrifice a pawn for an initiative. For instanse:} 5. exd5 cxd5 6. Qxe5+ (6. Bb5+ Nc6 7. Nf3 Bd6 8. Nxe5 O-O 9. Nxc6 bxc6 10. Bxc6 Bg4 11. f3 Rc8 12. fxg4 Rxc6 13. O-O Qc7 $44 {[%csl Rc2,Rh2]}) 6... Be7 7. Bb5+ Nc6 8. Bxc6+ bxc6 9. Nf3 O-O 10. O-O Bd6 $44) 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Bb3 d6 (6... d5 {Polgar,Judit: '!?'} 7. O-O Bg4 8. h3 Bxf3 9. Qxf3 Na6 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Re1 Bf6 12. Nd2 Nc5 13. Ne4 Nxb3 14. axb3 Be7 15. Ng3 $14 {0-1 Rathore,S (2372)-Sasikiran,K (2525)/Nagpur 1999/CBM 069 ext (40)}) 7. O-O Nbd7 8. c3 a5 {Polgar,Judit: '!?'} (8... Nc5 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 9. a4 b5 {Polgar,Judit: 'N' Boris is going for an immediate queenside expansion.} (9... Nc5 {Polgar,Judit: '!?'} 10. Bc2 Ne6 {was another logical option.} (10... b6 {Polgar,Judit} 11. Nbd2 Ba6)) (9... Qc7 {Polgar,Judit}) 10. Bc2 Ba6 (10... Nc5 $6 {Polgar,Judit} 11. axb5 cxb5 12. d4) 11. axb5 (11. Nbd2 {Polgar,Judit} b4 $5) 11... cxb5 (11... Bxb5 $6 {Polgar,Judit} 12. c4 Ba6 13. Bd2 $1) 12. Nbd2 Qc7 (12... Qb6 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 13. d4 a4 {Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (13... b4 $6 14. c4 $14 {The a5 might become a weakness.} Nb6 $1 {Polgar,Judit} 15. Rxa5 (15. dxe5 dxe5 16. Rxa5 Nbd7 (16... Nxc4 17. Rxa6 Nxd2 18. Rxa8 Nxf3+ 19. Qxf3 Rxa8 20. Bb3 Ra1) 17. Ra4 (17. Ra1 $2 Bxc4) 17... Rfb8 $1 (17... Nc5 18. Rxb4 Qa5 19. Rb5 Bxb5 20. cxb5 $44) 18. Qd1 Nc5 19. Ra1 b3 20. Bb1 Nfd7 $17) (15. Bd3 a4 $1) (15. b3 a4) 15... Nxc4 16. Rxa6 Nxd2 17. Rxa8 Nxf3+ 18. Qxf3 Rxa8 19. Bb3) 14. Bd3 Rfb8 15. Nh4 g6 16. f4 {The situation in the match urges Judith to play aggressively without really concerning about the risk.} (16. Ndf3 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 16... exf4 (16... exd4 $5 {Polgar,Judit} 17. cxd4 Qb6 $13) 17. Ndf3 (17. Qf3 $2 {Polgar,Judit} b4) (17. Rxf4 {Polgar,Judit} Nh5 18. Rg4 Ndf6) (17. Nb1 {Polgar,Judit} Nh5 18. Nf5 Bf8) 17... Nh5 18. Bd2 (18. g4 $2 {Polgar,Judit} fxg3 19. Ng5 Ndf6) 18... Nb6 (18... Qb6 $5 {Polgar,Judit} 19. g4 fxg3 20. Ng5 b4 21. Nf5 (21. Rxf7 Bxd3 22. Qxd3 Ne5 $19) (21. Bxa6 Qxa6 22. Qf3 Qc4 23. Nxf7 Bxh4 24. Nh6+ Kh8) 21... Bxg5 22. Bxg5 gxf5 23. Bxa6 (23. Qxh5 bxc3 24. bxc3 Bxd3 25. Rxf5 Ne5) 23... Rxa6 24. Qxh5 bxc3 25. bxc3 Qb2 $1) 19. g4 $1 {The only way to continue the initiative.} fxg3 20. Ng5 Nc4 $2 {Polgar,Judit: '?' Boris Gelfand played superbly in Khanty-Mansiysk, but in the current game he lost control over the position.} (20... gxh2+ 21. Qxh2 Bxg5 22. Bxg5 b4 {Black must exchange as many pieces as possible to reduce white's attacking potential.} 23. Bxa6 Rxa6 24. Nf5 f6 25. Nh6+ Kg7 {and Black defends successfully.}) (20... d5 {Polgar,Judit} 21. e5 (21. Rxf7 $2 gxh2+) (21. Nf5 Bxg5 22. Bxg5 gxh2+ 23. Kg2 f6 24. Nh6+ Kg7 25. Bxf6+ Nxf6 26. e5 (26. Rxf6 Kxf6 27. Rf1+ Kg7 28. Rf7+ Qxf7 29. Nxf7 Kxf7)) 21... Bxg5 22. Bxg5 Bc8 $1 (22... gxh2+ 23. Qxh2) 23. Rf6 (23. Qf3 Be6 (23... Bh3 24. hxg3 Bxf1 25. Rxf1 Ng7) 24. hxg3 a3 25. g4 Ng7 26. Bh6 (26. Nf5 Bxf5 27. gxf5 axb2) 26... Qe7) (23. Bxb5 Nc4 24. Bxc4 Qxc4) (23. Nf5 Bxf5 24. Rxf5 a3) 23... Nxf6 24. Bxf6 Nd7 (24... a3 25. Qd2 $18)) (20... Bxg5 {Polgar,Judit} 21. Bxg5 Bc8 $5 (21... Nc4 22. Nf5 {Ü 20...Nc4}) (21... f6 22. Bxf6 Rf8 23. Bg5 (23. e5 Rae8 24. Bxg6 hxg6 25. Nxg6 Nxf6 26. Nxf8 Qg7 $19) 23... Nc4 24. Bh6 gxh2+ 25. Qxh2 $13) (21... d5 $5) 22. Nf5 Bxf5 23. Rxf5 a3 24. Rxb5 axb2 25. Rxa8 Rxa8 26. Rxb2 Ra3 $17) 21. Nf5 $2 {This is tempting, but the simple 21.xf7 could yield White already a crushing attack.} (21. Rxf7 {Polgar,Judit: '!'} gxh2+ (21... Rf8 22. Rxh7 $18 Nxd2 {Polgar,Judit} (22... Rf2 {Polgar,Judit} 23. Nxg6 Rxe2 24. Bxe2) (22... gxh2+ {Polgar,Judit} 23. Kxh2 Nxd2 24. Rxh5 gxh5 25. Rg1) 23. Nxg6 Bxg5 (23... Nf3+ 24. Kh1) 24. Rxc7 Rf2 25. Qxh5 Nf3+ 26. Qxf3 Rxf3 27. Bb1 $3 $18) (21... Nxd2 {Polgar,Judit} 22. Nf5 $1 $18) (21... Qd8 {Polgar,Judit} 22. Rxh7 Bxg5 (22... gxh2+ 23. Kxh2 Bxg5 (23... Nf6 24. Bxc4+ bxc4 25. Rh6 $18) 24. Nxg6 $18) (22... Nxd2 23. Nxg6 Bxg5 24. Rh8+ Kg7 25. Rxd8 Bxd8 26. Qxh5 $18) 23. Nxg6 Qf6 (23... Kxh7 24. Qxh5+ Kg7 25. Bxg5) 24. Ne7+ $1 Kf8 (24... Kxh7 25. e5+) 25. Bxg5 Qxg5 26. Rf1+ Ke8 27. Nd5 gxh2+ 28. Kxh2 Qg3+ 29. Kh1 Qh3+ 30. Kg1 $18) 22. Kxh2 $3 {This recapture is amazing for a human, but in such a sharp position an engine knows better...} (22. Qxh2 $2 Nxd2 23. Rxh7 (23. Nf5 $4 Bxg5 24. Rxc7 Nf3+ $19 {reveals the drawback of 22.xh2 compared to the correct 22.xh2.}) 23... b4 24. Bxa6 Qa5 25. Rxh5 gxh5 26. Nf5 Bxg5 27. Qxh5 Qd8 28. Qg6+ Kf8 29. Qg7+ Ke8 30. Qg6+ Kf8 $11) 22... Nxd2 23. Nf5 $1 $18) 21... Bxg5 {Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (21... Nxd2 $1 {Polgar,Judit} 22. Nh6+ (22. Qxd2 gxf5) (22. Nxf7 gxh2+ 23. Qxh2 Kxf7) 22... Kh8 $1 (22... Kg7 23. Rxf7+ Kxh6 24. h4 Nf3+ 25. Nxf3) 23. Nhxf7+ (23. Rxf7 Bxg5 24. Rxc7 Bxh6 25. hxg3 (25. Qg4 Bc8) 25... Nxg3 (25... Rf8 26. Kg2 Rf3 27. Qxf3 Nxf3 28. Kxf3 Rb8 $1 29. b3 $140 Rf8+ 30. Kg2 Bc8 31. bxa4 bxa4 32. Rxa4 Be3 33. Ra2 Bg4) 26. Qg4 Nh5 27. Qd7 Nf6 28. Qc6 $13) 23... Kg8 24. Qxd2 Bxg5 25. Qxg5 (25. Nxg5 Qd7 $13) 25... gxh2+ 26. Kxh2 Rf8 27. Nh6+ Kh8 (27... Kg7 28. Nf5+ Kh8 29. Ne7 Nf4 $1 30. Rxf4 Rxf4 31. Nxg6+ hxg6 32. Qxf4 Kg7 33. Rf1 Qe7) 28. Be2 Qb7 29. Bxh5 b4 $3 30. Rxf8+ Rxf8 31. Qe3 gxh5 32. d5 Qg7 33. Rxa4 Qe5+ 34. Kg1) 22. Bxg5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 20...Nc4'} f6 (22... gxf5 $2 23. Qxh5 $18 {[%cal Gg5f6]} Nxb2 {Polgar,Judit} 24. Qh6 f6 25. Bxf6 Bc8 26. Rf3 $18) (22... gxh2+ {Polgar,Judit} 23. Kxh2 (23. Qxh2 $5)) (22... Kh8 {Polgar,Judit} 23. Nh6 f6 24. Rxf6) 23. Bh4 (23. Nh6+ {Polgar,Judit} Kg7) 23... gxh2+ (23... Rf8 {Polgar,Judit} 24. hxg3) (23... a3 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 24. Qxh2 Rf8 (24... gxf5 {Polgar,Judit: '!'} 25. Rxf5 (25. Kh1 {Polgar,Judit} fxe4 26. Be2 Ng7) 25... Ng7 (25... Qf7 {Polgar,Judit} 26. Kh1) 26. Rf3 $1 (26. Rxf6 {Polgar,Judit} Rf8 27. Rh6 Qd7 28. Qg2 Ne3 29. e5 $1 Nxg2 30. Bxh7+ Kf7 31. Bg6+ Ke6 32. Be4+ Kf7 33. Bg6+ $11) 26... Qf7 (26... f5 27. exf5 Bb7 28. Rg3 $40) 27. Bxf6 Nh5 28. e5 Nxf6 29. Rxf6 Qe7 30. Kf2 Nxb2 31. Qg2+ Kh8 32. Bxh7 Qxh7 33. Rh1 Ra7 34. Rxh7+ Rxh7 35. Qf3 Rg8 36. Rf8 $18) 25. Be2 (25. Bxc4+ {Polgar,Judit} bxc4 26. Qxd6) 25... gxf5 {Polgar,Judit: '?'} (25... Nd2 {Polgar,Judit: '!'} 26. Bxh5 Nxf1 27. Qg2 (27. Rxf1 {Polgar,Judit} b4 $1 28. Nh6+ Kg7 29. Rf2 bxc3 30. bxc3 Qxc3 $13) 27... Kh8 28. Bxg6 b4 (28... Ne3 {Polgar,Judit} 29. Nxe3 hxg6 30. Qxg6 Qg7 31. Qxg7+ Kxg7 32. Nf5+ Kh7 33. Nxd6 $44) 29. Rxa4 hxg6 30. Qxg6 Qf7 31. Bxf6+ Qxf6 32. Qh5+ Kg8 33. Nh6+ Kg7 34. Nf5+ Kg8 $11) 26. Bxh5 fxe4 $2 {Too greedy. Boris had to bring his queenside pieces into action as soon as possible.} (26... Qg7+ 27. Kh1 Bb7 28. Qf4 (28. d5 Qe7 {Polgar,Judit: '!'} 29. Rae1 fxe4 30. Qg2+ Kh8 31. Rxe4 Qd7 (31... Ne5 {Polgar,Judit} 32. Ref4 $40) 32. Re2 Ne5 $1 33. Bxf6+ Rxf6 34. Rxf6 Rg8 {with fine compensation for an exchange.}) 28... Kh8 29. Kh2 Bxe4 30. Rg1 Qe7 31. Qh6 a3 $1 32. bxa3 Nb6 33. Bg6 Nd5 34. Rae1 Rxa3 35. Bxh7 Ra2+ 36. Kh3 Nf4+ 37. Kg3 $1 Nh5+ $1 38. Kh3 $11 {Another spectacular line by an engine!} (38. Qxh5 $2 Qxh7 39. Qxh7+ Kxh7 $19)) 27. Qf4 $1 {Polgar,Judit: '!!'} (27. Bxf6 {would allow Black to sacrifice an exchange:} Rxf6 28. Rxf6 Qg7+ 29. Qg2 Qxg2+ 30. Kxg2 Nxb2 $13) 27... f5 (27... e3 28. Kh2 $40 {[%cal Gf1g1]}) (27... Qg7+ 28. Kh2 Kh8 29. Rg1 Qe7 30. Qh6 $40 {[%csl Rf6][%cal Ga1f1]} (30. Raf1 {Polgar,Judit})) 28. Kh1 Kh8 29. Rg1 {Most of black's pieces got stuck on the queenside and can't help his king.} Rf7 (29... Nb6 30. Qh6 Nd5 31. Rg2 Rg8 (31... f4 {Polgar,Judit} 32. Rag1 Qd7 33. Bg4 Qg7 34. Qxg7+ Kxg7 35. Be6+ Kh8 36. Bxd5) 32. Bf6+ Nxf6 33. Qxf6+ Rg7 34. Rag1 Rag8 35. Rxg7 Rxg7 36. Qf8+ $18) 30. Bxf7 Qxf7 31. Qh6 Rf8 32. Rg6 $1 {[%csl Rf6] There is no defense against 33.f6+ or 33.f6.} 1-0

