1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 f5 {Tony Kosten: 'Radjabov continues to show faith in this sharp variation.'} 4. Nc3 fxe4 5. Nxe4 Nf6 6. Qe2 d5 7. Nxf6+ gxf6 8. d4 Bg7 9. dxe5 O-O 10. e6 {Tony Kosten: 'White refuses to concede the bishop pair.'} (10. Bxc6 {is examined in Shirov, A-Radjabov, T, see the Archive.}) 10... Ne5 {Tony Kosten: 'Black attempts to exploit White's move order.'} (10... Re8 11. O-O Bxe6 (11... Rxe6 12. Be3 Ne5 13. Rad1 c6 {is also possible, Adams, M (2615)-Van Hul, C/Ostend 1991}) 12. Qd3 Qd6 13. Be3 a6 14. Bxc6 Qxc6 15. Nd4 Qd7 16. Nxe6 Qxe6 17. Rad1 Rad8 {White has a plus because of his superior structure, Timman, J (2630)-Kortschnoj, V  (2610)/ Brussels 1991/Candidates.}) 11. O-O (11. Bf4 c6 12. Bd3 Nxd3+ 13. Qxd3 Bxe6 14. Nd4 Re8 15. O-O-O {should also be a bit better for White, Psakhis, L-Grosar/ Portoroz-Ljubljana/1987, as} Bf7 16. h4 Bh5 17. f3 {and Nf5.}) 11... Bxe6 {Tony Kosten: '!?' Tony Kosten: 'Unusual, Black leaves the bishop on b5, hoping that it will become a target,'} (11... c6 {Tony Kosten: 'is the mainline,'} 12. Bd3 (12. Ba4 Bxe6 13. Nd4 Bd7 14. f4 Qb6 15. c3 Bg4 16. Qc2 Nc4 17. f5 Rfe8 $132 {0-1 Popovic,P (2540)-Kurajica,B (2535)/Sarajevo 1985/MCD (37)}) 12... Bxe6 (12... Re8 $2 13. Nxe5 fxe5 14. Bxh7+ (14. Qh5 $1 e4 15. Bg5 Re7 16. Bxe4 dxe4 17. Qf7+ Rxf7 18. exf7+ Kxf7 19. Bxd8 $18) 14... Kxh7 15. Qh5+ Kg8 16. Qf7+ Kh7 17. Qh5+ Kg8 18. Bg5 Re7 19. Qh4 Kf8 $2 (19... Bf8 20. Rae1 Qd6 21. Bxe7 Qxe7 22. Qg3+ Qg7 23. Qxe5 Qxe5 24. Rxe5 Bg7 $16) 20. f4 Bxe6 21. f5 Bg8 22. Bxe7+ Qxe7 23. f6 $18 {1-0 Speckner,R (2290)-Bredl,H (2275)/Bayern 1995/EXT 1999 (34)}) (12... Nxd3 $2 13. e7 {loses an exchange.}) 13. Nd4 Bg4 (13... Bd7 14. Bf5 Re8 15. f4 $2 (15. Qh5 Bxf5 16. Nxf5 $14) 15... Qb6 $132 {½-½ Mantovani,R (2370)-Godena,M (2425)/Chianciano 1989/EXT 2000 (18)}) 14. f3 Nxd3 {Tony Kosten: '!?' Tony Kosten: 'is interesting, as after'} (14... Bd7 15. Bf5 (15. Nf5 {Tony Kosten: '?!'} Nxd3 16. Qxd3 Qb6+ 17. Kh1 Bxf5 18. Qxf5 Rae8 $15 {0-1 Renet,O (2515)-Tseitlin,M (2445)/Palma de Mallorca 1989/TD (29)} 19. Bf4 Re2 $17 {Renet, O-Tseitlin, Mi/Palma de Mallorca GMA-op/1989}) 15... c5 (15... Re8 16. Bxd7 Qxd7 17. f4 c5 18. Nb3 Nc6 19. Qf3 f5 20. c3 b6 $15 {1-0 Becerra Rivero,J (2445)-Alonso Garcia,R (2380)/Cuba 1993/CBM 035 ext (53)}) 16. Ne6 (16. Bxd7 Qxd7 17. Nb3 b6 {and I like Black here, Lewis, J-Martinez, I (2290)/Dubai 1986.}) 16... Qc8 17. Nxg7 {Tony Kosten: 'Rytshagov, M (2495)-Boey, J (2285)/Antwerp 1996,'} Kxg7 (17... Bxf5 18. Nh5 Qc6 {the black kingside is a bit weaker, but otherwise Black is fine.}) 18. f4 Ng6 19. Bxg6 hxg6 $11 {1-0 Rytshagov,M (2495)-Boey,J (2285)/Antwerp 1996/EXT 1999 (31)}) 15. fxg4 Nxc1 16. Raxc1 Qb6 {Tony Kosten: 'White isn't able to bring the knight to the powerful f5-square,'} 17. c3 (17. Qf2 {Tony Kosten: '?'} f5 {Tony Kosten: '!'} 18. c3 fxg4 $17 {½-½ Kveinys,A (2545)-Binham,T (2330)/Kuopio 1992/EXT 2000 (41) Tony Kosten: 'with an extra pawn, Kveinys, A (2545)-Binham, T (2330)/ Kuopio 1992.'}) 17... Rae8 (17... f5 $5 18. gxf5 Bxd4+ 19. cxd4 Qxd4+ {and Black is OK.}) 18. Qf2 Re4 19. h3 Rfe8 20. Rce1 {Tony Kosten: 'and the knight will get to f5, Peters, J (2454)-Khachiyan, M (2473)/Costa Mesa 2003'} Qc7 21. Rxe4 Rxe4 22. Nf5 $14 {0-1 Peters,J (2454)-Khachiyan,M (2473)/Costa Mesa 2003/CBM 095 ext (49)}) (11... c5 $2 {is bad in view of} 12. Bf4) 12. Nd4 Bg4 {Provoking a concession.} 13. f3 {White does not have a better option.} Bc8 {Tony Kosten: 'Black holds onto this bishop, as otherwise his light squares might become vulnerable.'} (13... Bd7 {Tony Kosten: '!?'} 14. Bxd7 Qxd7 {Tony Kosten: 'is playable, though,'} 15. f4 Nc6 16. Qe6+ (16. Be3 Rfe8 17. Qd2 Re4) 16... Rf7 17. Qxd7 Rxd7 18. Nxc6 bxc6 19. f5 {Tony Kosten: 'with the better pawn structure, Govedarica, R (2395) -Grujic, Z (2275)/Vrbas 1994.'} Re8 $11 {1-0 Govedarica,R (2395)-Grujic,Z (2275)/Vrbas 1994/EXT 2002 (34)}) 14. f4 {From now on, and until the end of game the play is quite forced!} c6 $1 {This is tactically justified. Radjabov exploits the weakness of the diagonal a7-g1.} 15. fxe5 {Tony Kosten: '?!' Tony Kosten: 'This move simply irons out the black pawn formation.'} (15. Ba4 {Tony Kosten: 'is a better try, Alatulkkila, J-Jauhiainen, K/Finland 1990, although'} Qb6 (15... Nc4 $5 16. c3 f5 {is possible, the black knight can get to e4.}) 16. c3 Bg4 17. Qc2 Rae8 {and Black is at least not worse.}) 15... fxe5 16. Rxf8+ Qxf8 17. Bd3 ({The point is that White can't take on c6 in view of} 17. Nxc6 $2 bxc6 18. Bxc6 $2 Qc5+ $19) 17... e4 {Tony Kosten: '!'} (17... exd4 $4 18. Qh5 {Tony Kosten: 'wins on the spot.'} h6 19. Qg6 $18) 18. Bxe4 $1 {Tony Kosten: 'White forces a draw, as otherwise she might be worse.'} (18. Be3 exd3 19. Qxd3 Qf6 (19... Bd7 $5) 20. Rf1 Qg6 {Black is slightly better thanks to pair of strong bishops.} 21. Nf5 Bxf5 22. Rxf5 Re8 23. Bd2 Bd4+ 24. Kf1 Re5 25. Rf3 Qxd3+ 26. Rxd3 Rf5+ 27. Ke1 {and with careful play White managed to draw, Cisler, P  (2170)-Rybak, M (2280)/Czechia 1998.}) 18... Bxd4+ 19. Be3 Bxe3+ (19... Qc5 $2 20. Bxh7+ $1 Kg7 (20... Kxh7 $4 21. Qh5+ Kg7 22. Qg5+ {wins}) 21. Bxd4+ Qxd4+ 22. Kh1 Kxh7 23. Qh5+ Kg7 (23... Kg8 24. Rf1 Bg4 25. Qf7+ Kh8 26. h3 Bxh3 27. Qh5+ (27. gxh3 {leads to a perpetual after} Qe4+ 28. Kh2 Qe5+ 29. Kh1) 27... Kg8 28. Qxh3 {and White has the safer king.}) 24. Rf1 {[%cal Gf1f7]} Be6 $8 25. Qg5+ Kh7 26. Qe7+ $18) 20. Qxe3 dxe4 21. Qg5+ Qg7 22. Qd8+ Qf8 23. Qg5+ Qg7 {This game is short but rich in content and important for theory.} 1/2-1/2

