1. d4 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Ba6 5. Qc2 c5 6. d5 exd5 7. cxd5 Bb7 8. Bg2 Nxd5 9. O-O Be7 10. Rd1 Nc6 {This line was examined by GM Evgeny Postny in his theoretical survey in CBM116. See also my annotations to Bologan-A.Ivanov in CBM117.} 11. Qf5 (11. Qa4 {Bareev,Evgeny}) 11... Nf6 12. e4 d6 $146 {Bareev,Evgeny: 'N!?'} (12... g6 {Bareev,Evgeny: 'Ü 98/386'} 13. Qf4 O-O (13... h6 $5 14. e5 Nh5 15. Qg4 Ng7 16. Nc3 Ne6 17. Be3 h5 18. Qa4 a6 19. Rd2 (19. Nd5 $44) 19... b5 20. Qd1 c4 21. Nd5 Nb4 22. Bb6 $44 {0-1 Loeffler,S-Sakaev,K/Dresden GER 2007/The Week in Chess 648 (38)}) 14. e5 Nh5 15. Qg4 $1 (15. Qh6 Nd4 16. Nxd4 Bxg2 17. Kxg2 cxd4 18. g4 Rc8 $3 19. Rxd4 Ng7 20. Nc3 f5 21. Qd2 Bc5 22. Rxd7 Qh4 $17 {½-½ Aronian,L-Leko,P/Moscow RUS 2006/The Week in Chess 627 (27)}) 15... d5 16. exd6 Bf6 $6 (16... Bxd6 17. Bg5 $44) 17. Nc3 Nd4 18. Nxd4 Bxg2 19. Nf5 Bc6 20. d7 Qc7 21. Nd5 Bxd5 22. Rxd5 Rfd8 23. Be3 Bxb2 24. Nh6+ Kf8 25. Rad1 Bg7 26. Rxh5 gxh5 27. Qf5 {1-0 Carlsen,M-Ivanchuk,V/Monte Carlo MNC 2007/The Week in Chess 646}) 13. e5 (13. Nc3 {Bareev,Evgeny} Qc8 (13... Qb8) 14. Qxc8+ Rxc8 15. Bf4 Rd8 16. Rd2 O-O 17. Rad1 Rfe8 $15) 13... Qd7 (13... g6 {Bareev,Evgeny} 14. Qc2 Nb4 15. Qb3 Bd5 16. Rxd5 Nfxd5 17. a3 c4 18. Qa4+ Qd7 19. axb4 $16) 14. Qxd7+ (14. Qg5 {Bareev,Evgeny} h6 15. Qxg7 Rh7 16. exf6 Rxg7 17. fxg7 O-O-O $17) (14. Nh4 {Bareev,Evgeny} g6 15. Qf3 Ng4 16. exd6 O-O-O 17. Nc3 Bxh4 18. gxh4 Nd4 $17) (14. Qf4 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nh5 15. Qc4 O-O (15... d5 16. Rxd5 Qe6 17. Ng5 Bxg5 18. Bxg5 Na5 19. Qa4+ Bc6 20. Qd1 Bxd5 21. Qxd5 Qxd5 22. Bxd5 Rc8 23. g4 $16) (15... Na5 16. Qe2 d5 17. h3 g6 18. Bh6 $44) 16. exd6 (16. g4 Na5) (16. h3 g6 17. Nc3 Na5 18. Qd3 Rad8) 16... Bxd6 17. Nc3 Rad8 18. Qh4 Nd4 19. Nxd4 cxd4 20. Qxd4 Bxg2 21. Kxg2 Nf6 $11) 14... Nxd7 15. exd6 Bf6 16. Re1+ (16. Nc3 {Bareev,Evgeny} O-O-O 17. Bg5 (17. Ng5 Nde5 18. Bf4 (18. Nge4 Nd4 19. Nxf6 gxf6 20. Bxb7+ Kxb7 21. Ne4 f5 $17) 18... Bxg5 19. Bxg5 f6 20. Be3 Nb4 21. Ne4 Kb8 $15) 17... h6 18. Bxf6 Nxf6 19. h4 Rhe8 20. Rd2 (20. Rac1 Kb8) 20... Kb8 21. Rad1 Na5 22. b3 Ne4 23. Nxe4 Bxe4 24. Re2 f5 $11) 16... Kf8 (16... Kd8 {Bareev,Evgeny} 17. Bg5 (17. Ng5 Bxg5 18. Bxg5+ f6 19. Bd2 Rb8 (19... Re8 20. Na3 Rxe1+ 21. Rxe1 Nde5 22. f4 Nd3 23. Bxc6 Bxc6 24. Re7) 20. Na3 Nce5 21. Bc3 Bxg2 22. Kxg2 $14) 17... h6 18. Bxf6+ Nxf6 19. Na3 Re8 20. Nc4 Ne4 21. Rad1 $14) 17. Nc3 Nb4 {White's d6-pawn is the main strategical problem in this kind of position. It can be weak or strong. As Black's h8 rook is out of play, the former possibility is more probable.} 18. Bg5 $6 {Bareev,Evgeny: '!' A dubious exchange sac.} (18. Rd1 $14) 18... Bxf3 $6 {Black "believes" her opponent - and wrongly so!} (18... Nc2 $1 19. Bxf6 Nxf6 20. Re7 Bxf3 21. Bxf3 Re8 $1 22. Rxe8+ Kxe8 23. Bc6+ (23. Rd1 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nd4 24. Bg2 Kd7 (24... Kd8 25. Bf1 Re8 26. Bc4 $11) 25. Bf1 Kxd6 (25... Re8 26. Bc4 Kxd6 27. Nb5+ Kc6 28. Nxa7+) 26. Nb5+ Kd5 27. Bg2+ $11) 23... Kd8 24. Rd1 Nd4 $15 {[%csl Rd6]}) 19. Bxf3 Rd8 20. Bxf6 Nxf6 21. Re7 Nc2 22. Rd1 Nd4 23. Kg2 g6 (23... Rd7 {Bareev,Evgeny} 24. Rxd7 Nxd7 25. Re1 $16) (23... g5 $1 {Bareev,Evgeny} 24. Rxa7 Rxd6 25. Be2 Kg7 26. Bc4 Rf8 27. Rb7 g4 28. h3 h5 29. hxg4 hxg4 30. a3 $14) 24. Rxa7 Rxd6 $14 {[%mdl 32] In this position White's bishop is very strong. Compared to the game Gelfand-Kasimdzhanov from this issue, there is much more material on the board. Still, if Black's h8 rook safely comes out without her having to make any concessions, the position will almost equalize.} 25. Be2 $1 (25. b4 $5 {Bareev,Evgeny} Kg7 (25... cxb4 26. Ne2 Nb5 27. Rxd6 Nxd6 28. Ra4 Ke7 29. Rxb4 Nd7 30. Nc3 Rb8 31. a4 $14) 26. bxc5 bxc5 27. Rc7 Rhd8 28. Rxc5 Nxf3 29. Rxd6 Nh4+ 30. gxh4 Rxd6 31. a4 $14) 25... Kg7 (25... Rd7 {Bareev,Evgeny} 26. Rxd7 Nxd7 27. Nb5 $16) 26. Bc4 Rd7 {Bareev,Evgeny: '!'} (26... Rf8 {Bareev,Evgeny} 27. Rb7 $1 (27. a4 Nf5 28. Rxd6 (28. Re1 Rd4) 28... Nxd6 29. Ba2 Rd8 30. Nb5 Nfe8) 27... Nf5 28. b3 Rxd1 29. Nxd1 Nd6 30. Rxb6 Nxc4 31. bxc4 Rd8 32. Rb1 Ne4 33. Ra1 Rd4 34. a4 (34. Ne3 Rd2) 34... Rxc4 35. a5 Rd4 36. a6 Rd8 37. Ne3 $16) 27. Rxd7 Nxd7 {[%mdl 4096]} 28. Re1 Kf8 $6 {Bareev,Evgeny: '?' Cutting off his own rook once again. Black's further attempts to free it take valuable time and the invasion of White's rook, combined with the advance of his pawns, decides. The lesser evil was to remove his strong knight from d4:} (28... Nf5 $142 {Bareev,Evgeny: '!'} 29. Bd3 (29. Nb5 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nf6 (29... h5 30. Bd3 (30. h3 Nf6 31. Bd3 Nh6 32. Re7 Rd8 33. Bc4 Rd2 $11) 30... Nh6 31. Nd6 Rd8 32. Re8 Rxe8 33. Nxe8+ Kf8 34. Nc7 Ng4 35. h3 Ngf6 36. f4 Ke7 37. Kf3 Nb8 $11) 30. Bd3 (30. Rd1 h5 31. h3 Ra8 (31... Re8 32. Nd6) 32. a3 Kf8 33. Kf3 Re8 34. b3 g5) 30... Nh6 (30... Nd4 31. Nxd4 cxd4 32. Rc1 Ng4 33. Be2) 31. Kf3 Rd8) 29... Nd6 30. Nb5 $14 (30. Rd1 {Bareev,Evgeny} Ne5 31. Bxg6 (31. Bf1 Nf5) 31... Ndc4 32. Be4 Nxb2 33. Rb1 Nbc4 $11) 30... Nxb5 {Bareev,Evgeny} (30... c4 {Bareev,Evgeny} 31. Nxd6 cxd3 32. Rd1 Nc5 33. b4 Ne6 34. Rxd3 $16) 31. Bxb5 Nf6 32. Rd1 Rb8 33. f4 (33. Rd6 Ne4 34. Rd7 Nf6 35. Ra7 Rd8 36. Bc4 (36. a4 Rd2 37. Bc4 Nd7) 36... Rd7 37. Rxd7 Nxd7 38. f4 f5 $11) 33... Kf8 34. Kf3 (34. Rd6 Ke7 35. Rc6 Ne8 36. a4 Nd6 37. Rc7+ Ke6 $11) 34... h5 35. h3 Ke7 36. g4 hxg4+ 37. hxg4 Rd8 $11) 29. a4 (29. Nd5 $1 {Bareev,Evgeny} b5 (29... Kg7 30. Re7 Rd8 31. Nc7 Kh6 32. Bxf7 Nf5 33. Ne6 Nxe7 34. Nxd8 $18) 30. Bf1 Kg7 31. Nc7 Rb8 (31... b4 32. Ne8+ Kf8 33. Nd6 Nb6 (33... Rg8 34. Re8+ Kg7 35. Re7 $18) 34. Re8+ Kg7 35. Rxh8 Kxh8 36. Nxf7+ $18) 32. Rd1 b4 (32... Ne5 33. Na6 Rc8 34. Nxc5 $16) 33. Nb5 (33. Na6 Rd8 34. Nxb4 $16) 33... Nxb5 34. Rxd7 Nd4 35. Bc4 $16) 29... h5 (29... Nf6 $1 {Bareev,Evgeny} 30. h3 h5 31. Nb5 Nxb5 32. Bxb5 Kg7 (32... g5 33. Re5 g4 34. Be2 Kg7 35. hxg4 hxg4 36. Rg5+ Kh6 37. Rf5 Kg6 38. Rf4 Rd8 39. Bxg4 Rd2) 33. Rd1 Rb8 $14) 30. Nd5 h4 31. g4 (31. Re7 $2 {Bareev,Evgeny} h3+ 32. Kf1 Nf6 33. Rb7 Ng4 34. Nxb6 Kg7 35. Rxf7+ Kh6 36. Bd5 Nxh2+ 37. Kg1 Ng4) (31. f4 $5 {Bareev,Evgeny} hxg3 (31... h3+ 32. Kf2) 32. hxg3 f5 33. Re7 Nf6 34. Rb7 Nxd5 35. Bxd5 Nc2 36. Kf3 Rh2 37. Rxb6 $16) 31... g5 {[%csl Rg5]} 32. Nc7 {[%cal Re1e8,Re8e7] Bareev,Evgeny: '!'} (32. Re7 $2 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nf6 (32... h3+ 33. Kg3 Nf6 34. Re5 Nc6 35. Re3 Nxd5 36. Bxd5 Nd4 37. f4 gxf4+ 38. Kxf4 $14) 33. Rb7 (33. Re5 $2 Nxg4 34. Rxg5 h3+) 33... h3+ 34. Kh1 Nxg4 35. Nxb6 Nxf2+ 36. Kg1 Ng4) 32... Nf6 33. h3 Kg7 (33... Rh6 {Bareev,Evgeny} 34. Re5 Rg6 35. a5 bxa5 (35... Nc6 36. a6 Nxe5 37. a7) 36. Rxc5 Ne4 37. Rxa5 $16) 34. Re5 {Bareev,Evgeny: '?'} (34. Re7 {Bareev,Evgeny} Rf8 35. Ne6+ Nxe6 36. Bxe6 Ne8 (36... Re8 37. Rxf7+ Kg6 38. Ba2 Re2 39. Rb7 Rxb2 40. Be6 Kh6 41. Bf5 $18) 37. Rb7 Nd6 38. Rxb6 fxe6 39. Rxd6 Kf6 (39... Rb8 40. Rxe6 Rxb2 41. Re5 Kf6 42. Rf5+ Kg6 43. Rxc5 Ra2 44. a5 Kf6 45. Rc6+ Kf7 46. a6 $18) 40. a5 Ra8 41. a6 $16) 34... Kh6 (34... Kg6 $142 $1 35. Bd3+ Kh6 36. f4 Rg8 37. Nb5 (37. a5 $1 {Bareev,Evgeny} bxa5 (37... c4 38. Bxc4 bxa5 39. Bxf7 Rg7 40. Ne6 Nxe6 41. Bxe6 gxf4 42. Rxa5 $18) 38. Rxc5 gxf4 39. Rxa5 Ne6 (39... Kg7 40. Rg5+ Kf8 41. Rxg8+ Kxg8 $14) 40. Nxe6 fxe6 41. Kf3 Nd5 42. Bc4 Kg6 (42... Rb8 43. Ra6 Ne3 44. Bxe6 Rxb2 45. Bd7+ Kg7 46. Kxf4 Ng2+ 47. Kg5 $18) 43. Ra6 Kf7 44. Bxd5 exd5 45. Kxf4 Rb8 46. Kg5 Rxb2 47. Kxh4 d4 48. Kg5 d3 49. Rd6 d2 $11) 37... Nxb5 38. axb5 gxf4 39. Kf3 $16) 35. f4 Nh7 36. f5 Nc6 (36... f6 37. Rd5 {[%cal Yd5d6]}) 37. Rd5 Kg7 (37... Rd8 38. Rxd8 Nxd8 39. Nd5) 38. f6+ $5 Kh6 (38... Nxf6 {Bareev,Evgeny} 39. Rxg5+ Kf8 40. Rf5 Kg7 41. g5 Nh7 42. Rxf7+ Kg6 43. Rf4 (43. Rd7 Ne5 44. Rd6+ Kxg5 45. Ba2 Nf8 46. Rxb6 Nfd7 (46... Nfg6 47. Ne6+) 47. Rb5 Rc8 48. Nd5 Rf8 $14) 43... Ne5 44. Rxh4 Nxc4 45. Rxc4 Nxg5 46. h4 Nf7 47. Nd5 $16) 39. Bb5 {Bareev,Evgeny: '?'} (39. Rd6 $1 {Bareev,Evgeny} Ne5 40. Bb5 Ng6 (40... Rc8 41. Nd5 c4 42. Rxb6 Rd8 43. Ne3 Rd2+ 44. Kf1 Rxb2 45. Nf5+ Kg6 46. Ne7+ Kh6 47. Bc6 Rxb6 48. Ng8+ Kg6 49. Be4# {#}) (40... Rb8 41. Nd5 $18) 41. Ne8 Nf4+ 42. Kh2 Nf8 43. Rxb6 N8e6 44. a5 $18) 39... Nb4 $6 {Bareev,Evgeny: '?'} (39... Nd4 40. Rd6 Nxb5 (40... Rc8 {Bareev,Evgeny} 41. Nd5 Nxb5 42. axb5) 41. axb5 Rb8 42. Nd5 (42. Kf3 {Bareev,Evgeny} Kg6 43. Nd5) 42... Ra8 43. Nc3 (43. Rxb6 {Bareev,Evgeny} Ra2 44. Rb7 Rxb2+ 45. Kf3 Kg6 46. Rb8 Rh2 47. Rg8+ Kh6 48. b6 Rxh3+ 49. Ke4 Rb3 50. Ke5 h3 51. b7 h2 52. Ne7 Nxf6 53. Kxf6 Kh7 $11) (43. Nxb6 {Bareev,Evgeny} Ra5) 43... Rb8 (43... Nf8 {Bareev,Evgeny} 44. Rxb6 Ne6 45. Rc6 Rd8) 44. Kf2 $16) (39... Rc8 $2 {Bareev,Evgeny} 40. Bxc6 Rxc7 41. Rd6 Nf8 42. Kf3 c4 (42... Ne6 43. Be4) 43. Ke4 Ne6 44. Kd5) 40. Rd6 Rb8 41. Na6 Nxa6 42. Bxa6 {Bareev,Evgeny: '[R 9/i]'} Nf8 43. Bc4 {The advantage of the bishop over the knight is now obvious.} Rb7 (43... Ng6 {Bareev,Evgeny} 44. Bxf7 Nf4+ 45. Kh2) 44. Kf3 Nd7 (44... Ng6 45. Ke4 Nf4 46. Kf5 Nxh3 47. Rd8 Kh7 48. Rf8 $18) 45. Ke4 Kg6 46. Bd3 {Bareev,Evgeny: '?'} (46. Kd5 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nxf6+ 47. Kc6 Rb8 (47... Re7 48. Kxb6 Re3 49. a5 Rxh3 50. a6 Re3 51. a7 Re8 52. Bd5 Kg7 53. Bc6 $18) 48. Kc7 Ra8 (48... Re8 49. Rxb6 Re7+ 50. Kd6 Re3 51. a5 Rxh3 52. a6) 49. Bb5 Kg7 50. Kxb6 Ne4 51. Rd5 Kh6 52. Rf5 (52. a5 Rb8+ 53. Kc6) 52... Rd8 53. a5 $18) 46... c4 (46... Nxf6+ {Bareev,Evgeny} 47. Ke5+ Kg7 48. Rxf6 Re7+ 49. Kf5 Re3 50. Be4 Rxe4 51. Rxf7+ Kxf7 52. Kxe4 Ke6 53. b3 $18) 47. Bxc4 (47. Bc2 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nxf6+ 48. Ke5+ Kg7 49. Rxf6 Re7+ 50. Kf5 Re2 51. Rxb6 Rxc2 52. Kxg5 c3 53. bxc3 Rxc3 54. Kxh4 $18) 47... Nxf6+ 48. Kd4 Kg7 49. Bb5 (49. b3 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nd7 50. Bd5 Ra7 51. Kc4 Kf8 52. Bc6 Ke7 $11) 49... Re7 {Desperation.} (49... Rb8 50. b4 (50. Ke5 {Bareev,Evgeny} Ne8 51. Bxe8 Rxe8+ 52. Kf5 Re3 53. Rxb6 f6 54. Rb7+ Kh6 55. a5 Rxh3 56. a6 Rd3 (56... Rh1 57. Rb3) 57. a7 Rd5+ 58. Kxf6 Ra5 59. b4 Ra2 60. Kf7 h3 61. Kg8 $18) 50... Rb7 51. Bc4 {[%cal Ra4a5]} (51. Bc6 {Bareev,Evgeny} Re7 52. Kc4 Re5 53. b5 Re2 54. a5 bxa5 55. b6 Ne4 56. Bxe4 Rxe4+ 57. Kb5 Rb4+ 58. Kxa5 Rb3 59. Rd5 Kf6 60. Rb5 $18) 51... Ra7 (51... Nd7 {Bareev,Evgeny} 52. a5 (52. Bb5 Nf8 53. Kd5 Ne6) (52. Bd5 Rc7 53. Bc6 Nf6 54. Ke5 Ng8 55. Bb5 Re7+ 56. Kd4 Nf6 57. Bd3 Ra7 $132) 52... bxa5 53. bxa5 Rc7 54. Rd5 f6 55. Rd6 $18) 52. Rxb6 Rxa4 53. Rb7 Ra3 54. b5 Rxh3 55. b6 Rh2 56. Rxf7+ Kg6 57. b7 Rb2 58. Re7 Nxg4 (58... h3 59. Bd3+ Kh6 60. Rf7) 59. Kc3 Rxb7 60. Rxb7 h3 61. Bd3+ Kf6 62. Kd4 $18) (49... Ng8 $1 {Bareev,Evgeny} 50. b4 Rb8 (50... Ne7 51. Rd7) 51. Rd5 f6 52. Rd7+ Kf8 53. Bc6 Ne7 54. b5 Kf7 $16) 50. Rxb6 Re4+ 51. Kd3 (51. Kc5 {Bareev,Evgeny} Re5+ (51... Re3 52. a5 Rxh3 53. a6) 52. Kc6 Nxg4 (52... Re6+) 53. hxg4 h3 54. Bf1 (54. Kc7 h2 55. Bc6 Rc5 $11) 54... h2 55. Bg2 Re2 56. Bd5 Rd2 57. Bf3 Rf2 $11) 51... Rb4 52. Kc2 (52. a5 {Bareev,Evgeny} Nd5 (52... Rxb2 53. a6 Ra2 54. Kd4 Ra3 55. Bf1 Ne8 56. Rb7 Ra1 57. Bd3 Nd6 58. Rd7 Nc8 59. Rc7 $18) 53. Rb7 Rxb2 54. a6 Nf4+ 55. Kc3 Rb1 56. a7 Ra1 57. Kb4 Nxh3 58. Ba4 Rb1+ 59. Bb3 Ra1 60. Rxf7+ $18) 52... Nxg4 (52... Nd5 {Bareev,Evgeny} 53. Rc6 Nf4 54. Rc3 Kf6 55. Ra3 Ke5 56. Bf1 $18) 53. Kc3 Re4 54. hxg4 h3 (54... Rxg4 {Bareev,Evgeny} 55. a5 (55. Rd6 h3 56. Rd1) 55... h3 56. a6 h2 57. Bc6 Ra4 58. Kd3 $18) 55. Rd6 h2 56. Rd1 Rxg4 {Bareev,Evgeny: '[R 8/g6]'} 57. Rh1 Rg3+ (57... Rh4 {Bareev,Evgeny} 58. a5 g4 59. Bc6 (59. a6 g3 60. a7 g2 61. a8=Q g1=Q 62. Qd5 Rh3+ (62... Rg4 63. Qe5+ Kg8 64. Qb8+ Kg7 65. Qxh2 Rg3+ 66. Kc4 Rg4+ 67. Kb3 $18) 63. Kb4 Qe3 64. Bc4 Qb6+ 65. Qb5 Qd6+ 66. Qc5 Qd2+ $11) 59... Rh6 (59... g3 60. Ra1) 60. Bb7 g3 61. Ra1 Ra6 62. b4 $18) 58. Kb4 Rg2 (58... Rh3 {Bareev,Evgeny} 59. a5 g4 60. a6 g3 61. Bc6 $18) 59. Kb3 (59. Ka3 {Bareev,Evgeny} g4 60. a5 g3 61. a6 Rc2 $1) 59... g4 60. a5 g3 61. Bc6 (61. a6 $2 {Bareev,Evgeny} Rxb2+ 62. Kxb2 g2 $19) 61... Re2 62. a6 Re7 63. Ra1 Ra7 64. Bg2 Kf6 {Bareev,Evgeny} 65. Kc4 Ke5 66. b4 f5 67. b5 1-0

