1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 c5 4. Nc3 cxd4 5. Nxd4 {*} Qb6 6. g3 Bc5 7. e3 Nc6 8. Bg2 Nxd4 9. exd4 Bxd4 10. O-O O-O $6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Judit plays a dangerous line, but in the critical position even avoids the main defence 10...e5 that has yet to be refuted. White has a dangerous initiative for the pawn, but can he aspire to more than the equality?'} (10... Be5 {Ü 99/20}) (10... a6 11. Na4 Qa7 12. Bf4 $1 d5 (12... e5 13. Bxe5 $1 Bxe5 14. Re1 O-O 15. Rxe5 d5 16. cxd5 b5 17. Nc3 b4 18. Na4 Bb7 19. Qd2 a5 20. b3 Rad8 21. Rd1 {1-0 Greenfeld,A (2549)-Rocius,M (2240)/Saint Vincent 2005 (25)}) 13. Bd6 $1 e5 (13... dxc4 14. Rc1) 14. c5 Bg4 15. Qd2 Rd8 16. Rae1 $16 {Umansky-Schmittdiel/Absam 2002/}) (10... Bxc3 $6 11. bxc3 O-O 12. Ba3 $1 $14) 11. Bg5 $1 $146 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'N'} (11. Na4 Qd6 12. Bf4 $5 (12. Be3 Be5) 12... e5 13. Be3 Qb4 14. Bxd4 exd4 15. b3 d5 16. a3 Qa5 17. cxd5 Nxd5 18. Qxd4 $14 {1-0 Bricard,E (2460)-Olafsson,H (2270)/Reykjavik 1993 (52)}) 11... e5 (11... Qc5 $5) 12. c5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!?' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Carlsen is uncorking a dangerous idea, that would be challenging enough without the limitations of the blindfold game..'} Qxc5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: '?!'} (12... Qxb2 13. Bxf6 $40 Qxc3 14. Rc1 $1 (14. Qg4 g6 15. Rac1 Qd2 $1) 14... Qb2 (14... Qb4 15. a3 $1) 15. Qg4 g6 16. Rc4 Qd2 17. Qh4 h5 (17... Re8 $2 18. Rc2 $1 $18) 18. Rxd4 Qxd4 (18... exd4 19. Bxd4 g5 (19... a5 20. Qf6 Qh6 21. Bd5 $16) 20. Qe4 $16) 19. Qg5 Kh7 20. Bxe5 $5 f6 21. Bxd4 fxg5 22. Re1 Rf7 23. Bd5 Rg7 24. Re8 $18) (12... Bxc5 $5 13. Na4 Qa5 14. Bxf6 gxf6 15. Qg4+ Kh8 16. Qh4 Kg7 17. Be4 Rh8 18. Qg4+ Kf8 $13) (12... Qe6 $6 13. Nb5 Qf5 14. Be3 $1 Bxe3 15. fxe3 Qg5 16. Qb3 $14) (12... Qa6 13. Be3 (13. Rc1 d5 14. Bxf6 Qxf6 15. Nxd5 Qd8 $15) 13... Bxc3 14. bxc3 d5 15. cxd6 Rd8 $13) 13. Bxf6 gxf6 14. Nd5 (14. Qg4+ Kh8 15. Qh4 $1 Kg7 (15... Bxc3 $2 16. Be4 $1 $18) 16. Be4 Rh8 17. Nd5 Qd6 18. Rad1 $1 h5 19. Rd3 $16) 14... d6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: '?' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar feels, that developing the bishop from c8 is imperative, but unfortunately it is too slow. Suddenly the black queen is cut off from the kingside and White will just win.'} (14... Kh8 15. Qh5 $40) (14... f5 $1 15. Rc1 (15. Qh5 Qd6 16. Qxf5 Qh6 $13) 15... Qd6 16. Nc7 Rb8 17. Nb5 Qb4 18. Nxd4 exd4 19. Qh5 $40) 15. Qh5 Kg7 (15... f5 $2 16. Qg5+ Kh8 17. Qf6+ Kg8 18. Ne7#) 16. Be4 h6 (16... Rh8 17. Qh4 $18) 17. Rac1 Bxf2+ (17... Qa5 18. Rxc8 Rfxc8 19. Qf5 Rg8 20. Qxf6+ Kf8 21. Qxh6+ Ke8 22. Qxd6 $18) 18. Kg2 Qd4 19. Qh4 $18 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Black has grabbed three pawns, but her position is completely hopeless.'} f5 (19... Rg8 20. Qxf6+ Kf8 21. Qxd6+ Kg7 22. Qf6+ Kf8 23. Qxh6+ $18) 20. Qf6+ Kg8 (20... Kh7 21. Bxf5+ Bxf5 22. Qxf5+ Kg7 23. Nf6 $18) 21. Ne7+ Kh7 22. Bxf5+ Bxf5 23. Qxf5+ (23. Nxf5 Qe4+ 24. Kxf2 $18) 23... Kg7 24. Rxf2 e4 25. Rc4 $1 {Carlsen is enjoying himself and tries to win with an impressive attack.} (25. Qh5 $18) 25... Qxc4 26. Qf6+ Kh7 27. Nf5 $1 {1-0 (27) Carlsen,M (2714)-Polgar,J (2708) Bilbao 2007 CBM 121 [Ftacnik,Lubomir]} *

