6. Nxe8 Nxe8 17. Ra4 $1 {is problematic for Black, e.g.} Bc5 (17... d6 $2 18. Rxd4 $1 exd4 19. Re1 $18) 18. Bd5 Qd6 19. Qb3 Qf8 20. Be3 $1 d6 21. Bxc5 dxc5 22. a6 $18) (12... Bc5 13. Qe1 $5 {A clever multi-purpose move, threatening the e5-pawn and the advance b2-b4 at the same time.} (13. a5 Qd8 14. Be3 $1 {with excellent positional compensation for the sacrificed pawn} (14. a6 $6 Rb8 {is fine for Black})) 13... a5 $6 {Black prevents the b2-b4 advance, but at the same leaves no option for kicking the b5-knight away.} (13... a6 $5 14. a5 Qd8 15. Nc3 $44) 14. Qxe5 d6 15. Qf4 $14 {, White has both the initiative and the better pawn structure, Rahman, Z-Hossain, E/Dhaka 1999}) 13. Nxd4 exd4 14. b3 d5 15. c5 Qc6 16. Qxd4 Bf5 17. Bb2 Rfe8 18. Rfe1 $14 {Nielsen, P-Gelfand, B/playchess.com INT 2004}) ({D)} 10... Be5 {Hansen, Carsten RR: 'Ü 99/20'} 11. Qe2 Bb8 12. Be3 Qd8 13. c5 O-O 14. Rfd1 Qe7 15. Rac1 Rd8 16. Nb5 $5 ({White can improve with} 16. Bg5 $1 Qf8 {(Nd5 was threatened)} 17. Bxf6 gxf6 18. Ne4 Qh6 19. Nd6 Bxd6 20. cxd6 {, and Black is completely tied up}) 16... Nd5 17. Bd4 Qf8 18. Be5 b6 19. Bd6 Bxd6 20. Nxd6 bxc5 21. Bxd5 exd5 22. Rxd5 $16 {Marin, M-Ionescu, C/Predeal ROM 2006}) 11. Bg5 $146 {RR: 'N!' RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'N''} ({Hansen, Carsten: 'This is a new move. In an earlier game, White had proved that'} 11. Na4 {Hansen, Carsten: '!' Hansen, Carsten: 'is uncomfortable for Black:'} Qd6 12. Bf4 $5 {Hansen, Carsten: '!'} (12. Be3 Be5 13. Qe2 {Hansen, Carsten} Qe7 14. Rfd1 d5 15. cxd5 Bd6 16. Nc3 exd5 17. Nxd5 Nxd5 18. Rxd5 Be6 19. Rb5 {leaves White with a fair-sized initiative, Green, P-Martin, B/Dunedin 1988}) 12... e5 13. Be3 {Hansen, Carsten: ''} Qb4 14. Bxd4 exd4 15. b3 (15. Rc1 $5 {Hansen, Carsten} d5 $2 (15... d6 $5) 16. a3 Qa5 17. cxd5 $16) 15... d5 16. a3 Qa5 17. cxd5 Nxd5 18. Qxd4 $14 {1-0 Bricard,E (2460)-Olafsson,H (2270)/Reykjavik 1993 (52) Hansen, Carsten: 'Bricard, E-Olafsson, H/Reykjavik 1993'}) 11... e5 {Hansen, Carsten: '?!' RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hansen, Carsten: '?!'''} (11... Qc5 $5 {Hansen, Carsten RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hansen, Carsten''} 12. Bxf6 Bxf6 13. Ne4 Qxc4 14. Nxf6+ gxf6 15. b3 Qb4 16. a3 Qb5 {, and White has some compensation for the pawn thanks to Black's weakened kingside pawn structure, and problematic queenside development}) 12. c5 $5 {RR: '!' RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!?'' Carlsen is uncorking a dangerous idea, that would be challenging enough without the limitations of the blindfold game.. RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Carlsen is uncorking a dangerous idea, that would be challenging enough without the limitations of the blindfold game..''} Qxc5 $6 {RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '?!''} (12... Qxb2 $6 13. Bxf6 {RR: ''} Qxc3 14. Rc1 $1 (14. Qg4 g6 15. Rac1 Qd2 $1) 14... Qb2 (14... Qb4 15. a3 $1) 15. Qg4 g6 16. Rc4 Qd2 17. Qh4 h5 (17... Re8 $2 18. Rc2 $1 $18) 18. Rxd4 Qxd4 (18... exd4 19. Bxd4 g5 (19... a5 20. Qf6 Qh6 21. Bd5 $16) 20. Qe4 $16) 19. Qg5 Kh7 20. Bxe5 $5 f6 21. Bxd4 fxg5 22. Re1 Rf7 23. Bd5 Rg7 24. Re8 $18) (12... Bxc5 $5 13. Na4 Qa5 14. Bxf6 gxf6 15. Qg4+ Kh8 16. Qh4 Kg7 17. Be4 Rh8 18. Qg4+ Kf8 $13) (12... Qe6 $6 13. Nb5 Qf5 14. Be3 $1 Bxe3 15. fxe3 Qg5 16. Qb3 $14) (12... Qa6 13. Be3 (13. Rc1 d5 14. Bxf6 Qxf6 15. Nxd5 Qd8 $15) 13... Bxc3 14. bxc3 d5 15. cxd6 Rd8 $13) 13. Bxf6 gxf6 14. Nd5 (14. Qg4+ Kh8 15. Qh4 $1 Kg7 (15... Bxc3 $2 16. Be4 $1 $18) 16. Be4 Rh8 17. Nd5 Qd6 18. Rad1 $1 h5 19. Rd3 $16) 14... d6 $2 {[%mdl 256] Hansen, Carsten: '??' RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '?' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Hansen, Carsten: '??''' Polgar feels, that developing the bishop from c8 is imperative, but unfortunately it is too slow. Suddenly the black queen is cut off from the kingside and White will just win. RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Polgar feels, that developing the bishop from c8 is imperative, but unfortunately it is too slow. Suddenly the black queen is cut off from the kingside and White will just win.''} (14... f5 $1 15. Rc1 (15. Qh5 Qd6 16. Qxf5 Qh6 $13) 15... Qd6 16. Nc7 (16. Qh5 {Hansen, Carsten} Bxb2 17. Rc2 Bd4 18. Qxf5 Qh6 19. Rfc1 Kh8 20. Ne7 {, and just when it looks like White is winning, Black has} Bb2 $1 {Hansen, Carsten: '=!' Hansen, Carsten: 'is of course a draw by repetition' RR: '=!' RR: 'Hansen, Carsten: '=!' Hansen, Carsten: 'is of course a draw by repetition' Ftacnik,Lubomir: '=!''} 21. Rd1 Bd4 22. Bd5 $5 (22. Rdc1 Bb2 $1 $11 {is of course a draw by repetition}) 22... Re8 23. Nxc8 Rexc8 24. Rxc8+ Rxc8 25. Qxd7 Bxf2+ $1 26. Kxf2 Rc2+ {Hansen, Carsten: '=' RR: '=' RR: 'Hansen, Carsten: '=' Ftacnik,Lubomir: '=''} 27. Kf3 Rc3+ 28. Kg4 (28. Kf2 Rc2+ $11) 28... Qg6+ 29. Kh4 Qh6+ 30. Kg4 Qg6+ $11) 16... Rb8 17. Nb5 Qb4 18. Nxd4 exd4 19. Qh5 $40) (14... Kh8 15. Qh5 $40) 15. Qh5 Kg7 (15... f5 $2 16. Qg5+ Kh8 17. Qf6+ Kg8 18. Ne7#) 16. Be4 h6 (16... Rh8 17. Qh4 $18) 17. Rac1 Bxf2+ (17... Qa5 18. Rxc8 Rfxc8 19. Qf5 Rg8 20. Qxf6+ Kf8 21. Qxh6+ Ke8 22. Qxd6 $18) 18. Kg2 Qd4 19. Qh4 $1 {RR: '+-' RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: '!'' Black has grabbed three pawns, but her position is completely hopeless. RR: 'Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Black has grabbed three pawns, but her position is completely hopeless.''} f5 (19... Rg8 20. Qxf6+ Kf8 21. Qxd6+ Kg7 22. Qf6+ Kf8 23. Qxh6+ $18) 20. Qf6+ Kg8 (20... Kh7 21. Bxf5+ Bxf5 22. Qxf5+ Kg7 23. Nf6 $18) 21. Ne7+ Kh7 22. Bxf5+ Bxf5 23. Qxf5+ ({Hansen, Carsten: 'After'} 23. Nxf5 {Hansen, Carsten: '!' Hansen, Carsten: 'it is immediate curtains'} Qe4+ 24. Kxf2 $18 {Hansen, Carsten: ', and Black doesn't have anything better than'} Qxf5+ {Hansen, Carsten} 25. Qxf5+) 23... Kg7 24. Rxf2 e4 25. Rc4 $1 {Hansen, Carsten: '!?' Carlsen is enjoying himself and tries to win with an impressive attack.} ({Hansen, Carsten: 'Strictly speaking, the strongest move is'} 25. Qh5 $18 {Hansen, Carsten: '!'} Qxf2+ {Hansen, Carsten} 26. Kxf2 {, though the text move is more than adequate as well.}) 25... Qxc4 26. Qf6+ Kh7 27. Nf5 $1 {RR: '1-0 (27) Carlsen,M (2714)-Polgar,J (2708) Bilbao 2007 CBM 121 [Ftacnik,Lubomir]'} 1-0

