1. d4 {Polgar,Judit} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. d5 Na6 {Avoiding the main system} (7... exd5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 99/369' Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 99/369'} 8. Nh4) 8. Nd4 exd5 9. Nc3 c6 10. cxd5 Nxd5 (10... cxd5 11. Nf5 Nc7 {leads to one of the main theoretical lines after 7...exd5 8.h4.}) 11. Nxd5 cxd5 12. Nf5 Bf6 13. Bxd5 {White has recaptured the pawn and now has a superior pawn structure; however, he has yet to develop his queenside.} Bc6 {Polgar,Judit: 'N' 'N'} (13... Bxd5 $5 14. Qxd5 Nc7 15. Qb3 d5 16. Bf4 Qd7 17. Rac1 Ne6 18. Bd6 Rfd8 19. Ba3 g6 20. Ne3 Nd4 21. Qd3 Qb5 $11 {½-½ Summerscale,A-Ikonnikov,V/France 1998/CBM 064 ext (37)}) 14. Qb3 $6 {A strange move voluntarily losing time.} (14. e4 $5 Nb4 {Polgar,Judit} 15. a3 Nxd5 16. exd5 Bb7 $14) (14. Rb1 $5) 14... Nc5 15. Qf3 Bxd5 16. Qxd5 Qe8 $1 {Polgar,Judit: '=' '='} 17. Qf3 $6 (17. e3 Qe6 18. Rd1 Ne4 $1 {[%cal Ya8c8]}) (17. Be3 Bxb2 18. Rad1 (18. Rab1 Bf6 19. Bxc5 bxc5 20. Qxc5 Qxe2) 18... Ne4 (18... Qe6 19. Bxc5 bxc5 20. Qxc5 Qxa2 21. Rxd7 $132) 19. Qxd7 {was probably the lesser evil although Black keeps the better chances due to her queenside pawn advantage.} ({or} 19. Bd4 Nf6 $15)) 17... Qe6 {White's queenside is now completely paralysed} 18. Ne3 (18. Rd1 {Polgar,Judit}) 18... Ne4 19. Rd1 Rac8 20. Nd5 Rc2 $6 (20... Rfe8 $142) 21. Nxf6+ $6 {Polgar,Judit: '?' '?'} (21. Qd3 $1 Bxb2 (21... Rfc8 22. f3 Nd6 {Polgar,Judit} (22... Ng5 {Polgar,Judit}) 23. Nf4 Qe5 24. Qxd6 Qxd6 25. Rxd6 Rxc1+ 26. Rxc1 Rxc1+ 27. Kf2 Ra1) 22. Qxc2 Bxa1 23. Nf4 $1 (23. Ba3 d6 24. Nf4 Qe5) 23... Qe5 24. Rxd7 $11) 21... Nxf6 22. Rd2 Rc5 {Polgar,Judit: '' ''} 23. Rd4 (23. b4 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 23... Re8 24. Be3 {The bishop has come out, Black's d-pawn is still isolated but... White has not equalized! His pieces are placed awkwardly and his king is unsafe.} Rf5 25. Qb7 (25. Rf4 $6 Rxf4 26. gxf4 $8 (26. Qxf4 Nd5 $17)) 25... Re5 (25... Nd5 $5 26. Rd3 Rh5 27. h4 Re5 28. Bd2 Nf6 29. e3 Ne4 $17) (25... d5 $5 {Polgar,Judit} 26. Qxa7 Rh5 27. Qa4 Ne4) 26. Qf3 (26. Rd3 {Polgar,Judit} d5 { h3 Polgar,Judit: ' Qh3'}) 26... h5 {[%cal Rf6g4]} 27. Rad1 $6 {White loses patience but what could he do?} (27. Rdd1 Rf5 28. Qb7 h4 $17) (27. Rd3 $5 {Polgar,Judit} Ng4 28. Rad1) 27... Qxa2 28. R4d2 Qa4 {Black has won a pawn and tactics is in her favour.} 29. h3 (29. Bd4 {Polgar,Judit: '!' '!'} Rxe2 (29... Ne4 {Polgar,Judit} 30. Bxe5 Nxd2 31. Rxd2 Rxe5) 30. Bxf6 Rxd2 31. Rxd2 gxf6 (31... Re1+ {Polgar,Judit} 32. Kg2 gxf6) 32. Qxf6 (32. Qxh5 Re1+ 33. Kg2 Qc4 $17 {[%cal Yc4f1,Yf1h1]} (33... Qc6+ {Polgar,Judit} 34. f3 Qe6)) 32... Re1+ 33. Kg2 Qc6+ 34. Qxc6 dxc6 $19 {}) 29... Qb5 30. Bd4 {Polgar,Judit: '?!' '?!'} Rf5 (30... Rxe2 {Polgar,Judit} 31. Bxf6 Rxd2 32. Rxd2 Re1+ 33. Kh2 Qf1 34. h4 gxf6 $17) 31. Qb7 Rxe2 32. Bxf6 gxf6 $1 33. Qc8+ (33. Rxe2 Qxe2 34. Rf1 h4 35. gxh4 (35. g4 Rf3) (35. Qxd7 Qf3) 35... Rh5 {is equally hopeless.}) (33. Rxd7 {Polgar,Judit} Qc5) 33... Kg7 34. Rxd7 {Desperation.} Rfxf2 35. Rxf7+ Kxf7 36. Rd7+ Re7 37. Rxe7+ Kxe7 38. Qb7+ Ke6 39. Qe4+ Qe5 40. Qc6+ (40. Qc4+ {Polgar,Judit} Kd6 41. Qd3+ Qd5 42. Qa3+ Qc5) 40... Kf5 41. Kxf2 {Polgar,Judit} Qc5+ 42. Qxc5+ bxc5 $19 0-1

