{Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'B11: Caro-Kann: Two Knights Variation '} 1. e4 {Polgar,Judit Ftacnik,L Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s)} c6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Nf3 Bg4 4. h3 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 e6 6. Be2 Nd7 7. d3 g6 8. O-O Bg7 9. Bf4 (9. Qg3 {(Polgar,Judit) Ü 54/131}) 9... Qb6 {Polgar,Judit: 'N' Bareev was in the lead by two points and his choice of opening is laudable. Polgar will be struggling to create active play for her pieces.} (9... Ne7 {Polgar,Judit}) 10. Nd1 (10. Rab1 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 10... Ngf6 (10... Ne7 {Polgar,Judit}) 11. a4 a5 12. g4 {A rather courageous decision dictated by the situation in the match.} (12. g3 $5 {Polgar,Judit} O-O 13. Qg2) 12... e5 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'last book move. Black threatens to win material: e5xf4' Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (12... O-O 13. Bd6 Rfd8 14. Qg3 Ne8 15. Be7 Rdc8 $11) 13. Bd2 Nc5 14. g5 {Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (14. exd5 Nxd5 $1 (14... cxd5 15. Qg2 e4 16. d4 Ne6 17. Bb5+ Kf8 18. c3 $14) 15. Ne3 Nf4 16. Nc4 Qc7 17. Rfe1 O-O $11) 14... dxe4 15. dxe4 Nfd7 $2 {Bareev is playing unduly modestly and gives his opponent the chance to generate an attack.} (15... Nfxe4 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): '!?' Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'should be examined more closely' Polgar,Judit: '!'} 16. Be3 Nd6 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): ''} (16... Qc7 17. Qg2 Qd6 18. Bf3 f5 19. gxf6 Nxf6 20. Nc3 Ne6 $15) 17. Ra3 (17. Nc3 O-O (17... Nf5 {Polgar,Judit} 18. Ne4 Nxe3 19. Nd6+ Kd7 20. Qxf7+ Kxd6 21. fxe3) 18. Ra3 Nf5 19. Rb3 Qa7 $17) 17... Nf5 18. Rb3 Qa7 19. Bxc5 Qxc5 20. Rxb7 Nd6 21. Rc7 e4 22. Qe3 Bd4 23. Qd2 O-O $15) 16. Bc4 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): '='} (16. Ne3 O-O (16... Qxb2 17. Nc4 Qxc2 18. Rfc1 Qb3 19. Rc3 Qb4 20. Re3 $18) 17. Nc4 Qc7 $11) 16... O-O (16... Rf8 17. Qg4 O-O-O 18. Ne3 $14) 17. h4 $1 {Polgar,Judit: '' The advance of the h-pawn openly announces White's aggressive ambitions.} Ne6 (17... Rae8 18. h5 gxh5 19. Ra3 $1 $16) 18. Bxe6 fxe6 19. Qh3 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'White threatens to win material: Qh3xe6' Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (19. Qe2 $16 {Polgar,Judit}) 19... Qd4 $1 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'Black threatens to win material: Qd4xd2'} (19... Rae8 20. h5 Rf7 $13) 20. Nc3 ({Inferior is} 20. Qxe6+ {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s)} Rf7 21. Be3 Qxe4 $17) 20... Qxd2 21. Rad1 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'White threatens to win material: Rd1xd2'} Qxc2 (21... Qf4 $1 {Polgar,Judit} 22. Rxd7 Rad8 23. Rxb7 Rd2 $13) 22. Rxd7 {Black's position is still fine, but due to the activity of the white pieces extreme caution is called for.} (22. Qxe6+ Kh8 23. Rxd7 Qxb2 $13) 22... Qxb2 $2 {Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (22... Rae8 23. h5 Rf7 (23... gxh5 24. Rxb7 $11) 24. Rxf7 Kxf7 25. h6 Bf8 $13) (22... Qb3 $1 23. h5 Rad8 24. hxg6 hxg6 $15) 23. h5 $1 gxh5 $4 {[%mdl 128] Polgar,Judit: '?' With this nervous move Black has managed to prove, that he is not sensing the danger clearly enough. Judit now wins with a forcing manoeuvre.} (23... Rf7 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): '' Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'was possible'} 24. Qxe6 (24. Rxf7 Kxf7 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): '='} 25. Rb1 Qd2 26. Rxb7+ Kf8 $1 27. Qf3+ (27. Qxe6 Qxg5+ 28. Kf1 {Polgar,Judit} Qf6 (28... Qc1+ 29. Nd1 Qxd1+ 30. Kg2 $18) 29. Qc4 gxh5 30. Rc7 Rd8) (27. Qg3 {Polgar,Judit} gxh5 28. g6 Qh6 29. gxh7 Qxh7) 27... Qf4 28. Qxf4+ exf4 29. Ne2 Be5 30. Kg2 gxh5 31. Rxh7 Rb8 32. Rxh5 Rb3 $132) 24... Raf8 25. hxg6 (25. Nd1 {Polgar,Judit} Qe2 26. h6 Qh5 27. hxg7 Qxg5+ 28. Kh2 Qh4+ $11) 25... hxg6 26. Rd3 Qc2 27. Rh3 Rd8 28. Qxg6 Rd3 $11) 24. Qxe6+ {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): '+-'} Kh8 25. Rxg7 $1 Kxg7 26. Qh6+ {Polgar,Judit: '!'} Kg8 (26... Kf7 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s): 'there is nothing better in the position'} 27. Rb1 {Polgar,Judit: '+-'} Qxc3 (27... Qxb1+ {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s)} 28. Nxb1 Kg8 $18) 28. Rxb7+ Ke8 29. Qe6+ $18) 27. g6 hxg6 28. Qxg6+ Kh8 29. Kh1 $1 {It is possible, that the defender has overlooked the motif of activizing the rook via the g1-square.} Rf4 (29... Qb3 30. Qxh5+ Kg7 31. Rg1+ Kf6 32. Nd5+ cxd5 33. Rg6+ Ke7 34. Qxe5+ $18) (29... Qxf2 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s)} 30. Qxh5+ Kg7 31. Qg5+ Kh7 32. Rxf2 Rxf2 33. Qh4+ Kg6 34. Qg3+ Kf7 35. Qxf2+ Ke6 36. Qf5+ Kd6 37. Qf6+ Kd7 38. Qxe5 Re8 39. Qxa5 Rh8+ 40. Kg2 Rg8+ 41. Kf3 Rf8+ 42. Ke3 Rf6 43. Qb6 Rg6 44. Qxb7+ Ke6 45. Qxc6+ Kf7 46. Qc7+ Kf8 47. Nd5 Rg7 48. Qd8+ Kf7 49. Qf6+ Kg8 50. Ne7+ Rxe7 51. Qxe7 Kh8 52. Kf4 Kg8 53. Kf5 Kh8 54. Kf6 Kg8 55. Qg7#) (29... Qd2 {Polgar,Judit} 30. Qxh5+ Kg7 31. Rg1+ Kf6 32. Qf5+ Ke7 33. Qxe5+ Kd8 34. Rd1 $18) 30. Qxh5+ Kg8 (30... Kg7 {(Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s)) is not much help} 31. Rg1+ Kf6 32. Rg6+ Kf7 33. Rh6+ Kf8 34. Rh8+ Kg7 35. Rh7+ Kf8 36. Qh6+ Ke8 37. Qe6+ Kf8 38. Qe7+ Kg8 39. Qg7#) 31. Rg1+ Kf8 32. Qh8+ Kf7 33. Qg7+ (33. Qg7+ Ke8 (33... Ke6 34. Rg6+ Rf6 35. Rxf6#) 34. Qxe5+ Kd8 (34... Kf8 {Stockfish 6 64 POPCNT (10s)} 35. Qxf4+ Ke8 36. Rg8+ Kd7 37. Rg7+ Ke8 38. Qf7+ Kd8 39. Rg8#) 35. Rg8+ Kd7 36. Rg7+ $18) 1-0

