{[%mdl 4]} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Bb4 5. e5 h6 6. Bd2 Bxc3 7. bxc3 Ne4 8. Qg4 Kf8 9. Bd3 Nxd2 10. Kxd2 c5 11. h4 c4 {Kortschnoj always blocks the position.} (11... Nc6 12. Rh3 c4 13. Bf1 b5 ({counterattacking with the queen by} 13... Qb6 $5 $13 {could be an interesting alternative  b2}) 14. a3 a5 15. Ne2 Bd7 (15... Rg8 $5 16. Nf4 Ra7 17. Rf3 Qd7 18. Rb1 Rb7 19. Be2 Ne7 20. Qh5 Ke8 21. Qg4 $11 {65-move ½-½ Aronian,L (2390)-Vallejo Pons,F (2420)/Menorca 1996/Juniors (43)}) 16. Nf4 Rg8 (16... b4 17. Rf3 bxc3+ 18. Kd1 $6 h5 $2 19. Nxh5 Rg8 20. Ke1 $2 Qb6 $132 {Lutz,C (2644)-Kortschnoj,V (2635)/Essen 2002}) 17. Rf3 Ke7 18. Nh5 b4 19. Qf4 bxc3+ 20. Ke1 Be8 21. Rxc3 $36 {1-0 Leko,P (2707)-Kortschnoj,V (2635)/Essen 2002/CBM 090 (60)}) 12. Bf1 {Is another possibility in order to play e2, f4.} Nc6 13. Ne2 b5 14. a3 a5 15. Rh3 Rg8 $5 16. Nf4 Ne7 17. Rf3 Nf5 18. Qh3 Ke8 (18... g5 $5 19. hxg5 hxg5 20. g4 Nh4 21. Nh5 Nxf3+ 22. Qxf3 $13) 19. h5 Qh4 20. g4 Qxh3 21. Nxh3 Ne7 22. g5 Rh8 $132 {Black keeps his counterplay in a balanced ending.} 23. Be2 hxg5 24. Nxg5 Nf5 $15 25. Rf4 Ke7 (25... f6 $5) 26. Rg1 Bd7 27. Bg4 Nh6 28. Bf3 Rag8 29. Nh3 Be8 30. Rg5 f6 $2 {[%mdl 8192] Blitz blunder.} (30... Bc6 $11) 31. Rxg7+ $1 Rxg7 32. exf6+ Kf8 33. fxg7+ Kxg7 34. Ng5 Bf7 35. Nxf7 Nxf7 36. Rg4+ Kf8 37. Rg6 Rh6 38. Bg4 Ke7 39. Bxe6 1-0

