cal one for the f6 square and consequently a tactical one hunting down the black king.} Bg6 (23... Bb7 24. Bxh8 Rxh8 25. Ng7+ Kd7 (25... Kd8 26. Ndxe6+ $18) 26. Qxf7+ $1 Nxf7 27. Rxf7+ Kd8 28. Ndxe6#) 24. Bxh8 Rxh8 (24... Bxh5 25. Bxe5 dxe5 26. Nxe6 Qc6 (26... Qc4 27. Nd4 Bg6 28. Rfe1 Qc7 29. Rd2 $16) 27. Nd4 exd4 28. gxh5 {Polgar,Judit: ''} Rg7 29. Rxd4 $18) 25. Nf6+ Kd8 {Polgar,Judit: ''} (25... Kf8 {Polgar,Judit} 26. Nd5 $1 $18) (25... Ke7 {Polgar,Judit} 26. Qh4) 26. h4 Qc5 {It seems that Veselin was not able to stop White's advance, enemy's pieces would manage to get into his position anyway.} (26... h5 27. Qd2 $5 (27. gxh5 Bxh5 28. Nxh5 Rxh5 29. Rg1 Rh7 (29... Qe7 30. Nf3 $1 d5 $13) 30. Rg5 Ke7 $14) (27. Qf4 $1 {Polgar,Judit} Bxc2+ (27... hxg4 28. Qg5 $18) 28. Nxc2 Qxc2+ 29. Ka1 hxg4 (29... Ke7 30. Ne4) 30. Ne4 Rc6 31. Nxd6) 27... hxg4 28. Qg5 {Polgar,Judit: '+-'} Bxc2+ 29. Ka1 Nf3 30. Nxf3 Qe7 31. Ne5 Bxd1 32. Nxf7+ Qxf7 33. Nd5+ Ke8 34. Rxf7 $18) 27. h5 Bh7 28. Qh4 $1 {Polgar,Judit: '+-'} Bxc2+ (28... Kc7 29. Nxh7 Rxh7 30. Rxf7+ $1 Rxf7 31. Nxe6+ $18) 29. Nxc2 $6 {Polgar must have been very happy about the position, she somewhat loses her concentration. Much easier was the simple king retreat and Black would have been doomed.} (29. Ka1 $1 Kc7 (29... Bxd1 30. Nd5+ $18) (29... Qa7 30. Ne4+ Qe7 31. Nxe6+ fxe6 32. Rxd6+ Ke8 (32... Nd7 33. Rf7 Qxh4 34. Rdxd7+ Ke8 35. Nd6#) 33. Nf6+ Kf8 34. Nd5+ $18) 30. Nxc2 Qxc2 31. Rc1 $18) 29... Qxc2+ 30. Ka1 Rc4 (30... Ke7 31. Nd5+ (31. Ng8+ {Polgar,Judit} Kf8 32. Ne7 Re8 33. Ng6+ Nxg6 34. Qf6) 31... Kf8 32. Qf6 Rh7 33. Qe7+ Kg7 (33... Kg8 34. Nf6+ Kh8 35. Nxh7 Kxh7 36. Qxd6 Nc4 37. Qd4 $16) 34. g5 $1 exd5 35. g6 $16) (30... Rc6 31. Nd5+ Kd7 32. Qe7+ Kc8 33. Nb4 Rc7 34. Qxd6 $16) (30... Nd3 {Polgar,Judit} 31. Nd5+ Kd7 32. Qe7+ Kc6 33. Nb4+ $1 Nxb4 34. Rxd6+ Kc5 35. Rxe6+ Kd5 36. Qd6+ Kc4 37. Rf4+) 31. Ne4+ Kc7 (31... Ke8 32. Nxd6+ Kf8 33. Nxc4 $18) 32. Nxd6 Rf4 (32... Rc5 33. Qe7+ Kb6 34. Qb7+ Ka5 35. Qa7 $1 $18) 33. Qe7+ Kb6 34. Qb7+ Ka5 (34... Kc5 35. Qc7+ Nc6 36. Nb7+ $18) 35. Qa7 $1 {A fine move that aquares the black king on the annatural spot a5.} b4 (35... Rxf1 36. Nb7+ Kb4 (36... Ka4 37. Qxa6+ Kb4 38. Qa3+ Kc4 39. Nd6#) 37. Qd4+ Nc4 (37... Qc4 38. Qd6+ $18) 38. Qc5+ Ka4 39. b3+ $18) 36. Rfe1 Nf3 37. Rc1 (37. Nb7+ Kb5 38. Rd6 $18) 37... Nxe1 38. Rxc2 Nxc2+ 39. Kb1 {A truly imaginative attack by Judit!} (39. Kb1 Nd4 40. Nb7+ Kb5 41. Qc5+ Ka4 42. Qa5#) 1-0

