1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6 12. d4 Bd6 13. Re1 Qh4 14. g3 Qh3 {* Finkel,Alexander: 'RR: '*''} 15. Be3 {Finkel,A: 'The classical way to treat the Marshall Attack. In the first lag Anand tried the more ambitious'} (15. Re4 $5 {but ran into problems in the opening.}) 15... Bg4 16. Qd3 Rae8 17. Nd2 Re6 18. a4 Qh5 19. axb5 axb5 20. Qf1 Rfe8 {Finkel,A: 'Diagram '} (20... Bh3 21. Bd1 (21. Qe2 Bg4) 21... Qf5 22. Qe2 g6 (22... c5 23. Nf1 cxd4 24. cxd4 Nb4 25. Ra3 Nc6 26. Rd3 Bb4 $44 {Sax,G-Sokolov,I/Haninge 1989}) 23. Qf3 Qd3 24. Bb3 Rxe3 25. Rxe3 Qxd2 26. Bxd5 cxd5 27. g4 Qxb2 28. Rae1 b4 29. Qxh3 Bf4 $11 {Ivanchuk,V-Grischuk,A/Sochi 2005}) 21. Bxd5 Qxd5 22. h3 Bh5 {Finkel,A: 'The bishop is better placed on h5, as Black's counterplay involves the advance of the f-pawn.'} (22... Bf5 {Ü 93/(286) Finkel,A: '?!' '?!' Finkel,Alexander: '?!' '?!' '?!' Finkel,Alexander: 'RR: 'Ü 93/(286)''} 23. Qg2 Qxg2+ 24. Kxg2 R6e7 25. b3 f6 26. Ra2 Be6 27. c4 Bb4 28. Rc1 Bf5 29. g4 Bd3 30. Nf1 Be4+ 31. Kg1 f5 32. Ng3 $14 {Leko,P-Kasimdzhanov,R/Linares 2005}) 23. Qg2 Qxg2+ {Finkel,A: '!?' '!?' Finkel,Alexander: '!?' '!?' '!?' Finkel,A: 'This move is a novelty. In the previous game Black tried'} (23... f5 {letting White to capture on d5, which proved sufficient to hold a draw. The move in the game makes more sense, even though it seems that White keeps slightly better chances in any case.} 24. Qxd5 cxd5 25. Nf1 f4 26. Bd2 Rxe1 27. Rxe1 Rxe1 28. Bxe1 Be2 29. Nh2 Kf7 30. Kg2 $14 {Gurevich,I-Benjamin,J/New York 1992}) 24. Kxg2 f5 25. Nf3 {Finkel,A: '?!' '?!' Finkel,Alexander: '?!' '?!' '?!' Finkel,A: 'This move is anaccuracy after which the draw is inevitable.'} (25. Ra6 $142 $5 f4 26. gxf4 Bxf4 27. Bxf4 Rxe1 28. Rxc6 Bg6 29. Rc5 $14) 25... f4 26. Bd2 (26. gxf4 Bxf4 27. Bxf4 $140 $2 Bxf3+ 28. Kxf3 Rxe1 $17) 26... fxg3 $5 $146 {Finkel,Alexander: 'RR: 'N!?''} (26... Rxe1) 27. Rxe6 (27. fxg3 $2 Re2+ $19) 27... Rxe6 28. Ra8+ Bf8 29. Ne5 {Finkel,A: 'White can't keep the extra pawn, as after'} (29. Kxg3 $2 Rg6+ 30. Ng5 h6 31. Kh4 Bd1 32. Nh7 $1 {Finkel,Alexander: 'RR: '!''} Kxh7 33. Rxf8 Rg2 $1 {Finkel,A: '' '' Finkel,Alexander: '' '' '' Finkel,Alexander: 'RR: '!'' Finkel,A: 'the white king is in big troubles.'} 34. Rf7 Kg8 35. Rf5 Bc2 $1 36. Re5 Kh7 37. Re7 Rxf2 $17 {Shipov,S}) 29... gxf2 30. Kxf2 Re8 31. Ra6 Bd6 {Finkel,A: '!' '!' Finkel,Alexander: '!' '!' '!' Finkel,A: 'Eliminating white hopes to fight for a win.'} (31... c5 $143 $6 32. b4 cxd4 33. cxd4 Bd1 34. Rb6 Ba4 35. Ke3 Be7 36. Ke4 $14) 32. Bf4 Bxe5 33. Bxe5 Re6 $11 {Finkel,Alexander: 'RR: '=''} 34. b4 Kf7 35. Ra7+ Re7 36. Rxe7+ Kxe7 37. Bxg7 {½-½ (37) Polgar,J (2735)-Adams,M (2719) San Luis 2005 CBM 110 [Finkel,A]} *

