il Golubev (www.chesstoday.net): 'as a serious alternative.'} a5 24. Rxc7 (24. Bxc7 Bxd4 25. Re1 Rxe1+ 26. Qxe1 Bc5 27. Qe8+ Bf8 28. h3 Nd3 $11) 24... Bxd4 $11) 23... Na2 (23... Qf5 24. Bg3 Nd5 25. Qc6 Qe6 26. Qxe6 fxe6 27. Kf1 Rb8 28. Bxc7 Rb4 29. a5 Rb5 $14) 24. Re1 (24. Qc4 $5 Qe4 25. Qxa2 Qxf4 26. Qc4 g6 27. a5 Rd8 28. Qxc7 Qxc7 29. Rxc7 Rd5 $1 (29... Bxd4 30. Kf1 $14 Bf6 31. Rc6 Ra8 32. Nd2 $14) 30. Rc5 Rxc5 31. dxc5 Kf8 $1 32. Nd2 Ke7 33. c6 Bc3 34. Ne4 Bxa5 35. Nc5 Bb6 36. Nxa6 Kd6 $11) 24... Rxe1+ 25. Qxe1 h6 26. Bxc7 Bxd4 $11 27. h3 Bf6 28. Qe8+ Kh7 29. Be5 Qd1+ (29... Bxe5 30. Qxe5 (30. Nxe5 Qe4 $15) 30... Qd1+ 31. Kh2 Qxa4 32. Qf5+ $11) 30. Kh2 Qe2 31. Qb8 Bxe5+ 32. Qxe5 Qxe5+ 33. Nxe5 f6 34. Nd3 Kg6 35. Kg3 Kf5 36. Kf3 Nc3 37. a5 Nb5 38. g4+ Kg5 39. Nc5 f5 40. Nxa6 fxg4+ 41. hxg4 Nd4+ 42. Kg3 Nc6 43. Nc7 Nxa5 {Mikhail Golubev (www.chesstoday.net): 'The players were allowed to agree to a draw. Indeed, the continuation'} 44. Ne8 {Mikhail Golubev (www.chesstoday.net): '='} g6 $4 {Mikhail Golubev (www.chesstoday.net)} 45. f4# {was not likely to happen. At the press conference, Polgar said that it was really nice to pose some problems for Kramnik, but she hardly thought at any moment that she should win. She does not feel either especially happy or unhappy with her overall performance (50%). Somewhere she missed chances, somewhere her opponents did. "It's balanced. It's fifty per cent", said Judit. She also said that Topalov seems to play the most interesting chess among top players. "He also makes mistakes, but he fights, and he has news ideas"... Kramnik confessed that he still not fully [physically] recovered after the Brissago match. Of course, he feels better than after the match, but still not everything is OK. He needs to improve and he will work on improvement. He hopes to play in Dortmund "much better" than in Sofia. He was asked, when, during the last 10 years, did he share the last place in a tournament. Kramnik recalled Novgorod-1996, the similar tournament where he scored -1 and shared 4th-6th places. But he still has one game to play in Sofia, said Vladimir.} 1/2-1/2

