1. e4 {Polgar,Judit Wedberg Wedberg} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Nb8 10. d4 Nbd7 11. Nbd2 Bb7 12. Bc2 c5 13. d5 (13. Nf1 {is more common, but often it's just a transposition, since d5 comes later anyway.}) 13... g6 14. Nf1 a5 $146 {[%mdl 8] Polgar,Judit: 'N!?' In the main line White often takes the initiative on the -side with a timely a2-a4. So Sokolov concentrates on the -side right away.} (14... Nh5 {Polgar,Judit: 'Ü 90/308'} 15. Bh6 Ng7 16. Ne3 Nf6 17. a4 Kh8 18. b3 Rb8 19. Qe2 Bc8 20. axb5 axb5 21. Ra7 $14 {1-0 Karpov,A-Gligoric,S/Leningrad 1973/IZT/[ChessBase] (62)}) 15. a4 b4 {White is invited to close the -side.} 16. Bd3 (16. c4 {is possible, but it gives Black a clear picture of what to do (play on the -side). Judit prefers to keep more options.}) (16. Ne3 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 16... Qc7 (16... Ba6 {Polgar,Judit} 17. Bxa6 Rxa6 18. N3d2 $14) 17. Ne3 (17. N3d2 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 17... bxc3 (17... c4 {Polgar,Judit} 18. Nxc4 bxc3 19. b3) 18. bxc3 c4 19. Bc2 (19. Nxc4 Ba6 $132 (19... Nxe4 $2 {Polgar,Judit} 20. Rxe4 Bxd5 21. Ne3 $16) 20. Na3 {Polgar,Judit} (20. Nb2 {Polgar,Judit} Qxc3) 20... Qxc3) 19... Ba6 20. Nd2 (20. Ng4 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 20... Rfc8 21. Ba3 Bf8 22. Qf3 Bg7 (22... h5 $5 $13 {Polgar,Judit}) (22... Bh6 $5 {Polgar,Judit}) 23. g3 (23. g4 $6 {Polgar,Judit} Bh6) 23... Rab8 24. Kg2 Nb6 {Polgar,Judit: '?!'} (24... h5 $1 {Polgar,Judit}) 25. g4 $1 {White must start to attack before Black manages to open lines on the other side.} Nfd7 26. h4 Nc5 {[%cal Yc5d3]} 27. Bxc5 $1 {Else Black jumps in on d3 with serious play coming.} Qxc5 28. h5 (28. g5 $142 {Polgar,Judit}) 28... Nd7 $6 {Polgar,Judit: '?'} (28... Bh6 $5 {Polgar,Judit: '!'} 29. Qf6 (29. Rh1 Bf4 30. hxg6 fxg6 31. Qh3 Rc7) (29. hxg6 {Polgar,Judit} fxg6 $1 (29... hxg6 30. Rh1 Bf4 31. g5 $1 (31. Qh3 Kf8 32. Qh8+ Ke7 33. Qh4+ Kd7 34. Qf6 Rf8 35. Rh3 (35. Rh7 $6 Bxe3 36. Rxf7+ Rxf7 37. Qxf7+ Kc8 38. fxe3 Qxe3) 35... Kc7) 31... Kf8 (31... Kg7 32. Rh7+ $1 Kxh7 33. Qh3+ Kg8 34. Rh1 $18) (31... Bxg5 32. Rh8+ $1 Kxh8 33. Qxf7 Bh4 34. Rh1 g5 35. Qf6+ Kg8 36. Nf3 $18) 32. Rh7 $40)) 29... Nd7 30. Qh4 Bf4 31. hxg6 fxg6 32. g5 Rb2 33. Rh1 Nf8 34. Ndf1 Qc7 $15) 29. Rh1 Nf8 30. g5 $1 $14 {Black is subdued on the -side and can only wait to see how White is going to increase the pressure against the .} Rb2 {Polgar,Judit: '?'} (30... Qc7 $8 {Polgar,Judit}) 31. Ng4 {Polgar,Judit: '!'} gxh5 {Polgar,Judit: '?'} (31... Rxc2 {Polgar,Judit: '?'} 32. h6 f5 (32... Bh8 33. Nf6+ $18) 33. gxf6 Bxf6 (33... Bh8 $4 34. f7#) 34. Nxf6+ Kh8 35. Nd7 $1 (35. Ne8 {Polgar,Judit} Kg8 36. Qf6 Qa7 37. Nxd6 Rxd2 38. Rh3 Rb8 39. Rf3 $18) 35... Nxd7 36. Qf7 Rg8 37. Qxd7 Qb6 38. Rhb1 Qd8 39. Qxd8 Rxd8 40. Rb6 Rxd2 41. Rxa6 $16) (31... Nd7 {Polgar,Judit} 32. hxg6 (32. Rac1 $5) 32... fxg6 33. Rxh7 $1 Rf8 (33... Kxh7 34. Qf7 $1) 34. Qh3 Rf4 35. Rc1 Nf8 36. Rh4 Bc8 37. Qg3 $16) 32. Nf6+ (32. Nh6+ $2 {Polgar,Judit} Bxh6 33. gxh6 Ng6 34. Qf6 Kf8 35. Rac1 Ke8 $13) 32... Bxf6 33. gxf6 Ng6 (33... Rxc2 34. Qxh5 Rxd2 35. Qg5+ Ng6 36. Qxd2 Nf4+ 37. Kf3 $18 {Black is helpless against the attack on the h-file.} Kh8 {Polgar,Judit} 38. Rh6 $18) 34. Kf1 h4 (34... Kf8 {Polgar,Judit} 35. Qxh5 Rxc2 36. Qxh7 Ke8 37. Qg8+ Nf8 (37... Kd7 38. Qxf7+ Kd8 39. Rh8+ Nxh8 40. Qe7# {#}) 38. Qxf8+ $1 $18) 35. Qh5 Kh8 (35... Kf8 {Polgar,Judit} 36. Qxh7 Rxc2 37. Rxh4 $18) 36. Nf3 (36. Rc1 {Polgar,Judit} Qa3 37. Nf3 Rxc2 38. Rxc2 Qa1+ 39. Ne1 $16) 36... Rxc2 37. Rh2 $1 Rxf2+ (37... Nf4 38. Qxh4 h5 39. Qg5 Rxf2+ 40. Rxf2 Qxf2+ 41. Kxf2 Nh3+ 42. Ke3 Nxg5 43. Nxg5 $18 Kg8 {Polgar,Judit} 44. Rh1 $18) 38. Rxf2 Nf4 39. Qxh4 Rg8 (39... Qe3 {Polgar,Judit} 40. Ng5 h5 41. Rxf4 Qxf4+ 42. Qxf4 exf4 43. Nxf7+ $18) 40. Rh2 h5 {Polgar,Judit} 41. Qxh5+ Nxh5 42. Rxh5# {#} 1-0

