1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Nf3 Ngf6 6. Bd3 c5 7. O-O Nxe4 (7... cxd4 8. Nxd4 Be7 9. Re1 O-O 10. c3 Nxe4 11. Bxe4 Nf6 12. Bc2 Bd7 13. Qd3 g6 14. Bh6 Re8 15. Qf3 Qb6 16. Bb3 Rad8 17. Re2 Bc6 18. Nxc6 Qxc6 19. Qxc6 bxc6 20. h3 $16 {Yemelin,V-Erendzhenov,S/RUS-ch Elista 1995/1-0 (67)}) 8. Bxe4 Nf6 (8... Be7 $5 9. Qe2 (9. c4 $5 O-O 10. Re1 Nf6 11. Bc2 cxd4 12. Bg5 h6 13. Bh4 d3 $5 (13... Bc5 14. Qd3 Re8 15. Rad1 $14) 14. Bxd3 Nh5 15. Bxe7 Qxe7 16. Ne5 $14 {Zapata Alonso-Hoffman Alejandro/It (open), Buenos Aires (Argentina) 1996 (38)}) 9... Qb6 (9... Nf6 $6 10. dxc5 $1 Nxe4 $6 (10... Bxc5 11. Bg5 O-O 12. Rad1 Qb6 13. Bxf6 gxf6 14. c3 $14) 11. Qxe4 Bxc5 12. Qe5 $1 $36 Bf8 13. Re1 Qd6 14. Qb5+ Qd7 15. Qh5 Qc7 16. Nd4 $16 {Tseshkovsky Vitaly-Doroshkievich Vladimir K/Tournament, Novorossijsk (Russia) 1995 (38)}) 10. Rd1 O-O 11. c3 Rd8 12. Bc2 Nf8 13. Be3 $14 {Ebeling,M-Kujala,A/FIN-chT 1989 (31)}) 9. Bg5 $5 {Very popular variation during last couple of years.} cxd4 (9... h6 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. c3 $5 (11. Qd3 $5 $14) 11... Bd6 12. Qa4+ Bd7 (12... Ke7 $5) 13. Qa3 Qe7 14. dxc5 Bxc5 15. b4 Bb6 16. Bxb7 $16 {Honfi,K-Dolgener,T/Budapest FS09 IM-B 1995/1-0 (50)}) 10. Nxd4 (10. Qe2 Be7 11. Rad1 Nxe4 (11... Qb6 12. Rxd4 (12. Nxd4 Qxb2 (12... Bd7 13. Bxf6 gxf6 14. Rfe1 Bc5 15. Nb3 Bb4 16. c3 Be7 17. Qh5 $36 {Kovacevic,A-Kosic,D/YUG 2000/EXT}) 13. Nb5 O-O 14. Nc7 Rb8 15. Bf4 Nxe4 16. Qxe4 Qxa2 $13) 12... Qxb2 13. Rfd1 O-O 14. Ne5 $44) 12. Rxd4 $1 Qxd4 $6 (12... Bd7 $142 $5 13. Bxe7 Qxe7 14. Qxe4 Bc6 $11) 13. Nxd4 Nxg5 14. f4 Nh3+ (14... O-O $5 15. fxg5 Bxg5 16. Nf3 Bd8 $6 17. Qe4 $1 $16 {Rublevsky,S-Zakharevich,I/Maikop 1998/CBM 66}) 15. gxh3 O-O 16. Qe4 $14 {Morozevich-Zakharevich,Russia,1997,1-0} (16. Qe4 Bf6 17. Rd1 Rd8 $6 18. Rd3 $1 Rb8 19. Nf3 Bd7 20. Ne5 $16 {Morozevich,A-Zakharevich,I/Krasnodar 1997/EXT})) 10... Be7 (10... Bc5 11. Nb3 (11. c3 h6 $5 12. Bxf6 $5 Qxf6 13. Qa4+ Bd7 14. Qc4 Bxd4 15. cxd4 Rc8 16. Qb4 $14 {Rublevsky,S-Christiansen,L/Luzern 1997/CBM 62}) 11... Bd6 12. Bxf6 gxf6 13. Qh5 f5 $13 {Morozevich,A-Zakharevich,I/Novgorod 1997/CBM 60}) (10... h6 11. Bxf6 Qxf6 12. Qd3 a6 13. Rad1 Be7 14. Nc6 $1 $14 {Ciganikova,A-Rakay,K/SVK 1999/EXT 2000}) 11. Bf3 $5 {[%cal Gf3a8] Keeping the bishop on diagonal a8-h1 looks more logical than} (11. Bd3 O-O 12. c3 Qd5 $1 13. Nf3 Rd8 14. Bc2 Qxd1 15. Raxd1 Bd7 $11 {Pandavos,P-Ellison,D/Balatonbereny op 1992}) 11... O-O 12. Re1 (12. c3 e5 13. Nc2 h6 14. Bxf6 Bxf6 15. Ne3 Rb8 $11) 12... Qb6 13. Nb3 Rd8 14. Qe2 Bd7 15. Bd2 $5 {[%cal Gd2a5]} Bb4 {Black must play this move first:} (15... a5 $6 16. Qe5 $1 {[%csl Ra5]} Bb4 (16... Bd6 $2 17. Bxa5 Bxe5 18. Bxb6 Bxb2 19. Rab1 Bc3 20. Bxd8 $18) (16... a4 17. Ba5 Rxa5 18. Qxa5 Qxa5 19. Nxa5 $18) 17. Be3 Qa6 18. Nc5 Bxc5 19. Bxc5 $14) 16. c3 Bd6 {[%csl Ge5]} 17. c4 $5 a5 18. Rac1 $5 {Starting extremly interesting complications.} (18. c5 $2 Bxc5 19. Nxc5 Qxc5 20. Bxb7 Rab8 {[%csl Rb2]} 21. Be3 Qb4 22. Bf3 Qxb2 $17) (18. Bc3 Qc7 19. h3 Bc6 $13) 18... a4 19. c5 Bxh2+ 20. Kh1 $5 ({Not perfectly clear is} 20. Kxh2 Qc7+ 21. Kg1 (21. Qe5 Qxe5+ 22. Rxe5 axb3 23. axb3 Bc6 $15 {[%cal Gd8d2]}) 21... axb3 22. axb3 Bc6 23. Bg5 $13) 20... Qc7 21. Na5 (21. Ba5 $2 Qf4 22. Bxd8 Rxd8 $1 (22... Qh6 $2 {[%cal Gh6h1]} 23. Bxf6 Bf4+ 24. Bh5 axb3 25. Rcd1 Qxf6 26. g3 Bc6+ 27. Kg1 $16) 23. g3 Qh6 24. Qe3 g5 25. Kg2 e5 $19 {[%cal Gh6h3]}) 21... Bb5 $1 {Great defensive resourse! After this move black siezes the initiative.} 22. Qxb5 Rxd2 23. Nc4 $8 (23. Qxb7 $2 Rxa5 $19) (23. Nxb7 Rxf2 24. Nd6 Rb8 $17) 23... Rxf2 24. Qxb7 Rb8 $1 {Another great move from black's side.} 25. Qxc7 (25. Qc6 $6 Qf4 $1 {[%cal Gf4h4]} 26. Qd6 $8 Qxc1 $1 27. Qxb8+ Bxb8 28. Rxc1 a3 $1 $15) 25... Bxc7 26. Kg1 Bg3 27. c6 (27. Red1 $5 a3 {[%cal Gf2a2]} 28. b4 $6 g5 $1 (28... Rxa2 $6 29. Na5 g5 30. Nc6 Re8 31. Ra1 $44 {[%csl Ra3]}) 29. Nb6 Rxa2 $19) 27... Ne8 28. Red1 a3 29. bxa3 Rxa2 30. Rd7 g6 $5 31. Rb7 Rd8 32. Rd7 Rc8 33. Rb7 (33. Nb6 $4 Bf2+ $19 {[%cal Gf2g1,Gf2b6]}) 33... Rd8 34. Rd7 Rc8 35. Rf1 Nf6 {Black is a pawn up, but strong passed pawn on c6 makes black's task extremly difficult.} 36. Rb7 Rc7 (36... Nd5 $5 37. Bd1 Rxc6 38. Bb3 Re2 39. Rbxf7 g5 $15 {[%cal Gd5f4]}) 37. Rd1 Kg7 $6 {Black keeps winning chanses after the move in the game as well,but better was} (37... Nd5 $5 38. Bxd5 (38. Rxc7 Bxc7 39. Bxd5 exd5 40. Rxd5 Bg3 $17) 38... exd5 39. Rxc7 Bxc7 40. Rxd5 Bg3 $17 {[%csl Rg1]}) 38. Nd6 Bxd6 39. Rxd6 Rc8 (39... Rxb7 $4 40. cxb7 Rb2 41. Rd8 $18) 40. Rxe6 Rxa3 41. Ree7 Rf8 42. Kf2 Rc3 43. Rb5 Ra8 44. Rbb7 Rf8 45. Rb5 Re8 (45... h5 $5) 46. Rxe8 Nxe8 47. Ke2 Nd6 48. Rb1 Kf6 49. Kd2 Rc5 50. Kd3 Nb5 51. Bg4 Nc7 (51... Ke5 $2 52. Rxb5 $1 Rxb5 53. c7 Rc5 54. c8=Q Rxc8 55. Bxc8 Kf4 56. Ke2 Kg3 $11) 52. Bd7 Ke7 53. Rb8 h5 54. Rc8 Nb5 55. Re8+ Kd6 56. Rf8 Ke7 57. Re8+ Kf6 58. Rb8 Nd6 59. Rb1 Ke7 60. Rb8 Rg5 61. Rb2 Kd8 62. Kd4 Kc7 63. Ra2 Nb5+ (63... h4 $5) 64. Ke3 Re5+ 65. Kd3 Kd6 66. Kc4 Rc5+ 67. Kd3 Nc7 68. Ke4 Re5+ $6 (68... Nd5 $5 69. Rd2 f5+ 70. Kf3 Ke5 71. Re2+ Kf6 $17) 69. Kf3 g5 70. Rb2 Nb5 71. Kf2 Rd5 72. Be8 Rf5+ 73. Kg3 Ke7 74. Re2+ Kf6 75. Rd2 Ke7 76. Re2+ Kd6 77. Rd2+ Ke7 78. Re2+ 1/2-1/2

