1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Be7 6. Bxf6 gxf6 7. Nf3 a6 $5 {Morozevich is ready to play variation which braught him to painful losses in Frankfurt against Leko and Lutz.} (7... Nd7 $5 8. Bd3 c5 9. O-O O-O 10. Qd2 f5 11. Nxc5 Nxc5 12. dxc5 Bf6 $5 $44 {Rogers,I-Short,N/Novi Sad olm 1990}) (7... Qd5 8. Bd3 Bd7 9. O-O Nc6 10. c4 Qh5 11. Ng3 Qg4 12. d5 $14 {Lendwai,R-Fauland,A/Graz 1991}) 8. g3 (8. Qd2 f5 9. Nc3 b5 10. O-O-O {½-½ Watson,W-Anand,V/Palma de Mallorca GMA 1989}) (8. Bd3 Nd7 9. Qe2 c5 10. dxc5 Qa5+ 11. Qd2 Qxd2+ 12. Nfxd2 Nxc5 13. Nxc5 Bxc5 $11 {Cohn,E-Swiderski,R/Wien 1908}) 8... b5 9. Bg2 Bb7 10. Qe2 Nd7 $146 {This move is the novelty.After} (10... Bd5 11. Nc3 c6 (11... Bb4 $5 12. Qe3 c6 13. O-O-O Bxc3 14. Qxc3 Nd7 15. Rhe1 Qb6 $14) 12. O-O-O Nd7 13. Kb1 Nb6 (13... Bc4 14. Qe3 b4 15. Ne2 Nb6 16. Nd2 Nd5 17. Qf3 Bb5 18. Rhe1 $14) 14. Rhe1 $14 {white has got better chanse in Leko,P-Morozevich,A/Frankfurt-West Masters 1999}) 11. O-O O-O 12. Rad1 Bd5 13. Rfe1 Kh8 14. Nfd2 {This game is interesting and quiet unusual:J.Polgar simply didn't manage to find a plan or reasonable set up for the pieces and it looked like she was just making moves without visible connection between them.} (14. a3 c6 15. Nc3 f5 16. Ne5 Nxe5 17. dxe5 $14 {[%cal Ge2e3,Gc3e2,Ge2f4]}) 14... c6 15. c4 bxc4 16. Nxc4 a5 $5 (16... Nb6 17. Nxb6 Qxb6 18. Nc3 Bd6 19. Bxd5 cxd5 20. Qf3 f5 21. b3 $13) 17. Nc3 Re8 18. Ne3 $6 f5 19. Nc4 Qb8 20. Na4 $6 (20. Ne5 Nxe5 21. dxe5 Rg8 22. Qh5 Rg6 23. Rd2 (23. Ne2 Qxb2 24. Nf4 Rg7) 23... Qb4 $13) 20... Qb4 21. b3 Bf6 22. Qc2 Rg8 23. Qc1 (23. a3 Qf8 $5 {[%csl Ra3,Rb3]} (23... Qb8 24. Nc5 Nxc5 25. dxc5 Rg4 26. Nb6 $14) 24. Nab6 Nxb6 25. Nxb6 Ra7 $13) 23... Rg4 24. Ne5 Nxe5 25. dxe5 Be7 26. Rd3 Rag8 $36 {I don't see where white made mistake,but now her position is pretty bad!} 27. Red1 f4 28. Qc3 $6 fxg3 29. hxg3 h5 $1 $17 {[%csl Ra4] The knight on a4 is out of play,while black develops the inititive on the kingside.} 30. Bxd5 cxd5 31. Rf3 Kg7 (31... R8g7 $5) 32. Qc7 (32. Rfd3 h4 33. Rd4 $6 Rxd4 34. Rxd4 Qxc3 35. Nxc3 hxg3 36. Rg4+ Kf8 37. Rxg8+ Kxg8 38. fxg3 Bc5+ 39. Kg2 Bd4 $19) 32... h4 33. Kg2 hxg3 34. fxg3 Qe4 $1 $19 {After this simple and very strong move at the sme time white is helpless.} 35. Qc3 (35. Qxe7 Qe2+ 36. Rf2 (36. Kh3 Qxf3 37. Qf6+ Qxf6 38. exf6+ Kxf6 $19 {[%csl Gg4][%cal Gg8g4]}) 36... Rxg3+ $1 37. Kxg3 Kh8+ {[%cal Gg8g3]} 38. Kh3 Qg4+ 39. Kh2 Qh5+ 40. Qh4 Qxh4#) (35. Nc3 Rxg3+ $1 36. Kxg3 Kh8+ 37. Kf2 Bh4+ $19) (35. Rdf1 Rxg3+ $1 36. Kxg3 Qh4+ 37. Kg2 Kh8+ $19) 35... Qe2+ 36. Kh3 Rg5 0-1

