1. e4 {Psakhis,L} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 O-O 8. Bd3 Nbc6 9. Qh5 Ng6 10. Nh3 {This rare move got some popularity between Hungarinan chessplayers} (10. Nf3 Qc7 11. Be3 c4 12. Bxg6 fxg6 13. Qg4 Qf7 14. Ng5 Qe8 15. h4 h6 16. Nh3 Bd7 17. Nf4 Ne7 18. Qe2 b5 19. g4 a5 $13 {½-½ Balogh,C-Almasi,I/Budapest-4 GM 2000/ (42)}) 10... Qc7 11. Be3 $146 (11. O-O cxd4 (11... c4 12. Be2 f6 13. f4 Qf7 14. a4 Nge7 15. Ba3 Qxh5 16. Bxh5 f5 17. a5 a6 18. Rfb1 g6 19. Be2 Re8 20. Kf2 Na7 21. Bc1 Nb5 22. Bd2 Bd7 {Almasi,Z-Holzke,F/Elekes Memorial 1993/1-0 (39)}) 12. cxd4 Nxd4 13. Ng5 h6 14. Nxf7 Qxf7 15. Bxg6 Qc7 16. Bd2 a5 17. Rad1 Nf5 18. g4 Nd4 19. f4 Bd7 20. g5 Be8 21. Bxe8 Raxe8 22. gxh6 Re7 23. Bxa5 Qxa5 24. Rxd4 Qc5 25. Qd1 gxh6 26. Qd3 {Almasi,Z-Portisch,F/Zalakaros 1992/½-½ (63)}) 11... Nce7 12. f4 Qa5 13. Bd2 Qa4 {[%cal Rc5c4] A typical move in these positions.} 14. g4 $6 {[%mdl 512] Maybe too agressive, White could take on c5-} (14. dxc5 b6 $5 15. cxb6 axb6 {[%csl Rc2,Rc3][%cal Gc8a6] with unclear position}) 14... c4 15. Be2 ({Deserves attention} 15. Bxg6 $5) 15... Qxc2 16. Rc1 Qb2 17. Ng5 {Provoces h6} h6 18. Nh3 {[%cal Gg4g5]} f6 $1 {Strong defensive move} 19. g5 hxg5 20. exf6 (20. fxg5 $2 fxe5 21. dxe5 Bd7 $17) 20... Rxf6 21. Nxg5 (21. fxg5 $2 Rf7 $17) 21... Nf8 22. Qe8 Nf5 (22... Qxa3 $5 23. Bh5 $140 Nf5 24. Bf7+ Kh8 25. Bxe6 Qe7 $17 {leads to black's advantage}) 23. Bg4 Qxa3 24. Bxf5 Rxf5 {White hasn't sufficient compensation for two pawns.} 25. O-O Qd6 26. Rce1 Rb8 27. Rf3 {[%cal Rf3h3]} Bd7 (27... g6 $5 {[%cal Rc8d7]} 28. Qa4 a6 $17) 28. Qh5 g6 (28... Be8 $2 29. Qh4 Bg6 30. Rh3 Nh7 31. Nxh7 Rh5 32. Nf6+ gxf6 33. Qxf6 Rxh3 34. Qxg6+ Kh8 35. Qf6+ Kg8 36. Kh1 $18 {[%cal Re1g1]}) 29. Qh4 Qe7 $8 30. Ra1 $1 {[%cal Gd2c1,Gc1a3] Judit tries to find chances in very bad position.} e5 $5 (30... a6 $5 31. Bc1 Nh7) 31. dxe5 (31. fxe5 $5 Rxf3 32. Nxf3 Qxh4 33. Nxh4 a6 $15) 31... Ne6 32. Rh3 Nxg5 33. fxg5 Qg7 34. e6 (34. Re1 Rxe5 35. Rxe5 Bxh3 36. Bf4 Rf8 $1 $17) 34... Bxe6 35. Re1 Re8 $2 ({Why not} 35... Bd7 {[%cal Gb8f8] and} 36. Re7 $140 {fails} (36. Be3 Re8 37. Bd4 Rxe1+ 38. Qxe1 Rxg5+) {because of} 36... Rf1+ $1 37. Kxf1 Bxh3+ 38. Qxh3 Qxe7 $19) 36. Rhe3 Qf7 $2 ({After} 36... Qd7 37. Rh3 Rf1+ 38. Rxf1 Bxh3 $17 {Black still could get better game}) 37. Rh3 Qg7 38. Rhe3 Qf7 39. Rh3 1/2-1/2

