1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 Qc7 8. Qxg7 Rg8 9. Qxh7 cxd4 10. Ne2 Nbc6 11. f4 dxc3 12. Qd3 d4 (12... Bd7 {is most popular move in this position}) 13. Rb1 (13. Nxd4 Nxd4 14. Qxd4 Bd7 15. Rg1 Nf5 16. Qf2 Qc6 17. Bd3 Qd5 18. g3 Nd4 19. Rf1 Bc6 $13 {0-1 Semina,S-Ludwig,K/BLw 0001 2000/ (59)}) 13... Bd7 14. Ng3 O-O-O 15. Be2 Nf5 16. Kf2 $5 $146 {New and interesting move} (16. Nxf5 {After "normal" continuation} exf5 17. Bf3 f6 $5 (17... Be6 18. a4 Qa5 19. Qb5 Qxb5 20. axb5 Na5 21. Ra1 b6 22. Kf2 $16 {1-0 Zhuravlev,V-Kuzmichev,A/Rostov 1975 (39)}) 18. exf6 Rgf8 19. O-O Rxf6 {Black is getting sufficient counterplay}) ({Just bad} 16. Ne4 $2 {- after typical sacrifice} Nxe5 $1 17. fxe5 Qxe5 18. g3 Bc6 19. Bf3 Nh4 $1 20. gxh4 f5 $17 {advantage of Black is obvious}) 16... Nce7 (16... Nxg3 17. hxg3 Rh8 18. Rh3 $1) ({Worth considering} 16... f6 $5 17. exf6 Rdf8 18. Ne4 Nd6 $13) 17. Ne4 Bc6 18. g4 $1 Nh4 ({After} 18... Nh6 19. Rg1 {[%csl Rh6] Black will have troubles with a knight}) 19. Rd1 (19. Nd6+ Rxd6 $1 20. exd6 Qxd6 $44) 19... Kb8 ({It looks that} 19... Bxe4 20. Qxe4 Nc6 21. a4 {[%cal Gc1a3]} Ng6 {[%cal Gg8h8] leads to nice position for Black}) 20. Rb4 Bxe4 21. Qxe4 Nc6 22. Rb1 Ka8 ({Again} 22... Ng6 {[%cal Gg8h8] was not a bad idea, for example} 23. Ba6 b6 24. Be2 Rh8 25. Bf3 Nge7 $13) 23. a4 a6 (23... Ng6 $1) 24. Ba3 {[%cal Ga3d6,Ga3c5]} Rd5 $4 {[%mdl 8192] It was a last chance to play} (24... Ng6 $142 $5 {with the idea to organize couterplay on the h line and i am not sure, that White can get any advantage, for example} 25. Bc5 (25. Rb3 Rh8 26. Kg1 f5 $1 $132) 25... Rd5 26. Bd6 Rxd6 27. exd6 Qxd6 28. Rb6 $140 Nxf4 29. Bxa6 Nd5 $1 30. Bxb7+ Ka7 $17) 25. Qh7 $1 $18 {Now game is over, Judit doesn't lose her chance to win key pawn and , soon , game.} Qd8 $8 26. Qxf7 Rd7 27. Qf6 Qa5 28. Qxe6 Rgg7 29. Bd3 1-0

