{[%mdl 1]} 1. e4 {Ftacnik} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Be7 6. Bxf6 Bxf6 7. Nf3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nd7 9. O-O-O Be7 10. Bd3 b6 11. Neg5 $5 {A new move in very popular position. White is starting an actions on the kingnside without preliminary preparations.} (11. h4 Bb7 12. Rh3 (12. Qe2 Nf6 13. Neg5 Bxf3 14. Nxf3 Qd6 15. Ne5 c5 16. dxc5 Qxc5 17. Kb1 Bd6 18. Nc4 Rfd8 19. g4 Bf8 20. Nd2 $14 {Van den Doel,E-Sakalauskas,V/Bled 2002}) (12. c3 c5 13. Neg5 (13. dxc5 Qc7 14. Neg5 Nf6 15. Qe2 Qf4+ 16. Kb1 Bxc5 17. g3 Bxf3 18. Nxf3 Qc7 $11 {Al Modiahki,M-Arizmendi Martinez,J/Biel 2002}) 13... Nf6 14. Qc2 g6 15. h5 Nxh5 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Bxg6 Nf4 18. Bxh7+ $40 {Ivanchuk,V-Radjabov,T/Moscow 2002}) 12... c5 13. Rg3 Qc7 14. dxc5 Rfd8 15. Nfg5 $1 bxc5 16. Nd6 Bxd6 17. Bxh7+ Kf8 18. Qxd6+ Qxd6 19. Rxd6 $16 {Gashimov,V-Dizdar,G/Dubai 2003}) (11. Qf4 $5 Bb7 12. h4 Nf6 13. Neg5 Qd6 14. Ne5 Rad8 15. Rh3 h6 16. g4 c5 17. Ngxf7 Qxd4 18. Qxd4 Rxd4 19. g5 $36 {Guliev,L-Gouliev,N/Baku 2001}) 11... h6 12. Bh7+ $1 {It's very important to drag black king to h8 for the further combination. Ftacnik: 'The dreams of a great chessplayers include the desire to ocassionally win the game stright from the preparation. In a well known position Polgar comes with a concept of violent attack on the black king with little concern for the material sacrifices. '} (12. h4 Bb7 13. Bh7+ Kh8 14. Be4 Bxe4 15. Nxe4 c5 16. d5 exd5 17. Qxd5 Nf6 18. Qf5 Qc8 19. Qxc8 Rfxc8 20. Nxf6 Bxf6 21. g4 $14 {Al Modiahki,M-Abdul,M/Doha 2002}) 12... Kh8 13. Be4 hxg5 $2 {My guess is that black overlooked Judit's reply, otherwise he wouldn't dare to take the knight which was beging to be taken.} (13... Rb8 14. h4 Ba6 (14... Nf6 15. Ne5 Nxe4 16. Ngxf7+ Kg8 17. Nxd8 Nxd2 18. Ndc6 $18) 15. Qf4 $36) 14. g4 $3 $40 {Brilliant move! White's idea is to open an h-file and deliver a mate. For this purpose white is ready to waste a precious tempo. However this tempo doesn't help black to build up a defensive line up on the kingside since his rook is attacked and he has to move it.} (14. Bxa8 $2 g4 $15 {[%cal Ge7g5]}) 14... Rb8 15. h4 g6 ({It's hard to believe that black would've survived also after} 15... gxh4 16. g5 Kg8 17. Qf4 f5 18. Bc6 Kf7 19. Qxh4 Bd6 20. Rde1 $40) 16. hxg5+ Kg7 17. Qf4 {Ftacnik: 'It is almost sure that white had this very position on the board during preparation, black pieces are too passive for the sucessful coping with the threats along the open h file.'} Bb7 ({An only move not to lose on the spot was} 17... Rh8 $8 {however it wouldn't influence an outcome of the game.} 18. Rxh8 (18. Rh6 $6 Bxg5 19. Nxg5 Rxh6 20. Qxf7+ Kh8 21. Qf4 Qf8 22. Nf7+ Kh7 $17) 18... Qxh8 19. Ne5 Qe8 20. Rh1 $18 {[%cal Gf4h2] and black is helpless against h2.}) 18. Rh7+ $1 Kxh7 (18... Kg8 19. Rdh1 f5 20. gxf6 Bxf6 21. Rh8+ Bxh8 22. Rxh8+ Kxh8 23. Qh6+ Kg8 24. Qxg6+ Kh8 25. Qh7#) 19. Qh2+ Kg8 20. Rh1 Bxg5+ 21. Nxg5 Qxg5+ 22. f4 Qxf4+ 23. Qxf4 Bxe4 24. Qxe4 1-0

